hadiths[1148]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","(1) Abu 'Abd Allah — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz — and Abu Zakariyya — Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya, may Allah have mercy upon them both, informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman — informed us: al-Shafi'i — informed us: Malik.\n\n(And the second chain:) Abu 'Ali — al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Rudhbari, may Allah have mercy upon him, informed us in the Kitab al-Sunan: Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Razzaq, known as Ibn Dasah, in al-Basrah — informed us: Abu Dawud — Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath al-Sijistani — informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Maslamah, from Malik, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Sa'id ibn Salamah of the family of Ibn al-Azraq, that al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah — who was from Banu 'Abd al-Darah — informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say:\n\n\A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," we ride the sea and carry with us a small amount of water. If we perform ablution with it"," we become thirsty. Shall we perform ablution with the water of the sea?' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Its water is purifying (tahur)"," and its dead (creatures) are lawful (halal).'\""\n\nAnd al-Julah Abu Kathir corroborated Safwan ibn Sulaym in his narration from Sa'id ibn Salamah.\n\n[Sound. Narrated by Abu Dawud (83)"," al-Tirmidhi (69)"," and al-Nasa'i (332).]"""
"2","(2) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: 'Ali ibn Hamshadh al-'Adl informed us: 'Ubayd ibn 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Sharik informed us: Yahya ibn Bukayr informed me: al-Layth narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, and al-Julah Abu Kathir informed us that Ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi narrated to him that al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say:\n\n\We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) one day when a hunter came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," we set out to the sea seeking game"," and one of us carries a small water vessel"," hoping to catch game nearby. Sometimes it is so"," and sometimes he does not find game until he reaches a part of the sea he never expected to reach. He may experience a wet dream or need ablution. If he bathes or performs ablution with this water"," perhaps thirst will destroy one of us. Do you see any issue with us bathing or performing ablution with the water of the sea when we fear that?' He (al-Mughirah) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Bathe from it and perform ablution with it"," for its water is purifying (tahur)"," and its dead (creatures) are lawful (halal).'\""\n\nAnd Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari and Yazid ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi corroborated Sa'id in his narration"," except that there was disagreement regarding it from Yahya ibn Sa'id. It was narrated from him: from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah"," from a man of Banu Mudlij"," from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\n\nAnd it was narrated from him: from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah"," that a man of Banu Mudlij.\n\nAnd it was narrated from him: from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mughirah al-Kindi"," from a man of Banu Mudlij.\n\nAnd it was narrated from him: from al-Mughirah ibn 'Abd Allah"," from a man of Banu Mudlij.\n\nAnd from him: from al-Mughirah ibn 'Abd Allah"," from his father.\n\nAnd other than this was also said. They also differed regarding the name of Sa'id ibn Salamah. It was said as Malik said"," and it was said: 'Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Makhzumi.\n\nAnd it was said: Salamah ibn Sa'id"," and he is the one whom al-Shafi'i (may Allah be pleased with him) intended by his statement: \""In its chain is someone I do not know"," or al-Mughirah"," or both of them — except that the one who established its chain is trustworthy.\"" Malik ibn Anas recorded it in al-Muwatta'"," and Abu Dawud narrated it in al-Sunan.\n\nAnd the hadith has been narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him)"," Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah"," and 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr (may Allah be pleased with them)"," from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\n\n[Sound through other chains. Narrated by Ahmad (2/378).]"""
"3","(3) Al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar narrated from Sa'id ibn Thawban, from Abu Hind al-Firasi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \Whoever the sea does not purify"," Allah will not purify him.\""\n\nAbu Hazim — 'Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Hafiz — informed us: Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz — informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah — al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ufayr al-Ansari — informed us: Muhammad ibn Humayd — informed us: Ibrahim ibn Mukhtar — informed us: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar"," and he mentioned it with its like"," except that he did not say \""al-Firasi.\""\n\n[Very weak. Narrated by al-Daraqutni (1/35).]"""
"4","(4) Abu al-Husayn — 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran — in Baghdad, informed us: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar — informed us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan — informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Tufayl — 'Amir ibn Wathilah — that Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about the dead (creatures) of the sea, and he said: \Its water is purifying (tahur)"," and its dead (creatures) are lawful (halal).\""\n\n[Sound. Narrated by al-Daraqutni (1/35).]"""
"5","(5) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, may Allah have mercy upon him, informed us: 'Ali ibn Hamshadh — informed us: 'Ubayd ibn 'Abd al-Wahid — informed us: Ibn Abi Maryam — informed me: Yahya ibn Ayyub — informed me: Khalid ibn Yazid — informed me that Yazid ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to him, from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said:\n\n\A group of people came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'We hunt in the sea and have with us some fresh water. We sometimes fear thirst. Is it permissible for us to perform ablution from the salty sea water?' He said: 'Yes"," perform ablution from it…' And he mentioned the hadith.\""\n\n[Sound through other chains. Narrated by al-Hakim (1/239).]"""
"6","(6) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan — informed us: Abu Usamah — from al-Walid ibn Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Rafi' ibn Khadij, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said:\n\nIt was said: \O Messenger of Allah"," shall we perform ablution from the well of Buda'ah? It is a well into which filth"," carrion"," menstrual cloths"," and dead dogs are thrown.\"" He said: \""Water is pure (tahur)"," and nothing renders it impure.\""\n\nAbu Dawud narrated it in al-Sunan. He said"," and some of them said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi'.\n\n(Q) Shaykh Ahmad"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: The hadith is upon its purity provided no impurity is thrown into the well. If impurity is thrown into it"," then the meaning of the hadith pertains to water that reaches the measure of two qullahs and has not changed. Its evidence will come in its proper place"," if Allah the Most High wills."""
"7","(7) Abu al-Hasan — Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-'Alawi, may Allah the Most High have mercy upon him, informed us: Abu Hamid — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Bilal al-Bazzar — informed us: Ahmad ibn Hafs — informed me: My father — informed me: Ibrahim ibn Tahman — from 'Abbad ibn Ishaq, from his father, from Thabit ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, who said:\n\n\I saw myself with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in water from the sky"," and I was rubbing his back and washing it.\""\n\n[Weak. Narrated by Ibn Tahman in his Mashyakha (7).]"""
"8","(8) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Ahmad — 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-'Adl — both informed us, saying: Abu 'Abd Allah — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Hafiz — informed us: Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah — informed us: Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi — informed us: Shu'bah, from Majza'ah ibn Zahir al-Aslami, who said: I heard 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Awfa say:\n\nThe Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: \O Allah"," to You is praise filling the heavens"," filling the earth"," and filling whatever You will besides. O Allah"," purify me with snow"," hail"," and cold water. O Allah"," purify me of sins and cleanse me from them as a white garment is cleansed of dirt and filth.\""\n\nAbu al-Husayn Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated it in al-Sahih through various routes from Shu'bah.\n\n[Sound. Narrated by Muslim (204).]"""
"9","(9) Abu Muhammad — 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf — informed us: Abu Sa'id Ibn al-A'rabi — informed us: Sa'dan ibn Nasr — informed us: Abu Mu'awiyah, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to seek refuge, saying: \O Allah"," wash my heart with the water of snow and hail.\"" And she mentioned the hadith.\n\nAl-Bukhari and Muslim both narrated it in al-Sahih from the hadith of Abu Mu'awiyah. And some of them said in the hadith: \""O Allah"," wash my sins with the water of snow and hail.\""\n\n[Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhari (6016) and Muslim (589).]"""
"10","(10) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Walid al-Faqih — informed us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan — informed us: Muhammad ibn Marzuq — informed us: al-'Ala' ibn al-Fadl ibn 'Abd Allah — informed us: al-Haytham ibn Ruzayq, from his father, from al-Asla' ibn Sharik, who said:\n\n\I used to prepare the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for travel. I experienced a nocturnal emission on a cold night"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to set out with the mount. I disliked preparing his mount while I was in a state of janabah"," and I feared that if I bathed with cold water I would die.\"" And he mentioned the hadith.\n\nHe said: \""Then I placed stones and heated water in them and bathed. Then I caught up with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and he said: 'O Asla'"," why do I see your mount trembling?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I did not prepare it.' And he mentioned the hadith until he said: I said: 'So I heated water and bathed.'\""\n\n[Very weak. Narrated by al-Tabari in al-Kabir (877).]"""
"11","(11) The jurist Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Idrīs ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Ghurāb narrated from Hishām ibn Saʿd, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Aslam, the freedman of ʿUmar, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, used to have water heated for him in a flask (qumqumah) and would perform ghusl with it.\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan said: This is a sound (ṣaḥīḥ) chain of narration. [Sound through other routes. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it (1/37).]"
"12","(12) Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad informed me; Ṣadaqah ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, that ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to dislike performing ghusl with sun-heated water, and he said: \Indeed"," it causes leprosy (baraṣ).\""\n\n[Very weak (ḍaʿīf jiddan). Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it in al-Umm and al-Musnad"," as mentioned in al-Talkhīṣ (1/22).]"""
"13","(13) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd the jurist informed us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Khālid al-ʿAbdī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us; Ismāʿīl, that is Ibn ʿAyyāsh, narrated from Ṣafwān ibn ʿAmr, from Ḥassān ibn Azhar, who said: ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Do not perform ghusl with sun-heated water"," for indeed it causes leprosy (baraṣ).\""\n\n[Weak (ḍaʿīf). Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it in his Sunan (1/39).]"""
"14","(14) A mursal hadith has been narrated concerning this: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf ibn Aḥmad al-Aṣbahānī narrated it to us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān the trustworthy narrator in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; he said: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Khālid ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \I heated water in the sun"," and the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: 'Do not do that"," O Ḥumayrāʾ"," for indeed it causes leprosy (baraṣ).'\""\n\nAnd this is not sound (lā yaṣiḥḥ). (J) The jurist Abū Bakr informed us; he said: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī said: Khālid ibn Ismāʿīl is abandoned (matrūk).\n\nAnd Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣūfī informed us; he said: Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAdī the Ḥāfiẓ said: Khālid ibn Ismāʿīl"," Abū al-Walīm al-Makhzūmī"," fabricates hadith against trustworthy Muslims.\n\n(T) He said: Wahb ibn Wahb"," Abū al-Bakhtarī"," also narrated this hadith from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah alongside Khālid"," and he is worse than him.\n\nShaykh Aḥmad"," may Allah the Most High have mercy upon him"," said: It has also been narrated through another reprehensible (munkar) chain from Ibn Wahb"," from Mālik"," from Hishām"," and it is not sound. And ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad al-Aʿṣam narrated it from Fulayḥ"," from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUrwah.\n\n(J) The jurist Abū Bakr informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar said: ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad al-Aʿṣam is a narrator of reprehensible (munkar) hadith"," and no one other than him narrated it from Fulayḥ"," and it is not sound from al-Zuhrī.\n\n[Fabricated (mawḍūʿ). Al-Thaqafī narrated it in al-Tafḍīlāt (3/21/1).]"""
"15","(15) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq the jurist informed us; Abū al-Muthannā informed us; Musaddad narrated to us; Khālid narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ, from Abū Qilābah, from ʿAmr ibn Bujdān, from Abū Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Pure earth (al-ṣaʿīd al-ṭayyib) is the ablution (wuḍūʾ) of the Muslim"," even if for ten years. When you find water"," then let it touch your skin"," for that is better.\"""""
"16","(16) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us; Hishām narrated from Ḥafṣah bint Sīrīn, from Umm ʿAṭiyyah al-Anṣāriyyah, who said: One of the daughters of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, passed away, so he came to us and said: \Wash her with water and lotus leaves (sidr)"," and wash her an odd number of times—three"," five"," or more than that if you see fit. And place camphor (kāfūr) in the last washing"," or some camphor.\"" And she mentioned the remainder of the hadith.\n\n[Narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs by Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī and Abū al-Ḥusayn Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj al-Qushayrī from the hadith of Hishām ibn Ḥassān and others. [Sound. Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh). Its detailed citation will appear in the Book of Funerals.]]"""
"17","(17) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān the trustworthy narrator in Baghdād informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-ʿAwwām narrated to us; Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Nāfiʿ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, from Umm Hānīʾ, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and Maymūnah performed ghusl from a single vessel—a large bowl in which there were traces of dough.\n\n[Sound (ṣaḥīḥ). Al-Nasāʾī narrated it (240).]"
"18","(18) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us; Abū Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; Abū Isḥāq narrated from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from a man, from Abū Murrah, the freedman of ʿAqīl, from Umm Hānīʾ bint Abī Ṭālib, who mentioned the story of the Conquest (of Makkah). She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, came with the smell of dust on his face, and he said: \O Fāṭimah"," pour water for me for ghusl.\"" So she poured for him into a large bowl in which there were traces of dough"," and she screened him"," and he performed ghusl and prayed eight rakʿahs.\n\nIt has also been narrated from Mujāhid"," from Abū Fākhitah"," from Umm Hānīʾ"," but what we have narrated"," despite its being mursal"," is more sound.\n\n[Sound through other routes. Al-Ḥumaydī narrated it in his Musnad (331).]"""
"19","(19) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Khārijah narrated from Abū Umayyah; Mujāhid narrated to me from Abū Fākhitah, the freedman of Umm Hānīʾ. He said: Umm Hānīʾ said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, during the days of the Conquest (of Makkah) in the morning (ḍuḥā). He ordered for water to be brought, and it was poured for him into a large bowl in which I could see traces of dough. He ordered for a garment, and he was screened from me, and he performed ghusl. Then he prayed the morning prayer (ṣalāt al-ḍuḥā), eight rakʿahs.\n\n[Reprehensible chain of narration (munkar al-isnād). This chain of narration is very reprehensible. It contains Khārijah ibn Muṣʿab.]"
"20","(20) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from al-Muṭṭalib ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥanṭab, from Umm Hānīʾ, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, descended at the upper part of Makkah on the day of the Conquest. I came to him, and Abū Dharr came with a large bowl containing water. She said: I could see traces of dough in it. She said: Abū Dharr screened him, and he performed ghusl. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, screened Abū Dharr, and he performed ghusl. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, prayed eight rakʿahs, and that was in the morning (ḍuḥā).\n\n[Weak (ḍaʿīf). Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it (1457).]"
"21","(21) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥārithī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: Abū Isḥāq al-Fazārī narrated from al-Awzāʿī, from a man he named, from Umm Hānīʾ: that she disliked performing wuḍūʾ with water in which bread had been soaked.\n\n(And this, if it is sound, is only intended when the bread has overwhelmed the water to the extent that it is attributed to it.) [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī, 1/39]"
"22","(22) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqrīʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us: Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ narrated from Abū Qilābah, from ʿAmr ibn Budjān, who said: I heard Abū Dharr saying — and he mentioned his account — then he said, from the Prophet ﷺ: \The pure earth is the wuḍūʾ of the Muslim"," even if for ten years; but when he finds water"," let him let it touch his skin"," for that is better.\""\n\n[Sound. Its takhrīj will follow in the aḥādīth.]"""
"23","(23) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Every drink that intoxicates is ḥarām.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," both from Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 239"," and Muslim"," 2001]"""
"24","(24) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, meaning Ibn Mahdī, informed us: Bishr ibn Manṣūr narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ: that he disliked performing wuḍūʾ with milk or with nabīdh, and he said: \Indeed"," tayammum is more preferable to me than that.\"" [Sound. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 86]"""
"25","(25) Abū ʿAlī informed us: Abū Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us: Abū Khaldah said: I asked Abū al-ʿĀliyah about a man who experiences janābah and has no water, but has nabīdh — may he perform ghusl with it? He said: \No.\"" [Sound. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 87]"""
"26","(26) As for the ḥadīth that Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī informed us in Baghdād: Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: al-Thawrī narrated from Abū Fazārah al-ʿAbsī: Abū Zayd, the mawlā of ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth, narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: On the Night of the Jinn, two men from among the jinn lagged behind. Al-Ramādī said: I think ʿAbd al-Razzāq said: They said: \We wish to attend the prayer with you"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: When the prayer time came"," the Prophet ﷺ said to me: \""Do you have wuḍūʾ water?\"" I said: \""No"," I have a small vessel containing nabīdh.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""A pure date and purifying water.\"" So he performed wuḍūʾ. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 84]"""
"27","(27) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Muḥāribī informed us in al-Kūfah: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah informed us: Abū Ghassān informed us: Qays, meaning Ibn al-Rabīʿ, informed us: Abū Fazārah al-ʿAbsī narrated from Abū Zayd, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and said: \I have been commanded to recite to your brothers from among the jinn. Let one man from among you stand with me"," and let no man stand with me who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride.\"" He said: So I stood with me a small vessel of water — he said this — until when we went out"," he drew a line around me and said: \""Do not exit from it"," for if you exit from it"," you will not see me and I will not see you until the Day of Resurrection.\"" He said: Then he departed until he disappeared from my sight. He said: So I remained standing until when Fajr rose"," he came and said: \""Why do I see you standing?\"" He said: I said: \""I did not sit"," fearing that I might exit from it.\"" He said: \""If you had exited from it"," you would not have seen me and I would not have seen you until the Day of Resurrection. Do you have any wuḍūʾ water?\"" I said: \""No.\"" He said: \""What is in the vessel?\"" I said: \""Nabīdh.\"" He said: \""A sweet date and good water.\"" Then he performed wuḍūʾ and established the prayer. When he finished the prayer"," two men from the jinn came to him and asked him about provisions. He said: \""Did I not command you and your people what would benefit you?\"" He said: \""Yes"," but we loved that some of us attend the prayer with you.\"" He said: \""From where are you two?\"" He said: \""From the people of Naṣībīn.\"" He said: \""These two have succeeded"," and their people have succeeded.\"" He commanded them that bones and dung are food and fodder"," and he forbade us from using a bone or dung for istinjāʾ.\n\n(c) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: I heard Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥammād say: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""Abū Zayd"," who narrated the ḥadīth of Ibn Masʿūd that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'A pure date and purifying water' — he is an unknown man"," not established as having met ʿAbd Allāh.\""\n\n(t) ʿAlqamah narrated from ʿAbd Allāh that he said: \""I was not present on the Night of the Jinn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""\n\nShuʿbah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah: I asked Abū ʿUbaydah: \""Was ʿAbd Allāh with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Night of the Jinn?\"" He said: \""No.\""\n\n(c) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī said: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī said: \""This ḥadīth revolves around Abū Fazārah from Abū Zayd"," the mawlā of ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth"," from Ibn Masʿūd. Abū Fazārah is well-known — his name is Rāshid ibn Kaysān — and Abū Zayd"," the mawlā of ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth"," is unknown. This ḥadīth is not authentic from the Prophet ﷺ"," and it contradicts the Qurʾān.\""\n\n(t) The Shaykh Aḥmad"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""This ḥadīth has also been narrated from Ḥammād ibn Salamah from ʿAlī ibn Zayd ibn Judʿān from Abū Rāʿif from Ibn Masʿūd; and from Abū Sālām from Fulān ibn Ghaylān al-Thaqafī from Ibn Masʿūd; and from Ibn Lahīʿah from Qays ibn al-Ḥajjāj from Ḥanash from Ibn ʿAbbās from Ibn Masʿūd; and Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn Ḥabbān narrated it from al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah with his chain to Ibn Masʿūd; and al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-ʿIjlī narrated it with his chain from Ibn Masʿūd — and none of that is authentic.\""\n\n(c) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh said: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ said in weakening these chains: \""ʿAlī ibn Zayd is weak"," and this ḥadīth is not among the narrations of Ḥammād ibn Salamah. The Thaqafī man who narrated it from Ibn Masʿūd is unknown — it is said his name is ʿAmr"," and it is said ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn Ghaylān. Ibn Lahīʿah is weak in ḥadīth"," and his ḥadīth is not used as proof. Al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah and Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā are both weak. And al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-ʿIjlī fabricates ḥadīth against reliable narrators.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""Ibn Masʿūd denied having been present with the Prophet ﷺ on the Night of the Jinn in the narration of ʿAlqamah from him"," and his son denied it"," and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī denied it.\"" [Weak. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr"," 9962]"""
"28","(28) As for the ḥadīth of ʿAlqamah: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us by dictation: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-ʿAbdī and Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Khālid, meaning al-Ḥadhāʾ, narrated from Abū Maʿshar, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: \I was not present on the Night of the Jinn with the Prophet ﷺ"," and I wish I had been with him.\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Sound. Narrated by Muslim"," 450]"""
"29","(29) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Naḍr, Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym, and Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib said: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to me: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated from Dāwūd, from ʿĀmir, who said: \I asked ʿAlqamah: 'Was Ibn Masʿūd present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Night of the Jinn?' ʿAlqamah said: 'I asked Ibn Masʿūd: \""Did any of you witness the Night of the Jinn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" He said: \""No. Rather"," we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night and we lost him. We searched for him in the valleys and mountain passes and said: 'He has been carried off or seized.' We spent the worst night a people ever spent. When morning came"," he came from the direction of Ḥirāʾ. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," we lost you and searched for you but could not find you"," and we spent the worst night a people ever spent.' He said: 'The caller of the jinn came to me"," so I went with him and recited the Qurʾān to them.' He said: 'Then he took us and showed us their traces and the traces of their fires. They asked him about provisions"," and he said: \""Every bone over which the name of Allah has been mentioned"," when it falls into your hands"," will be the fullest of flesh"," and every dropping is fodder for your animals.\""' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not perform istinjāʾ with them"," for they are the food of your brothers.'\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. [Sound. Narrated by Muslim"," 450]"""
"30","(30) As for the ḥadīth of Abū ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd: Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who said: \I asked Abū ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAbd Allāh: 'Was ʿAbd Allāh with the Prophet ﷺ on the Night of the Jinn?' He said: 'No.' And I asked Ibrāhīm"," and he said: 'Would that our companion had been there!'\"" [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 33946]"""
"31","(31) As for the hadith which Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdy al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Yūsuf ibn Baḥr informed us, al-Musayyib ibn Wāḍiḥ informed us, Mubashshir ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from al-Awzāʿī, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Nabīdh is a means of ablution for one who finds no water.\""\n[Munkar. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/75]"""
"32","(32) He said: and Abū Aḥmad informed us, Muḥammad ibn Tamām informed us, al-Musayyib ibn Wāḍiḥ informed us, Mubashshir narrated it with his chain, similarly, as a mawqūf (stopped narration).\nThis is a hadith concerning which there is disagreement regarding al-Musayyib ibn Wāḍiḥ, and he is weak in it in two respects: in the mention of Ibn ʿAbbās and in the mention of the Prophet (ﷺ).\n(T) What is preserved (al-maḥfūẓ) is that it is from the statement of ʿIkrimah, not raised (to the Prophet). Thus narrated Hiql ibn al-Ziyād and al-Walīd ibn Muslim from al-Awzāʿī, and likewise Shaybān al-Naḥwī and ʿAlī ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿIkrimah. Al-Musayyib, may Allah, the Most High, have mercy on him and on us, was frequently in error.\n(T) ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥarrar narrated it from Qatādah, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, as a statement of Ibn ʿAbbās. And ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥarrar is abandoned (matrūk).\n(T) It was narrated through a weak chain from Abān ibn Abī ʿAyyāsh, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, as a marfūʿ (raised narration). And Abān is abandoned (matrūk).\nAbū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī said, as Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us from him: what is preserved is that it is from the statement of ʿIkrimah, not raised to the Prophet (ﷺ) nor to Ibn ʿAbbās.\n(T) The Shaykh, may Allah, the Most High, have mercy on him, said: and al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī: that he used to see no harm in performing ablution with nabīdh.\nAnd Abū Isḥāq al-Kūfī, whose name is ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mayṣarah, also called Abū Laylā al-Khurāsānī, narrated from Mazīdah ibn Jābir, from ʿAlī: \There is no harm in performing ablution with nabīdh.\""\n(T) ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mayṣarah is abandoned (matrūk)"," al-Ḥārith al-Aʿwar is weak"," and al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh is not used as a proof. I have mentioned the statements of the ḥuffāẓ regarding them in al-Khilāfiyāt.\n[Munkar. Narrated by Ibn ʿAdy"," 7/170]"""
"33","(33) Then, the description of their preparation of nabīdh is mentioned in what ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad informed us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, my father informed us, Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd narrated from al-Ḥasan, from his mother, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \We used to prepare nabīdh for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in a waterskin whose top was tied"," having three spouts hung for it. We would prepare it in the morning and he would drink it in the evening"," and we would prepare it in the evening and he would drink it in the morning.\""\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā"," from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd al-Thaqafī"," with the same meaning.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 2005]"""
"34","(34) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed us, Isḥāq, meaning al-Ḥanẓalī, informed us, al-Naḍr informed us, Abū Khaldah narrated from Abū al-ʿĀliyah, who said: \We consider this nabīdh of yours to be impure; it was only water into which dates were thrown"," making it sweet.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ up to Abū al-ʿĀliyah]"""
"35","(35) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā both informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us.\nAnd Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us, he said: it was read to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sālim, Mālik ibn Anas, and ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed you, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from Fāṭimah bint al-Mundhir, from Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that she said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about a garment that is affected by menstrual blood"," and he said: 'Let her scrape it"," then let her rub it with water"," then let her sprinkle it"," then let her pray in it.'\""\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj extracted it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Ṭāhir"," from Ibn Wahb"," and al-Bukhārī extracted it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"," from Mālik.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 225"," and Muslim"," 291]"""
"36","(36) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān narrated from Hishām, from Fāṭimah, from Asmāʾ, who said: \I asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about menstrual blood that affects a garment"," and he said: 'Scrape it"," then rub it with water"," then sprinkle it"," then pray in it.'\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān"," 1389]"""
"37","(37) Abū Saʿīd — Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Isfarāʾīnī — informed us; Abū Baḥr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan — informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā — narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī — narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah — narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿUrwah — narrated to us, from Fāṭimah bint al-Mundhir, from her grandmother Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that a woman asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about menstrual blood that gets upon clothing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Scrape it off"," then rub it with water"," then sprinkle water upon it"," and pray in it.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah (275)]"""
"38","(38) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdān al-Ṣayrafī in Marw — informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ghālib — narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Masʿūd — narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Nāfiʿ — narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan ibn Muslim ibn Yannāq, from Mujāhid, who said: ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: \Each of us had only one garment in which she would menstruate. If any blood got upon it"," she would moisten it with her saliva and then scrape it off with her fingernail.\""\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym"," from Ibrāhīm ibn Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn Abī Najīḥ"," from Mujāhid.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (306)]"""
"39","(39) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah — narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd — narrated to us; al-Nufaylī — narrated to us; Sufyān — narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from ʿAṭāʾ, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \Each of us would have a shift dress in which she would menstruate and in which janābah would befall her. Then she would see a drop of blood in it and would scrape it off with her fingernail after it had dried.\""\n(Q) This pertains to a small amount of blood"," which is pardoned. As for a large amount of it"," it is authentically established from her that she would wash it. Its evidences will come in their proper place"," if Allah the Most High wills.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (364)]"""
"40","(40) And it has been narrated from Salmān al-Fārisī: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī — informed me; Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan — narrated to us; Muslim, meaning Ibrāhīm — narrated to us; Shuʿbah — narrated to us, from Ḥammād, from ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭiyyah, from Salmān, who said: \When one of you scratches his skin"," let him not wipe it with his dried saliva"," for it is not pure.\""\nHe (the narrator) said: \""I mentioned that to Ibrāhīm"," and he said: 'Wipe it with water.'\""\n(Q) What Salmān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," intended — and Allah knows best — is that scraping does not purify the blood that has exited from the skin.\n(T) As for the ḥadīth of ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir that the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \""O ʿAmmār"," your phlegm and the tears of your eyes are of the same status as the water in your vessel. You need only wash your garment from urine"," faeces"," semen"," blood"," and vomit\"" — this is baseless and has no foundation. It was narrated only by Thābit ibn Ḥammād from ʿAlī ibn Zayd from Ibn al-Musayyab from ʿAmmār.\n(J) ʿAlī ibn Zayd is not a valid authority"," and Thābit ibn Ḥammād is accused of fabricating ḥadīth.\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Khaṭīb in Tārīkh Baghdād (9/168)]"""
"41","(41) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us: al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam, who said: I heard Ibn Abī Laylā narrating from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUkaym, who said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was read out to us: \That you should not benefit from a carcass by its hide (ihāb) nor by its sinews (ʿaṣab).\"""""
"42","(42) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUkaym, who said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was read out to us in the land of Juhaynah while I was a young boy: \That you should not benefit from a carcass by its hide (ihāb) nor by its sinews (ʿaṣab).\"""""
"43","(43) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl, client of Banī Hāshim, narrated to us: al-Thaqafī narrated from Khālid from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah: that he and a group of people with him went to ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUkaym, a man from Juhaynah. Al-Ḥakam said: They entered and I sat at the door, then they came out to me and informed me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUkaym had told them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wrote to Juhaynah one month before his death: \Do not benefit from a carcass by its hide (ihāb) nor by its sinews (ʿaṣab).\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy on him) said: It has also been narrated in this hadith through another chain that he wrote it forty days before his death. And it has been narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUkaym that he said: Our elders from Juhaynah narrated to us that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wrote to them"," and that will be mentioned"," if Allah"," the Most High"," wills."""
"44","(44) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdad: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us: al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Ghassān narrated to us, who said: Abū Zakariyyā—meaning Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn—said: The hadith of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUkaym—\A letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us: 'Do not benefit from a carcass by its hide (ihāb) nor by its sinews (ʿaṣab)'\""—is in the narration of trustworthy people. Our companions narrated to us that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wrote: \""Do not benefit.\""\n\nThe Shaykh—meaning Abū Zakariyyā (may Allah have mercy on him)—said: The hadith is qualified by that"," and it is understood by us to refer to before tanning"," on the basis of what is more authentic than it in the chapters that follow."""
"45","(45) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf ibn Aḥmad al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated to us in Makkah: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah from Ibn ʿAbbās: that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a dead sheep belonging to a freed slave of Maymūnah and said: \Why did you not take its hide"," tan it"," and benefit from it?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," it is a carcass.\"" He said: \""Only its flesh is forbidden to eat.\"""""
"46","(46) And ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bashrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Sufyān narrated it with a similar version, except that he said: from Ibn ʿAbbās from Maymūnah, and he said: \Why did you not remove its hide"," tan it"," and benefit from it?\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah.\n\nAnd Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated from Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī regarding this hadith"," who said: Sufyān would sometimes narrate it from Ibn ʿAbbās without mentioning Maymūnah in it. But when he was asked about it"," he said: It is from Maymūnah. And it was said to him: \""Indeed"," Maʿmar does not say in it 'fa-dabaghtumūh' (and tan it)","\"" and he said: \""Al-Zuhrī used to reject tanning.\"" So Sufyān said: \""But I have better memory of it than he.\""\n\nAnd in the other hadith—the hadith of ʿAmr from ʬāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās—\n\nThe Shaykh said: A group narrated it from al-Zuhrī—Mālik ibn Anas"," Yūnus ibn Yazīd"," Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān"," and others—and they did not mention in it \""fa-dabaghtumūh\"" (and tan it). But Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah preserved it"," and an addition from one such as him is accepted when it has corroborating evidence.\n\nAnd ʿUqayl ibn Khālid"," Sulaymān ibn Kathīr"," and al-Zubaydī corroborated him in what has been narrated from them. And it is also in his hadith from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ"," as:"""
"47","(47) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: ʿAmr narrated from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās: that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a dead sheep belonging to Maymūnah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \If only they had taken its hide"," tanned it"," and benefited from it.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar and others from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah.\n\nAnd Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAmr from ʿAṭāʾ"," and ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān narrated from ʿAṭāʾ"," and they did not mention the word of tanning (dibāgh) in the hadith"," but Ibn ʿUyaynah preserved it. And Usāmah ibn Zayd corroborated him from ʿAṭāʾ"," as:"""
"48","(48) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Usāmah ibn Zayd al-Laythī narrated to me from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to the people whose sheep had died: \Why did you not remove its skin"," tan it"," and benefit from it?\""\n\nAnd thus al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated it from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from ʿAṭāʾ. And likewise Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated it from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ. And Saʿīd ibn Jubayr narrated it from Ibn ʿAbbās in absolute terms without mentioning tanning in it.\n\nAnd the hadith of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Waʿlah from Ibn ʿAbbās is a witness to the accuracy of the memory of Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah and those who corroborated him."""
"49","(49) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī and Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bashrān informed us, both saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān—meaning Ibn Waʿlah—who narrated it from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Any hide (ihāb) that has been tanned has become pure.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah.\n\nAnd all are agreed in this hadith upon the mention of tanning (dibāgh) in it: Mālik ibn Anas"," Sufyān ibn Saʿīd al-Thawrī"," Sulaymān ibn Bilāl"," ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī"," Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān"," and Hishām ibn Saʿd narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam with its meaning. And Abū al-Khayr al-Yazanī narrated it from Ibn Waʿlah with its meaning. And the brother of Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd narrated it from Ibn ʿAbbās"," as:"""
"50","(50) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Khāliq al-Muʾadhdhin informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Baghdādī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rūḥ al-Madāʾinī narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Misʿar ibn Kidām narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from his brother from Ibn ʿAbbās from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding the skin of a carcass, who said: \Its tanning removes its filth (khabath)"," its impurity (rijs)"," or its uncleanness (najas).\""\n\nAnd this is a sound (ṣaḥīḥ) chain of narration.\n\nAnd I asked Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī about this brother of Sālim"," and he said: His name is ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī al-Jaʿd."""
"51","(51) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Mālik ibn Anas informed me from Yazīd ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Qusayṭ, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān, from his mother, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded that benefit be derived from the skins of dead animals once they have been tanned. Abū Dāwūd recorded it in the book of Sunan.\n\nIt has also been narrated from al-Aswad ibn Yazīd and ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from ʿĀʾishah regarding this same meaning. [Weak. Mālik reported it, 1064]"
"52","(52) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, Hammām narrated from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Jūn ibn Qatādah, from Salamah ibn al-Muḥabbiq that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came, during the expedition of Tabūk, to a house, and there was a water-skin hanging there. He asked for water, and they said: \O Messenger of Allah"," it is from a dead animal.\"" He said: \""Its tanning is its purification.\""\n\nAnd thus Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj"," Hishām al-Dastawāʾī"," and Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated it in the more authentic of the two narrations from him"," from Qatādah"," as a connected (mawṣūl) chain. [Weak. Without his words \""its tanning is its purification\"" it is ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd reported it"," 4125]"""
"53","(53) Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah informed me that Abū al-Khayr narrated to him, saying: Ibn Wʿalah al-Sabāʾī narrated to me, saying: I asked ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās and said: \We are in the Maghrib"," and the Magians come to us with water-skins containing water and fat.\"" He said: \""Drink.\"" I said: \""Is this your personal opinion?\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Its tanning is its purification.'\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim reported it"," 366]"""
"54","(54) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥalīm al-Marwazī narrated to us, Abū al-Muwajjih narrated to us, ʿAbdān narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khāld narrated from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from Sawdah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \A sheep of ours died"," so we tanned its skin"," and we continued to use it for making nabīdh until it became an old water-skin.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muqātil from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak.\n\nAnd similarly ʿAbdah ibn Sulaymān and al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated it from Ismāʿīl.\n\nAnd ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā likewise narrated it from Ismāʿīl"," but said \""Maymūnah\"" instead of \""Sawdah.\"" [Al-Bukhārī reported it"," 6308]"""
"55","(55) Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh narrated to us, Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, ʿUbaydullāh narrated it with his chain from Maymūnah.\n\nAnd Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated it from ʿIkrimah likewise. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its narrators are trustworthy and its chain is connected]"
"56","(56) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Simāk, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \A sheep belonging to Sawdah ibn Zamʿah died"," and she said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," so-and-so has died","' meaning the sheep. He said: 'Why did you not take its skin?' She said: 'Should I take the skin of a sheep that has died?' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: 'Allah"," the Most High"," said: {Say: I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats it"," except that it be a dead animal"," or blood poured forth"," or the flesh of swine} [al-Anʿām: 145]. You do not eat it; you only tan it and then benefit from it.' So she sent for it"," and its skin was flayed and tanned"," and she made a water-skin from it until it wore out in her possession.\""\n\n[Weak. Ibn Ḥibbān reported it"," 50415]"""
"57","(57) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, Aḥmad narrated to us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb, Musaddad, and al-ʿAbbās al-Narsī narrated to us that Abū ʿAwānah narrated it to them with its chain and its meaning. [Weak. As in the one before it]"
"58","(58) Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish (may Allah, the Most High, have mercy on him) narrated to us, Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Bazzār narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Aḥmasī narrated to us, Asbāṭ ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, al-Shaybānī narrated from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUkaym al-Juhanī, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wrote to us: 'Do not derive benefit from a dead animal by means of its hide or its sinews.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Its detailed verification will come in Ḥadīth 41]"""
"59","(59) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Saʿdī narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from Abū al-Malīḥ al-Hudhalī, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the use of the skins of predatory animals.\n\nAbū Dāwūd recorded it in the book of Sunan. Abū al-Malīḥ is ʿĀmir ibn Usāmah ibn ʿUmayr; it is also said Zayd ibn Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd reported it, 4132]"
"60","(60) Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzakkī narrated to us, Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Muzanī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Sulaymān al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us, Minjāb ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Mushir narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abī Ṣāliḥ and Abī Razīn, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When a dog licks the vessel of any one of you"," let him pour it out"," then wash it seven times.\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr from ʿAlī ibn Mushir"," and he said in it: \""Let him pour it out (falyurqihū).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its detailed verification will come in Ḥadīth 1140]"""
"61","(61) Abū Zakariyyā — Yaḥyā b. Abī Isḥāq — informed us. Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb — informed us. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʦd al-Ḥakam — informed me. Ibn Wahb — informed me. ʿAmr b. al-Ḥārith and al-Layth b. Saʿd — informed me from Kathīr b. Farqad.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbdān — informed us. Aḥmad b. ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār — informed us. ʿUbayd b. Sharīk — narrated to us. Yaḥyā b. Bukayr — narrated to us. al-Layth — narrated to me. Kathīr b. Farqad — narrated to me that ʿAbd Allāh b. Mālik b. Ḥudhāfah narrated to him from his mother, al-ʿĀliyah b. Subayʿ, that Maymūnah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to her: that some men of Quraysh passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dragging a sheep of theirs like a donkey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \If only you had taken its skin!\"" They said: \""It is a carcass.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Water and qaraz (acacia bark) purify it.\""\n\nSuch is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb"," except that he said: \""from Umm al-ʿĀliyah.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 4248.]"""
"62","(63) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī — informed us. Abū Bakr b. Dāsah — informed us. Abū Dāwūd — informed us. Aḥmad b. Ṣāliḥ — informed us. Ibn Wahb — informed me. ʿAmr b. al-Ḥārith — from Kathīr b. Farqad, from ʿAbd Allāh b. Mālik b. Ḥudhāfah, who narrated from his mother al-ʿĀliyah b. Subayʿ, that she said: \I had a flock of sheep at Uḥud"," and death befell one of them. I entered upon Maymūnah"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ"," and mentioned that to her. Maymūnah said to me: 'If only you had taken their skins and made use of them!' I said: 'Is that permissible?' She said: 'Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by some men…' and she then mentioned the rest of the narration similarly.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. In its chain is ʿAbd Allāh b. Mālik"," mentioned above"," with a break (inqitāʿ).]"""
"63","(64) The jurist Abū Bakr Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Ḥārithī — informed us. Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī b. ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us. Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī — informed us. Ibrāhīm b. Hāniʾ — informed us. ʿAmr b. al-Rabīʿ b. Ṭāriq — informed us. Yaḥyā b. Ayyūb — from Yūnus and ʿUqayl, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said: \Why did you not make use of its skin?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," it is a carcass.\"" He said: \""Only eating it is forbidden.\"" ʿUqayl added: \""Is there not in water and qaraz (acacia bark) that which purifies it?\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/41.]"""
"64","(65) And Abū Bakr — informed us. ʿAlī — informed us, saying: Yaḥyā b. Ṣāʿid — narrated to us. Muḥammad b. Isḥāq — informed us. ʿAmr b. al-Rabīʿ b. Ṭāriq — with this same chain of narration, a similar report, and he said: ʿUqayl added in his ḥadīth that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Is there not in water and qaraz (acacia bark) that which purifies it"," or tanning?\"" [Ḥasan. See the preceding.]"""
"65","(66) And Abū Saʿd Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. al-Khalīl al-Ṣūfī — informed us. Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. al-Mughallis — and I asked him — narrated to us. Aḥmad b. al-Azhar b. Ḥāmid al-Balkhī — narrated to us. Maʿrūf b. Ḥassān al-Khurāsānī — narrated to us. ʿUmar b. Dharr — narrated to us from Muʿādhah, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Make use of the skins of carcasses when they have been tanned with soil"," ash"," salt"," or anything after which their condition improves or doubt concerning them is removed.\"" [Munkar. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī with this wording"," 1/49.]\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: \""This is munkar with this chain of narration.\"" (c) And Maʿrūf b. Ḥassān al-Samarqandī"," whose kunya is Abū Muʿādh"," is munkar al-ḥadīth (a narrator of rejected ḥadīth)."""
"66","(67) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us. Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb — informed us. Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā b. Muḥammad b. Yaḥyā and Jaʿfar b. Muḥammad b. al-Ḥusayn — both said: Yaḥyā b. Yaḥyā — informed us. Sulaymān b. Bilāl — from Zayd b. Aslam, that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Waʿlah informed him from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās, who said: \I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'When the skin has been tanned"," it has become pure.'\""\n\nMuslim b. al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ with this wording from Yaḥyā b. Yaḥyā. (t) And likewise Mālik b. Anas and Hishām b. Saʿd narrated it from Zayd: \""When the skin has been tanned…\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 366.]"""
"67","(68) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥarbī, from the people of al-Ḥarbiyyah in Baghdad — informed us. Abū Bakr Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī — informed us. Ibrāhīm b. al-Haytham — informed us. ʿAlī b. ʿAyyāsh — narrated to us. Muḥammad b. Muṭarrif — from Zayd b. Aslam, from ʿAṭāʾ b. Yasār, from ʿĀʾishah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The purification of every skin is its tanning.\"" All its narrators are trustworthy (thiqāt). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by the author in his Sunan al-Ṣughrā.]"""
"68","(69) As for the ḥadīth which Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb — informed us. Abū Bakr Muḥammad b. Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī — narrated to us. ʿAffān — narrated to us. Hammām — narrated to us. Qatādah — from al-Ḥasan, from Jawn b. Qatādah, from Salamah b. al-Muḥabbiq, that the Prophet ﷺ came upon a house before which a water-skin was hanging. The Prophet ﷺ asked for a drink. They said: \It is from a carcass.\"" He said: \""Its tanning is its slaughtering (dhakāh).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by the author in his Sunan al-Ṣughrā"," 208.]\n\nThus ʿAffān b. Muslim narrated it. (t) And we have received it from the ḥadīth of Ḥafṣ b. ʿUmar"," from Hammām b. Yaḥyā"," who said: \""Its tanning is its purification.\"" And likewise it was narrated from Shuʿbah"," from Qatādah. And Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated it as well."""
"69","(70) Abū Bakr Muḥammad b. al-Ḥasan b. Fūrak — informed us. ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaʿfar — informed us. Yūnus b. Ḥabīb — informed us. Abū Dāwūd — narrated to us. Hishām — from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Jawn b. Qatādah, from Salamah b. al-Muḥabbiq al-Hudhalī, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The tanning of leather is its slaughtering (dhakāh).\""\n\n(q) In the story of the ḥadīth there is an indication that it pertains to the skin of an animal whose flesh may be eaten"," and in its chains of narration there is an indication that what is meant by \""slaughtering\"" (dhakāh) is its purification (ṭahārah).\n\n(t) And in the narration of Muʿādh b. Hishām"," from his father"," in this ḥadīth: He asked for water from a woman"," and she said: \""I have nothing except in a water-skin of mine from a carcass.\"" He said: \""Have you not tanned it?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Its slaughtering is its tanning.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/45.]"""
"70","(71) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us. Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb — informed us. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh — informed us. Yazīd b. Hārūn — informed us. Shuʿbah — from Yazīd al-Rishk, from Abū al-Malīḥ, from his father, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the skins of predatory animals to be spread as bedding.\"" Thus he informed us.\n\n(t) And others narrated it from Shuʿbah"," from Yazīd"," from Abū al-Malīḥ"," as a mursal narration"," without the mention of his father. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by the author in his Sunan al-Ṣughrā"," 209.]"""
"71","(72) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us; Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Ḥabīr, from Khālid, who said: al-Miqdād ibn Maʿdīkarib came to Muʿāwiyah and said: \I adjure you by Allah"," do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade wearing the skins of predatory animals and riding upon them?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"""""
"72","(73) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-ʾAlāʾ, Ayyūb ibn Muḥammad al-Raqqī, and ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān al-Ḥimṣī said: Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us; Hilāl ibn Maymūn al-Juhanī informed us, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī. Hilāl said: \I do not know of it except from Abū Saʿīd.\"" And Ayyūb and ʿAmr said: \""I think it is from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a boy who was skinning a sheep. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: 'Step aside so that I may show you.' He then placed his hand between the skin and the flesh"," and thrust it in until it disappeared into the armpit. Then he went and led the people in prayer and did not perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: ʿAmr added in his ḥadīth"," meaning: \""He did not touch water.\"" And he said: \""From Hilāl ibn Maymūn al-Ramlī.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād and Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated it from Hilāl"," from ʿAṭāʾ"," from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," as a mursal ḥadīth"," without mentioning Abū Saʿīd."""
"73","(74) Abū Ḥāzim ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Baghawī informed us in Baghdad; Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm informed us; al-Minḥāl ibn Baḥr informed us; Baziʿ Abū al-Ḥawārī narrated to us, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \We used to transport water in the skins of camels during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and no one objected to us.\""\n\nThis chain of narration is not strong."""
"74","(75) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Ṭahmān al-Raqāshī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated to us. He said: Muʿāwiyah said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Do not ride upon khazz (silk) or nimār (tiger skins).'\""\n\nMuḥammad said: \""Whenever Muʿāwiyah narrated a ḥadīth like this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," he was not accused (of falsehood).\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the Kitāb al-Sunan.\n\nHe said: Regarding khazz (silk)"," it is interpreted as being disliked (makrūh)"," and its evidence will appear in the Kitāb al-Ṣalāh"," if Allah the Most High wills.\n\nAbū al-Shaykh al-Hunāʾī narrated from Muʿāwiyah similarly regarding the skins of nimār (tigers)."""
"75","(76) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Khalīl al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Nāblusī narrated to us in al-Ramlah. He said: Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Baghdādī narrated to us while I was present. He said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rawwād narrated to us. He said: My father narrated to me, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Bury the nails"," the hair"," and the blood"," for they are carrion (maytah).\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from his father"," from Nāfiʿ"," ḥadīths which no one corroborated him upon.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah the Most High have mercy on him) said: This chain of narration is weak. There have been narrated regarding the burial of nails and hair ḥadīths whose chains are all weak."""
"76","(77) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Hāshim ibn al-Qāsim narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from Abū Wāqid, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: \Whatever is cut from a living animal is carrion (maytah).\""\n\nThis ḥadīth may be used as evidence regarding hair and nails"," even though it was stated on account of a specific reason."""
"77","(78) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Hāshim ibn al-Qāsim informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from Abū Wāqid al-Laythī, who said: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived in Madīnah while the people were cutting off the humps of camels and the tails of sheep. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Whatever is cut from a living animal is carrion (maytah).'\""\n\nSome of our companions used as evidence with this ḥadīth."""
"78","(79) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Abū ʿĀṣim informed us. And Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥamdān narrated to us, and the wording is his: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān al-Nawfalī narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj. He said: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār informed me. He said: ʿAṭāʾ informed me some time ago. He said: Ibn ʿAbbās informed me that Maymūnah informed him: \A domestic sheep belonging to one of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Why did you not take its skin and make use of it?'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān al-Nawfalī.\n\nHe said: He specified the skin (ihāb) for making use of it.\n\nThose who hold the other opinion use as evidence:"""
"79","(80) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us. They said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed me, from Ibn Shihāb. He said: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah narrated to me, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) found a dead sheep that had been given as charity to a freed slave of Maymūnah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Why did you not make use of its skin?\"" They said: \""It is carrion (maytah).\"" He said: \""Only its eating is forbidden.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Kathīr ibn ʿUfayr"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Ṭāhir"," both from Ibn Wahb.\n\nThey said: He specified eating as being forbidden.\n\nAbū Bakr al-Hudhalī narrated from al-Zuhrī an addition in this ḥadīth which no trustworthy narrator corroborated him upon."""
"80","(81) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim narrated to us; Shabbābah narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Hudhalī narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, from Ibn ʿAbbās: \Only that which is eaten from the dead animal is forbidden"," and that is the flesh. As for the skin"," the tooth"," the bone"," the hair"," and the wool"," they are all lawful (ḥalāl).\""\n\nʿAlī said: \""Abū Bakr al-Hudhalī is weak (ḍaʿīf).\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us. He said: Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn said: \""This ḥadīth is narrated only by Abū Bakr al-Hudhalī"," from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," that he considered the flesh of the dead animal to be disliked"," but as for the tooth"," the hair"," and the skin"," there is nothing wrong with them.\""\n\nYaḥyā said: \""Abū Bakr al-Hudhalī is nothing (i.e."," of no significance).\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah the Most High have mercy on him) said:"""
"81","(82) ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Muslim narrated it from al-Zuhrī with his chain of narration: \Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ only prohibited the flesh of the carrion. As for the skin"," the hair"," and the wool"," there is no harm in them.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd al-Rahmān al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Aylī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Busrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ādam narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us from his brother"," ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Muslim"," and he mentioned it with his chain of narration.\n\n(c) ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: \""ʿAbd al-Jabbār is weak (ḍaʿīf).\"" [Very weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/47.]"""
"82","(83) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥārithī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; Abū Ṭalḥah Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Karīm narrated to us; Saʿd ibn Muḥammad narrated to us in Beirut; Abū Ayyūb Sulaymān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn al-Safar narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: \I heard Umm Salamah"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ"," saying: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""There is no harm in the hide of a carrion when it has been tanned"," and there is no harm in its wool"," its hair"," and its horns when they have been washed with water.\""'\""\n\n(c) ʿAlī said: \""Yūsuf ibn al-Safar is abandoned (matrūk)"," and no one reported it besides him.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Abū ʿAlī al-Qabbānī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī said: \""Yūsuf ibn al-Safar"," Abū al-Fayḍ"," the scribe of al-Awzāʿī"," is a denier of hadith (munkar al-ḥadīth).\""\n\n[Baseless (bāṭil). The author cited it in al-Maʿrifah"," 35.]"""
"83","(84) The Shaykh said: \It has also been narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qays al-Baṣrī"," who heard Ibn Masʿūd saying: 'Indeed"," only the flesh and the blood of the carrion have been prohibited.'\""\n\nAbū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī said: \""Isrāʾīl narrated it from Ḥumrān ibn Aʿyan"," from Abū Ḥarb"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qays"," similarly.\""\n\n[Weak. It contains ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qays al-Baṣrī.]\n\nAnd whoever held the view that the hair on the skin of a carrion becomes pure when the skin has been tanned"," cited as evidence:"""
"84","(85) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn al-Rabīʿ ibn Ṭāriq narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, that Abū al-Khayr narrated to him, saying: \I saw upon Ibn Waʿlah al-Sabāʾī a fur garment"," so I touched it. He said: 'Why do you touch it? I asked about it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās"," saying: \""We are in the Maghreb accompanied by Berbers and Magians. A sheep is brought to us and they slaughter it"," though we do not eat their slaughtered animals. And waterskins containing fat are brought to us.\""' Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Its tanning is its purification.\""'\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr and others"," from ʿAmr ibn al-Rabīʿ.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 106.]"""
"85","(86) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal narrated to us; al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Bayhaqī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Muḥammad ibn Abī Laylā, from Abū Baḥr — who resided in Kūfah and was originally from Baṣrah — who narrated from Abū Wāʾil, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, that he said regarding fur skins (al-farāʾ): \Its tanning is its slaughter (dhakāh).\"" This is how Shuʿbah narrated it from Ibn Abī Laylā. [Weak. It contains Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā.]"""
"86","(87) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Ibn Abī Laylā narrated from Thābit al-Bunānī, who said: \I was sitting with ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā when a man with two braids came to him and said: 'O Abū ʿĪsā"," narrate to me what you heard from your father regarding fur skins (al-farāʾ).' He said: 'My father narrated to me that he was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came to him and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," may I pray upon fur skins?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Where is the tanning?\""'\"" Thābit said: \""When the man departed"," I asked: 'Who is this?' He said: 'Suwayd ibn Ghafalah.'\""\n\nSome people narrated it from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā with his chain from Thābit"," from Anas"," and that is an error.\n\n[Weak. It contains Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā.]"""
"87","(88) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, known as Abū al-Shaykh, narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Thaqafī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Azdī narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Ibn Abī Laylā narrated from Thābit al-Bunānī, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what do you think about praying upon fur skins (al-farāʾ)?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Where is the tanning?'\""\n\nThe first chain is more deserving of being preserved.\n\n(c) And this Ibn Abī Laylā is very prone to error (kathīr al-wahm). [Weak. It contains Muḥammad ibn Abī Laylā.]"""
"88","(89) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū al-Jawwāb narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿĀʾishah, that she was asked about fur skins (al-farāʾ) and she said: \Perhaps their tanning is their slaughter (dhakāh).\"" [In its chain is al-Aʿmash"," the ḥāfiẓ"," the trustworthy narrator who practiced tadlīs…]"""
"89","(90) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamm al-Faqīh narrated to us; Abū Saʿīd ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Muslim narrated to us; Hishām narrated to us; Qatādah said: \Dāwūd al-Sarrāj asked al-Ḥasan about the skins of leopards (numūr) and martens (samūr) that are tanned with salt.\"" He said: \""Their tanning is their purification.\""\n\n(t) The Shaykh said: \""And ʿAmr ibn ʿUbayd narrated from al-Ḥasan regarding the wool of a carrion: 'Wash it.'\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from ʿAṭāʾ that he disliked that.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Ibn Sīrīn"," al-Ḥakam"," and Ḥammād that they disliked the use of pig hair.\n\n[Weak. It contains Dāwūd al-Sarrāj"," who is al-Thaqafī al-Miṣrī.]"""
"90","(91) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf ibn Aḥmad al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Hishām, meaning Ibn Ḥassān, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned the jamrah and sacrificed his offering"," he gave the right side of his head to the barber"," who shaved it"," and then he gave it to Abū Ṭalḥah. Then he gave him the left side"," and he shaved it"," and he commanded him to distribute it among the people.\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar"," from Sufyān"," and he said at the end of the hadith: \""Then he called Abū Ṭalḥah al-Anṣārī and said: 'Distribute it among the people.'\""\n\nAnd al-Bukhārī narrated part of its meaning from the hadith of Ibn ʿAwn"," from Ibn Sīrīn.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 326.]"""
"91","(92) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu Bakr al-Qattan informed us — Abu al-Azhar informed us — Habban ibn Hilal informed us — Aban informed us — Yahya informed us — that Abu Salamah narrated to him — that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd narrated to him: that his father witnessed the slaughtering place (al-manhar) near the Prophet ﷺ, he and a man from the Ansar. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed sacrificial animals among his companions, but nothing came to him or to his companion. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then shaved his head into his garment and gave it to him, and he distributed portions of it among people. And he clipped his nails and gave them to his companion, and they are with us, dyed with henna and katam.\n\n(T) Musa ibn Isma'il followed him (in narration) from Aban. (Q) And the dyeing was done by them so that it would not change. And Allah knows best."
"92","(93) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us — Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Isbahani informed us — Yunus ibn Habib informed us — Abu Dawud informed us — Abu Awanah informed us — from al-Hakam and Abi Bishr — from Maymun ibn Mihran — from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade every fanged beast of prey and every bird with a talon.\n\nMuslim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi."
"93","(94) Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Walid al-Faqih informed us — al-Bushanji informed us — Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us — Ayyub ibn Hassan informed us — Yazid ibn Abi Maryam —\n\n(H) And Abu Abdullah informed us — Abu al-Walid said — and al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us — al-Hakam ibn Musa informed us — Sadaqah informed us — from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam — al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah informed us — Abdullah ibn Ukaym informed us — elders from our tribe of Juhaynah informed us: that the Prophet ﷺ wrote to them: \Do not make use of anything from the carcass (al-maytah).\"""""
"94","(95) Abu Sa'd ibn Abi Amr informed us — Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i said — and Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated — that he heard Ibn Umar disapproving of placing oil into a vessel made of elephant bones, because it is a carcass (maytah). Thus he mentioned it in the new (version). And he narrated it in the old (version) as: [Weak. The author has narrated it in Ma'rifat al-Sunan 36.]"
"95","(96) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Walid al-Faqih informed us — Mu'ammal ibn al-Hasan informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'faran'i — from al-Shafi'i, may Allah be pleased with him, who said — Ibrahim ibn Muhammad informed us — from Abdullah ibn Dinar — from Ibn Umar: that he disapproved of being oiled with elephant bone. And in another place: that he used to disapprove of elephant bones.\n\n(T) The Sheikh said: And it is narrated from Ata' that he disapproved of making use of the bones and tusks of the elephant. And from Tawus and Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz that they both disapproved of ivory (al-'aj). [False.]"
"96","(97) As for the hadith which Abu Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us — Abu Dawud informed us — Musaddad —\n\n(H) And Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Khalil informed us — Abu Ahmad ibn Adi informed us — al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab informed us — Musaddad informed us — Abd al-Warith ibn Said — from Muhammad ibn Juhadah — from Humayd al-Shami — from Sulayman al-Manbahi — from Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would travel, the last person he would visit from his family was Fatimah, and the first person he would visit upon his return was Fatimah. He returned from a military expedition, and she had hung a cloth or a curtain over her door, and she had adorned al-Hasan and al-Husayn with two silver bracelets. He arrived but did not enter. She thought that what she had seen prevented him from entering. So she tore down the curtain and removed the bracelets from the two boys and separated them between the two. They went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weeping. He took one of them from them and said: \O Thawban"," take this to the family of so-and-so"," a household in Madinah. Verily"," these are the people of my household; I dislike that they should enjoy their good things in the life of this world. O Thawban"," buy for Fatimah a necklace of sinew and two ivory (ʿāj) bangles.\""\n\n(J) Abu Ahmad ibn Adi al-Hafiz said: This Humayd al-Shami — this hadith of his is rejected (munkar)"," and it is his hadith; I know of no other from him. Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us — Abu Ahmad ibn Adi informed us — ibn Abi Ismah informed us — Abu Talib Ahmad ibn Hamid said: I asked Ahmad ibn Hanbal about this Humayd al-Shami. He said: \""I do not know him.\""\n\nAnd Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Ushnani — they said: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdus informed us — he said: I heard Uthman ibn Said al-Darimi saying: I said to Yahya ibn Ma'in: \""What about Humayd al-Shami — his hadith which he narrates from Sulayman al-Manbahi from Thawban?\"" He said: \""I do not know either of them.\""\n\nAnd another rejected (munkar) hadith has been narrated concerning it. [Weak. Abu Dawud narrated it 4231.]"""
"97","(98) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us — Abu al-Hasan al-Tara'ifi —\n\n(H) And Abu al-Khayr Jami' ibn Ahmad al-Muhammadabadi — and the wording is his — and Abu Tahir al-Muhammadabadi — both said: Uthman ibn Said al-Darimi informed us — Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih al-Jurjusi informed us — Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid — from Amr ibn Khalid — from Qatadah — from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would take his bed at night, he would place his water for purification (tahur), his tooth-stick (siwak), and his comb (mishat). When Allah, the Most High, would rouse him during the night, he would use the tooth-stick, perform ablution, and comb his hair. He (Anas) said: And I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ combing with a comb made of ivory (ʿāj).\n\nUthman said: This is rejected (munkar).\n\n(J) The Sheikh said: The narration of Baqiyyah from his unknown teachers is weak.\n\n(G) And Abu Sulayman al-Khattabi said: Al-Asma'i said: Al-ʿāj is the dried bone (dhabl), and it is said it is the bone of the back of the sea turtle. As for the ʿāj that the common people know, it is the bone of the elephant's tusk, and it is a carcass (maytah); its use is not permissible."
"98","(99) Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz — among the last ones — said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Malik —\n\n(H) And Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Hafiz informed us — Ja'far ibn Muhammad and Muhammad ibn al-Salam — both said: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us — he said: I read to Malik — from Nafi' — from Zayd ibn Abdullah ibn Umar — from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq — from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The one who drinks from a vessel of silver is only dragging the fire of Jahannam into his belly.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Isma'il ibn Abi Uways"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya — both from Malik.\n\nAnd Muslim narrated it from Abi Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and al-Walid ibn Shuja' — from Ali ibn Mushir — from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar — from Nafi'"," adding: \""The one who eats and drinks in vessels of gold and silver.\"" The mention of eating and gold is not preserved in any narration other than that of Ali ibn Mushir. And it has been narrated by other than Muslim from Abi Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and al-Walid ibn Shuja' without the mention of either. And Allah knows best."""
"99","(100) Abu Ali al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Mahwiyah al-Askari informed us — Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi informed us — Adam ibn Abi Iyas informed us — Shu'bah informed us — al-Ash'ath ibn Sulaym said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Suwayd ibn Muqarrin saying: I heard al-Bara' ibn Azib saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade seven things upon us: he forbade the gold ring — or he said the gold bangle — and silk, and silk brocade (istabraq), and dibaj, and the red mi'tharah, and qassi cloth, and silver vessels.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Adam, and Muslim narrated it from another direction from Shu'bah."
"100","(101) Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated it from al-Ash'ath and added in it: \And he forbade us from drinking from silver. Whoever drinks from it in this world shall not drink from it in the Hereafter.\""\n\nAbu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed him — Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab informed us — Ja'far ibn Awn informed us — Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani — and he mentioned it.\n\nBoth (al-Bukhari and Muslim) have narrated it from various directions from al-Shaybani. [Al-Bukhari 5110 and Muslim 2068.]"""
"101","(102) Al-Sayyid Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī narrated to us by dictation: Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdawayh ibn Sahl al-Marwazī informed us: Maḥmūd ibn Ādam narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us: Abū Farwah al-Juhanī narrated to us — he heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUkaym narrating from Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān that he asked for water to be brought for him in al-Madāʾin, and a landowner (dihqān) came to him with a vessel of silver. He threw it aside — the narrator said: and Ḥudhayfah was a man of sharp temperament — and he said: \I apologise to you for this; I had indeed moved toward it"," but the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood among us and forbade us from drinking in vessels of gold and silk"," and from wearing silk and brocade"," and he said: 'It is for them in this world and it is for you in the Hereafter.'\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar and others"," from Sufyān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (110) and Muslim (2067).]"""
"102","(103) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Ibrāhīm al-Shāfiʿī informed us in Baghdād: Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: Sayf narrated to us — he said: I heard Mujāhid saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā narrated to me that they were with Ḥudhayfah and he asked for water, so a Zoroastrian (majūsī) gave him water in a silver cup. When he placed the cup in his hand, he threw it and said: \Were it not that I had forbidden him once or twice before\"" — Abū Nuʿaym said: \""It was as if he were saying"," 'I would not have done this'\"" — \""but I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Do not wear silk or brocade"," and do not drink in vessels of gold or silver"," and do not eat from their dishes"," for they are for them in this world and for you in the Hereafter.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym"," and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Numayr"," from his father"," from Sayf ibn Abī Sulaymān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5110) and Muslim (2067).]"""
"103","(104) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Abū Khaythamah narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us: My father narrated to me — he said: I heard Ibn Abī Najīḥ narrating from Mujāhid, from Ibn Abī Laylā, who said: \Ḥudhayfah asked for water"," and a landowner came to him with a vessel of silver. He took it and threw it"," and said: 'Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade us from drinking in vessels of gold and silver"," and from eating from them"," and from wearing silk and brocade"," and from sitting upon them"," and he said: \""They are for them in this world and for you in the Hereafter.\""'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī"," from Wahb ibn Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim.\n\n(T) And Manṣūr ibn al-Muʿtamir narrated from Mujāhid"," similar to the narration of Sayf and Ibn Abī Najīḥ"," regarding the prohibition of eating from them.\n\nAnd it has been narrated concerning this from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) and from Anas ibn Mālik"," from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""
"104","(105) As for the ḥadīth of ʿAlī: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ḥātim al-Anṣārī narrated to us in al-Baṣrah: Abū Bakr al-Ḥanafī narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated from Abū Burdah, who said: \My father and I went to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and he said to us: 'Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade vessels of gold and silver"," that one should drink from them or eat from them"," and he forbade al-Qassī and al-Mītharah"," and garments of silk and rings of gold.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī (1/41).]"""
"105","(106) As for the ḥadīth of Anas ibn Mālik: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī narrated to us by dictation: Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: Quṭn ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj, from Anas ibn Sīrīn, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade eating and drinking in vessels of gold and silver.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī in al-Kubrā (6632).]"""
"106","(107) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr al-Qaṭrānī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us: Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd narrated from Anas ibn Sīrīn, who said: \I was with Anas ibn Mālik in the company of a group of Zoroastrians. A dish of fālūdhaj (sweet pastry) was brought on a vessel of silver"," and he did not eat from it. It was said to him: 'Transfer it to another vessel.' So he transferred it to a vessel of khalanj (wood)"," and it was brought to him"," and he ate from it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Its narrators are trustworthy (thiqāt) and its chain is connected (muttaṣil).]"""
"107","(108) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī informed us — and Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Bazzāz informed us in Baghdād: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī informed us in Makkah — both of them said: Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrat narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-Jārī narrated to us: Zakariyyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Muṭīʿ narrated from his father, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever drinks from a vessel of gold or silver"," or a vessel in which there is something of that"," he is merely dragging the fire of Jahannam into his belly.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in his Fawāʾid from al-Ṭūsī and al-Fākihī together"," and he added in the isnād after \""from his father\"" the words \""from his grandfather"," from Ibn ʿUmar.\"" I consider this to be an error (wahm)"," for Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq narrated it to us from the original of his book"," in the handwriting of Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī (may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy on him)"," as mentioned above.\n\nLikewise"," Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it in his book"," and likewise Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb"," from Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrat"," in his book"," without mentioning his grandfather. And the well-known narration from Ibn ʿUmar regarding the silver-plated vessel is a mawqūf (stopped) narration traced back to him.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ"," except his words \""or a vessel in which there is something of that\"" — this addition is munkar. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5311) and Muslim (2065).]"""
"108","(109) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he would not drink from a cup that had a ring of silver or a handle of silver.\n\n[Ḥasan. Al-Ḥāfiẓ mentioned it in al-Lukhaṣ (1/54).]"
"109","(110) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Shuʿayb al-Kaysānī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Maʿbad narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Aʿyan narrated from Khuṣayf, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that a silver-plated cup was brought to him to drink from, but he refused to drink from it. I asked him, and he said: \Since Ibn ʿUmar heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbid drinking in vessels of gold and silver"," he has not drunk from a silver-plated cup.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated concerning this from ʿĀʾishah and Anas ibn Mālik.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Tāmmām in his Fawāʾid (2/291).]"""
"110","(111) As for the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her): Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd narrated from Ibn Sīrīn, from ʿAmrah, who said: \We were with ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," and we remained with her until she granted us permission regarding jewellery (ḥuliyy)"," but she did not grant us permission regarding the silver-plated vessel.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Wahhāb said: Saʿīd — and he is Ibn Abī ʿArūbah — said: \""We understood this to refer to the ring (ḥalqah) and the like.\""\n\n[Ḥasan through other chains. Ibn Abī Shaybah in his Muṣannaf (25158).]"""
"111","(112) As for the hadith of Anas ibn Malik: it was narrated to us by Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz, who was told by Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who was told by al-Abbas — meaning Muhammad ibn Dawri — who was told by Yahya, who is ibn Ma'in, who was told by Ibn Mahdi, from 'Imran, from Qatadah: that Anas disliked drinking from a vessel overlaid with silver. [Hasan]"
"112","(113) As for the hadith which was narrated to us by Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Adib, who was told by Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili, who was told by al-Hasan ibn Sufyan and al-Haytham ibn Khalaf, who both said: Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Hasan — meaning Ibn Shaqiq — narrated to us, who said: my father narrated to me, who was told by Abu Hamzah, from 'Asim ibn Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas: that the cup of the Prophet ﷺ broke, and he placed a chain of silver where the crack was. 'Asim said: \I saw the cup and drank from it.\"" His father said: \""I saw the cup and drank from it.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 5315]"""
"113","(114) Abu 'Amr narrated to us, who was told by Abu Bakr, who said: and 'Ali ibn al-'Abbas narrated to me, who was told by Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari, who was told by 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman ibn Jabalah, who was told by Abu Hamzah, and he mentioned it with the same meaning, except that he said \inkasara\"" (broke) instead of \""insada'a\"" (cracked). Al-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih in this manner"," and he was uncertain as to whether the Prophet ﷺ actually placed a chain of silver where the crack was. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 2942]"""
"114","(115) Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, who was told by 'Ali ibn Hamshadh al-'Adl, who was told by Musa ibn Harun and 'Uthman ibn 'Ali al-Za'farani, who both said: Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq al-Marwazi narrated to us, who said: I heard my father say: Abu Hamzah — who is al-Sukkari — narrated to us, who was told by 'Asim ibn Sulayman, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas: that the cup of the Prophet ﷺ cracked, and I placed a chain where the crack was — meaning that Anas placed a chain where the crack was.\n\nThe Shaykh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: \Thus it is in the hadith; I do not know whether Musa ibn Harun said it or someone above him.\"" [Sahih. Its grading was mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"115","(116) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, who said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Nasawi narrated to me, who was told by Hammad ibn Shakir, who was told by Muhammad ibn Isma'il, who was told by al-Hasan ibn Muddarik, who said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to me, who was told by Abu 'Awanah, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, who said: \I saw the cup of the Prophet ﷺ in the possession of Anas ibn Malik — it had cracked"," and he had joined it with silver. He said: 'It was a fine"," wide cup made of solid wood.' Anas said: 'I gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to drink from this cup more than such and such (a number of times).'\""\n\nIbn Sirin said: \""There was an iron ring on it"," and Anas wanted to replace it with a ring of gold or silver"," but Abu Talhah said to him: 'Do not change anything that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made.' So he left it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih in this manner. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 5315]"""
"116","(117) Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, who was told by Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who was told by Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani, who was told by 'Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi, who was told by Humayd, from Anas, who said: \The prayer time came"," and those who were near their homes went to their families to perform ablution"," and a group of people remained. The Prophet ﷺ was brought a stone vessel containing water"," but the vessel was too small for him to spread his hand in it. Yet all the people performed ablution.\"" We asked: \""How many were they?\"" He said: \""Eighty and more.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from 'Abdullah ibn Munir from 'Abdullah ibn Bakr."""
"117","(118) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Hafiz narrated to us, who was told by Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Isbahani, who was told by Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah, who was told by Ahmad ibn 'Abdah al-Dabbi, who was told by Hammad ibn Zayd, from Thabit, from Anas: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water"," and a cup containing water was brought to him — I think he said"," a glass cup — and he placed his fingers in it. The people began to perform ablution one after another"," and I estimated them to be between seventy and eighty. I kept looking at the water as though it was gushing forth from between his fingers.\""\n\nIbn Khuzaymah said: \""Others besides Hammad ibn Zayd narrated this report and said 'rahrāḥ' (wide) instead of 'zujāj' (glass).\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""It is as he said.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 5315]"""
"118","(119) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, who was told by Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq, who was told by Abu Muslim, who was told by Sulayman ibn Harb. And Abu 'Abdullah narrated to us, who was told by Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani', who was told by Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn al-'Ala', who was told by Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani. And Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Muqri' narrated to us, who was told by al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who was told by Yusuf ibn Ya'qub, who was told by Musaddad. They all said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: \The Prophet ﷺ called for a vessel of water"," and a wide cup containing a small amount of water was brought. He placed his fingers in it.\"" Anas said: \""I kept looking at the water springing forth from between his fingers.\"" Anas said: \""I estimated those who performed ablution from it to be between seventy and eighty.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 197]"""
"119","(120) Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, who was told by Yahya ibn Mansur, who was told by Isma'il ibn Qutaybah. And Abu 'Abdullah narrated to us, who said: and Abu al-Nadr narrated to me, who was told by Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Mahan al-Hamdani. They both said: Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Yunus narrated to us, who was told by 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Salamah, from 'Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from 'Abdullah ibn Zayd, the companion of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The Prophet ﷺ came to us"," and we brought him water in a brass vessel"," and he performed ablution with it. He washed his face three times"," his arms twice each"," wiped his head — moving his hands forward and back — and washed his feet.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Yunus. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 197]"""
"120","(121) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to me, who was told by Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih, who was told by 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi, who said: we read it to Abu al-Yaman, from Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah, from al-Zuhri, who said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn 'Utbah informed me.\n\nThat 'A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: \When the Prophet ﷺ became heavy and his pain intensified"," he asked his wives for permission to be nursed in my house"," and they gave him permission. The Prophet ﷺ went out between two men"," his feet dragging on the ground"," between 'Abbas and another man.\"" 'Ubaydullah said: \""I informed 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas of this"," and he said: 'Do you know who the other man was?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'It was 'Ali.'\""\n\nAnd 'A'isha used to relate that the Prophet ﷺ said after he entered her house and his pain intensified: \""Pour over me from seven water-skins whose ties have not been undone"," so that I may address the people.\"" He was then seated in a vessel belonging to Hafsah"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ"," and we began to pour water over him from those until he began to signal to us that we had done enough. Then he went out to the people.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Abu al-Yaman. It is said that that vessel was made of copper"," and that is in what follows. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 655]"""
"121","(122) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā said: I heard ʿAbd al-Razzāq, and Ibn Rāfiʿ said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us. He said: Maʿmar informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah or ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the illness in which he passed away: \Pour over me from seven water-skins whose straps have not been untied"," so that I may find relief and address the people.\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: We seated him in a copper basin belonging to Ḥafṣah"," and we poured the water over him until he gestured to us that you have done enough. Then he went out.\n\nHe said: And Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us once"," ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us"," Maʿmar narrated to us"," from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUrwah"," from ʿĀʾishah"," something similar"," except that he did not say \""of copper\"" and did not say \""then he went out.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it in 6/151.]"""
"122","(123) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us. They said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, Maʿmar narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, and ʿUrwah informed me, from ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said something similar: \so that I may find relief.\"" Thus he informed us in al-Mustadrak by way of ijāzah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ḥākim narrated it in al-Mustadrak 1/123.]"""
"123","(124) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us, they said: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Aḥmad al-Faqīh in Ṭabarān informed us, Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Ṣawwāf narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, Ḥawtharah ibn Ashras Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAdawī narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Shuʿbah, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl from a vessel of brass"," and he would hasten to take the water before me.\""\n\nḤawtharah ibn Ashras narrated it with excellence"," though some of them fell short of Ḥammād and said \""from a man\"" without naming Shuʿbah"," and some of them sent it as a mursal narration and did not mention ʿUrwah in its isnād. Abū Dāwūd also narrated it in the Sunan. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it in 98.]"""
"124","(125) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, Abū Ghassān narrated to us, Abū Ḥāzim narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Saʿd, who said: A woman from among the Arabs was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he mentioned the hadith.\n\nSahl said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came that day until he sat in the saqīfah of Banī Sāʿidah along with his Companions. Then he said: \Give us water to drink"," O Sahl!\"" He said: \""So I brought out this vessel for them and gave them water from it.\""\n\nAbū Ḥāzim said: \""Sahl brought out that vessel for us and we drank from it.\"" He said: \""Then ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz asked him to gift it to him"," and he gifted it to him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq and others from Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam.\n\n(T) And we have narrated from Anas ibn Mālik regarding the vessel of the Prophet ﷺ"," in which there is evidence that it was made of wood. It is mentioned that Muḥammad ibn Abī Ismāʿīl said: \""I visited Anas ibn Mālik and saw in his house a wooden vessel"," and he said: 'The Prophet ﷺ used to drink from it and perform wuḍūʾ from it.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in 5314.]"""
"125","(126) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, Maʿmar informed us, from ʿAwf, from Abī Rajāʾ al-ʿUṭāridī, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out on a journey, he and his Companions, and they were afflicted by severe thirst. Two of his Companions came forward — I think he meant ʿAlī and al-Zubayr, or others besides them. He said: \You will find at such and such a place a woman with a camel upon which are two water-skins. Bring her to me.\"" He said: \""So they went to the woman and found her mounted between two water-skins on the camel. They said to her: 'Respond to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' She said: 'Who is the Messenger of Allah? Is this the Ṣābiʾ?' They said: 'He is the one you mean"," and he is truly the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So they brought her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded"," and water from her two water-skins was placed into a vessel. Then he said over it whatever Allah willed him to say. Then he returned the water to the two water-skins. Then he commanded that the openings of the water-skins be tied"," and they were opened. Then he commanded the people"," and they filled their vessels and their water-skins. They did not leave that day any vessel or water-skin without filling it.\"" ʿImrān said: \""It seemed to me that it only increased in fullness.\"" He said: \""Then the Prophet ﷺ commanded that her garment be spread out. Then he commanded his Companions"," and they came with their provisions until they filled her garment for her. Then he said to her: 'Go"," for we have not taken anything from your water"," but Allah has given us to drink.'\"" He said: \""She came to her family and informed them. She said: 'I have come to you from the greatest sorcerer among people"," or indeed he is truly the Messenger of Allah.'\"" He said: \""Then the people of that ḥāʾiṭ (enclosure) came until all of them embraced Islam.\""\n\nIt is narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of ʿAwf ibn Abī Jamīlah"," and in it is: \""The last of the matter was that the Prophet ﷺ gave the one who was in a state of janābah a vessel of water and said: 'Go and pour it over yourself","' while she was standing"," watching what was being done with her water.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in 337.]"""
"126","(127) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to me, from ʿAwf, and he mentioned it with its meaning along with his addition. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ḥākim narrated it in 3/213.]"
"127","(128) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us, Burd Abū al-ʿAlāʾ informed us. And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā and Ismāʿīl narrated to us, from Burd ibn Sinān, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir, who said: \We used to go on military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and we would come upon the vessels and water-skins of the polytheists"," and we would make use of them"," and that was not considered objectionable on their part.\"" And in the narration of Ibn ʿAbdān: \""and no blame was attached to us.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ from another chain. Abū Dāwūd narrated it in 3838.]"""
"128","(129) Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqob informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) performed wuḍūʾ from the water of a Christian woman in a Christian jar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. The author narrated it in his al-Sughrā in 221.]"
"129","(130) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us. He said: \They narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam\"" — and I did not hear it from his father — who said: \""When we were in al-Shām"," I brought water to ʿUmar and he performed wuḍūʾ from it. He said: 'From where have you brought this? I have not seen water from a well or water from the sky more pleasant than this.' He said: 'I said: From the house of this elderly Christian woman.' When he had performed wuḍūʾ"," he came to her and said: 'O elderly woman"," embrace Islam and you will be safe. Allah sent Muḥammad ﷺ with the truth.' He said: 'She uncovered her head"," and it was like the thaghāmah (white plant). She said: 'And I am to die now?' He said: 'ʿUmar said: O Allah"," bear witness.'\""\n\n[Weak. The author narrated it in al-Maʿrifah in 41.]"""
"130","(131) As for the ḥadīth which Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baghdādī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Suwayd narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd informed us, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to avoid drinking from the vessels of the Christians.\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh said: \""Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd al-Khūzī is alone in narrating it from Ibn Abī Mulaykah.\""\n\n(C) The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And Ibrāhīm al-Khūzī is not used as a ḥujjah.\""\n\n(D) Then it is carried upon the meaning of tanzīh (avoidance for the sake of purity)"," based on what has preceded.\n\n[Very weak.]"""
"131","(132) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qāsim ibn al-Qāsim al-Sayyārī informed us in Marw: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ḥātim informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq informed us: ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Ḥaywah ibn Shurayḥ informed us — he said: I heard Rabiʿah ibn Yazīd al-Dimashqī say: Abū Idrīs ʿĀʾidh Allāh informed me — he said: I heard Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī say: I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," we are in a land of the People of the Book and we eat from their vessels"," and we are in a land of game — I hunt with my bow"," and I hunt with my trained dog"," and with my dog that is not trained. So tell me what is lawful for us from that.\"" He said: \""As for what you mentioned — that you are in a land of a people of the People of the Book and you eat from their vessels: if you find other than their vessels"," do not eat from them"," and if you do not find [others]"," then wash them and then eat from them. As for what you mentioned — that you are in a land of game: whatever you hunt with your bow"," then mention the name of Allah over it and eat it; and whatever you hunt with your trained dog"," then mention the name of Allah over it and eat; and whatever you hunt with your dog that is not trained"," if you reach it while it is still alive [so that you can slaughter it properly]"," then eat.\""\n\nIt is narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak.\n\n(Q) And it has been narrated from Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī that which indicates that the command to wash was given upon knowledge of the impurity of their vessels.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 517.]"""
"132","(133) Al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Naṣr ibn ʿĀṣim informed us: Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Zabr informed us, from Abū ʿUbayd Allāh Muslim ibn Mishkam, from Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \We are neighbors of the People of the Book"," and they cook pork in their pots and drink wine in their vessels.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""If you find other than them [i.e."," other vessels]"," then eat and drink in them"," and if you do not find other than them"," then wash them with water"," and then eat and drink.\""\n\nThus Abū Dāwūd narrated it in the book of the Sunan. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 517.]"""
"133","(134) And Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb has another chain of narration for it: Al-ʿAnbar ibn al-Ṭayyib ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAnbarī informed him: my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dimashqī — his laqab being Duḥaym — informed us: Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd ibn Jābir informed us, from ʿUmayr ibn Hānʾ, that he informed him from Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī, and he mentioned its meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its narrators are trustworthy (thiqāt) and its chain is connected (muttaṣil).]"
"134","(135) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Hushaym informed us, from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from Abū Qilābah, from Abū Asmāʾ, from Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī — he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \We wage war and travel in the land of the polytheists"," and we need vessels from among their vessels"," so we cook in them.\"" He said: \""Wash them with water"," then cook in them and make use of them.\""\n\n(T) And thus Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated it from Ayyūb"," from Abū Qilābah"," in a connected (mawṣūl) chain"," while a group narrated it in a disconnected (mursal) manner from Ayyūb and Khālid"," not mentioning Abū Asmāʾ in its chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī"," 1464.]"""
"135","(136) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī, among others, informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn ʿUyaynah informed us, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Ibn Abī ʿAtīq, from ʿĀʾishah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The siwāk is a means of cleansing for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord.\""\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated it from Ibn ʿUyaynah"," from Misʿar"," from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī ʿAtīq"," from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it (i.e."," ṣaḥīḥ through other chains). Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 5.]"""
"136","(137) Abū Saʿd Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad al-Shuʿaybī informed it to me: Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Sabīʿī al-Ḥāfiẓ in Baghdād informed me, from memory, by dictation: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd informed me.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīm al-Ghaḍāʾirī in Ḥalab informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Abī ʿUmar al-ʿAdanī informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us, from Misʿar, and he mentioned it in a similar manner, except that he said: \He heard ʿĀʾishah"," the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ)"," say…\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Ibn Abī ʿAtīq is ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and Muḥammad is known by the kunya Abū ʿAtīq.\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated it from his father likewise"," and he clarified in it his father's having heard it [directly]. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its narrators are trustworthy and its chain is connected.]"""
"137","(138) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqrīʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī ʿAtīq informed us — he said: I heard my father narrate that he heard ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) say that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The siwāk is a means of cleansing for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Raḥmān is Ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī ʿAtīq — Yazīd traced his lineage to his grandfather. And it is also said that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated it from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad"," as though he heard it from both of them together. [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it.]"""
"138","(139) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī ʿAtīq informed us, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The siwāk is a means of cleansing for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it.]"""
"139","(140) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Qazʿah ibn ʿUbayd al-Hāshimī informed us: Sufyān ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Abī Sulaymān informed us: ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr informed us, from ʿĀʾishah — she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The siwāk is a means of cleansing for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it.]"""
"140","(141) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqrīʾ informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Misʿar informed us, from al-Miqdām ibn Shurayḥ ibn Hānʾ, from his father — he said: I said to ʿĀʾishah: \With what would the Prophet (ﷺ) begin when he entered his house?\"" She said: \""With the siwāk.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Misʿar ibn Kidām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 43.]"""
"141","(142) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us, ʿĀrim narrated to us, Ḥammād narrated to us from Ghaylān ibn Jarīr from Abū Burdah — meaning Ibn Abī Mūsā — from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found him using a siwāk that was in his hand, and he was saying, \Aʿ aʿ","\"" while the siwāk was in his mouth"," as though he was retching.\n\nIsmāʿīl said: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated it to us"," he said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated it with his isnād from Abī Mūsā"," who said: I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was using the siwāk and the tip of the siwāk was on his tongue.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿĀrim"," Abū al-Nuʿmān"," except that he said in the hadith: \""Uʿ uʿ.\""\n\nAnd Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabīb al-Ḥārithī from Ḥammād"," with wording close to the hadith of ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Madanī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 241.]"""
"142","(143) Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtī al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū Maʿmar informed us, ʿAbd al-Wārith informed us, Shuʿayb — meaning Ibn al-Ḥabbāb — informed us from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I have emphasized the siwāk to you excessively.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Maʿmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 848.]"""
"143","(144) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Shuʿbah informed us from Abī Isḥāq from al-Tamīmī, who said: I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about the siwāk, and he said: The Prophet ﷺ continued to command us with it until we feared that it would be revealed as an obligation upon him regarding it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī, 2739.]"
"144","(145) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, among others, informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān informed us from Abī al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abī Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Were it not that I would place hardship upon my Ummah"," I would have commanded them to delay the ʿIshāʾ prayer and to use the siwāk at every prayer.\""\n\nAbū Saʿīd added in his narration that al-Shāfiʿī said: \""In this there is evidence that the siwāk is not obligatory"," but rather it is a matter of choice"," for had it been obligatory"," he would have commanded them with it whether it was difficult for them or not.\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd and others from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 252.]"""
"145","(146) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us, Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh informed us, al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways informed us, Mālik ibn Anas informed me from Ibn Shihāb from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, from Abī Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Were it not that I would place hardship upon my Ummah"," I would have commanded them to use the siwāk with every wuḍūʾ.\"" Thus he informed us in al-Fawāʾid. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"," 146.]"""
"146","(147) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us, al-Ḥārith ibn Muḥammad informed us, Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah informed us, Mālik ibn Anas informed us, and he mentioned it as a marfūʿ narration.\n\nThis hadith is known through Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah and Bishr ibn ʿUmar al-Zahrānī from Mālik as a marfūʿ narration. Likewise, al-Shāfiʿī narrated it in the narration of Ḥarmalah as marfūʿ. And it is in al-Muwaṭṭāʾ with this isnād as a mawqūf narration without mention of wuḍūʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"147","(148) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us, ʿĀrim ibn al-Faḍl informed us, and Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Ḥajabī informed us — they both said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sarrāj informed us from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Were it not that I would place hardship upon my Ummah"," I would have made the siwāk obligatory upon them along with wuḍūʾ"," and I would have delayed the ʿIshāʾ prayer until half of the night.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 1/442.]"""
"148","(149) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Ḥammād ibn Masʿadah informed us from ʿUbayd Allāh from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Were it not that I would place hardship upon my Ummah\"" — I think he said: \""I would have commanded them to use the siwāk with wuḍūʾ"," and I would have delayed the ʿIshāʾ prayer until one-third of the night or half of it\"" — and he mentioned the remainder of the hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 2/250.]"""
"149","(150) Abū Ṭāhir informed us, Abū Ḥāmid informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Aḥmad ibn Khālid informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī from ʿAṭāʾ, the freedman of Umm Ṣubayyah, from Abī Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \Were it not that I dislike placing hardship upon my Ummah\"" — and he mentioned something similar.\n\nHe said: And Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us"," Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd informed us"," he said: My father narrated to me from Ibn Isḥāq"," something similar. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain.]"""
"150","(151) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh informed me, Yazīd ibn al-Haytham informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth informed us, al-Ashjaʿī informed us from Sufyān from Abī ʿAlī al-Ṣayqal from Ibn Tamām from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Why do I see you coming to me with yellowed teeth? Were it not that I would place hardship upon my Ummah"," I would have made the siwāk obligatory upon them just as wuḍūʾ has been made obligatory upon them.\"" Thus narrated al-Thawrī. [Muḍṭarib. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 1/214.]"""
"151","(152) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Farisī informed us; Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Muhammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris informed us; Muhammad ibn Ismāʿīl — that is, al-Bukhārī — informed us; he said: Muḥammad ibn Maḥbūb informed me; ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us, from Manṣūr, from Abū ʿAlī, from Jaʿfar ibn Tamīm, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \You come to me with yellowed teeth — use the siwāk.\""\n\n(T) Al-Bukhārī said: And Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr"," from Abū ʿAlī"," from Jaʿfar ibn Tamīm"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," something similar to it. And al-Thawrī said"," meaning: it is like what we have narrated.\n\nAbū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṭalaqānī"," from Jarīr"," with his isnād"," from his father"," from the Prophet ﷺ. And from Surayj ibn Yūnus"," from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," with his isnād"," from his father"," from al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib"," from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nAnd it was said otherwise; it is a hadith whose isnād is disputed. [Muḍṭarib (disputed)]"""
"152","(153) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; Wakīʿ narrated to us, from Zakariyyā — that is, Ibn Abī Zāʾidah — from Muṣʿab ibn Shaybah, from Ṭalq — that is, Ibn Ḥabīb — from Ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Ten things are from the natural disposition (fiṭrah): trimming the moustache"," letting the beard grow"," using the siwāk"," sniffing water into the nose"," cutting the nails"," washing the knuckles"," plucking the armpit hair"," shaving the pubic hair"," and rinsing the mouth.\"" Muṣʿab said: \""And I have forgotten the tenth"," except that it may be gargling (al-maḍmaḍah).\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others. [Ḥasan for other than its narrator. Muslim narrated it"," 261.]"""
"153","(154) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed me; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abū al-Zinād.\n\n(H) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Abū al-Faḍl al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb al-ʿAdl informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Qabbānī informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Saʿīd informed us; Sufyān narrated to us, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Were it not that I would place hardship upon my Ummah"," I would have commanded them to delay the ʿIshāʾ prayer and to use the siwāk at every prayer.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUyaynah.\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of Mālik: \""Or upon the people — I would have commanded them to use the siwāk.\"" He did not add anything further.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"," from Mālik"," and he said: \""I would have commanded them to use the siwāk with every prayer.\"" And most of the people did not mention that from Mālik.\n\n(T) And Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from Abū al-Zinād"," similar to the narration of Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah from him. And likewise Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated it from Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"154","(155) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, who said: Abū Salamah narrated to me, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Were it not that I would place hardship upon my Ummah"," I would have commanded them to use the siwāk with every prayer.\""\n\nAnd it was said: from Abū Salamah"," from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it with this wording"," 847.]"""
"155","(156) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā informed us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \Were it not that I would place hardship upon my Ummah"," I would have commanded them to use the siwāk at every prayer.\""\n\nAbū Salamah said: \""I saw Zayd sitting in the mosque"," and the siwāk was at his ear in the place where a scribe places his pen at his ear; whenever he stood for prayer"," he would use the siwāk.\""\n\nAnd it has reached me from al-Bukhārī that he used to say: \""The ḥadīth of Abū Salamah from Zayd ibn Khālid is more authentic.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: Both of them are"," in my view"," ṣaḥīḥ.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And the end of this ḥadīth from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār has been transmitted through another isnād. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"156","(157) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī informed us; al-Ḥaḍramī informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Yamān narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Abū Jaʿfar, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \The siwāk used to be at the ear of the Prophet ﷺ in the place where a scribe places his pen at his ear.\""\n\nAbū al-Qāsim said: No one narrated it from Sufyān except Yaḥyā.\n\n(C) The Shaykh said: And Yaḥyā ibn Yamān is not strong (qawī) according to them"," and it is likely that it is an error from the first ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq leading to this. [Munkar. Al-Ḥāfiẓ mentioned it in al-Talkhīṣ"," 1/71.]"""
"157","(158) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us; Abū al-Naḍr Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qurashī al-Dimashqī informed us; Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā al-Lakhmī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us.\n\n(H) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf al-Ṭāʾī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Khālid informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: I said: \What do you think about Ibn ʿUmar's performing wuḍūʾ for every prayer"," whether in a state of purity or not — what is the reason for that?\"" He said: \""Asmāʾ bint Zayd ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated to me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī ʿĀmir narrated to her that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was commanded to perform wuḍūʾ for every prayer"," whether in a state of purity or not. When that became difficult for him"," he was commanded to use the siwāk for every prayer. And Ibn ʿUmar used to consider that he had the strength"," so he would not leave performing wuḍūʾ for every prayer.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Aḥmad ibn Khālid al-Wahbī.\n\nAnd Saʿīd said in his ḥadīth: from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," and he said: \""When that became difficult for them.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated it from Ibn Isḥāq"," and he said: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh. [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 48.]"""
"158","(159) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed us; he said: My father narrated to me.\n\n(H) And he said: Abū Zakariyyā al-ʿAnbarī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us; they both said: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd informed us; my father narrated to me, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, who said: Muḥammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhrī mentioned, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A prayer for which the siwāk is used is superior to a prayer for which the siwāk is not used by seventy times.\""\n\nAnd this ḥadīth is among the things most feared to be from the tadlīs (concealments) of Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār"," and that he did not hear it from al-Zuhrī.\n\n(T) And Muʿāwiyah ibn Yaḥyā al-Ṣadafī narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," and he is not strong (qawī). And it was narrated through another chain from ʿUrwah"," from ʿĀʾishah"," and through another chain from ʿAmrah"," from ʿĀʾishah.\n\nAnd both of them are weak. [Ḍaʿīf. Aḥmad narrated it"," 6/272.]"""
"159","(160) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us by way of ijāzah; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us; Aḥmad ibn al-Khalīl informed us; al-Wāqidī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Yaḥyā al-Aslamī narrated to us, from Abū al-Aswad, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, from the Prophet ﷺ: \The two rakʿahs after the siwāk are more beloved to me than seventy rakʿahs before the siwāk.\""\n\n(C) Al-Wāqidī is not a valid authority (lā yuḥtajju bihi).\n\nAnd it was narrated from ʿĀʾishah through another chain. [Mawḍūʿ (fabricated)]"""
"160","(161) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed him; Abū al-Faḍl al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Qūhyār informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-Sulamī informed us; Ḥammād ibn Qīrāṭ informed us; Faraj ibn Faḍālah narrated to us, from ʿUrwah ibn Ruwaym, from ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A prayer performed with the siwāk is better than seventy prayers performed without the siwāk.\""\n\nAnd this isnād is not strong. (T) And in that regard"," it was narrated from Jubayr ibn Nufayr"," raised as a marfūʿ hadith but as a mursal (disconnected) narration. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf. Tamām narrated it in his Fawāʾid"," 248.]"""
"161","(162) Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlawī and Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhabārī informed us, saying: Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us: Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUbayd Allāh from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \We were commanded to use the siwāk"," and he said: 'Indeed"," when a servant stands to pray"," an angel comes to him and stands behind him"," listening to the Qurʾān and drawing near. He continues to listen and draw near until he places his mouth upon the servant's mouth. Then the servant does not recite a single verse except that it enters into the interior of the angel.'\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bazzār"," 603.]"""
"162","(163) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr and Ḥuṣayn.\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh al-Muzakkī, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Sulaymān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Sufyān from Manṣūr, al-Aʿmash, and Ḥuṣayn from Abū Wāʾil from Ḥudhayfah, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood at night"," he would cleanse his mouth with the siwāk.\""\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Ibn Mahdī.\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Mūsā and Bindār from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 242.]"""
"163","(164) Hushaym ibn Bashīr narrated it from Ḥuṣayn, and he said in the ḥadīth: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," when he stood to perform tahajjud"," would cleanse his mouth with the siwāk.\""\nMuḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Hushaym mentioned it.\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n(Ġ) Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī said: \""Al-Shawṣ means rubbing the teeth horizontally with the siwāk"," the finger"," or the like.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 255.]"""
"164","(165) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bishr al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated to us: Qatādah narrated from Zurārah ibn Awfā from Saʿd ibn Hishām from ʿĀʾishah, in a lengthy ḥadīth, she said: \We used to prepare the siwāk and the water for ablution for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and Allah would send him awake whenever He willed during the night. He would use the siwāk"," perform ablution"," and then pray.\""\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Muḥammad ibn Bishr. And Bahz ibn Ḥakīm narrated it from Zurārah"," and he said in the ḥadīth: \""His ablution water and his siwāk would be placed for him. When he rose at night"," he would relieve himself and then use the siwāk.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 139.]"""
"165","(166) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Ḥammād narrated to us: Bahz ibn Ḥakīm narrated it. [Ḥasan]"
"166","(167) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Ibn Kathīr narrated to us: Hammām narrated from ʿAlī ibn Zayd from Umm Muḥammad from ʿĀʾishah: \The Prophet (ﷺ) would never sleep"," whether at night or during the day"," and then wake up without using the siwāk before performing ablution.\"""""
"167","(168) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Dalaj ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Junayd al-Rāzī narrated to us: al-Nufaylī narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated.\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ibn Milḥān narrated to us: ʿAmr, who is ibn Khālid, informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Qābūs ibn Abī Ẓabyān narrated from his father from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Two men came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with the same need. One of them spoke"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) detected an unpleasant odour from his mouth. He said to him: 'Do you not use the siwāk?' He said: 'Yes"," indeed"," but I have not eaten for three days.' He then ordered one of his Companions to host him and fulfil his need.\""\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbdān"," and thus a group narrated it from Zuhayr. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 267.]"""
"168","(169) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us: ʿAnbasah ibn Saʿīd al-Kūfī al-Ḥāsib said: Kathīr narrated to me from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) would use the siwāk and then give it to me so that I might wash it. I would begin by using it myself"," then wash it"," and then hand it back to him.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd.]"""
"169","(170) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād informed us: Ibn Abī Uways narrated.\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī informed me: My grandfather said: Ibn Abī Uways narrated to me: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah. My father informed me from ʿĀʾishah: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)…\"" She mentioned a story about his illness"," in which she said: \""ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr entered with a siwāk that he was using. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) looked at it"," so I said to him: 'Give me this siwāk"," O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.' He gave it to me. I chewed it"," then softened it"," and gave it to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He used it while he was leaning against my chest (ﷺ).\""\nIn the ḥadīth of Abū Zakariyyā from ʿĀʾishah"," she said: \""ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr entered…\"" and he mentioned it.\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 850.]"""
"170","(171) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī in Baghdād informed us: Isḥāq ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥarbī narrated to us: ʿAffān narrated to us: Ṣakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \I was shown myself using the siwāk"," and then two men came to me"," one of them older than the other. I handed the siwāk to the younger of the two"," and it was said to me: 'Give to the elder.' So I gave it to the older one.\""\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ"," saying: ʿAffān said"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 243.]"""
"171","(172) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-'Abbas al-Qasim ibn al-Qasim al-Sayyari informed us that Abu al-Muwajjih informed us that 'Abdan informed us that 'Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us that Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that Nafi' reported that Ibn 'Umar said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ using the siwak"," and he gave it to the eldest among the people"," then said: 'Indeed"," Jibril commanded me to give it to the elder.'\"" Al-Bukhari cited this narration as evidence. [Da'if. Narrated by Ahmad 2/138]"""
"172","(173) A hadith has been narrated regarding using the siwak widthwise that I do not use as evidence. Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sufi informed us that Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adiyy al-Hafiz informed us that Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman informed us that Yahya ibn 'Uthman informed us that al-Yaman ibn 'Adiyy Abu 'Adiyy al-Himsi informed us that Thubayt ibn Kathir al-Dabbi informed us that Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab informed us that Bahz said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to use the siwak widthwise.\"" This is how it appears in this narration. [Munkar]"""
"173","(174) Al-Hakim Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Uqbah al-Shaybani informed us in Kufa that Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi informed us that 'Umar ibn 'Ali ibn Abi Bakr al-Kindi informed us that 'Ali ibn Rabi'ah al-Qurashi al-Madani informed us that Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab informed us that Rabi'ah ibn Aktham said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to use the siwak widthwise and drink by sucking"," and he would say: 'It is more wholesome"," more pleasant"," and more healing.'\"" This is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Aktham. And in the hadith of Bahz it adds: \""And he would take three breaths and say: 'It is more wholesome"," more pleasant"," and more healing.'\"" Bahz is only known through this hadith; Ibn Mani' and Ibn Mandah mentioned him. As for Rabi'ah ibn Aktham"," he was martyred at Khaybar. [Da'if. Narrated by al-'Uqayli in al-Du'afa' 3/229]"""
"174","(175) Abu Dawud narrated in al-Marasil from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbagh from Hushaym from Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Qurashi from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When you drink"," drink by sucking"," and when you use the siwak"," use it widthwise.\"" Muhammad ibn Muhammad informed us that Abu al-Husayn al-Fasawi informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Lu'lu'i informed us that Abu Dawud narrated it. [Da'if. Narrated by Abu Dawud in al-Marasil]"""
"175","A weak hadith has been narrated regarding using the fingers as a substitute for the siwak.\n\n(176) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us that Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adiyy informed us that al-Saji said: Muhammad ibn Musa informed me that 'Isa ibn Shu'ayb informed us that 'Abd al-Hakam al-Qasmali informed us from Anas from the Prophet ﷺ who said: \The fingers suffice in place of the siwak.\"" (b) Abu Sa'd informed us that Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adiyy informed us"," and I heard Ibn Hammad say that al-Bukhari said: \""'Abd al-Hakam al-Qasmali al-Basri"," who narrates from Anas and from Abu al-Siddiq"," is munkar al-hadith (one whose narrations are rejected).\"" The Shaykh said: 'Isa ibn Shu'ayb also narrated it through another chain from Anas. [Munkar. Narrated by Ibn 'Adiyy in al-Kamil 5/334]"""
"176","(177) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us that Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd informed me that Abu al-Dahhak ibn Abi 'Asim al-Nabil informed us that Muhammad ibn Musa informed us that 'Isa ibn Shu'ayb informed us that Ibn al-Muthanna informed us that al-Nadr ibn Anas informed from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The fingers suffice in place of the siwak.\"" (c) 'Uqbah ibn Mukram al-'Ammi followed them both"," narrating from 'Isa ibn Shu'ayb. 'Isa is the sole narrator through both chains. [Da'if]"""
"177","(178) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us by way of ijazah that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us that al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Dawri informed us that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sadir al-Mada'ini informed us that Musa ibn Shu'ayb informed us that 'Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna informed us that al-Nadr ibn Anas informed from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The fingers serve in place of the siwak.\"" This is how I found it in my book from Musa ibn Shu'ayb. However"," the preserved narration from the hadith of Ibn al-Muthanna is: [Da'if]"""
"178","(179) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us that Abu Ja'far al-Razzaz informed us that Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Salih informed us that Khalid ibn Khidash informed us that 'Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna al-Ansari said: A member of my household informed me from Anas ibn Malik that a man from the Ansar, from Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf, said: \O Messenger of Allah"," you have encouraged us greatly regarding the siwak; is there anything less than that?\"" He said: \""Your two fingers serve as a siwak during your wudu; pass them over your teeth. Indeed"," there is no deed for one who has no intention"," and no reward for one who has no expectation [of reward from Allah].\"" [Da'if]"""
"179","(180) Al-Ustadh Isma'il ibn Abi Nasr al-Sabuni informed us that Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Makhladi informed us that Muhammad ibn Hamdun ibn Khalid informed us that Abu Umayyah al-Tarsusi informed us that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar al-Hammal informed us that 'Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna informed us from Thumamah from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The finger suffices in place of the siwak.\"" [Da'if]"""
"180","(181) Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmish al-Faqih informed us that Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muhammadabadi informed us that 'Uthman ibn Sa'id informed us that Muhammad ibn Kathir informed us that Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, informed us that Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi informed us that 'Alqamah ibn Waqqas al-Laythi said: I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \Actions are but by intentions"," and each person shall have only what he intended. So whoever's migration was for the sake of Allah and His Messenger"," his migration is for the sake of Allah and His Messenger; and whoever's migration was for worldly gain or to marry a woman"," his migration is for that which he migrated.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari 1]"""
"181","(182) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī narrated to us: Ḥammād narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, and he mentioned it with its like, except that he said: \O people"," indeed actions are judged solely by intentions.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr from al-Thawrī"," and from Musaddad from Ḥammād ibn Zayd. And Muslim narrated it from Abī al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. This wording is found in al-Ṭayālisī 37]"""
"182","(183) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Qutaybah narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Mūsā narrated to us, from Yaʿqūb ibn Salamah, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no ṣalāh for one who does not perform wuḍūʾ"," and there is no wuḍūʾ for one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Abū Dāwūd narrated it 101]"""
"183","(184) Abū ʿAlī informed us: Abū Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Sarḥ narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from al-Dārawardī. He said: And Rabīʿah mentioned that the interpretation of the Prophet's (ﷺ) hadith: \There is no wuḍūʾ for one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it","\"" is that it refers to the one who performs wuḍūʾ or ghusl without intending wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh or ghusl for janābah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it 102]"""
"184","(185) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us: Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us: ʿAffān narrated to us: Abān narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Salām, from his grandfather Maṭṭūr, from Abū Mālik al-Ashʿarī, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: \Purity (ṭahārah) is half of faith. Al-ḥamdu lillāh fills the scales. Subḥān Allāhu wa Allāhu akbar fill what is between the heavens and the earth. Fasting (ṣawm) is a shield (junnah). Patience (ṣabr) is illumination (ḍiyāʾ). Charity (ṣadaqah) is proof (burhān). The Qurʾān is an argument (ḥujjah) for you or against you. Every person goes forth"," trading his own soul — either freeing it or destroying it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr from Ḥibbān ibn Hishām from Abān ibn Yazīd al-Aṭṭār. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it 223]"""
"185","(186) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, and he mentioned it with its chain, and said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Purity (ṭahārah) is half of faith.\"" He substituted \""Allāhu akbar\"" in place of \""al-ḥamdu lillāh","\"" and he placed \""al-ṣalāh nūr\"" (ṣalāh is light) in place of \""al-ṣawm junnah\"" (fasting is a shield). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it 223]"""
"186","(187) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us: Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Juʿfī narrated to us, from Zāʾidah, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Allah does not accept charity (ṣadaqah) from stolen goods (ghulūl)"," nor does He accept ṣalāh without purity (ṭahārah).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it 224]"""
"187","(188) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn Fāris informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Qatādah, who said: I heard Abā al-Malīḥ al-Hudhalī narrating from his father, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in a house, and I heard him say: \Indeed"," Allah does not accept ṣalāh without purity (ṭahārah)"," nor does He accept charity (ṣadaqah) from stolen goods (ghulūl).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 2/51]"""
"188","(189) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī al-Razzāz informed us: Saʿdān informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us orally: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī in Makkah informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr al-Mukharramī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, who heard Saʿīd ibn al-Ḥuwayrith saying, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) when he went to relieve himself. Then he returned and was brought food. It was said: \O Messenger of Allah"," will you not perform wuḍūʾ?\"" He said: \""Am I to perform wuḍūʾ because I intend to pray?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it 118]"""
"189","(190) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Mulaykah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out from relieving himself and food was presented to him. They said: \Shall we not bring you water for wuḍūʾ?\"" He said: \""I have only been commanded to perform wuḍūʾ when I stand for ṣalāh.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it 376]"""
"190","(191) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us: Maʿmar narrated to us, from Thābit and Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) looked for water for wuḍūʾ but did not find any. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Here!\"" I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) place his hand in the vessel containing the water"," then he said: \""Perform wuḍūʾ in the name of Allah (bismillāh).\"" I saw the water gushing forth from between his fingers"," and the people performed wuḍūʾ until the last among them had done so. Thābit said: I asked Anas: \""How many do you think they were?\"" He said: \""They were approximately seventy men.\"" This is the most authentic narration regarding the tasmiyah (mentioning the name of Allah).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī 78]"""
"191","(192) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us: Kathīr ibn Zayd narrated from Rubayḥ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no ṣalāh for one who does not perform wuḍūʾ"," and there is no wuḍūʾ for one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it.\"" [Ḥasan for other than its own chain. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 101.]"""
"192","(193) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: ʿAffān narrated to us: Wuhaib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥarmalah narrated that he heard Abā Thifāl narrating, saying: I heard Rabāḥ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Sufyān ibn Ḥuwayṭib say: My grandmother narrated to me that she heard her father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \There is no ṣalāh for one who does not perform wuḍūʾ"," and there is no wuḍūʾ for one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it. And he does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me"," and he does not believe in me who does not love the Anṣār.\"" [Ḥasan for other than its own chain.]"""
"193","(194) And Abū Saʿīd Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā al-Mihrajānī in Naysābūr informed us: Abū Baḥr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Kawthar al-Barbarī in Baghdād narrated to us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥarmalah narrated from Abī Thifāl al-Murrī, from Rabāḥ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Sufyān ibn Ḥuwayṭib, who said: My grandmother narrated to me from her father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no ṣalāh for one who does not perform wuḍūʾ"," and there is no wuḍūʾ for one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it. And he does not believe in me who does not love the Anṣār.\""\n\nAbū Thifāl al-Murrī — his name is said to be Thumāmah ibn Wāʾil"," and it is also said Thumāmah ibn Ḥuṣayn. The grandmother of Rabāḥ is Asmāʾ bint Saʿīd ibn Zayd ibn ʿAmr ibn Nufayl. [Ḥasan for other than its own chain.]"""
"194","(195) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Nuṣayr al-Khuldī narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Hārūn al-Bazzāz narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Makhzūmī narrated from Yaʿqūb ibn Salamah, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no ṣalāh for one who does not perform wuḍūʾ"," and there is no wuḍūʾ for one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it.\""\n\n(b) And Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ al-Saʿdī said: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal — meaning while he was present — was asked about the tasmiyah (mentioning Allah's name) in wuḍūʾ. He said: \""I do not know of any ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth regarding it. The strongest thing in this regard is the ḥadīth of Kathīr ibn Zayd from Rubayḥ"," and Rubayḥ is a man who is not well-known (maʿrūf).\""\n\n(c) And it has reached me from Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī"," from Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī"," that he said: \""There is no ḥadīth in this chapter that is better"," in my view"," than the ḥadīth of Rabāḥ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.\""\n\n(d) Abū ʿĪsā said: This ḥadīth has also been narrated from Ḥammād ibn Salamah"," from Ṣadaqah"," the mawlā of Ibn al-Zubayr"," from Abī Thifāl"," from Abī Bakr ibn Ḥuwayṭib"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," and it is a mursal ḥadīth.\n\n(e) The Shaykh said: And Abū Thifāl is not well-known.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris narrated to us"," from Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī"," who said: \""Salamah al-Laythī's narration from Abū Hurayrah — meaning regarding the tasmiyah — it is not known that Salamah heard from Abū Hurayrah"," nor that Yaʿqūb heard from his father.\"" [Ḥasan for other than its own chain. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 160.]"""
"195","(196) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us: Maḥmūd ibn Muḥammad Abū Yazīd al-Ẓafarī narrated to us: Ayyūb ibn al-Najjār narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abī Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \He has not performed wuḍūʾ who did not mention the name of Allah upon it"," and he has not prayed who did not perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nThis ḥadīth is not known from the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Abī Salamah except through this chain.\n\n(b) And Ayyūb ibn al-Najjār used to say: \""I did not hear from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr except one ḥadīth — the ḥadīth of Ādam and Mūsā meeting.\"" Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn mentioned this in what he narrated from him through Ibn Abī Maryam. Thus his ḥadīth is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan for other than its own chain. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/71.]"""
"196","(197) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us: Hammām narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Yaḥyā ibn Khallād narrated from his father, from his uncle Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ, that he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he mentioned the ḥadīth about a man's prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The ṣalāh of any one of you is not complete until he performs wuḍūʾ thoroughly"," as Allah has commanded him — he washes his face and his hands up to the elbows"," wipes his head"," and washes his feet up to the ankles.\"" And he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth.\n\nOur companions (aṣḥābunā) used this ḥadīth as evidence for negating the obligation of the tasmiyah (mentioning Allah's name). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 858.]"""
"197","(198) And Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl ibn Shādhān informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Mihrān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Abū Zakariyyā — that is, Yaḥyā ibn Hāshim al-Simsār — narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated from Shaqīq ibn Salamah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \When any one of you performs purification"," let him mention the name of Allah"," for his entire body becomes purified. And if any one of you does not mention the name of Allah upon his purification"," only that upon which the water passes becomes pure. And when any one of you finishes his purification"," let him bear witness that there is no deity except Allah and that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger"," and then let him send blessings upon me. When he does that"," the doors of mercy are opened for him.\""\n\nThis ḥadīth is weak — I do not know anyone other than Yaḥyā ibn Hāshim who narrated it from al-Aʿmash. (b) And Yaḥyā ibn Hāshim is matrūk al-ḥadīth (abandoned in ḥadīth). And it has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar through another weak chain. [Mawḍūʿ (fabricated). Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/73.]"""
"198","(199) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: Hishām ibn Bahrām narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥakīm Abū Bakr narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Muḥammad, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever performs wuḍūʾ and mentions the name of Allah upon his wuḍūʾ"," it becomes purification for his entire body. And whoever performs wuḍūʾ and does not mention the name of Allah upon his wuḍūʾ"," it becomes purification for his limbs only.\""\n\nThis ḥadīth is also weak. (b) Abū Bakr al-Dāhirī is not trustworthy (thiqah) according to the scholars of ḥadīth. And it has been narrated through another weak chain from Abū Hurayrah"," raised (marfūʿ). [Very weak (ḍaʿīf jiddan). Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/74.]"""
"199","(200) The faqīh Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥārithī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Zuhrī narrated to us: Mirdās ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Burdah narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abān narrated from Ayyūb ibn ʾĀʾiḥ al-Ṭāʾī, from Mujāhid, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever performs wuḍūʾ and mentions the name of Allah"," his entire body becomes purified. And whoever performs wuḍūʾ and does not mention the name of Allah"," only the place of wuḍūʾ becomes purified.\"" [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/74.]"""
"200","(201) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāl al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik narrated.\n\nAnd Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān al-Ahwāzī informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh — meaning al-Qaʿnabī — narrated from Mālik, from Abī al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When any one of you awakens from his sleep"," let him wash his hand before he places it in his wuḍūʾ water"," for any one of you does not know where his hand spent the night.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Abī al-Zinād.\n\n(b) And it is established from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn"," Hammām ibn Munabbih"," ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaʿqūb"," and Thābit"," the mawlā of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd"," from Abū Hurayrah"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," this ḥadīth without the mention of repetition (takrār). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 160.]"""
"201","(202) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, among the last of those who narrated to us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me: my father narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you awakens from his sleep"," let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times"," for he does not know where his hand spent the night.\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and a group"," from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah.\n\n(T) And that was confirmed from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab"," from Abū Hurayrah"," with its meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 278.]"""
"202","(203) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-ʿUṭāridī informed us: Abū Muʿāwiyah informed us.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Musaddad informed us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Rāzin and Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you rises at night"," let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times"," for he does not know where his hand spent the night.\""\n\nThus both narrated from Abū Muʿāwiyah regarding this hadith: \""When one of you rises at night.\""\n\nAnd likewise ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated it from al-Aʿmash"," except that he said: \""two or three times","\"" and he did not mention Abū Rāzin in his chain of narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 768.]"""
"203","(204) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed him: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Musaddad informed us: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus, and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj extracted it from Abū Kurayb, from Abū Muʿāwiyah, in the narration of the group: \When one of you awakens from his sleep.\"" And likewise Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated it from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 104.]"""
"204","(205) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed him from the original of his hearing: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Tājir informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ and Abū Rāzin, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: al-Aʿmash said: he raised it (to the Prophet), and said: \When one of you awakens from his sleep"," let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times"," for he does not know where his hand spent the night.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb and others"," from Wakīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 238.]"""
"205","(206) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us: Naṣr ibn ʿAlī informed us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal informed us: Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shaqīq, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \When one of you awakens from his sleep"," let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times"," for he does not know where his hand spent the night.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Naṣr ibn ʿAlī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 278.]"""
"206","(207) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd informed us: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from Khālid, with this same chain of narration, similar to it, and he said: \where his hand spent the night from it (i.e."," on which part of his body).\""\n\nHis statement: \""from it\"" — Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd al-Busrī was alone in narrating it.\n\n(C) And he is trustworthy"," and Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 10.]"""
"207","(208) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Aḥmad ibn al-Sarḥ and Muḥammad ibn Salamah al-Murādī both said: Ibn Wahb narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Maryam, who said: I heard Abū Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: \When one of you awakens from his sleep"," let him not place his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times"," for one of you does not know where his hand spent the night"," or where his hand has been roaming.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 105.]"""
"208","(209) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥārithī al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Wahb informed us: my uncle informed us: Ibn Lahīʿah and Jābir ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ḥaḍramī narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from his father, who said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you awakens from his sleep"," let him not place his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times"," for he does not know where his hand spent the night"," or where his hand has been roaming.\"" A man said to him: \""What do you think if it is a pool (ḥawḍ)?\"" Ibn ʿUmar pelted him with pebbles and said: \""I am narrating to you from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and you say: 'What do you think if it is a pool?'\"" ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar said: \""Its chain of narration is ḥasan.\"" The Shaykh said: \""Because Jābir ibn Ismāʿīl is alongside Ibn Lahīʿah in its chain of narration.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/49.]"""
"209","(210) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed me: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās informed us: Shuʿbah informed us: al-Nuʿmān, meaning Ibn Sālim, said: I heard Ibn ʿAmr ibn Aws narrating from his grandfather, Aws ibn Abī Aws, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform wuḍūʾ and he filled his palms three times.\""\n\nShuʿbah said: I said to al-Nuʿmān: \""What does 'he filled his palms' mean?\"" He said: \""He washed his palms three times.\""\n\nĀdam ibn Abī Iyās established its chain of narration"," and there was disagreement regarding it from Shuʿbah. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 4/9.]"""
"210","(211) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Maḥmawayh al-ʿAskarī informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad informed us: Ādam informed us: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from his grandfather, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he ordered water to be brought for him for wuḍūʾ, and said: \Perform wuḍūʾ"," O Abū Jubayr!\"" Abū Jubayr began with his mouth"," so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \""Do not begin with your mouth"," O Abū Jubayr"," for the disbeliever begins with his mouth.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called for water and washed his palms until he purified them"," then he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose three times"," and washed his face three times"," and washed his right hand up to the elbow three times"," and his left hand three times"," and wiped his head"," and washed his feet. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān"," 1089.]"""
"211","(212) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to me, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī narrated to us, saying: Salamah ibn Shabīb narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan, meaning Ibn Muḥammad ibn Aʿyan, narrated to us, saying: Maʿqil ibn ʿUbayd Allāh narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, from Abū Hurayrah, that he informed him that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \When one of you awakens"," let him pour water over his three times before he places his vessel"," for he knows not where his hand spent the night.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Salamah ibn Shabīb.\n\n(T) ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaʿqūb said"," from Abū Hurayrah: \""Let him pour water over his hands.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 88.]"""
"212","(213) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, saying: ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, saying: Zāʾidah narrated from Khālid ibn ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Khayr, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ʿAlī prayed the Fajr prayer, then entered the open courtyard, and we entered with him. He called for water for wuḍūʾ, so the young man brought him a vessel containing water and a basin. He took the vessel in his right hand and poured water over his left hand, then washed both of them together. Then he took the vessel in his right hand and poured water over his left hand and washed both of them together. He washed his palms three times before placing them in the vessel, and he mentioned the hadith. At the end of it, he said: \Whoever wishes to see the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," then this was his purification.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 111.]"""
"213","(214) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, saying: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā informed us, saying: ʿĪsā narrated to us, saying: ʿUbayd Allāh, meaning Ibn Abī Ziyād, narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayr ibn ʿUmayr, from Abū ʿAlqamah, that ʿUthmān called for water and performed wuḍūʾ. He poured water from his right hand over his left hand, then washed both up to the wrists. He then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose three times, then mentioned the wuḍūʾ three times. He wiped his head, then washed his feet, and said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform wuḍūʾ in the same manner as you have seen me perform it.\"" And he narrated the hadith.\n\n(Q) The Shaykh said: This washing"," according to us"," a Sunnah and a preferred practice"," not an obligation. This was the view of ʿAṭāʾ"," Ibn Sīrīn"," and the companions of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 109.]"""
"214","(215) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī informed us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿUbayd said: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, who traced it back (to the Prophet), saying: \When one of you rises from sleep"," let him pour water over his hands before placing them in the vessel.\""\n\nQays al-Ashjaʿī said to him: \""Then when we come to your miḥrās (large basin)"," what should we do with it?\"" Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""I seek refuge in Allah from your evil.\""\n\n(GH) Abū ʿUbayd said: al-Aṣmaʿī said: \""The miḥrās is a large"," elongated"," hollowed-out stone like a trough"," from which people perform wuḍūʾ"," and no one is able to move it.\"" [Ḥasan. Abū Yaʿlā narrated it"," 5963.]"""
"215","(216) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us, saying: Mālik ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: Abū Badr Shuʿjāʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, saying: Sulaymān ibn Mihrān narrated from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you awakens from sleep"," let him not place his hand in the vessel until he washes his hand"," for he knows not where his hand spent the night.\""\n\n(T) Sulaymān said: This was mentioned to Ibrāhīm"," who said: \""The companions of ʿAbd Allāh said: 'What should Abū Hurayrah do with the miḥrās?'\"" Sulaymān said: \""They saw no harm in placing the hands in it if they were clean.\""\n\n(Q) Al-Shāfiʿī cited as evidence the hadith of Ibn ʿAbbās from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding the omission of wuḍūʾ before eating after having relieved oneself"," and its mention has already passed.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Our companions cited as evidence the hadith of Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and its mention has already passed. [Ḥasan. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it"," 1052.]"""
"216","(217) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Faqīh informed us, saying: ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid informed us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, who informed me: ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī informed me from Ḥumrān, the freedman of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, who said: I saw ʿUthmān perform wuḍūʾ. He poured water over his hands from the vessel and washed them three times. Then he placed his right hand in the water for wuḍūʾ, rinsed his mouth, and sniffed water into his nose. He washed his face three times and his hands up to the elbows. He wiped his head, then washed his right foot three times, then washed his left foot three times. Then he said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform wuḍūʾ similar to this wuḍūʾ of mine.\"" Then he said: \""Whoever performs wuḍūʾ like this wuḍūʾ of mine"," then prays two rakʿahs in which he does not speak to himself of anything"," his previous sins will be forgiven.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 1162.]"""
"217","(218) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, saying: ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid and Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīh ibn Milḥān narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā narrated it with its meaning and added regarding the feet: \up to the ankles.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"218","(219) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Muzakkī informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdūn narrated to us, saying: ʿImrān ibn Bakkār narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Yamān informed us, saying: Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated from al-Zuhrī, who informed me: ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd narrated it with its meaning, saying: \Then he placed his right hand in the water for wuḍūʾ"," then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 162.]"""
"219","(220) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us, saying: Abū Yaḥyā ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Yamān informed us, saying: Shuʿayb narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī informed me from Ḥumrān, the freedman of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, that he saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) call for water for wuḍūʾ. He poured water over his hand from his vessel and washed them three times. Then he placed his right hand in the water for wuḍūʾ, then rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, and blew it out. He washed his face three times and his hands up to the elbows three times. He wiped his head, then washed each of his feet three times. Then he said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform wuḍūʾ similar to this wuḍūʾ of mine.\"" Then he said: \""Whoever performs wuḍūʾ like this wuḍūʾ of mine"," then stands and prays two rakʿahs in which he does not speak to himself of anything"," his previous sins will be forgiven.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 162.]"""
"220","(221) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us from the original of his book, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn Shawdhb in Wāsiṭ narrated to us, saying: Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, saying: Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Juʿfī narrated from Zāʾidah, saying: Khālid ibn ʿAlqamah al-Hamdānī narrated to us from ʿAbd Khayr, from ʿAlī, that water for wuḍūʾ was brought to him, or a vessel containing water was brought to him. He poured water over his hands from the vessel and washed them three times before placing his hand in the vessel. He placed his right hand in the vessel, filled his mouth, rinsed it, sniffed water into his nose, and blew it out with his left hand, doing this three times. He then placed his hand in the vessel and washed his face three times. He washed his right hand three times up to the elbow, then washed his left hand three times up to the elbow. He placed his right hand in the vessel until the water submerged it, then raised it with the water it carried and wiped it with his left hand. He wiped his head with both of his hands once. He poured water with his right hand three times over his right foot, then washed it with his left hand. He poured water with his right hand over his left foot three times, then washed it with his left hand. Then he said: \This is the purification of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Whoever wishes to see the purification of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," then this is his purification.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"221","(222) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar reported from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \When one of you performs wuḍūʾ"," let him sniff water into his nostrils and then blow it out.\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 2371.]"""
"222","(223) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī and Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan both said: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik from Abū al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you performs wuḍūʾ"," let him put water into his nose and then blow it out. And whoever cleanses himself with stones"," let him use an odd number.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Abū al-Zinād. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 160.]"""
"223","(224) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us.\n\nAnd Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed you from Ibn Shihāb from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī, who reported that Ḥumrān, the freedman of ʿUthmān, informed him that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān one day called for water for wuḍūʾ and performed wuḍūʾ. He washed his hands three times, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nostrils three times.\n\nHe mentioned the hadith and said at its end: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day perform wuḍūʾ similar to my wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir and Ḥarmalah from Ibn Wahb"," except that they did not mention the repetition in rinsing the mouth and sniffing water.\n\n(c) It has also been narrated in the hadith of Ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam and Baḥr ibn Naṣr thus"," and both of them are trustworthy"," and Allah knows best.\n\nThe repetition in both has also been narrated from ʿUthmān through other chains. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"224","(225) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd al-Iskandarānī narrated to us; Ziyād ibn Yūnus narrated to me; Saʿīd ibn Ziyād al-Muʾadhdhin reported from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Taymī, who said: Ibn Abī Mulaykah was asked about wuḍūʾ, so he said: \I saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) being asked about wuḍūʾ"," so he called for water. A vessel was brought to him and he poured it onto his right hand"," then placed it into the water. He rinsed his mouth three times and blew water from his nostrils three times…\"" He mentioned the hadith"," and at its end he said: \""Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n\n(T) The Shaykh said: It was also narrated by Abū ʿAlqamah from ʿUthmān"," and this is established from ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nAnd we have narrated it from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib from the Prophet ﷺ. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 8/1.]"""
"225","(226) Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhṭawayh narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah and Abū Thābit both said: Ibn Abī Ḥāzim narrated to us from Yazīd ibn al-Hād from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm from ʿĪsā ibn Ṭalḥah from Abū Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \When one of you awakens from his sleep and performs wuḍūʾ"," let him blow water from his nostrils three times"," for the shayṭān spends the night in his nasal passage.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Yazīd ibn al-Hād. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 21/3.]"""
"226","(227) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Dhiʾb reported from Qāriẓ, i.e., Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Ghaṭafān, who said: \I saw Ibn ʿAbbās perform wuḍūʾ; he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water twice"," and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you rinses his mouth and sniffs water"," let him do so two thorough times or three times.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 141.]"""
"227","(228) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī in Marw narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Sayyār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān reported from Ismāʿīl ibn Kathīr from ʿĀṣim ibn Laqīṭ ibn Ṣabrah from his father, who said: \He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned some things"," and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Perform wuḍūʾ thoroughly"," interlace your fingers"," and when you sniff water into your nose"," do so vigorously"," unless you are fasting.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 142.]"""
"228","(229) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh informed me, and the wording is his: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Imām, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān, and Abū Bakr ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us; they said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah informed us; Khālid ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā narrated to me from his father from ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd ibn ʿĀṣim, a man from Banī al-Najjār, who was a Companion. He said: \We said to him: 'Perform for us the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So he called for water and poured it over his hands and washed them three times. Then he inserted his hand and brought it out"," and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water from a single handful"," doing that three times. Then he washed his face three times. Then he washed his hands up to the elbows twice each. Then he inserted his hand and wiped his head"," moving his hands forward and backward once. Then he washed his feet up to the ankles. Then he said: 'Such was the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ"," both from Khālid ibn ʿAbdillāh. They both also narrated it from the hadith of Sulaymān ibn Bilāl from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā"," who said: \""Then he inserted his hand into the vessel and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water three times from a single scoop\""—meaning"," and Allah knows best"," he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water each time from a single scoop"," then he did that three times with three scoops. This is supported by what follows: [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 188.]"""
"229","(230) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Wuhaib ibn Khālid narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā narrated to me from his father, who said: \I witnessed ʿAmr ibn Abī Ḥasan asking ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd about the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So he called for a vessel of water and performed wuḍūʾ for them. He poured water over his hands three times from the vessel"," then washed his hands. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel and rinsed his mouth"," sniffed water"," and blew it out three times from three scoops of water. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel and washed his face three times. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel and washed his forearms up to the elbows twice each. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel and wiped his head"," moving his hands forward and backward. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel and washed his feet up to the ankles.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"," and in the hadith he said: \""He rinsed his mouth"," sniffed water"," and blew it out three times with three scoops of water.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr from Bahz ibn Asad from Wuhaib"," and in the hadith he said: \""He rinsed his mouth"," sniffed water"," and blew it out from three scoops.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"230","(231) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Muzanī informed us; Abū Khalīfah al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd Hishām ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad reported from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Prophet ﷺ performed wuḍūʾ once each (for each limb), and combined rinsing the mouth with sniffing water. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by al-Dārimī, 697.]"
"231","(232) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Abū ʿAwwānah narrated from Khālid ibn ʿAlqamah from ʿAbd Khayr, who said: ʿAlī came to us after having performed the prayer, and he called for water for purification. And he mentioned the hadith, saying: Then he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose three times, and he rinsed and expelled water from the palm from which he had taken it. And he mentioned the hadith and said at its end: Whoever would like to know the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), then this is it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 111]"
"232","(233) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Mālik ibn ʿUrfuṭah from ʿAbd Khayr al-Khaywānī: that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought a chair, and he sat upon it. Then he was brought a vessel of water, and he washed his hands three times. Then he rinsed his mouth three times along with sniffing water into the nose, using one handful of water. He washed his face three times with one hand, and he washed his forearms three times. He placed his hand into the vessel, then wiped his head, moving his hands forward over his head. And I do not know whether he moved them backward or not. He washed his feet three times, then said: Whoever would like to see the purification of the Prophet (peace be upon him), then this is his purification (peace be upon him). [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī, 149]"
"233","(234) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ḥumayd ibn Masʿadah narrated to us; Muʿtamir narrated, he said: I heard Layth mention from Ṭalḥah from his father from his grandfather, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) while he was performing wuḍūʾ, and water was flowing from his face and his beard onto his chest. I saw him separating between rinsing the mouth and sniffing water into the nose.\n\n(c) And Abū Dāwūd said in another hadith of Layth ibn Abī Sulaym from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif from his father from his grandfather regarding wuḍūʾ: Musaddad narrated it, so I narrated it to Yaḥyī, meaning al-Qaṭṭān, and he rejected it. Abū Dāwūd said: I heard Aḥmad say that Ibn ʿUyaynah used to reject it and say: What is this—Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif from his father from his grandfather?\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṭarāʾifī informed me, he said: I heard ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī say: I heard ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Madīnī say: I said to Sufyān—meaning Ibn ʿUyaynah—indeed Layth narrated from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif from his father from his grandfather that he saw the Prophet (peace be upon him) perform wuḍūʾ. So Sufyān—meaning Ibn ʿUyaynah—rejected that, and he was astonished that the grandfather of Ṭalḥah could have met the Prophet (peace be upon him).\n\nʿAlī said: And I asked ʿAbd al-Raḥmān—meaning ibn Mahdī—about the lineage of Ṭalḥah's grandfather, and he said: ʿAmr ibn Kaʿb or Kaʿb ibn ʿAmr, and he had companionship (ṣuḥbah). And someone else said: ʿAmr ibn Kaʿb, without doubt.\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated, he said: I said to Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn: Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif from his father from his grandfather—did his grandfather see the Prophet (peace be upon him)? Yaḥyā said: The hadith scholars say that he did see him, but the family of Ṭalḥah say that he did not have companionship. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 139]"
"234","(235) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Ḥassān ibn Ibrāhīm al-Kirmānī narrated from Yūnus ibn Yazīd.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥalīm al-Ṣāʾigh in Marw informed us; Abū al-Muwajjah informed us; ʿAbdān informed us; ʿAbdullāh—meaning ibn al-Mubārak—informed us; Yūnus narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: Abū Idrīs informed me that he heard Abū Hurayrah narrate from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: \Whoever performs wuḍūʾ should sniff water into his nose"," and whoever uses stones (for cleaning) should use an odd number.\"" This is the hadith of Ibn al-Mubārak. And Ḥassān added in his hadith: Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," so he mentioned it from both of them from the Prophet (peace be upon him).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān"," and Muslim narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 159]"""
"235","(236) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAmr al-Bazzāz in Baghdad narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us; Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad narrated from Ibn Jurayj.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us, and he said: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us—and the wording is his: Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ismāʿīl ibn Kathīr narrated to me from ʿĀṣim ibn Laqīṭ ibn Ṣabrah from his father: that he came to ʿĀishah, he and a companion of his, seeking the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), but they did not find him. So ʿĀishah fed them dates and porridge. They had not remained long before the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came, walking with a heavy, leaning gait. He said: \Did either of you eat anything?\"" I said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" Then I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," tell us about the prayer.\"" He said: \""Perform wuḍūʾ thoroughly"," interlace the fingers"," and when you sniff water into the nose"," do so vigorously"," unless you are fasting.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 143]"""
"236","(237) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Fāris narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim informed us; Ibn Jurayj narrated this hadith, and in it he said: \When you perform wuḍūʾ"," rinse your mouth.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 144]"""
"237","(238) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us; Hudbah ibn Khālid narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿAmmār ibn Abī ʿAmmār from Abū Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) commanded rinsing the mouth and sniffing water into the nose.\n\nHe said: And he said another time in a mursal narration—he did not mention \from Abū Hurayrah.\"" The Shaykh said: Thus it is in this hadith; I think Hudbah narrated it once in mursal form and another time in connected (mawṣūl) form.\n\n(b) And Dāwūd ibn al-Muḥabbar followed him regarding its connection (waṣl)"," and others narrate it in mursal form. Abū Bakr al-Faqīh mentioned it to me from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Ibrāhīm ibn Sulaymān al-Khallāl"," a shaykh of Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān"," opposed them both"," and he said: from Ḥammād from ʿAmmār from Ibn ʿAbbās. And neither of the two is preserved (maḥfūẓ)."""
"238","(239) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣūfī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn Mihrān narrated to us; ʿIṣām ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Sulaymān from al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Rinsing the mouth and sniffing water into the nose are from the wuḍūʾ that is indispensable.\""\n\n(b) The Shaykh said: Ismāʿīl ibn Bishr al-Balkhī narrated something similar from ʿIṣām"," except that he said: \""From the wuḍūʾ without which the prayer is not valid.\""\n\n(c) Abū Bakr al-Faqīh narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated"," he said: ʿIṣām was alone in narrating it"," and he erred in it. The correct version is from Ibn Jurayj from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā in mursal form from the Prophet (peace be upon him): \""Whoever performs wuḍūʾ should rinse his mouth and sniff water into his nose.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/84]"""
"239","(240) ʿAlī said: Muḥammad ibn Makhlad narrated it to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ḥassānī narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Whoever performs wuḍūʾ should rinse his mouth and sniff water into his nose.\""\n\n(b) And thus Sufyān al-Thawrī"," Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah"," and others narrated it from Ibn Jurayj. And Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar al-Jūzajānī narrated it from al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā al-Sīnānī from Ibn Jurayj with the chain of ʿIṣām and the text of the group.\n\n(c) ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar said: This Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar is weak"," and this is an error. The mursal version is more correct. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/84]"""
"240","(q) And al-Ḥasan and ʿAṭāʾ said this as their final position, as did al-Zuhrī, Qatādah, Rabiʿah, and Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī.\n\n(241) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated from Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah from Muṣʿab ibn Shaybah from Ṭalq ibn Ḥabīb from Ibn al-Zubayr from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Ten things are from the natural disposition (fiṭrah): trimming the moustache"," growing the beard"," using the siwāk"," sniffing water into the nose with water"," clipping the nails"," washing the knuckles"," plucking the armpit hair"," shaving the pubic hair"," and reducing the water\""—meaning using water for istinjāʾ (cleaning after relieving oneself). Zakariyyā said: Muṣʿab said: \""And I have forgotten the tenth"," unless it is rinsing the mouth.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from Wakīʿ"," and he mentioned in it \""using water for istinjāʾ.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"241","(242) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṣādiq Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Fawāris narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, saying: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from ʿAlī ibn Zayd from Salamah ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir from ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Ten things are from the natural disposition (fiṭrah): rinsing the mouth"," sniffing water into the nose"," using the tooth-stick (siwāk)"," trimming the moustache"," clipping the nails"," plucking the armpit hair"," shaving the pubic hair"," washing the knuckles"," sprinkling water on the private parts"," and circumcision.\"" [Ḥasan for other than its chain]"""
"242","(243) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Abū Salamah al-Khuzāʿī narrated to us, saying: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Ibn ʿAbbās that he performed wuḍūʾ. He washed his face. He then took a handful of water and rinsed his mouth with it and blew his nose. Then he took another handful and added it to his other hand, and washed his face with both of them. Then he took a handful of water and washed his right hand. Then he took a handful of water and washed his left hand. Then he wiped his head. Then he took a handful of water and sprinkled it upon his right foot until he washed it. Then he took another handful and washed his left foot. Then he said: \Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performing wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm from Abū Salamah Manṣūr ibn Salamah al-Khuzāʿī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 401.]"""
"243","(244) Abū Ḥāzim ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Fāryābī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khālid narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us from Ibn Shihāb that ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd informed him:\n\nThat Ḥumrān, the freed slave of ʿUthmān, informed him: He saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān call for a vessel. He poured water over his hands three times and washed them. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel and rinsed his mouth and blew his nose. He washed his face three times, and his hands up to the elbows three times. Then he wiped his head. Then he washed his feet three times up to the ankles. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever performs wuḍūʾ similar to this wuḍūʾ of mine"," then prays two rakʿahs during which he does not speak to himself of anything"," his previous sins will be forgiven.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Uwaysī from Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd. And Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm from his father.\n\n(T) And we have narrated something similar from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālliib (may Allah be pleased with him) and ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 581.]"""
"244","(244) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, saying: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to me from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah ibn Yazīd ibn Rukānah from ʿUbaydullāh al-Khawlānī from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: ʿAlī came to me after he had relieved himself. He called for water for wuḍūʾ, so we brought him a vessel containing water and placed it before him. He said: \O Ibn ʿAbbās"," shall I not show you how the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to perform wuḍūʾ?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" So he inclined the vessel towards his hand and washed them. Then he inserted his right hand and poured with it over the other. Then he washed his palms. Then he rinsed his mouth and blew his nose. Then he inserted both his hands together into the vessel and took a handful of water with them"," and struck it upon his face. Then he inserted his thumbs into the front part of his ears. Then he did the second and the third time likewise. Then he took a handful of water with his right hand and poured it upon the front of his head"," and let it flow down upon his face.\"" And he mentioned the remainder of the hadith. [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 117.]"""
"245","(246) Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī in Marw narrated to us, saying: Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us, saying: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us, saying: Isrāʾīl narrated to us.\n\n(H) And Abū ʿAbdillāh narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, saying: Isrāʾīl narrated from ʿĀmir ibn Shaqīq, meaning Ibn Jamrah, from Shaqīq ibn Salamah, who said: I saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān perform wuḍūʾ. He mentioned the hadith.\n\nHe said: He then combed through his beard three times when he washed his face, and said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) do what you have seen me do.\""\n\nIt has reached me from Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī that he was asked about this hadith and he said: \""It is ḥasan.\""\n\nMuḥammad said: \""The most authentic thing I have regarding combing through the beard is the hadith of ʿUthmān.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Ḥibbān narrated it"," 1081.]"""
"246","(247) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, saying: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, saying: Abū Tawbah al-Rabīʿ ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Malīḥ narrated to us, saying: al-Walīd ibn Zawrān narrated to us from Anas ibn Mālik that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed wuḍūʾ, he would take a handful of water and insert it beneath his chin, and comb through his beard with it, and say: \Thus has my Lord"," the Mighty and Majestic"," commanded me.\""\n\n(T) And we have narrated something similar from al-Zuhrī"," Mūsā ibn Abī ʿĀʾishah"," and others"," from Anas ibn Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than its chain. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 145.]"""
"247","(248) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, saying: Muʿādh ibn Asad narrated to us, saying: al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated to us, saying: al-Sukkari, meaning Abū Ḥamzah, narrated to us from Ibrāhīm al-Ṣāʾigh from Abī Khālid from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: I prepared wuḍūʾ water for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he combed through his beard and his goatee with his fingers, and said: \Thus has my Lord"," the Mighty and Majestic"," commanded me.\""\n\n(T) And we have narrated regarding combing through the beard from ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir"," ʿĀʾishah"," and Umm Salamah from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and then from ʿAlī and others. And we have narrated regarding the permissibility of leaving it from Ibn ʿUmar"," al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī"," and then from al-Nakhaʿī and a group of the Tābiʿīn. [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than its chain.]"""
"248","(249) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣūfī narrated to us, saying: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Duḥaym and a group narrated to us, saying: Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abī al-ʿIshrīn narrated to us, saying: al-Awzāʿī narrated to me, saying: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Qays narrated to me from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed wuḍūʾ, he would rub his cheeks somewhat, and then interlace his beard with his fingers from beneath it.\n\n(C) ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Qays is alone in narrating it. And they differed regarding his reliability. Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn, his father Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān, and Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī declared him trustworthy.\n\nAnd Abū Bakr al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abī Ḥātim said: My father said: al-Walīd narrated this hadith from al-Awzāʿī from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid from Yazīd al-Raqāshī and Qatādah, who both said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) used to…\"" — making it marfūʿ — and that is correct.\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan said: And Abū al-Mughīrah narrated it from al-Awzāʿī as a mawqūf narration from Ibn ʿUmar"," and that is correct."""
"249","(250) Abū Bakr narrated it to us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Mughīrah narrated to us, saying: al-Awzāʿī narrated to me, saying: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Qays narrated to me from Yazīd al-Raqāshī from the Prophet (ﷺ) something similar to it. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it, 1/107.]"
"250","(251) And with his chain, he said: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Qays informed us from Nāfiʿ that when Ibn ʿUmar performed wuḍūʾ, he would rub his cheeks and sometimes interlace his beard with his fingers, and sometimes leave it. [Ḍaʿīf.]"
"251","(252) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Sūsī informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazyad informed me that my father informed me that al-Awzāʿī said: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʀmir informed me that Nāfiʿ informed me that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar used to rub his cheeks and run his fingers through his beard at times, and at other times he would leave it thus — and he demonstrated in this manner. [Weak]"
"252","(253) Abū Ḥāzim ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Layth Naṣr ibn al-Qāsim al-Farāʾiḍī informed us in Baghdād that Abū Bakr, meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah, informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs informed us from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlan from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed wuḍūʾ. He scooped up a handful of water and rinsed his mouth and cleaned his nose from it. Then he scooped up a handful and washed his face. Then he scooped up a handful and washed his right hand. Then he scooped up a handful and washed his left hand. Then he scooped up a handful and wiped his head and his ears — the inner parts with his index fingers and the outer parts with his thumbs, thus wiping both the inner and outer surfaces. Then he scooped up a handful and washed his right foot. Then he scooped up a handful and washed his left foot. [Hasan. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah, 63]"
"253","(254) Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qāsim ibn al-Qāsim al-Sayyārī informed us that Abū al-Muwajjah informed us that ʿAbdān informed us that ʿAbdullāh informed us that Maʿmar informed us from al-Zuhrī from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī from Ḥumrān ibn Abān, who said: I saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) performing wuḍūʾ. He poured water over his hands three times and washed them. Then he rinsed his mouth and cleaned his nose. He washed his face three times. Then he washed his right hand up to the elbow three times, and then his left hand likewise. Then he wiped his head with his hand. Then he washed his right foot three times, and then his left foot likewise. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) perform wuḍūʾ similar to this wuḍūʾ of mine. Then he said: \Whoever performs wuḍūʾ like this wuḍūʾ of mine"," then prays two rakʿahs in which he does not let his mind wander to anything"," his previous sins will be forgiven.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 1832]"""
"254","(255) ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAbdawī informed us that Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Baghawī informed us in Baghdād that Suwayd, meaning Ibn Saʿīd, informed us that al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAqilī informed us from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl from Jābir, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) running water over his elbows. [Weak]"
"255","(256) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that al-Qāḍī Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Bahlūl informed us that ʿAbbād ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl informed us from his grandfather from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed wuḍūʾ, he would run the water over his elbows. [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī, 1/83]"
"256","(257) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Faḍl al-Muzakkī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us that Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us that Khalaf ibn Khalīfah informed me from Abū Mālik al-Ashjaʿī from Abū Ḥāzim, who said: I was behind Abū Hurayrah while he was performing wuḍūʾ for the prayer. He would extend his hand until it reached his armpit. I said to him: O Abū Hurayrah, what is this wuḍūʾ? He said to me: O son of Farūkh, are you here? Had I known that you were here, I would not have performed this wuḍūʾ. I heard my Khalīl (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \The adornment of the believer will reach as far as the wuḍūʾ reaches.\"" Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 25]"""
"257","(258) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Ḥusayn ibn Ḥasan ibn Muhājir informed us that Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī informed us that Ibn Wahb informed me that ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me from Saʿīd ibn Abī Hilāl from Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Mujmir from Abū Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)… [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"258","(259) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — and the wording is his — that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us that Ibn Milḥān informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us that al-Layth informed us from Khālid from Saʿīd ibn Abī Hilāl from Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Mujmir, who said: One day I ascended the roof of the mosque with Abū Hurayrah while he was wearing trousers beneath his shirt. He removed his trousers and then performed wuḍūʾ. He washed his face and his hands, raising the water up to his upper arms, and washed his feet, raising the water up to his shins. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \My Ummah will come on the Day of Resurrection with luminous faces"," hands"," and feet from the traces of wuḍūʾ. So whoever among you is able to increase his radiance"," let him do so.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr without mentioning the action of Abū Hurayrah"," and Muslim narrated it from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd and mentioned the action of Abū Hurayrah with the same meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 136]"""
"259","(260) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us that Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḍarīr informed us that Muʿammir ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydillāh informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydillāh informed me from his father ʿUbaydillāh from Abū Rāfiʿ, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed wuḍūʾ, he would move his ring. Abū Aḥmad said: I heard Ibn Ḥammād say that al-Bukhārī said: Muʿammir ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydillāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ is munkar al-ḥadīth (a narrator whose hadiths are rejected). The Sheikh said: The reliance in this matter is upon the athar from ʿAlī and others. [Munkar. Narrated by Ibn Ḥājjah, 449]"
"260","(261) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from the original of his hearing that Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Baṣrī informed us that Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn informed us that ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn Jābir ibn Rabīʿah al-Ḍabbī said: I heard Mujammiʿ ibn ʿAttāb ibn Shumayr from his father, who said: I prepared wuḍūʾ water for ʿAlī, and when he performed wuḍūʾ, he would move his ring. [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah, 421]"
"261","(262) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Khushaysh al-Tamīmī al-Muqriʾ in Kūfah informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Naṣr al-Tammār narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥimmānī narrated to us; Wakīʿ and Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ narrated to us, from al-Muʿallā ibn Jābir, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: I saw Ibn ʿUmar, when he performed wuḍūʾ, he would move his ring. [Weak]"
"262","(263) Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥarashī informed us; Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī, from Ḥumrān ibn Abān, who said: I saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allāh be pleased with him) perform wuḍūʾ. He poured water over his hands three times and washed them. Then he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose. Then he washed his face three times. Then he washed his right hand up to the elbow three times, then the left likewise. Then he wiped his head. Then he washed his right foot three times, then the left likewise. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him) perform wuḍūʾ similar to this wuḍūʾ of mine. Then he said: \Whoever performs wuḍʾ similar to this wuḍūʾ of mine"," then prays two rakʿahs in which he does not converse with himself"," his previous sins will be forgiven.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibn al-Mubārak from Maʿmar as mentioned above"," and Muslim narrated it through other chains from al-Zuhrī. [Authentic]"""
"263","(264) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn al-Juʿfī narrated to us, from Zāʾidah; Khālid ibn ʿAlqamah al-Hamdānī narrated to us, from ʿAbd Khayr, from ʿAlī, that he called for water for wuḍūʾ. He mentioned the ḥadīth.\n\nHe said in it: Then he placed his right hand into the vessel until it was submerged in the water, then he raised it carrying the water, then wiped it with his left hand. Then he wiped his head with both his hands once. And he mentioned the ḥadīth.\n\nAnd at its end: \Whoever wishes to look at the purification of the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him)"," then this is his purification.\"" [Authentic]"""
"264","(265) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Rabiʿah al-Kinānī narrated to us, from al-Minhāl ibn ʿAmr, from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh, that he heard ʿAlī being asked about the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him). He mentioned the ḥadīth and said: He wiped over his head until the water was dripping, and washed his feet three times each. Then he said: \Such was the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him).\"" [Authentic. Abū Dāwūd narrated it as no. 114]"""
"265","(266) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Bishr ibn Mūsā al-Asadī narrated to us; Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Hishām ibn Saʿd narrated to us; Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said to us: \Would you like me to show you how the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him) used to perform wuḍūʾ?\"" He then called for a vessel containing water. He mentioned the ḥadīth"," and in it: Then he scooped a handful of water"," shook his hand"," and wiped his head and his ears with it. [Authentic. Abū Dāwūd narrated it as no. 147]"""
"266","(267) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Abū al-Muthannā and Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥarbī both said: Musaddad narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ narrated to us; Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated to us; Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī narrated to us, from Ḥamzah ibn al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him) lagged behind, and I stayed behind with him. When he had relieved himself, he said: \Do you have water with you?\"" I brought him a vessel of purification water. He washed his palms and his face. Then he tried to pull out his forearms"," but the sleeve of the jubbah was tight"," so he brought his hands out from beneath the jubbah and cast the jubbah over his shoulders. Then he washed his forearms and wiped over his forelock"," over his turban"," and over his khuffs. And he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bazīʿ from Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ"," except that he said: from ʿUrwah ibn al-Mughīrah (may Allāh be pleased with them both). [Authentic. Muslim narrated it as no. 274]"""
"267","(268) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī in Marw informed us; Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us; Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated to us, from Bakr, from Ibn al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him) wiped over his khuffs, wiped the front of his head, and placed his hand upon the turban or wiped over the turban.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Umayyah ibn Bisṭām and others from Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān from his father.\n\n(T) Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān also narrated it from al-Taymī, from Bakr, from al-Ḥasan, from Ibn al-Mughīrah. Bakr said: \And I heard it from Ibn al-Mughīrah.\"" [Authentic. Muslim narrated it as no. 247]"""
"268","(269) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us; Ayyūb narrated to us, from Muḥammad, from a man, from ʿAmr ibn Wahb al-Thaqafī, who said: We were with al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, and he mentioned the ḥadīth from the Prophet (peace be upon him), and in it: He performed wuḍūʾ, washed his face, washed his forearms, wiped over his forelock, and wiped over his turban and his khuffs.\n\n(T) And likewise Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim said, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, and it has been narrated from Qatādah, ʿAwf, Hishām, and others, from Muḥammad, from ʿAmr ibn Wahb. [Authentic]"
"269","(270) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: \Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed you from Mālik ibn Anas.\""\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; he said: And Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed me — and the wording is his — Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb al-Bajalī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us; Mālik narrated to me"," from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā al-Māzinī"," from his father"," that a man said to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd ibn ʿĀṣim — who was the grandfather of ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā and was among the Companions of the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him): \""Can you show me how the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him) used to perform wuḍūʾ?\"" ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd said: \""Yes.\"" He then called for water for wuḍūʾ and poured it over his hands. He washed his hands twice each. Then he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose three times. He washed his face three times. Then he washed his hands up to the elbows twice. Then he wiped his head with his hands"," moving them forward and backward. He began with the front of his head"," then moved his hands to the back of his head"," then returned them to the place where he had begun. Then he washed his feet.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Mūsā al-Anṣārī from Maʿn from Mālik. [Authentic. Al-Bukhārī narrated it as no. 183]"""
"270","(271) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Zāʾidah narrated to us, from Khālid ibn ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Khayr, from ʿAlī. He mentioned the ḥadīth regarding his wuḍūʾ and said: He wiped his head with both his hands entirely — its front and its back — once. Then he mentioned the ḥadīth. Then he said: \Whoever wishes to look at the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him)"," then this was his purification.\"" [Authentic. Abū Dāwūd narrated it as no. 112]"""
"271","(272) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Maḥmūd ibn Khālid and Yaʿqūb ibn Kaʿb al-Anṭāqī — the wording is his — both said: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ḥarīz ibn ʿUthmān, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Maysarah, from al-Miqdād ibn Maʿdīkarib, who said:\n\n\I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performing wuḍūʾ. When he reached the wiping of his head"," he placed both his palms on the front of his head"," then drew them back until he reached the nape of his neck"," then returned them to the place from which he had begun.\""\n\nMaḥmūd said: Ḥarīz informed me — \""until he raised (his hands).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," nos. 123"," 122.]\n\n---"""
"272","(273) Abū ʿAlī informed us; Abū Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muʾammal ibn al-Faḍl al-Ḥarrānī informed us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us; Abū al-Azhar — al-Mughīrah ibn Farwah and Yazīd ibn Abī Mālik — narrated to us: that Muʿāwiyah performed wuḍūʾ for the people just as he had seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) perform wuḍūʾ. When he reached his head, he scooped up a handful of water and received it with his left hand, then placed it on the middle of his head until the water dripped — or nearly dripped — then he wiped from the front of his head to the back, and from the back of his head to the front.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, no. 124.]\n\n---"
"273","(274) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Munqidh narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to us, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl ibn Abī Ṭālib, from al-Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿawwidh ibn ʿAfrāʾ, who said:\n\n\I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performing wuḍūʾ. He wiped the front of his head and the back"," and he wiped his temples and his ears — their outer parts and their inner parts — and joined them together.\""\n\n---"""
"274","(275) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us; Yaḥyā — meaning Ibn Bukayr — narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn ʿAjlān, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl ibn Abī Ṭālib, from al-Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿawwidh: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed wuḍūʾ at her place, and he wiped his head — he wiped the entire head from above the hair, every side to where the hair grows, without moving the hair from its position. In another narration: \from the crown of the head.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," no. 128.]\n\n---"""
"275","(276) ʿAlī ibn Bishrān informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk informed us; Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal — narrated to us; Sahl ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, from Ḥumayd, from Anas: that when he wiped his head, he did not turn his hair over.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh said: \This and the ḥadīth of al-Rubayyiʿ carry the same meaning — he did not turn the hair from its natural course.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]\n\n---"""
"276","(277) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī informed us; Ṭalq ibn Ghannām and ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth both said: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us; Ṭalḥah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said:\n\n\When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wiped his head"," he placed both his hands at the front of his head until he reached his ears and the upper part of his head.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf.]\n\n---"""
"277","(278) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn al-Najjār al-Muqriʾ in al-Kūfah informed us; Abū al-Qāsim Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Aḥmasī informed us; Abī Ḥuṣayn al-Wādiʿī narrated to us; Yaḥyā al-Ḥimmānī narrated to us; Ḥafṣ narrated to us, from al-Layth, from Ṭalḥah, from his father, from his grandfather: that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) when he performed wuḍūʾ — he wiped his head and his ears, and he passed his hands over the back of his neck.\n\n(T) ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated it from al-Layth ibn Abī Sulaym, and he said: \He wiped his head until he reached the qadhāl — which is the beginning of the nape — and he did not mention the passing (of the hands over the nape).\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," no. 132.]\n\n---"""
"278","(279) ʿAbd al-Wāḥid informed us; Abū al-Qāsim ibn ʿAmr informed us; Abū Ḥuṣayn informed us; Yaḥyā informed us; Abū Isrāʾīl narrated to us, from Fuḍayl ibn ʿAmr, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿUmar: that when he wiped his head, he wiped the back of his neck along with his head.\n\nThis is mawqūf (a statement stopping at the Companion), and the musnad version has weakness in its chain. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf.]\n\n---"
"279","(280) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Imām narrated to us; Ḥumayd ibn Masʿadah narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us; Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated to us; Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī narrated to us; Ḥamzah ibn al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah narrated to us, from his father, who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fell behind (the group)"," and I fell behind with him. When he had relieved himself"," he said: 'Do you have water?' So I brought him a vessel of purification water. He washed his hands"," then washed his face. Then he began to pull up his forearms"," but the sleeve of the jubbah was too tight"," so he brought his hands out from beneath the jubbah and cast the jubbah over his shoulders. Then he washed his forearms"," and he wiped over his forelock"," his turban"," and his leather socks. Then he mounted (his ride).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ"," as I have previously mentioned.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," no. 274.]\n\n---"""
"280","(281) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to you, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muslim, from Abī Maʿqil, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said:\n\n\I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performing wuḍūʾ while wearing a Qaṭrī turban. He inserted his hands from beneath the turban and wiped the front of his head"," and he did not remove the turban.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in Kitāb al-Sunan.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," no. 147.]"""
"281","(282) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan — narrated to us. Abu al-Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us. al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman — informed us. al-Shafi'i — informed us. Muslim — from Ibn Jurayj — from 'Ata': that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed wudu', then he removed the turban and wiped over the front of his head, or he said: he wiped his forelock with water.\n\nThis is a mursal hadith. Its meaning has been narrated to us as a musnad narration in the hadith of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. [Weak. Reported by al-Shafi'i, 45]"
"282","(283) Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya — informed us. Abu al-Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us. Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah — informed us. Ibn Wahb — narrated to us. And Bahr — narrated to us, saying: it was recited to Ibn Wahb: Ibn Lahi'ah and 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed you, from Bukayr ibn 'Abd Allah, from Umm 'Alqamah, the freed slave woman of 'Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), from 'Aishah: that when she performed wudu', she would insert her hand from beneath the covering and wipe over her entire head. [Weak]"
"283","(284) Abu al-Husayn — Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad — informed us. 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Darastawayh — narrated to us. Ya'qub ibn Sufyan — narrated to us. Muhammad ibn al-Minhal — narrated to us. Yazid ibn Zurai' — narrated to us. 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq — narrated from Abu 'Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ammar ibn Yasir.\n\nAnd Abu al-Fath — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far, the judge in Rayy — narrated to us. Ahmad ibn Habib ibn al-Hasan al-Qazzaz — narrated to us. al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Qadi — narrated to us. Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Abu Madh'ur — narrated to us. Yazid ibn Zurai' — narrated to us. 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq — narrated to us. Abu 'Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ammar ibn Yasir — narrated to us, saying: I asked Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah about wiping over the two khuffs, so he said: \O son of my brother"," that is the Sunnah.\"" And I asked him about wiping over the turban"," so he said: \""No. I touch the hair with water.\"" [Weak]"""
"284","(285) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, the jurist — informed us. 'Ali ibn 'Umar, the hafiz — informed us. al-Husayn ibn Isma'il — narrated to us. Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Umawi — narrated to us. My father — narrated to us. Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari — from Nafi' — from Ibn 'Umar: that when he wiped his head, he would raise the cap and wipe over the front of his head. [Hasan. Reported by al-Daraqutni, 1/107]"
"285","(286) Abu Ahmad — 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan, the trustworthy narrator — informed us. Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī — narrated to us. Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanji — narrated to us. Yahya ibn Bukayr — narrated to us. Malik — from Nafi': that he saw Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd, the wife of 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, remove her head-covering and then wipe over her head with water. And Nafi' at that time was a young boy. [Sound. Reported by Malik, 7]"
"286","(287) And with his chain of narration, he said: Malik narrated to us — from Hisham ibn 'Urwah: that his father used to remove the turban and wipe over his head with water.\n\nAnd in all of this, along with the apparent meaning of the Book, there is a clear indication of an abridgment that occurred on the part of the narrator in the hadith. [Sound. Reported by Malik, 69]"
"287","(288) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, and Abu Sa'id — Muhammad ibn Musa — both said: Abu al-Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us. Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar — informed us. Abu Mu'awiyah — narrated from al-A'mash — from al-Hakam — from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla — from Ka'b ibn 'Ujrah — from Bilal, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wipe over the two khuffs and the head-covering.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Kurayb and others, from Abu Mu'awiyah. [Sound. Reported by Muslim, 275]"
"288","(289) And that which further indicates it is what Abu Nasr — 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah — narrated to us. Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn al-Mu'mmal ibn al-Hasan ibn 'Isa — narrated to us. al-Fadl ibn Muhammad — narrated to us. 'Amr — he is ibn 'Awn — informed us. Khalid — narrated from Humayd — from Abu Raja', the freed slave of Abu Qilabah — from Abu Qilabah — from Abu Idris — from Bilal: that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wiped over the two khuffs, his forelock, and the turban.\n\nThis Humayd is al-Tawil, and this Khalid is 'Abd Allah al-Wasiti. This is a hasan chain of narration, and it is like the hadith of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding wiping over the turban and the forelock together. And it is likely that this abridgment also occurred in what (was mentioned). [Sound]"
"289","(290) Abu 'Ali al-Rawdhbari — informed us. Muhammad ibn Bakr — narrated to us. Abu Dawud — narrated to us. Ahmad ibn Hanbal — narrated to us. Yahya ibn Sa'id — narrated from Thawr — from Rashid ibn Sa'd — from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent a military expedition, and they were afflicted by cold. When they returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he commanded them to wipe over the head-wraps and the leather socks. [Sound. Reported by Abu Dawud, 146]"
"290","(291) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us in the book \Ikhtilaf al-Ahadith\"" of al-Shafi'i (may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy upon him). Abu al-Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us. al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman — informed us. al-Shafi'i — informed us. Sufyan — narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah — from his father — from Humran"," the freed slave of 'Uthman ibn 'Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) — from 'Uthman: that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed wudu'"," washing each part three times. [Sound. Reported by Muslim"," 230]"""
"291","(292) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Manṣūr informed us; Hārūn ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from Ḥumrān, who said: ʿUthmān performed wuḍūʾ sitting at the place of sitting, three times, and said: \Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing wuḍūʾ.\"" Then he said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no man who performs wuḍūʾ and does it well"," then prays"," except that Allah forgives him what is between that prayer and the next one"," until he prays it.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar.\n\n(Q) Al-Shāfiʿī relied upon this [ḥadīth] regarding the repetition of masḥ [wiping]"," and this narration is unrestricted (muṭlaq). However"," the established"," clarified narrations from Ḥumrān indicate that the repetition occurred in the limbs other than the head"," and that he wiped his head once only.\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us"," saying: Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī said: All the authentic aḥādīth of ʿUthmān indicate that the masḥ of the head is once"," for they mentioned the wuḍūʾ three times and said therein: \""And he wiped his head","\"" without specifying a number"," as they did regarding the other limbs.\n\nThe Shaykh said: It has been narrated through strange routes from ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioning the repetition in the masḥ of the head; however"," these"," being contrary to the reliable ḥuffāẓ"," are not a proof (ḥujjah) among the people of knowledge"," even though some of our companions use them as evidence.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 227.]"""
"292","(293) Among them is what Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Makhlad narrated to us. And Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — and the wording is his.\n\nAnd Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath al-Sijistānī in Baghdād informed us; Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr informed us; Abū ʀāṣim narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Wardān narrated to us, saying: Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed me; Ḥumrān informed me, saying: I saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān perform wuḍūʾ. He washed his hands three times, washed his face three times, his forearms three times, wiped his head three times, washed his feet three times, and then said: \Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform wuḍūʾ.\"" Then he said: \""Whoever performs wuḍūʾ less than this wuḍūʾ of mine"," it will suffice him.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 107.]"""
"293","(294) Among them is what Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqrīʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Isfarāyīnī informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us; Musaddad ibn Musarhad informed us; Ṣafwān ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Maryam said: I entered upon Ibn Dārah, the freedman of ʿUthmān, at his house, and he heard me rinsing my mouth [in preparation for wuḍūʾ]. He said: \O Muḥammad!\"" I said: \""At your service.\"" He said: \""Shall I not inform you of the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" I said: \""Yes"," indeed.\"" He said: \""I saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān at the place of sitting. He called for a vessel. He rinsed his mouth three times and sniffed water into his nose three times. He washed his face three times"," his forearms three times each"," wiped his head three times"," and washed his feet. Then he said: 'Whoever wishes to see the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," let him look at this wuḍūʾ of mine.'\"" Others also mentioned the tripling for the feet as well.\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Bazzār"," 9/4.]"""
"294","(295) Among them is what Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Qāḍī in al-Kūfah informed us; Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us; Abū Ghassān Mālik ibn Ismāʿīl informed us; Isrāʾīl narrated from ʿĀmir ibn Shaqīq, i.e., ibn Jamrah, from Shaqīq ibn Salamah, who said: I saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān performing wuḍūʾ. He washed his palms three times, rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his forearms three times, wiped his head three times and his ears — their outer and inner parts — and combed through his beard. He washed his feet three times, and combed through the toes of his feet. He said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do as you have seen me do.\""\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 1452.]"""
"295","(296) Among them is what ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Khāliq al-Muʾadhdhin informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khanb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Tirmidhī informed us; Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to me; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Uways said: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to me from Isḥāq ibn Yaḥyā, from Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib, from his father ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar, from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, that he performed wuḍūʾ. He washed his hands three times — each one of them — sniffed water into his nose three times, rinsed his mouth three times, washed his face three times, washed his hands up to the elbows three times each, wiped his head three times, washed his feet three times each — each one of them three times. Then he said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform wuḍūʾ thus.\""\n\n(T) It has been narrated regarding that from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from ʿUthmān"," and it is mursal.\n\nIt has also been narrated through strange routes from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him)"," but the preserved narration from him is other than that.\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/89.]"""
"296","(297) Al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Ṭūsī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn Shawdhab informed us; Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb informed us; ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd Abū Yaḥyā al-Ḥimyānī narrated from Abū Ḥanīfah, from Khālid ibn ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Khayr al-Hamdānī, that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) called for water and performed wuḍūʾ. He washed his palms three times each, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his hands three times each, wiped his head three times, washed his feet three times each. Then he said: \Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.\""\n\n(T) Al-Ḥasan ibn Ziyād al-Luʾluʾī and Abū Muṭīʿ likewise narrated from Abū Ḥanīfah regarding the masḥ of the head three times.\n\nZāʾidah ibn Qudāmah"," Abū ʀāwānah"," and others narrated it from Khālid ibn ʿAlqamah without mentioning the repetition in the masḥ of the head. Likewise"," the group narrated from ʿAlī"," except what is anomalous (shādhdh) among them. The best of what has been narrated from ʿAlī regarding it is what…\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/89.]"""
"297","(298) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir informed us; Ibn Wahb narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn, from his father, from his grandfather, from ʿAlī, that he performed wuḍūʾ. He washed his face three times, washed his hands three times, wiped his head three times, washed his feet three times, and said: \Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing wuḍūʾ.\"" Thus said Ibn Wahb: \""And he wiped his head three times.\""\n\n(T) And Ḥajjāj said regarding it"," from Ibn Jurayj: \""And he wiped his head once.\""\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi.]"""
"298","(299) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād informed us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā, from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd, that the Prophet ﷺ performed wuḍūʾ. He washed his face three times, his hands twice, wiped his head twice, and washed his feet twice.\n\nAbū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Nasāʾī narrated it in Kitāb al-Sunan from the ḥadīth of Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, thus: the masḥ of the head twice.\n\n(T) However, Mālik, Wahb, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, Khālid al-Wāsiṭī, and others opposed him, narrating it from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā regarding the masḥ of the head once, except that he said: \He brought [his hands] forward and backward.\""\n\n[Shādhdh. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 99.]"""
"299","(300) ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAbdawī informed us; Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Yūsuf Muḥammad ibn Sufyān al-Ṣaffār in al-Maṣṣīṣah informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Rummānī informed us; Bishr, i.e., ibn al-Mufaḍḍal, informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl narrated from al-Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿawwidh ibn ʿAfrāʾ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us. She said: She narrated to us that he said: \Pour wuḍūʾ water for me.\"" So I poured for him into a miḍaʾah — which is a rakwah — and he took a mudd and a third"," or a mudd and a quarter. He said: \""Pour upon my hands.\"" He washed his hands three times. Then he said: \""Set it down.\"" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wuḍūʾ while I was looking. He washed his face three times"," rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose once"," washed his right hand three times"," washed his left hand three times. Then he wiped his head twice"," beginning with the back of his head"," then the front of his head"," then the back of his head"," then the front of his head. Then he wiped his ears — both of them — their outer and inner parts. He washed his right foot three times and washed his left foot three times.\n\n(T) Others narrated it from Bishr without mentioning his words: \""then the back of his head"," then the front of his head.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated from Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq from Abū al-ʿAlāʾ"," from Qatādah"," from Anas"," that he used to wipe his head three times"," taking fresh water for each time.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 126.]"""
"300","(T) There has preceded in this regard the ḥadīth of Shaqīq ibn Salamah from ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\n(301) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd al-Iskandarānī informed us; Ziyād ibn Yūnus narrated to me; Saʿīd ibn Ziyād al-Muʾadhdhin narrated to me from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Taymī, who said: Ibn Abī Mulaykah was asked about wuḍūʾ. He said: \I saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān being asked about wuḍūʾ"," so he called for water.\"" He mentioned the ḥadīth until he said: \""Then he took water and wiped his head and his ears"," washing their inner and outer parts once. Then he washed his feet. Then he said: 'Where are those who ask about wuḍūʾ? Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing wuḍūʾ.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 126.]"""
"301","(302) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Hafiz narrated to us; Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqi narrated from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh that the Prophet (ﷺ) wiped his ears, their outer and inner parts. [Sahih by other than him]"
"302","(303) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Hisham narrated to us; Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us; Humaid narrated: Anas performed wudu' while we were with him, and he wiped the inner and outer parts of his ears. He noticed our intense gaze upon him and said: \Indeed"," Ibn Mas'ud used to command us to do this.\"" [Hasan]"""
"303","(304) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Asid ibn 'Asim narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated from Sufyan al-Thawri from Humaid, who said: I saw Anas ibn Malik perform wudu' and wipe his ears, their outer and inner parts. We looked at him, and he said: \Ibn Umm 'Abd (i.e."," 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud) used to command us to do that.\"" [Sahih by other than him]"""
"304","(305) al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Rudhbari narrated to us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Mahmud ibn Khalid and Hisham ibn Khalid — both with the same meaning — narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated from Hariz ibn 'Uthman from 'Abd Rahman ibn Maysarah from al-Miqdad ibn Ma'dikarib, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform wudu'. He said: And he wiped his ears, their inner and outer parts.\n\nHisham added: And he inserted his fingers into the ear-holes of his ears. [Sahih. Abu Dawud narrated it as no. 123]"
"305","(306) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-Walid al-Faqih narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn 'Ali al-Dhuhli narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us; Waki' narrated from Sufyan from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn 'Afra' that the Prophet (ﷺ) performed wudu' and inserted his fingers into his ears. [Da'if. Abu Dawud narrated it as no. 131]"
"306","(307) And al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Faqih narrated to us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Waki' narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil narrated it with a similar wording and said: \His fingers in the cavities of his ears.\"" [Da'if. Abu Dawud narrated it as no. 131]"""
"307","(308) Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus al-'Anazi narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us; al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to me; 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated from Hibban ibn Was'i al-Ansari that his father narrated to him that he heard 'Abd Allah ibn Zayd mentioning: He saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performing wudu', and he took water for his ears different from the water he had taken for his head. And this is a sahih isnad.\n\n(T) And similarly it was narrated from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Ibn 'Imran ibn Miqlas and Harmalah ibn Yahya from Ibn Wahb. [Sahih. Al-Hakim narrated it as 1/253]"
"308","(309) And Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated it in al-Sahih from Harun ibn Ma'ruf and Harun ibn Sa'id al-Ayli and Abi al-Tahir from Ibn Wahb with a sahih isnad: He saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performing wudu'. He mentioned his wudu' and said: He wiped his head with water other than the leftover water from his hands, and he did not mention the ears.\n\nAbu 'Ali al-Rudhbari narrated it to us; Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Sarh, i.e., Abi al-Tahir, narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated from 'Amr ibn al-Harith, and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd this is more sahih than the one before it. [Sahih. Malik narrated it as no. 67]"
"309","(310) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn Hafs ibn 'Asim ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and Malik ibn Anas narrated from Nafi' that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar used to dip his fingers in water and wipe his ears with them. [Sahih. Malik narrated it as no. 67]"
"310","(311) And Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us; my grandfather Abu 'Amr ibn Nujayd narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanj narrated to us; Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated from Nafi' that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, when he performed wudu', would take water with his fingers for his ears. As for what has been narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: \The ears are part of the head\"" — that has been narrated through weak asanid"," which we have mentioned in al-Khilaf. And the most famous isnad in it is what... [Sahih. Through its routes"," Abu Dawud narrated it as no. 134]"""
"311","(312) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Musaddad and Abū al-Rabīʿ both said: Ḥammād narrated to us: Sinān ibn Rabīʿah narrated from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab, from Abū Umāmah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed wuḍūʾ, washing his face three times, his hands three times, and wiping his head, and he said: \The two ears are part of the head.\"" And he used to wipe the inner corners of the eyes.\n\nThis ḥadīth is discussed from two perspectives: one is the weakness of some of its narrators"," and the other is the doubt regarding its being raised (marfūʿ) to the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī said: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn say: Sinān ibn Rabīʿah"," from whom Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrates"," is not strong (laysa bi-l-qawiyy).\n\nAbū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū Saʿīd al-Khallāl narrated to us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us: Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān narrated to us: al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us: Ibn ʿAwn narrated to us. Shahr ibn Ḥawshab was mentioned in his presence"," and he said: \""Indeed"," Shahr was impugned (nazakūh).\"" His statement \""nazakūh\"" means they criticized him and tongues spoke against him.\n\nWith his chain of narration"," Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān narrated to us: Shabbābah said: I heard Shuʿbah say: Shahr ibn Ḥawshab accompanied a man from the people of Shām"," and the man accused him of stealing his bag.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us: My father said: Shahr ibn Ḥawshab was in charge of the bayt al-māl"," and he took a purse containing dirhams"," whereupon a poet said:\n\n\""Indeed"," Shahr sold his religion for a purse—who will trust the Qurʾān reciters after you"," O Shahr?\""\n\nAbū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Daʿlaj ibn Aḥmad said: I asked Mūsā ibn Hārūn about this ḥadīth"," and he said: \""It is nothing. In it is Shahr ibn Ḥawshab"," and Shahr is weak (ḍaʿīf).\""\n\nAl-Bayhaqī said: The ḥadīth"," in its being raised (to the Prophet)"," contains doubt. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it through its chains"," no. 134.]"""
"312","(313) Abū Bakr informed us: ʿAlī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Khushaysh narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Mūsā al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Sinān ibn Rabīʿah, from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab, from Abū Umāmah that he described the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \When he performed wuḍūʾ"," he would wipe the inner corners of his eyes with water.\"" And Abū Umāmah said: \""The two ears are part of the head.\""\n\nSulaymān ibn Ḥarb said: \""The two ears are part of the head\""—this is only from the statement of Abū Umāmah. Whoever says otherwise has altered it"," or a word stated by Sulaymān"," i.e."," he has erred. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other routes. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it"," 1/104.]"""
"313","(314) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb, Musaddad, and Qutaybah narrated from Ḥammād ibn Zayd, from Sinān ibn Rabīʿah, from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab, from Abū Umāmah, who mentioned the wuḍūʾ of the Prophet (ﷺ). He said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would wipe the inner corners of the eyes"," and he said: 'The two ears are part of the head.'\""\n\nSulaymān ibn Ḥarb said: Abū Umāmah says it.\n\nQutaybah said: Ḥammād said: \""I do not know whether it is from the statement of the Prophet (ﷺ) or of Abū Umāmah\""—referring to the matter of the two ears.\n\nQutaybah said: From Sinān"," Abū Rabīʿah—thus it is in my book: \""al-maʾqayn\"" (the inner corners of the eyes). And in the narration of Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī from Ibn Dāsah it is \""al-māqayn.\""\n\nAbū Sulaymān explained it as the corner of the eye adjacent to the nose"," which is the outlet of tears.\n\nWhat has been narrated regarding his wiping his head and his two ears in some of the previously mentioned narrations is general (mujmal)"," and its detailed description (kayfiyyah) is found in this narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other routes. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," no. 134.]"""
"314","(315) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed wuḍūʾ. He mentioned the ḥadīth and said: \Then he took some water and wiped his head with it"," placing the two middle fingers inside his ears and the two thumbs behind his ears.\""\n\nOur companions said: \""It is as though he set aside two fingers from each hand; when he finished wiping his head"," he wiped his ears with them.\"" [Ḥasan.]"""
"315","(316) It has been narrated in this ḥadīth: \He wiped their ears"," inserting the two index fingers inside them"," and opposed with his thumbs"," wiping the inner and outer parts of the ears.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: Ibn Idrīs narrated from Ibn ʿAjlān"," and he mentioned it with its chain. [Ḥasan. Ibn Ḥibbān narrated it"," no. 1086.]"""
"316","(317) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl both said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Warqāʾ narrated to us: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said: \Shall I not show you the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" He said: \""He washed his hands once each"," rinsed his mouth once and sniffed water into his nose once"," washed his face once"," washed his forearms once each"," wiped his head once"," and washed his feet once each. Then he said: 'This is the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).'\"" This is a ṣaḥīḥ chain. [Ḥasan. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it"," no. 51.]"""
"317","(318) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us. And Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed you, from Ibn Shihāb, that ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī informed him that Ḥumrān, the freedman of ʿUthmān, informed him that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān one day called for water for wuḍūʾ and performed wuḍūʾ. He washed his palms three times, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water and blew it out three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his right hand up to the elbow three times, then washed his left hand likewise, then wiped his head, then washed his right foot up to the ankles three times, then washed his left foot likewise. Then he said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) one day perform wuḍūʾ similar to this wuḍūʾ of mine.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Whoever performs wuḍūʾ similar to this wuḍūʾ of mine"," then stands and prays two rakʿahs in which he does not speak to himself"," his previous sins will be forgiven.\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah and Abū al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb. Al-Bukhārī narrated it through other routes from Ibn Shihāb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," no. 226.]"""
"318","(319) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Musaddad ibn Musarhad informed us: Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Khālid ibn ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Khayr, who said: ʿAlī came to us after having prayed, and he called for water for purification. We said: \What does he want with purification when he has already prayed? He only intends to teach us.\"" So a vessel containing water and a basin were brought. He poured from the vessel onto his right hand and washed it three times"," then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water three times. He rinsed his mouth and blew the water from the same hand from which he took the water. Then he washed his face three times"," washed his right hand three times"," and washed his left hand three times. Then he placed his hand in the vessel and wiped his head once. Then he washed his right foot three times and his left foot three times. Then he said: \""Whoever would like to know the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," this is it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," no. 111.]"""
"319","(320) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Musaddad and al-Ḥajabī both said: Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Abī Bishr, from Yūsuf ibn Māhak, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) lagged behind us on a journey we were traveling"," and he caught up with us when the ʿAṣr prayer was upon us. We were performing wuḍūʾ and began wiping over our feet. He called out in his loudest voice: 'Woe to the heels from the Fire!'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl"," and Abū al-Nuʿmān. Muslim narrated it from Shaybān and Abū Kāmil"," all of them from Abī ʿAwanah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 60.]"""
"320","(321) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh, Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā, Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl, and Abū Saʿīd Masʿūd ibn Muḥammad al-Jurjānī all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Sulaymān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Sufyān, from Manṣūr.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr, from Hilāl ibn Yisāf, from Abī Yaḥyā, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: \We returned with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from Makkah to al-Madīnah. We stopped at a water source along the way"," and a group of people hastened to perform wuḍūʾ"," being hurried on account of the ʿAṣr prayer. We came upon them and their heels were gleaming white"," the water not having touched them. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Complete the wuḍūʾ! Woe to the heels from the Fire! Complete the wuḍūʾ!'\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Wakīʿ"," from al-Thawrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it for this wording"," no. 161.]"""
"321","(322) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated —\n\nAnd Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed me: Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi in Hamadan informed us: Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Abu Iyas narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated, saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah, who would pass by us while people were performing ablution from the water vessel, saying: \Complete the ablution"," for verily Abu al-Qasim (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Woe to the heels from the Fire.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of Adam's hadith. Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Adam"," and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Shu'bah."""
"322","(323) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq, the faqih, informed us: Abu al-Muthanna narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bakr both said: Al-Rabi' ibn Muslim narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah: that the Prophet (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man who had not washed his heels, so he said: \Woe to the heels from the Fire.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim. (T) And with its meaning"," Abu Salih narrated it from Abu Hurayrah."""
"323","(324) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dh'ib narrated from 'Imran ibn Bashir from Salim Sabalan, who said: I heard 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) say to her brother: \O 'Abd al-Rahman"," complete the ablution"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'Woe to the heels from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.'\"""""
"324","(325) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, narrated to us: Abu 'Ali al-Husayn ibn 'Ali, the hafiz, informed us verbally: 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman, 'Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Qudayd, and 'asim ibn Razih, the Egyptians, in Egypt, said: Abu al-Tahir narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated from Mukhrah ibn Bukayr from his father from Salim, the mawla of Shaddad: that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr entered upon 'A'ishah and performed ablution in her presence, so she said: \O 'Abd al-Rahman"," complete the ablution"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'Woe to the ankles from the Fire.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu al-Tahir"," except that he said: \""to the heels\"" (li-al-a'qab).\n\n(T) And Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman and Nu'aym ibn 'Abd Allah narrated it from Salim with its meaning."""
"325","(326) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us: 'Ubayd ibn Sharik narrated to us: Yahya narrated —\n\nAnd Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq, the faqih, informed us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Milhan narrated to us: Yahya ibn Bukayr said: Layth narrated to me from Haywah ibn Shurayh from 'Uqbah ibn Muslim from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi: that he heard the Prophet (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: \Woe to the heels and the soles of the feet from the Fire.\"""""
"326","(327) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, said: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Saydalani narrated to us: Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn A'yan narrated to us: Ma'qil narrated from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, who said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab informed me: that a man performed ablution and left a spot the size of a fingernail on his foot. The Prophet (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it and said: \Return and improve your ablution.\"" He then returned and prayed.\n\nMuslim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated it in his Sahih from Salamah ibn Shabib."""
"327","(328) And Abu 'Abd Allah narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim said: He heard Qatadah ibn Di'amah say: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: that a man came to the Prophet (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having performed ablution but having left on his foot a spot the size of a fingernail. The Messenger of Allah (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: \Return and improve your ablution.\"""""
"328","(329) Abu Nasr 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu Mansur al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl ibn Zakariyya al-Dabbi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Khalid narrated from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas: that he used to recite {"
"329","(330) And with his chain of narration, Hushaym informed us, saying: Abu Muhammad, a mawla of Quraysh, informed us: 'Abbad ibn al-Rabi' narrated from 'Ali: that he used to recite it likewise."
"330","(331) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali, the hafiz, informed us: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Bundar narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated from 'Asim from Zir ibn Hubaysh from 'Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Mas'ud: that he used to recite {"
"331","(332) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us — Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq narrated from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, who said: The Qurʾān reverts to washing (al-ghasl), and he recited {"
"332","(333) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Qays, from Mujāhid, who said: The Qurʾān reverts to washing (al-ghasl), and he recited {"
"333","(334) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Aṭāʾ informed us — ʿUmar ibn Qays narrated from Aṭāʾ that he used to recite {"
"334","(335) Abū ʿAbdillāh and Abū Saʿīd informed us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Yaḥyā informed us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā narrated from Usayd ibn Yazīd that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj used to recite {"
"335","(336) Abū ʿAbdillāh and Abū Saʿīd informed us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us — ʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ al-Qālūn said: I recited this recitation to Nāfiʿ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Nuʿaym al-Qāriʾ more than once, and he mentioned in it {"
"336","(337) Abū ʿAbdillāh and Abū Saʿīd informed us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn al-Jahm informed us — al-Walīd ibn Ḥassān al-Thawrī informed me that he recited the Qurʾān upon Abū Muḥammad Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq ibn Yazīd al-Ḥaḍramī, who was well-versed in the modes of recitation (wujūh al-qirāʾāt), and he mentioned in it {"
"337","(338) And Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān and Abū al-Qāsim Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Ṣaqr in Baghdād informed us — they both said: Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān al-Ādamī narrated to us — ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us — Abū al-Jawwāb narrated to us — ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī, that he said: Wash the two feet up to the ankles, as you have been commanded. (T) And it has been narrated in the authentic ḥadīth from ʿAmr ibn ʿAbasah from the Prophet ﷺ regarding wuḍūʾ, that he then washed his two feet up to the ankles as Allah, the Most High, had commanded him. (Q) And in that is an indication that Allah, the Most High, commanded their washing. And as for the athar which: [Weak (Ḍaʿīf)]"
"338","(339) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Aṭāʾ informed us — Ḥumayd narrated from Mūsā ibn Anas, who said: al-Ḥajjāj ibn Yūsuf addressed the people and said: Wash your faces, your hands, and your feet — wash their exterior and interior and their heels, for that is nearer to your Paradise. Anas said: Allah spoke the truth and al-Ḥajjā"
"339","(340) The faqīh Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥammād narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās ibn Yazīd narrated to us — Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl narrated to me that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn sent him to al-Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿādh to ask her about the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He mentioned the ḥadīth describing the wuḍūʾ of the Prophet ﷺ, in which she said: Then he washed his two feet. She said: And a cousin of yours came to me — meaning Ibn ʿAbbās — so I informed him, and he said: I find in the Book (the Qurʾān) nothing except two washings and two wipings. (Q) So if this is authentic, it is possible that Ibn ʿAbbās held the recitation to be with khafḍ (genitive), which implies wiping, and then when it reached him that the Prophet ﷺ threatened against abandoning their washing or abandoning any part of them, he went to the position of the obligation of washing and recited it with nasb (accusative). And we have narrated from him that he recited it with nasb (accusative). And as for the ḥadīth which: [Weak (Ḍaʿīf). Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī (1/96)]"
"340","(341) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — he said: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawīh narrated to us — Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us — Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us — Hishām ibn Saʿd informed us — Zayd ibn Aslam narrated from Aṭāʾ ibn Yasār, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said to us: Would you like me to narrate to you how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform wuḍūʾ? He then mentioned the ḥadīth and said: Then he scooped another handful and sprinkled it upon his foot while it had a sandal on it, and he did the same for the left foot, and he wiped the bottom of the two sandals. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (137)]"
"341","(342) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us — ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed wuḍūʾ and placed his vessel in the water container"," then he sniffed water into his nose and rinsed his mouth once. Then he placed his hand (in the water) and poured it upon his face once"," and poured upon his hands twice each. He wiped his head once"," then took a handful of water and sprinkled it upon his feet while he was wearing his leather socks (naʿl).\""\n\n(T) And thus did Hishām ibn Saʿd and ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī narrate it. However"," they were contradicted by Sulaymān ibn Bilāl"," Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān"," Warqāʾ ibn ʿUmar"," and Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Abī Kathīr. [Ḥasan. Al-Ṭaḥāwī referenced it (1/71)]"""
"342","(343) As for the ḥadīth of Sulaymān ibn Bilāl: ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Adīb informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us — al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā informed us — al-Ramādī informed us — Abū Salamah al-Khuzāʿī narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Bilāl from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he performed wuḍūʾ… and he mentioned the ḥadīth until he said: \Then he took a ladleful of water and sprinkled it upon his left foot. Then he said: 'Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performing wuḍūʾ.'\""\n\nAnd al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm from Abū Salamah al-Khuzāʿī"," and he said in the ḥadīth: \""He took a ladleful of water and sprinkled it upon his right foot — meaning until he washed it. Then he took another ladleful and washed his left foot with it. Then he said: 'Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performing wuḍūʾ.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī referenced it (140)]"""
"343","(344) As for the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAjlān: Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Layth Naṣr ibn al-Qāsim al-Farāʾiḍī in Baghdad narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān from Zayd ibn Aslam, and he mentioned it with his chain of narration, saying: \Then he took a ladleful and washed his right foot. Then he took a ladleful and washed his left foot.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihī. Al-Nasāʾī referenced it (2/1)]"""
"344","(345) As for the ḥadīth of Warqāʾ: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us — Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us — Warqāʾ narrated — Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said: \Shall I not show you the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" He said: \""He washed his hands once each"," rinsed his mouth once"," sniffed water into his nose once"," washed his face once"," his forearms once each"," wiped his head once"," and washed his feet once each. Then he said: 'This is the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).'\""\n\nAnd we have mentioned the narrations in what has passed"," except for the narration of Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar"," which is in what follows. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihī]"""
"345","(346) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — ʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar from Zayd ibn Aslam, and he mentioned it with his chain of narration, saying: \Then he took a handful and washed his right foot with it"," and took a handful and washed his left foot.\""\n\n(Q) So these narrations are agreed upon that he washed both feet"," and the ḥadīth of al-Dārawardī is susceptible to the possibility that it agrees with them by his having washed both feet while they were in the leather socks.\n\n(J) And Hishām ibn Saʿd is not a strong ḥāfiẓ"," so that which he contradicts the reliable and established narrators is not accepted from him — how so"," when they are a number and he is but one?\n\nAnd al-Thawrī and Hishām ibn Saʿd have narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam that which agrees with the narration of the majority. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihī]"""
"346","(347) Al-Bayrūtī narrated to me — Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn narrated to us — Hishām ibn Saʿd narrated to us — Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said: \Would you like me to narrate to you how the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to perform wuḍūʾ?\"" He said: \""He called for a vessel containing water","\"" and he mentioned his wuḍūʾ"," and said in it: \""Then he scooped up a handful of water and sprinkled it upon his right foot while it was in the leather sock. Then he wiped with his hand from above the foot and from beneath the foot.\"" Then he did the same with the left.\n\n\""This is the most authentic ḥadīth narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ) in this regard"," along with what agrees with the narration of the majority.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihī. Al-Ḥākim referenced it (1/247)]"""
"347","(348) The jurist Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr al-Ṭūsī informed us — Abū Bishr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥāḍir narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Sarrāj narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Samīnah narrated to us — al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-Jarmī narrated to us — Sufyān al-Thawrī and Hishām ibn Saʿd, both of them, from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said to me: \Shall I not show you the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" So he performed wuḍūʾ once"," then washed his feet while his leather socks were upon them.\n\n(Q) So this indicates that he washed his feet while they were in the leather socks. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"348","(349) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī said: \It has been narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) wiped upon the tops of his feet"," and it has been narrated that he sprinkled water upon their tops. One of the two ḥadīths has a sound chain of narration"," were it to stand alone"," it would be established. But the one that contradicts it is more numerous and more established. As for the other ḥadīth"," the scholars of ḥadīth do not establish it were it to stand alone.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""What he meant by the first ḥadīth is the ḥadīth of al-Dārawardī and others from Zayd. And what he meant by the other ḥadīth — and Allah knows best — is the ḥadīth of ʿAbd Khayr from ʿAlī regarding wiping upon the tops of the feet.\""\n\nAnd we have clarified that he intended"," if it is authentic"," the surface of the two leather slippers"," and it is mentioned in the chapter on wiping upon the leather slippers with its evidences.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from ʿAlī from another perspective regarding the meaning of the first ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"349","(350) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: My father informed me — Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq said: Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah ibn Yazīd ibn Rukānah narrated to me from ʿUbayd Allāh al-Khawlānī from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \ʿAlī entered upon me in my house and called for wuḍūʾ water"," so we brought him a bowl that held a mudd or close to it"," and it was placed before him. He had urinated"," so he said: 'O Ibn ʿAbbās"," shall I not perform for you the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?' I said: 'Yes"," may my father and mother be your ransom.' He said: \""So a vessel was placed for him. He washed his hands"," then rinsed his mouth"," sniffed water into his nose"," and blew it out. Then he took with both hands and struck his face with them"," and placed his thumbs into the openings of his ears. Then he returned to do the same three times. Then he took a palmful of water with his right hand and poured it upon his forelock"," then let it flow upon his face. Then he washed his right hand up to the elbow three times"," then his left hand likewise. Then he wiped his head and their outer parts (i.e."," his ears). Then he took with both palms of his hands from the water and struck his foot while the leather sock was in it"," so he soaked it. Then he did the same with the other foot.\"" I said: \""And in the leather socks?\"" He said: \""And in the leather socks.\"" He said: I said: \""And in the leather socks?\"" He said: \""And in the leather socks.\"" He said: I said: \""And in the leather socks?\"" He said: \""And in the leather socks.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: \""I asked Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī about this ḥadīth and he said: 'I do not know what this ḥadīth is","' as though he considered the first ḥadīth to be more authentic — meaning the ḥadīth of ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār.\""\n\n(Q) The Shaykh said: \""It is possible"," if it is authentic"," that he washed them while they were in the leather socks. For we have narrated from many perspectives from the Commander of the Faithful ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) that he washed his feet during wuḍūʾ.\"" Among them is: [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd referenced it (117)]"""
"350","(351) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us — Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī narrated from Zāʾidah — Khālid ibn ʿAlqamah narrated from ʿAbd Khayr from ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu): \He called for wuḍūʾ water"," so a vessel containing water was brought to him…\"" and he mentioned the ḥadīth until he said: \""Then he poured with his right hand three times upon his right foot"," then washed it with his left hand. Then he poured with his right hand upon his left foot three times"," then washed it with his left hand. Then he said: 'This is the purification of the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihī. Ibn Ḥibbān referenced it (79/1)]"""
"351","(352) And among them is what Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Warrāq narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym — al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtī al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, Ribʿah al-Kinānī narrated from al-Minhāl ibn ʿAmr, from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh: that he heard ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) when he was asked about the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He poured water into the courtyard and then said: \Where is the one who asked about the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?\"" He washed his hands three times"," his face three times"," his forearms three times"," and wiped over his head until it was nearly dripping"," and washed his feet three times each. Then he said: \""Thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nThe narration of al-Faqīh does not contain his words \""until it was nearly dripping.\"" The rest is the same. [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Bazzār"," 561.]"""
"352","(353) And among them is what Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us, Abū Isḥāq narrated from Abī Ḥayyah, who said: I saw ʿAlī perform wuḍūʾ. He washed his hands until he thoroughly cleansed them, then rinsed his mouth three times and sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times and his forearms three times, wiped over his head, and washed his feet up to the ankles. Then he stood, took the remaining water of his wuḍūʾ, and drank it while standing. Then he said: \I wanted to show you how the purification of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was.\"" Thus narrated Abū Isḥāq from Abī Ḥayyah"," and it is established in a similar narration that he wiped and stated that it was the wuḍūʾ of one who had not broken his wuḍūʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 116.]"""
"353","(354) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawyah al-ʿAskarī narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us, Ādam informed us, Shuʿbah informed us, ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Maysarah informed us, and he said: I heard al-Nazzāl ibn Sabrah narrate from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him): that he prayed Ẓuhr, then sat attending to the needs of the people in the courtyard of Kūfah until the time of ʿAṣr prayer came. Then he was brought a vessel of water, from which he took a handful and therewith wiped his face, his hands, his head, and his feet. Then he stood and drank the remainder while standing, and said: \Indeed"," some people dislike drinking while standing"," yet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did as I have done.\"" And he said: \""This is the wuḍūʾ of one who has not broken his wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās with part of its meaning.\n\n(Q) And in this established ḥadīth there is evidence that the ḥadīth narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding wiping over the two feet — if it is authentic — refers only to one who is pure and has not broken his wuḍūʾ. However"," it is as though some of the narrators abridged the ḥadīth and did not transmit his words: \""This is the wuḍūʾ of one who has not broken his wuḍūʾ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 5293.]"""
"354","(355) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, my father informed us, Ibn al-Ashjaʿī narrated from his father, from Sufyān, from al-Suddī, from ʿAbd Khayr, from ʿAlī: that he called for a vessel of water and then said: \Where are those who claim that they dislike drinking while standing?\"" He said: \""So he took it and drank while standing"," then performed a light wuḍūʾ"," wiped over his sandals"," and said: 'Thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when he had not broken his wuḍūʾ.'\""\n\nAnd Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth narrated something similar from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd al-Raḥmān al-Ashjaʿī. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 2/2.]"""
"355","(356) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, Abū Yaḥyā Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Bazzāz informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth informed us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd al-Raḥmān al-Ashjaʿī narrated from Sufyān, from al-Suddī, from ʿAbd Khayr, from ʿAlī: that he called for a vessel of water, then performed a light wuḍūʾ, then wiped over his sandals, and said: \Thus was the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for the pure one who has not broken his wuḍūʾ.\""\n\n(Q) And in this there is evidence that what has been narrated from ʿAlī regarding wiping over the two sandals pertains to a voluntary wuḍūʾ"," not to an obligatory wuḍūʾ required due to an act that necessitates wuḍūʾ. Or he intended washing the feet while in the sandals"," or he intended wiping over his socks and his sandals"," as some narrators have reported from him with the restriction of the two socks — and by the two socks he meant two sandals lined with leather. It is established from him (may Allah be pleased with him) that he washed the feet"," and it is established from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he washed the feet"," and there is a severe warning against omitting it. And with Allah lies success. [Ḥasan in other than this chain. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 200.]"""
"356","(357) Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, Salm ibn Junādah narrated to us, Wakīʿ narrated from Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah, Abū al-Qāsim al-Jadalī narrated to us, and he said: I heard al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) turned his noble face toward us and said: \Straighten your rows — three times — by Allah"," you must straighten your rows"," or Allah will cause discord between your hearts.\"" He said: \""So I saw a man pressing his ankle against his companion's ankle"," his knee against his companion's knee"," and his shoulder against his companion's shoulder.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 662.]"""
"357","(358) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us, Yūnus ibn Bukayr informed us, Yazīd ibn Ziyād ibn Abī al-Jaʿd narrated from Jāmiʿ ibn Shaddād, from Ṭāriq ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muḥāribī, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) pass by the market of Dhī al-Majāz while I was engaged in a transaction of mine. He passed by wearing a red ḥullah (garment), and I heard him say: \O people"," say 'Lā ilāha illa Allāh' and you will prosper.\"" And a man was following him"," pelting him with stones"," having bloodied his ankles — meaning Abū Lahab — and he mentioned the ḥadīth. [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 2/668.]"""
"358","(359) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Kathīr informed us, and he said: I heard ʿĀṣim ibn Laqīṭ ibn Ṣabrah narrate from his father, who said: I was among the delegation of Banī al-Muntafiq to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," tell me about wuḍūʾ.\"" He said: \""Perform wuḍūʾ thoroughly"," interlace between the fingers"," and be vigorous in sniffing water into the nose unless you are fasting.\""\n\n(T) And it has preceded in the ḥadīth of Shaqīq ibn Salamah from ʿUthmān regarding the description of the Prophet's wuḍūʾ (peace and blessings be upon him) that he interlaced between the toes of his feet. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 142.]"""
"359","(360) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, and he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Ibn Lahīʿah informed you from Yazīd ibn ʿAmr al-Maʿāfirī, who said: I heard Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥubulī say: I heard al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddād al-Qurashī say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) interlacing between the toes of his feet with his little finger. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ṭaḥāwī in Sharh al-Maʿānī, 1/36.]"
"360","(361) Abū Ḥāzim ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Ḥanẓalī in al-Rayy informed us, Aḥmad — meaning Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Wahb — said: I heard my paternal uncle say: I heard Mālik being asked about interlacing between the toes of the feet in wuḍūʾ, and he said: \That is not incumbent upon the people.\"" He said: \""So I left him until the people had lessened"," and I said to him: 'O Abū ʿAbd Allāh"," I heard you give a ruling regarding the matter of interlacing between the toes of the feet"," claiming that it is not incumbent upon the people"," yet we have a Sunnah regarding that.' He said: 'And what is it?' I said: 'Al-Layth ibn Saʿd"," Ibn Lahīʿah"," and ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us from Yazīd ibn ʿAmr al-Maʿāfirī"," from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥubulī"," from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddād al-Qurashī"," who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) interlacing between the toes of his feet with his little finger.' He said: 'Indeed"," this is a good ḥadīth"," and I had never heard it before except at that moment.' Then I heard him being asked after that"," and he commanded interlacing between the fingers.\"" My paternal uncle said: \""Few are those who perform wuḍūʾ without the line beneath the toe of the foot being missed"," for people bend their toes during wuḍūʾ. So whoever attends to that is safe.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Abī Ḥākim in the introduction of al-Jarḥ wa al-Taʿdīl"," 1/31.]"""
"361","(362) Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us; Khālid ibn Makhlad informed us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us; he said: ʿUmārah ibn Ghaziyyah al-Anṣārī narrated to me from Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Mujmir, who said: I saw Abū Hurayrah perform wuḍūʾ. He washed his face and performed the wuḍūʾ thoroughly, then he washed his right hand until he reached into the upper arm, then his left hand until he reached into the upper arm, then he wiped over his head, then he washed his right foot until he reached into the shin, then he washed his left foot until he reached into the shin. Then he said: \Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform wuḍūʾ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim (246)]"""
"362","(363) And with his chain of narration, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \You are the radiant and luminous ones on the Day of Resurrection by virtue of performing wuḍūʾ thoroughly. So whoever among you is able"," let him lengthen his radiance and his luminosity.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb and others"," from Khālid ibn Makhlad. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim (6410)]"""
"363","(364) Abū al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, from Abī ʿUbayd; Hushaym and Muʿādh informed us, from Ibn ʿAwn, from Abī Saʿīd, the brother of Umm al-Muʾminīn ʿĀʾishah (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhā) through foster-relationship, from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhā), regarding a woman who performs wuḍūʾ while she has dye (khiḍāb) on her. She said: \Remove it and compel her to do so.\"" Abū ʿUbayd said: Her statement \""compel her\"" means: \""Disgrace it and cast it away from you.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"364","(365) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Asadī informed me; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās informed us; Shuʿbah informed us, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, who said: Someone who heard ʿĀʾishah, Umm al-Muʾminīn, narrate to me, saying: \It reached me — or it was mentioned to me — that women apply dye"," and then one of them wipes over her dye when she performs wuḍūʾ for the prayer. That my hands be cut off with knives would be more beloved to me than that I should do that.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dārimī (1901)]"""
"365","(366) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me, from Qatādah, who narrated to him that Abū al-ʿĀliyah narrated to him — or another man — that he asked Ibn ʿAbbās about dye (khiḍāb). Ibn ʿAbbās said: \Shall I inform you how our women used to apply dye? They would pray ʿIshāʾ"," then apply the dye and go to sleep. When the time for Ṣubḥ prayer came"," they would remove it"," perform wuḍūʾ"," and pray. Then they would reapply it. When the time for Ẓuhr prayer came"," they would remove it with the finest dye"," without it preoccupying them from wuḍūʾ. Indeed"," the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) used to apply dye after the last ʿIshāʾ prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq (3930)]"""
"366","(367) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Abū Bakr ibn Bālawayh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yūnus informed us; Rūḥ informed us; Shuʿbah informed us, from Qatādah, from Lāḥiq ibn Ḥumayd, who said: \I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about dye (khiḍāb).\"" He said: \""Our women used to apply dye from the ʿIshāʾ prayer until the Ṣubḥ prayer. Then they would cleanse their hands and purify themselves. Then they would return to it from the Ṣubḥ prayer until the Ẓuhr prayer with the finest dye"," and that did not prevent them from the prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"367","(368) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Juhanī informed me; Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Ḥimṣī, the judge of Andalusia, informed me, from Abī ʿUthmān, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr and Rabiʿah ibn Yazīd, from Abī Idrīs al-Khawlānī, and ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Bukht, from al-Layth ibn Sulaym al-Juhanī — all of them narrating from ʿUqbah ibn ʀmir.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh and Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar both informed us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed me; he said: My father informed me; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī informed me; Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ informed me, from Rabiʿah — meaning Ibn Yazīd — from Abī Idrīs al-Khawlānī, who said: And Abū ʿUthmān narrated to him, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from ʿUqbah ibn ʀmir, who said: We were entrusted with tending the camels. My turn came, and I drove them back in the late afternoon. I came upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) standing, addressing the people. I caught the following from his words: \There is no Muslim who performs wuḍūʾ and performs it well"," then stands and prays two rakʿahs"," turning to them with his heart and his face"," except that Paradise becomes obligatory for him.\"" I said: \""How excellent this is!\"" Then someone in front of me was saying: \""What was said before it was even more excellent.\"" I looked and it was ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanh). He said: \""I saw you just now arriving.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) had said: \""There is none among you who performs wuḍūʾ and then says: 'I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah"," and I bear witness that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger' except that the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him"," and he may enter through whichever of them he wishes.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Ibn Mahdī. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī"," and he said in his chain: from Abī Idrīs al-Khawlānī"," from ʿUqbah ibn ʀmir"," who said: And Abī ʿUthmān narrated to me"," from Jubayr ibn Nufayr"," from ʿUqbah ibn ʀmir. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim (234)]"""
"368","(369) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us; Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us; Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us; Rabiʿah ibn Yazīd al-Dimashqī narrated to me, from Abī Idrīs al-Khawlānī, from Abī ʿUthmān, from ʿUqbah ibn ʀmir, that he heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever performs wuḍūʾ and performs it well"," then says: 'I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah alone"," with no partner"," and that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger","' the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him"," and he may enter through whichever of them he wishes.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (55)]"""
"369","(370) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us; Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbdullāh informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us. He mentioned it with his chain, and said: \And Abī ʿUthmān"," from Jubayr ibn Nufayr ibn Mālik al-Ḥaḍramī"," from ʿUqbah ibn ʀmir.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n\n(T) And it is narrated in the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar and Anas in this ḥadīth: \""O Allah"," make me among those who repent frequently and make me among those who purify themselves.\"" That"," along with other narrations"," is recorded in the Book of Supplications. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"370","(371) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; Wakīʿ informed us.\n\nHe said: And Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Hāshim informed us; Wakīʿ informed us, from Sufyān, from Abī al-Naḍr, from Abī Anas, who said: ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanh) performed wuḍūʾ near the sitting places and said: \Shall I not show you the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" Then he performed wuḍūʾ"," washing each part three times. Sufyān said: Abū al-Naḍr narrated from Abī Anas that there were men from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with him"," and he said to them: \""Did you not see the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform wuḍūʾ in this manner?\"" They said: \""Indeed"," yes.\""\n\nThus Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," and Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb"," from Wakīʿ"," and he said in his chain: from Abī Anas. And Abī Anas is Mālik ibn Abī ʿĀmir al-Aṣbaḥī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim (230)]"""
"371","(372) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us, from Sufyān.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, saying: al-Firyābī narrated to us, saying: Sufyān narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, saying: Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us, saying: Sufyān narrated from Sālim Abī al-Naḍr, from Busr ibn Saʿīd,\n\nfrom ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān: that he called for water and performed wuḍūʾ near the sitting place, washing each part three times, then he said to the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: \Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do this?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Ḥusayn.\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of al-Firyābī: that ʿUthmān performed wuḍūʾ washing each part three times"," then he said to the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \""Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it this way?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" And in the ḥadīth of Abū Ḥudhayfah: he called for water at the sitting place. And this is how it appears in the Jāmiʿ of al-Thawrī"," the narration of ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd al-ʿAdanī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 1/67]"""
"372","(373) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī and al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Qūhyār said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us, saying: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, saying: Sufyān narrated from Mūsā ibn Abī ʿĀʾishah, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about wuḍūʾ, so he showed him, washing each part three times, then he said: \This is the wuḍūʾ. Whoever adds to this has done wrong"," or transgressed and oppressed.\""\n\n(T) And al-Ashjaʿī narrated it similarly from al-Thawrī"," connected (mawṣūl). [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr 174]"""
"373","(374) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, saying: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, saying: Musaddad narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Mūsā ibn Abī ʿĀʾishah, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," how is purification (ṭahūr)?\"" So he called for water in a vessel and washed his hands three times"," then washed his face three times"," then washed his forearms three times"," then wiped his head"," inserting his two index fingers into his ears"," and wiped with his thumbs on the outer part of his ears"," and with the index fingers on the inner part of his ears"," then washed his feet three times each"," then he said: \""This is the wuḍūʾ. Whoever adds to this or decreases from it has done wrong and oppressed"," or oppressed and done wrong.\""\n\n(Q) His saying \""decreased\"" (naqaṣa) may refer to a deficiency in the limb. And his saying \""oppressed\"" (ẓalama) means he exceeded the limit. And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan"," without his saying \""or decreased\""]"""
"374","(375) Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, saying: Yūnus ibn Muḥammad narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Kāmil ibn Khalaf al-Qāḍī in Baghdād narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj al-Azraq narrated to us, saying: Yūnus ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr, from ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd: that the Prophet ﷺ performed wuḍūʾ washing each part twice. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿĪsā, from Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 157]"
"375","(386) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubbāb narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thābit ibn Thawbān narrated to us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Faḍl al-Hāshimī narrated, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wuḍūʾ washing each part twice. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 136]"
"376","(377) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, saying: Maʿmar, Sufyān, and Dāwūd ibn Qays narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Shall I not inform you of the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" He said: \""Then he called for a vessel containing water"," and he began scooping one scoop for each limb.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf"," from Sufyān with his chain"," and he said: \""The Prophet ﷺ performed wuḍūʾ washing each part once.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 411]"""
"377","(378) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Muʿallā ibn Asad narrated to us, saying: Wahīb narrated from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿUmārah ibn Abī al-Ḥasan, from his father, who said: I heard ʿAmr ibn Abī al-Ḥasan asking ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd ibn ʿĀṣim about the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So he called for a vessel of water and performed for them the wuḍūʾ of the Prophet ﷺ. He poured water over his hand from the vessel three times, then he placed his hand in the vessel and rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, and blew it out, with three scoops. Then he placed his hand in and washed his face three times. Then he placed his hands in and washed his hands up to the elbows twice. Then he placed his hands in and wiped his head, moving them forward and backward once. Then he washed his feet up to the ankles.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl and others, from Wahīb. And Muslim narrated it from another route from Wahīb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 184]"
"378","(379) Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿArūbah al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī Maʿshar al-Sulamī in Ḥarrān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿd Yaḥyā ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ṣāʾigh in al-Rayy and Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAlūshā in Asadābād Hamadān said: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī al-Jarrāḥī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath said: al-Musayyib ibn Wāḍiḥ narrated to us, saying: Ḥafs ibn Mayssarah narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Prophet ﷺ performed wuḍūʾ washing each part once, then he said: \This is the wuḍūʾ of one whose prayer is not accepted except with it.\"" Then he performed wuḍūʾ washing each part twice"," then he said: \""This is the wuḍūʾ of one whose reward is doubled.\"" Then he performed wuḍūʾ washing each part three times"," then he said: \""This is my wuḍūʾ and the wuḍūʾ of the Messengers before me.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿArūbah. And in the ḥadīth of ʿAbdullāh ibn Sulaymān: \""Allah does not accept his prayer except with it.\"" And he said: \""Allah will double his reward.\""\n\nThis ḥadīth"," from this route"," is narrated uniquely by al-Musayyib ibn Wāḍiḥ. (J) And it is not strong.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from another route from Ibn ʿUmar. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī 1/30]"""
"379","(380) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Khalīl al-Mālinī narrated to us, saying: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abī Suwayd al-Dharraʿ and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām ibn al-Nuʿmān said: Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī narrated to us, saying: Salām al-Ṭawīl narrated from Zayd al-ʿAmmī, from Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Prophet ﷺ called for water and performed wuḍūʾ washing each part once, and said: \This is the wuḍūʾ without which Allah does not accept the prayer.\"" Then he called for water and performed wuḍūʾ washing each part twice"," and said: \""This is the wuḍūʾ of one who is given his reward twice.\"" Then he called for water and performed wuḍūʾ washing each part three times"," and said: \""This is my wuḍūʾ and the wuḍūʾ of the Prophets before me.\"" (T) And similarly it was narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Zayd al-ʿAmmī from his father. Others contradicted them both"," and they are not among the strongest in narration. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 419]"""
"380","(381) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) They said, and Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, saying: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was recited to Ibn Wahb: Mālik ibn Anas informed you from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the Muslim or believing servant performs wuḍūʾ and washes his face"," every sin he looked at with his eyes departs from his face with the water"," or with the last drop of water. When he washes his hands"," every sin his hands committed departs from his hands with the water"," or with the last drop of water. When he washes his feet"," every sin his feet walked toward departs from his feet with the water"," or with the last drop of water"," until he emerges purified from sins.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir"," from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim 244]"""
"381","(382) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us; Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us; Abu al-Walid informed us; 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub and Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad both said: 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Shirawayh informed us; al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-'Azim al-'Anbari informed us; al-Nadr ibn Muhammad informed us; 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar informed us; Shaddad ibn 'Abdullah Abu 'Ammar and Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated from Abu Umamah. He said: 'Amr ibn 'Abasah al-Sulami said, and he mentioned a lengthy hadith concerning his coming to the Prophet (ﷺ) in Makkah and then his coming to him in Madinah. He said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," what is wuḍū'? Tell me about it.\"" He said: \""There is no one among you who brings close his water"," then rinses his mouth and snuffs water into his nose and then blows it out"," except that the sins of his mouth and nostrils depart with the water. Then when he washes his face as Allah has commanded him"," except that the sins of his face depart from the edges of his beard along with the water. Then he washes his hands up to the elbows"," except that the sins of his hands depart from his fingertips along with the water. Then he wipes his head"," except that the sins of his head depart from the ends of his hair along with the water. Then he washes his feet up to the ankles"," except that the sins of his feet depart from his toes along with the water. Then if he stands and prays"," praising Allah"," glorifying Him"," and extolling Him as He deserves"," and devotes his heart wholly to Allah"," he departs from his sin in the same state as the day his mother bore him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Ma'qiri from al-Nadr ibn Muhammad. And in the narration of Abu al-Walid from 'Ikrimah: \""Then he washes his feet up to the ankles as Allah has commanded him.\"" And he did not mention Yahya ibn Abi Kathir in its isnād.\n\n(T) And Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhali from Abu al-Walid"," and used it as evidence for the obligation of washing the feet. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 832.]"""
"382","(383) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr al-Khawlani said: It was recited to 'Abdullah ibn Wahb: Mālik ibn Anas informed you from Zayd ibn Aslam from 'Aṭa' ibn Yasar from 'Abdullah al-Ṣunabihi that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When the servant performs wuḍū' and rinses his mouth"," the sins depart from his mouth. When he blows his nose"," the sins depart from his nose. When he washes his face"," the sins depart from his face until they depart from beneath the edges of his eyelids. When he washes his hands"," the sins depart from his hands until the sins depart from beneath the nails of his hands. When he wipes his head"," the sins depart from his head until they depart from his ears. When he washes his feet"," the sins depart from his feet until the sins depart from beneath the nails of his feet. Then his walking to the mosque and his prayer are a supererogatory merit for him.\""\n\n(C) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; he said: I heard Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub say: I heard al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri say: I heard Yahya ibn Ma'in say: 'Abdullah al-Ṣunabihi narrates from 'Aṭa' ibn Yasar"," and he is a Companion"," and he is also called Abu 'Abdullah. Al-Ṣunabihi"," the companion of Abu Bakr"," is 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Raḥman ibn 'Usaylah. And al-Ṣunabihi"," the companion of Qays ibn Abi Ḥazim"," is called al-Ṣunabih ibn al-A'sar. Thus said Yahya ibn Ma'in.\n\nAl-Bukhari claimed that Mālik ibn Anas erred in this"," and that he is in fact Abu 'Abdullah 'Abd al-Raḥman ibn 'Usaylah al-Ṣunabihi"," who did not hear from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nThis hadith is mursal"," and 'Abd al-Raḥman is the one who narrated from Abu Bakr al-Ṣiddiq (may Allah be pleased with him). And al-Ṣunabih ibn al-A'sar is a Companion of the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nImam Ahmad said: Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Tarikh from the hadith of Mālik ibn Anas in this manner"," then he said: Ibn Abi Marym followed him"," from Abu Ghassan"," from Zayd.\n\nAnd Ishaq ibn 'Isa ibn al-Ṭabba' narrated it from Mālik"," and said: from al-Ṣunabihi Abu 'Abdullah"," and he used it as evidence along with other narrations he mentioned that the matter is as he said. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 4/349.]"""
"383","(384) Abu al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishran informed us; Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Razzaz informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Ubaidullah informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Ubaid al-Ṭanafisi and Abu Badr Shuja' ibn al-Walid both said: Sulayman ibn Mihran al-A'mash informed us from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Thawban from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Be upright"," though you will never fully enumerate it. And know that the best of…\"" Abu Badr said: \""…the best of your deeds is prayer"," and none maintains wuḍū' except a believer.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in virtue of other narrations. Narrated by Ibn Majah"," 277.]"""
"384","(385) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim, and Abu Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us.\n\nThey said: And Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; it was recited to 'Abdullah ibn Wahb: 'Amr ibn al-Ḥarith informed you that al-Ḥakam ibn 'Abdullah al-Qurashi informed him that Nafi' ibn Jubayr and 'Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah both informed him that Mu'adh ibn 'Abd al-Raḥman informed him from Ḥumran, the freedman of 'Uthman, from 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever performs wuḍū' for prayer and perfects the wuḍū'"," then walks to the obligatory prayer and prays it with the people"," or with the congregation"," or in the mosque"," his sins are forgiven.\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjaj narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abu al-Ṭahir and others from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 232.]"""
"385","(386) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya, Ahmad ibn al-Ḥasan, and Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Raḥman ibn Muhammad ibn Maḥbub al-Dahhan informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) They said: And Abu al-'Abbas informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; it was recited to Ibn Wahb: Mālik ibn Anas informed you from al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Raḥman from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said: \Shall I not inform you of that by which Allah erases sins and by which He raises ranks? Perfecting the wuḍū' under difficult conditions"," the abundance of steps toward the mosques"," and waiting for one prayer after another—that is ribāṭ"," that is ribāṭ"," that is ribāṭ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 251.]"""
"386","(387) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Faḍl ibn Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us; Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari and 'Abd al-Raḥman ibn Bishr al-'Abdi both said: Ma'n ibn 'Isa informed us; Mālik informed us, and he mentioned it in similar fashion.\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjaj narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ishaq ibn Musa. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"387","(388) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu al-Naḍr al-Faqih informed us; Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us; Isma'il ibn Abi Uways said: Mālik informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajanī informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanjī informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik informed us from al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Raḥman from his father from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out to the graveyard and said: \Peace be upon you"," O abode of a believing people. And indeed"," if Allah wills"," we shall join you. I wish I had seen our brothers.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," are we not your brothers?\"" He said: \""Rather"," you are my Companions. Our brothers are those who have not yet come. And I shall be preceding them at the Ḥawḍ.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," how will you recognize those of your Ummah who come after you?\"" He said: \""Tell me"," if a man had horses with white blazes and white markings among entirely black horses"," would he not recognize his horses?\"" They said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Then they will come on the Day of Resurrection with white blazes and white markings from the traces of wuḍū'"," and I shall be preceding them at the Ḥawḍ. Men will be driven away from my Ḥawḍ as a stray camel is driven away. I will call out to them: 'Come! Come! Come!' three times. It will be said: 'They have changed after you.' So I will say: 'Be far! Be far! Be far!'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 249.]"""
"388","(389) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Musa informed us; 'Ali ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Junayd informed us; al-Ansari, meaning Ishaq ibn Musa, informed us; Ma'n informed us; Mālik narrated this hadith.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"389","(390) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Ḥafiz informed us; Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah al-Tamimi informed us; Yazid ibn Harun informed us; Yahya informed us from Musa ibn 'Uqbah from Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd: He accompanied the Prophet (ﷺ) on the evening of 'Arafah until he turned aside into the valley to relieve himself. Usamah began pouring water over him while he performed wuḍū'. Usamah said to him: \Will you not pray"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: \""The prayer is ahead of you.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muhammad ibn Salam from Yazid ibn Harun"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Yahya ibn Sa'id. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 139.]"""
"390","(391) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us; Isma'il ibn Qutaybah informed us; Yahya ibn Yahya informed us; Abu al-Aḥwaṣ informed us from Ash'ath from al-Aswad ibn Hilal from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) one night when he dismounted and relieved himself. Then he came, and I poured water over him from a vessel that I had with me. He performed wuḍū' and wiped over his khuffs.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yahya ibn Yahya, and al-Bukhari narrated it through another chain from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhari, 356.]"
"391","(392) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ḥaywah ibn Shurayḥ narrated to us; Baqiyyah narrated from Baḥīr, meaning ibn Saʿd, from Khālid, meaning ibn Maʿdān, from some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) saw a man performing Ṣalāh while on the back of his foot there was a spot the size of a dirham that the water had not reached. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) commanded him to repeat his Wuḍūʾ and his Ṣalāh.\n\nThus it is in this Ḥadīth, and it is Mursal. It has also been narrated in a connected (Mawṣūl) Ḥadīth. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 175]"
"392","(393) Al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated from Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim that he heard Qatādah ibn Diʿāmah say: Anas informed us that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) having performed Wuḍūʾ, while on his foot there was a spot the size of a fingernail (that had not been washed). The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to him: \Go back and improve your Wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: This Ḥadīth is not well-known"," and no one narrated it from Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim except Ibn Wahb"," meaning through this chain of narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 173]"""
"393","(394) Abū Dāwūd said: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād informed us; Yūnus and Ḥumayd narrated from al-Ḥasan from the Prophet (peace be upon him) with the meaning of the Ḥadīth of Qatādah, and this is Mursal.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: It has also been narrated from Maʿqil ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Jazarī from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir from ʿUmar from the Prophet (peace be upon him) with a similar meaning: \Go back and improve your Wuḍūʾ.\"" He went back and then performed Ṣalāh.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us; Abū al-Faḍl Aḥmad ibn Salamah al-Bazzāz narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Aʿyan narrated to us; Maʿqil narrated it with a similar wording.\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Salamah ibn Shabīb"," meaning from al-Ḥasan"," and Abū Sufyān narrated it from Jābir contrary to what Abū al-Zubayr narrated. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihi. Narrated by Muslim"," 243]"""
"394","(395) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us; Sufyān ibn Muḥammad informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsā narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd al-ʿAdanī narrated from Sufyān, meaning al-Thawrī, from al-Aʿmash from Abū Sufyān from Jābir who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābl (may Allah be pleased with him) saw a man performing Wuḍūʾ, and a spot remained on his foot (unwashed). He said: \Repeat your Wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nAnd from Sufyān"," from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ from Abū Qilābah from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," a similar narration.\n\nIt has been narrated from ʿUmar that which indicates that his command to repeat the Wuḍūʾ was by way of recommendation (istiḥbāb)"," and that what is obligatory is only washing that particular spot. [Ḥasan]"""
"395","(396) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah narrated to us; Hushaym narrated from al-Ḥajjāj and ʿAbd al-Malik from ʿAṭāʾ from ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr al-Laythī that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) saw a man on the back of whose foot there was a spot that the water had not reached. ʿUmar said to him: \Will you attend the Ṣalāh with this Wuḍūʾ?\"" He said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," the cold is severe"," and I have nothing to warm myself.\"" So he (ʿUmar) felt compassion for him after he had intended to reprimand him"," and said to him: \""Wash what you have left of your foot"," and repeat the Ṣalāh.\"" And he ordered a garment (khameeṣah) to be given to him. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/109]"""
"396","(397) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Ḥamm al-Mihrījānī al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad ibn Bishr narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Nāfiʿ that Ibn ʿUmar performed Wuḍūʾ in the marketplace. He washed his hands, his face, and his forearms three times each. Then he entered the mosque and wiped over his leather socks after his Wuḍūʾ had dried, and then he performed Ṣalāh.\n\nThis is Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn ʿUmar, and it is well-known from Qutaybah with this wording.\n\nʿAṭāʾ used to see no harm in separating the acts of Wuḍūʾ, and this is the view of al-Ḥasan and al-Nakhaʿī, and it is the more correct of the two opinions of al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah be pleased with him). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"397","(398) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us; Layth narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sābit narrated from Abī Umāmah, or from the brother of Abī Umāmah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saw people, and on the heels of one of them there was a spot the size of a dirham or the size of a fingernail that the water had not reached. He began saying: \Woe to the heels from the Fire!\""\n\nHe (the narrator) said: One of them would look"," and if he saw a spot on his heel that the water had not reached"," he would repeat his Wuḍūʾ.\n\nIf this is authentic"," then it is something they chose for themselves"," and it may also be interpreted to mean that he repeated the Wuḍūʾ of that particular spot only. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/108]"""
"398","(399) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAnazī narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated, reciting to Mālik, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) when he exited the mosque intending to go to al-Ṣafā, saying: \We begin with what Allah began with.\"" So he began with al-Ṣafā.\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Hishām ibn ʿAlī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Ḥajabī narrated to us; Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad"," and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others from Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 1218]"""
"399","(400) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; al-Firyābī narrated to us. Sulaymān said: And Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; Qabīṣah narrated to us; both said: Sufyān narrated to us from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Begin with what Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," began with: 'Indeed"," al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah.'\"" [Al-Baqarah: 158] [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr"," 1/264]"""
"400","(401) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Shaybānī in Kūfah narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim al-Ghifārī narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us; ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās that a man came to him and said: Should I begin with al-Ṣafā before al-Marwah, or with al-Marwah before al-Ṣafā? Should I perform Ṣalāh before performing Ṭawāf, or perform Ṭawāf before performing Ṣalāh? Should I shave (my head) before slaughtering (the sacrifice), or slaughter before shaving? Ibn ʿAbbās said: Take that from the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, for it is more deserving of being preserved. Allah, the Most High, said: \Indeed"," al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah\"" — so al-Ṣafā comes before al-Marwah. And He"," the Most High"," said: \""And do not shave your heads until the sacrificial animal reaches its place\"" — so slaughtering comes before shaving. And He"," the Most High"," said: \""And purify My House for those who perform Ṭawāf"," those who stand (in prayer)"," and those who bow and prostrate\"" — so Ṭawāf comes before Ṣalāh. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 2/297]"""
"401","(402) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Tamtām narrated to us, Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyān narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir informed us, my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated to us, from Sufyān, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ, from Tamīm ibn Ṭarafah, from ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim, who said:\n\nA man delivered a sermon in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has been guided"," and whoever disobeys them has gone astray.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""What a bad speaker you are! Whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger has indeed gone astray.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Wakīʿ. The ḥadīth of Abū Ḥudhayfah is abridged; he said: \""Get up — what a bad speaker you are!\"" and did not mention what followed.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"," from Wakīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 870.]"""
"402","(403) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us, from Ashʿath ibn Sulaym, from his father, from Masrūq, from ʿĀʾishah, who said:\n\nIndeed, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) loved to begin with the right side in his purification when he performed wuḍūʾ, in his combing when he combed his hair, and in his wearing of shoes when he put them on.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 416.]"
"403","(404) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us, they said: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Ashʿath ibn Sulaym, mentioning it with its isnād: that the Prophet (ﷺ) liked tayammun (beginning with the right) as far as he was able in all his affairs: in his combing, his wearing of shoes, and his wuḍūʾ.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 15582.]"
"404","(405) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Fāmī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū al-Zinbāʿ Rūḥ ibn al-Faraj al-Miṣrī narrated to us, ʿAmr — meaning ibn Khālid — narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\When you put on clothes and when you perform wuḍūʾ"," begin with your right (limbs).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd.]"""
"405","(406) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us, Marwān narrated to us, Ismāʿīl — meaning ibn Abī Khālid — narrated to us, from Ziyād — meaning the freedman of Banī Makhzūm — who said:\n\nA man came to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked him about wuḍūʾ, saying: \Shall I begin with the right or the left?\"" ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) made a sound of derision at him"," then called for water and began with the left before the right.\n\n(T) And it was narrated by Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth"," from Ismāʿīl"," from Ziyād"," who said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""I would not care if I began with the left before the right when I perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nAnd it was narrated by ʿAwf"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn Hind"," who said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""I do not care"," when I have completed my wuḍūʾ"," with which of my limbs I begin.\""\n\n(Q) And it is possible that what he intended by his unrestricted statement in this is what he explained in the narration of Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth"," and Allah knows best. However"," it is munqaṭiʿ (discontinuous).\n\nAḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated it from al-Anṣārī"," from ʿAwf"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn Hind. Then he said: ʿAwf said: \""I did not hear it from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him).\"" [Ḥasan for other than its chain. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/88.]"""
"406","(407) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us, Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us, Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal — narrated to us, Wakīʿ narrated to us, al-Masʿūdī narrated to us, from Abū Baḥr, who said: Our elders from the Hilālīs narrated to us:\n\nIbn Masʿūd was asked about a man who performs wuḍūʾ and begins with his left before his right, and he gave permission for that.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh said: I heard Wakīʿ say: Abū Baḥr al-Hilālī's name is Aḥnaf.\n\n(T) The Shaykh said: And it was narrated by Furāt ibn Aḥnaf, who heard his father, who heard ʿAbd Allāh al-Hilālī, who heard Ibn Masʿūd: \If he wishes"," he may begin his wuḍūʾ with his left.\""\n\nAnd Abū al-ʿUbaydayn narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd that he was asked about a man who performed wuḍūʾ and began with his left"," and he said: \""There is no harm.\""\n\nAnd Sulaymān ibn Mūsā narrated from Mujāhid"," who said: ʿAbd Allāh said: \""There is no harm in beginning with your feet before your hands.\""\n\nAl-Dāraquṭnī said: This is mursal and is not established. (J) And this is because Mujāhid did not meet ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd. [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"407","(408) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, they said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr, from his father, who said:\n\nIn the letter of the Prophet (ﷺ) to ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm was: \That one should not touch the Qurʾān except in a state of purity.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ for other than its chain. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/121.]"""
"408","(409) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn Sahl al-Faqīh in Bukhārā informed us, Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us, from Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (ﷺ):\n\nThat he wrote to the people of Yemen a book containing the obligatory duties, the sunnah practices, and the blood-money compensations, and he sent it with ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm. He mentioned the ḥadīth, and in it was: \And none should touch the Qurʾān except one who is pure.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ for other than its chain. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/121.]"""
"409","(410) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad — meaning ibn Thawwāb — narrated to us, Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, who said: I heard Sālim narrating from his father, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said:\n\n\None should touch the Qurʾān except one who is in a state of purity.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ for other than its chain. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī"," 1/322.]"""
"410","(411) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad — meaning ibn Thawwāb — narrated to us, Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, who said: I heard Sālim narrating from his father, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said:\n\n\None should touch the Qurʾān except one who is in a state of purity.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"," 59.]"""
"411","(412) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūnus al-Ḍabbī narrated to us that Abū Badr Shujaʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated from al-Aʿmash.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us that al-Ḥasānī narrated to us that Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, who said: We were with Salmān when he went out to relieve himself. He then came back, and I said: \O Abā ʿAbdillāh"," if only you would perform wuḍūʾ so that perhaps we might ask you about certain verses.\"" He said: \""I have not touched it [the private part]; indeed"," none touches it except the purified ones.\"" Then he recited to us whatever we wished.\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Wakīʿ. Thus did a group narrate it from al-Aʿmash.\n\n(T) And Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated it in one of the two transmissions from him"," from al-Aʿmash"," from Ibrāhīm"," from ʿAlqamah"," from Salmān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 1/292]"""
"412","(413) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī al-Razzāz narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, meaning Ibn al-Munādī, narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf, meaning al-Azraq, narrated to us that al-Qāsim ibn ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: ʿUmar went out with his sword strapped [to his side]. He then mentioned the ḥadīth, in which it is stated: It was said to him: \Your brother-in-law and your sister have turned apostate and abandoned the religion upon which you are.\"" So ʿUmar walked until he came to them"," and with them was a man from the Muhājirūn called Khabbāb"," and they were reciting Ṭā Hā. ʿUmar said: \""Give me the book that is with you so that I may recite it.\"" ʿUmar used to recite the Book. His sister said: \""You are indeed impure; indeed"," none touches it except the purified ones. So rise and perform ghusl or wuḍūʾ.\"" ʿUmar stood"," performed wuḍūʾ"," then took the book and recited Ṭā Hā. This ḥadīth has many corroborating narrations.\n\n(Q) And it is the statement of the seven jurists of the people of Madīnah. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/133]"""
"413","(414) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdak al-Qazzāz narrated to us that Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Shuʿbah said: ʿAmr ibn Murrah narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: I entered upon ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālliib, may Allah be pleased with him, along with two men—one from my people and the other I think from Banī Asad. He sent them on a mission and said: \You are both strong men"," so stand firm for your religion.\"" Then he entered the privy and relieved himself. He then came out"," took a handful of water"," wiped himself with it"," and began recurring the Qurʾān. It was as though he saw that we found that objectionable"," so he said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to relieve himself and then recurr the Qurʾān"," and eat meat with us"," and nothing prevented him\""—and he sometimes said \""nothing withheld him\""—\""from the Qurʾān except janābah.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the book of Sunan from Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar from Shuʿbah. Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," mentioning it with the same meaning. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 229]"""
"414","(415) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb narrated to us. And Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Ibn Lahīʿah informed you from ʿAbdullāh ibn Sulaymān from Thaʿlabah ibn Abī al-Kanūd from ʿAbdullāh ibn Mālik al-Ghāfiqī that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb: \When I perform wuḍūʾ while in a state of janābah"," I eat and drink"," but I do not pray nor recurr [the Qurʾān] until I perform ghusl.\""\n\n(Q) Ibn Wahb said: And Mālik ibn Anas and al-Layth ibn Saʿd told me the same"," meaning from their own statement.\n\n(T) The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: And al-Wāqidī narrated it from ʿAbdullāh ibn Sulaymān thus. [Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/119]"""
"415","(416) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that Ayyūb ibn Suwayd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Wāʾil, that ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, disliked that one in a state of janābah should recurr the Qurʾān.\n\n(T) And others narrated it from al-Thawrī, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Wāʾil, from ʿUbaydah, from ʿUmar, and this is the correct version. [Ḥasan for other than it. Narrated by al-Dārimī, 992]"
"416","(417) And ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrawayh narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥayy narrated from ʿĀmir ibn al-Simṭ from Abī al-Gharīf from ʿAlī regarding the person in a state of janābah; he said: \He does not recurr"," not even a letter.\""\n\n(T) And Abū Isḥāq narrated from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī"," who said: \""Recurr the Qurʾān in every state"," so long as you are not in a state of janābah.\""\n\n(Q) And this is the statement of al-Ḥasan"," al-Nakhaʿī"," al-Zuhrī"," and Qatādah.\n\nIt is narrated that Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""There is no harm in the person in a state of janābah recurrning a verse or the like.\"" And it is narrated from him that he said: \""A verse or two verses.\"" Those who opposed him are more numerous"," and among them are two Imams"," and with them is the apparent meaning of the report. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"417","(418) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿUmar ibn Burhān and Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us, saying: Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \The person in a state of janābah and the menstruating woman do not recurr anything of the Qurʾān.\""\n\n(J) Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī said"," as it has reached me from him: \""This was only narrated by Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah"," and I do not know it from anyone else. And Ismāʿīl is munkar al-ḥadīth with respect to the people of the Ḥijāz and the people of al-ʿIrāq.\""\n\n(T) The Shaykh said: And it has been narrated from others besides him from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah"," but it is not ṣaḥīḥ.\n\nAnd it is narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh as his own statement regarding the person in a state of janābah"," the menstruating woman"," and the woman in postpartum bleeding"," but it is not strong. [Munkar. Narrated by Ibn Mājah"," 596]"""
"418","(419) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Bayhaqī informed us that Abū Aḥmad al-Ghiṭrīfī informed us that Abū Khalīfah narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam from Ibrāhīm that ʿUmar used to dislike that the person in a state of janābah should recurr [the Qurʾān].\n\nShuʿbah said: \I found in my notebook: 'and the menstruating woman","' and this is mursal.\"" [Ḥasan for other than it]"""
"419","(420) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: I read to Mālik from Makhrah ibn Sulaymān from Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, that Ibn ʿAbbās informed him: He spent a night at Maymūnah, the Mother of the Believers, who was his maternal aunt. He said: \I lay down across the cushion"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his family lay down along its length. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until when half the night had passed"," or a little before that or a little after that"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ awoke and began wiping the sleep from his face with his hand. Then he recited the last ten verses"," the concluding verses"," of Sūrat Āl ʿImrān. Then he stood up to a hanging waterskin and performed wuḍūʾ from it"," performing his wuḍūʾ excellently"," then he stood and prayed.\"" And he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways from Mālik.\n\n(T) And it has been narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās from his father from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: \""I saw him stand"," use the siwāk"," then perform wuḍūʾ while recurrning these verses: {Indeed"," in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of the night and the day are signs for those of understanding} [Āl ʿImrān: 190]"," until he completed the sūrah. And Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 181]"""
"420","(421) Abū Aḥmad ibn Mahrūyah al-ʿAdl informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Mālik narrated from Ayyūb ibn Abī Tamīmah al-Sakhtiyānī from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, was among a group of people while he was recurrning. He stood to relieve himself, then returned while recurrning. A man said to him: \You have not performed wuḍūʾ"," O Commander of the Faithful"," and you are recurrning.\"" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Who issued you a fatwā regarding this? Musaylamah?\""\n\n(T) And Hishām narrated it from Ibn Sīrīn from Abī Maryam Iyās ibn Ḍubayḥ"," who said: \""I was with ʿUmar","\"" and he mentioned the same meaning.\n\nAnd al-Bukhārī mentioned it in al-Tārīkh. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Mālik"," 470]"""
"421","(422) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, al-Aʿmash narrated from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, who said: We were with Salmān on a journey. He went away to relieve himself, then came back. We said to him: \O Abā ʿAbd Allāh"," perform wuḍūʾ so that we may ask you about a verse from the Qurʾān.\"" He said: \""Ask"," for I have not touched it"," and indeed it is not touched except by those who are purified (al-muṭahharūn).\"" So we asked him"," and he recited to us before performing wuḍūʾ. [Weak]"""
"422","(423) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī al-Harawī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated from ʿĀmir ibn al-Simṭ, from Abī al-Gharīf, who said: ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) said: \There is no harm in reciting the Qurʾān while you are not in a state of wuḍūʾ"," but as for when you are in a state of janābah"," then no — not even a single letter.\"" [Weak]"""
"423","(424) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, Ayyūb ibn Suwayd narrated to us, saying: Sufyān narrated to me from Sulaymān ibn Abī al-Jahm, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: Ibn ʿUmar and Ibn ʿAbbās used to say: \Indeed"," we would recite a portion of the Qurʾān after having committed a minor impurity (ḥadath).\""\n\n(T) ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAdanī narrated it from Sufyān"," from Salamah ibn Kuhayl"," from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr. [Hasan in virtue of corroborating chains. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 1316]"""
"424","(425) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿUrubah narrated to us, Abū Kurayb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated from his father, from Khālid ibn Salamah, from al-Bahiyy, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) would remember Allah at all times. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim, 117]"
"425","(426) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, Saʿīd informed us from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Ḥuḍayn ibn al-Mundhir, Abī Sāsān, from al-Muhājir ibn Qunfudh, that he greeted the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was performing wuḍūʾ, and he did not return the greeting. When he finished his wuḍūʾ, he said: \Nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I disliked mentioning Allah except in a state of purity (ṭahārah).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in virtue of corroborating chains. Narrated by Ibn Mājah"," 350]"""
"426","(427) Abū Saʿīd Sharīk ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, al-Layth narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he said: A man does not prostrate except in a state of purity, and he does not recite except in a state of purity, and he does not offer the funeral prayer except in a state of purity. Mawqūf. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"427","(428) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation, Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated to us in Makkah, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī, from Abī Ayyūb al-Anṣārī, who said: \Do not face the qiblah for defecation or urination"," and do not turn your back towards it.\"" On another occasion he said"," narrating it as marfūʿ"," reaching back to the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 21]"""
"428","(429) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Muslim narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī and al-Ramādī — meaning Ibrāhīm ibn Bashshār — both said: Sufyān narrated to us, mentioning it with his chain, and he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, and he added in it: \But face east or west.\"" Abū Ayyūb said: \""We arrived in al-Shām and found latrines that had been built facing the qiblah"," so we would turn away from them and seek forgiveness from Allah"," the Most High.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others"," all of them from Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 386]"""
"429","(430) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr and Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī both narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Abū Muʿāwiyah informed us from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, from Salmān, who said: It was said to him: \Your Prophet (ﷺ) has taught you everything"," even the matter of defecation.\"" He said: \""Yes"," indeed. He forbade us from facing the qiblah for defecation or urination"," and from cleaning ourselves (istinjāʾ) with the right hand"," or with fewer than three stones"," or with dung (rajīʿ) or a bone.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 262]"""
"430","(431) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ in Naysābūr and Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Shādhān in Baghdād both informed us, saying: Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us, ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from al-Qaʿqāʿ ibn Ḥakīm, from Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am to you like a father. When one of you goes to relieve himself"," let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back towards it. And when he cleans himself (istiṭābah)"," let him not clean with his right hand.\"" And he used to command the use of three stones and prohibit the use of dung (ruthth) and bones (rimmah). [Ṣaḥīḥ in virtue of corroborating chains. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 8]"""
"431","(432) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Ibn ʿAjlān; he said: al-Qaʿqāʿ ibn Ḥakīm narrated to me from Abū Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \I am to you like a father; I teach you. So when one of you goes to the privy"," let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back toward it"," and let him not cleanse himself with his right hand.\"" And he ﷺ used to command the use of three stones and would forbid the use of dung and decayed bones. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 40]"""
"432","(433) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, and he mentioned it with his chain of narration, except that he did not say \I teach you.\"" He said: \""So when one of you goes to relieve himself"," let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back toward it"," whether for stool or urine"," and let him cleanse himself with three stones.\"" And he ﷺ forbade the use of dung and decayed bones. Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ from his father"," in abridged form. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 2/247]"""
"433","(434) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Tamtām narrated to us; Mūsā, meaning Ibn Ismāʿīl, narrated to us; Wuhaib narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā narrated from Abū Zayd from Maʿqil ibn Abī Maʿqil al-Asadī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade facing either of the two qiblahs with urine or stool. Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated… and he mentioned it similarly. Abū Dāwūd said: He is Abū Zayd, a freedman of Banī Thaʿlabah. [Munkar. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 10]"
"434","(435) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān from his uncle Wāsiʿ ibn Ḥabbān from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who used to say: Some people say, \When you sit to relieve yourself"," do not face the qiblah or Bayt al-Maqdis.\"" ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: \""I climbed upon the roof of our house and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on two bricks"," facing Bayt al-Maqdis for his need.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 145]"""
"435","(436) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ghālib informed us; ʿAbd Allāh, meaning al-Qaʿnabī, narrated from Mālik, and he mentioned it with his chain of narration, similarly. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"436","(437) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūq informed us by dictation; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Yaḥyā informed that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān informed him that his uncle Wāsiʿ ibn Ḥabbān informed him; he said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: \One day I climbed upon the roof of our house and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting on two bricks for his need"," facing al-Shām and turning his back toward the qiblah.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaʿqūb al-Dawraqī from Yazīd ibn Hārūn"," and Muslim narrated it from another source from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 145]"""
"437","(438) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Bakkār ibn Qutaybah al-Qāḍī in Egypt narrated to us; Ṣafwān ibn ʿĪsā narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn Dhakwān from Marwān al-Aṣfar, who said: \I saw Ibn ʿUmar make his mount kneel facing the qiblah"," then he sat urinating toward it. I said: 'O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," has this not been forbidden?' He said: 'Yes"," but that was forbidden only in open terrain. If there is something between you and the qiblah that screens you"," then there is no harm.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 11]"""
"438","(439) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed him; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Fāris narrated to us; Ṣafwān ibn ʿĪsā… and he mentioned it similarly. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 11]"
"439","(440) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us. And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — and the wording is his — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm al-Bazzāz narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Shawkar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us; my father narrated from Ibn Isḥāq; he said: Abān ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me from Mujāhid from Jābir, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had forbidden us to face the qiblah or turn our backs toward it with our private parts when we discharge water (i.e."," urinate). Then I saw him"," a year before his death"," urinating while facing the qiblah.\"" In the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbd Allāh"," the phrase \""a year\"" is not present"," and the rest carries the same meaning. Abū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from the ḥadīth of Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim from Ibn Isḥāq"," and in it: \""I saw him"," before he was taken in death"," a year prior"," facing it.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 11]"""
"440","(441) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us; Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ narrated from Khālid ibn Abī al-Ṣalt, who said: \I was in the presence of ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz during his caliphate"," and ʿIrbāk ibn Mālik was with him. ʿUmar said: 'I have not faced the qiblah nor turned my back toward it for urine or stool since such and such time.' ʿIrbāk said: ʿĀʾishah"," the Mother of the Believers"," may Allah be pleased with her"," narrated to me that when the talk of the people regarding this reached the Messenger of Allah ￺"," he ordered his seat (i.e."," the place where he sat) to be positioned so that it faced the qiblah.\"" Ḥammād ibn Salamah followed it up from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ in establishing its chain of narration. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated it from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ from a man from ʿIrbāk ibn Mālik from ʿĀʾishah. And Abū ʿAwanah and others narrated it from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ from ʿIrbāk from ʿĀʾishah. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 6/184]"""
"441","(442) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us — he came to us in Qaṣabat Khusrawjird. Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdiyy informed us: Abū ʿAbd al-Malik Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid in Ṣūr narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Kaʿb al-Ḥalabī narrated to us: Ḥātim narrated to us from ʿĪsā al-Ḥannāṭ, who said: I said to al-Shaʿbī, \I am astonished by the difference between Abū Hurayrah and Ibn ʿUmar.\"" Nāfiʿ narrated from Ibn ʿUmar: \""I entered the house of Ḥafṣah"," and a glance chanced upon me"," and I saw the latrine of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) facing the qiblah.\"" And Abū Hurayrah said: \""When any one of you goes to relieve himself"," let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back toward it.\"" Al-Shaʿbī said: \""Both spoke the truth. As for the statement of Abū Hurayrah"," it pertains to the open desert — for indeed Allah has angels and jinn who pray"," so let no one face them with urine or excrement"," nor turn his back toward them. As for their latrines"," these are merely structures built in which there is no qiblah.\"" (T) And thus Mūsā ibn Dāwūd and others narrated it from Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl. (J) However"," this ʿĪsā ibn Abī ʿĪsā al-Ḥannāṭ is ʿĪsā ibn Mayṣarah"," and he is weak. [Weak]"""
"442","(443) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr informed me from Abū Salamah, from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, who said: \I was with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on one of his journeys"," and when he went to relieve himself"," he would go far away.\"" [Sahih in other than this chain. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (1)]"""
"443","(444) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbd al-Malik, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: \I went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) intended to relieve himself"," he would go far away until no one could see him. We stopped at a barren tract of land in which there was no landmark and no tree. He said to me"," 'O Jābir"," take the water vessel and set out with us.' I filled the water vessel with water"," and we set out on foot until we were almost out of sight. Then there were two trees with a space between them of about a forearm's length. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," 'O Jābir"," go and say to this tree: \""The Messenger of Allah tells you to join your companion so that I may sit behind you both.\""' I did as he said"," and the tree trembled until it joined its companion. He sat behind them until he had relieved himself.\"" (T) And the hadith of going far away has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar and from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Qurād from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its supporting narrations were narrated by al-Dārimī (17)]"""
"444","(445) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us from Abū al-Tayyāḥ, from a man, who said: \When Ibn ʿAbbās arrived in Baṣrah"," he heard the people of Baṣrah relating from Abū Mūsā from the Prophet (ﷺ) certain hadiths"," so he wrote to Abū Mūsā asking him about them. Abū Mūsā wrote to him: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was walking when he veered to one side and sat beside a wall and urinated. He said"," \""Indeed"," the Children of Israel"," when one of them urinated and the urine touched his body"," they would cut it off with scissors. So when any one of you wishes to urinate"," let him seek a soft spot for his urine.\""'\"" Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated it from Abū al-Tayyāḥ"," who said in the hadith: \""He came to a soft spot at the base of a wall"," then urinated"," and then said"," 'When any one of you wishes to urinate"," let him seek a soft spot for his urine.'\"" Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us: Ḥammād narrated it with the same meaning. [Weak. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (3)]"""
"445","(446) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʿ informed us: Mahdī ibn Maymūn informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Yaʿqūb narrated to us from al-Ḥasan ibn Saʿd, the mawlā of al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mounted me behind him one day and confided to me a hadith which I would not relate to anyone among the people. And the most beloved means of concealment the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used for his need was a raised mound or a palm grove — that is"," a walled garden of palm trees.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (242)]"""
"446","(447) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Adamī in Baghdād narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ziyād ibn Mihrān al-Simsār narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf narrated to us: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us from Yaʿqūb ibn Mujāhid Abī Ḥazrah, from ʿUbadah ibn al-Walīd ibn ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who said: \We visited Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh in his mosque"," and he related a story"," and Jābir said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went to relieve himself"," and I followed him with a vessel of water. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) looked around and saw nothing by which he could conceal himself. Then there were two trees on the bank of the valley. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went to one of them and took hold of one of its branches and said"," \""Submit to me"," by the permission of Allah"," the Most High.\"" It submitted to him like a docile camel that yields to its driver"," until he came to the other tree. He took hold of one of its branches and said"," \""Submit to me"," by the permission of Allah"," the Most High.\"" It likewise submitted to him. When he was midway between them"," he brought them together — that is"," he joined them — and said"," \""Come together over me"," by the permission of Allah"," the Most High.\"" They came together.\"" Jābir said: \""I sat talking to myself"," and a glance chanced from me"," and suddenly I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) approaching"," and the two trees had separated"," each one standing on its own trunk.\"" And he mentioned the rest of the hadith. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (2/3)]"""
"447","(448) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Mihrajānī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnūs and ʿAmr ibn al-Walīd both said: Thawr ibn Yazīd narrated to us from Ḥuṣayn al-Ḥubrānī, from Abū Saʿd al-Khayr, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever goes to relieve himself should conceal himself. If he finds nothing except a mound of sand"," he should gather it and then turn his back toward it"," for indeed the devils play with the posterity of Adam. Whoever does so has done well"," and whoever does not"," there is no blame upon him.\"" [Weak. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (35)]"""
"448","(449) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed us: Hudbah ibn Khālid narrated to us: Hammām narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī — may Allah, the Most High, have mercy on him — informed us by dictation: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Saʿd al-Nasawī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Fahd informed us: Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl informed us: Hammām, the companion of al-Baṣrī, narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhrī, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he entered the privy, would remove his ring. The wording is that of Ḥajjāj's hadith. And in the hadith of Hudbah ibn Khālid, he said: \And I do not know it except from al-Zuhrī"," from Anas.\"" [Munkar. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (19)]"""
"449","(450) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us. He said: Abū Dāwūd said, \This is a munkar hadith. It is only known from Ibn Jurayj"," from Ziyād ibn Saʿd"," from al-Zuhrī"," from Anas"," that the Prophet (ﷺ) had a ring made of silver and then discarded it.\"" The Shaykh said: \""This is the well-known narration from Ibn Jurayj"," not the hadith of Hammām.\"""""
"450","(451) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh informed us: ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Kaʿb al-Anṭākī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Baṣrī narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhrī, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wore a ring inscribed with \Muḥammad Rasūlullāh","\"" and when he entered the privy"," he would remove it. And this is a weak witness. And Allah knows best. [Weak. Al-Ḥākim narrated it (1/398)]"""
"451","(452) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Mūsā narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī informed me; Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: When the Prophet (ﷺ) entered the privy, he would say: \O Allah"," I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils (al-khubth wa al-khabāʾith).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: Mūsā said on the authority of Ḥammād"," and he mentioned it. Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. Al-Bukhārī said: And Ghundar said on the authority of Shuʿbah from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz: \""When he came to the privy.\""\n\nAnd Saʿīd ibn Zayd said on the authority of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz: \""When he intended to enter.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 142.]"""
"452","(453) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunayn narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he intended to go to the privy, would say: \I seek refuge in Allah from the male and female devils (al-khubth wa al-khabāʾith).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 375.]"""
"453","(454) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Qatāda from al-Naḍr ibn Anas from Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," these privies are frequented by devils. So when one of you comes to the privy"," let him say: 'I seek refuge in Allah from the male and female devils (al-khubth wa al-khabāʾith).'\""\n\n(T) And thus Maʿmar narrated it from Qatāda.\n\nAnd likewise Ibn ʿUlayya and Abū al-Jamāhir narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūba from Qatāda. And Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ and a group narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūba from Qatāda from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAwf al-Shaybānī from Zayd ibn Arqam.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: I asked Muḥammad"," meaning al-Bukhārī"," \""Which narration is most authentic in your view?\"" He said: \""Perhaps Qatāda heard from both of them together from Zayd ibn Arqam","\"" and he did not give a definitive ruling on this.\n\nImām Aḥmad said"," and it was narrated from Maʿmar from Qatāda from al-Naḍr ibn Anas from Anas"," and this is an error (wahm).\n\n(Gh) Abū Sulaymān said: \""Al-khubth\"" with a ḍamma on the bāʾ is the collective form of \""al-khabīth","\"" and \""al-khabāʾith\"" is the plural of \""al-khabītha","\"" meaning the male and female devils. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd.]"""
"454","(455) ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī al-Muʾadhdhin informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn Ḥamdān al-Ṣayrafī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yūnus al-Qurashī narrated to us; Khālid ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Sufyān al-Thawrī from Hishām ibn ʿUrwa from his father from ʿĀʾisha, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) used to cover his head when he entered the privy, and he also used to cover his head when he came to his family.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This hadith is one of the things for which Muḥammad ibn Yūnus al-Kudaymī has been criticized.\n\n(J) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us regarding this hadith: \I do not know anyone other than al-Kudaymī who narrated it with this chain"," and al-Kudaymī is too prominent a figure for his weakness to need to be demonstrated.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: The covering of the head upon entering the privy has also been narrated from Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq"," and it is authentic from him. It has also been narrated from Ḥabīb ibn Ṣāliḥ from the Prophet (ﷺ) as a mursal narration. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Nuʿaym in al-Ḥilya"," 2/182.]"""
"455","(456) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us by ijāza; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣibghī informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutayba narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Ḥabīb ibn Ṣāliḥ, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he entered the privy, would put on his shoes and cover his head. [Ḍaʿīf.]"
"456","(457) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me by ijāza; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from Rabīʿa from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from a man from Banī Mudlij from his father, who said: Surāqa ibn Juʿshum came to us and said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) taught us that when one of us enters the privy, he should lean on his left foot and keep his right foot upright. [Ḍaʿīf.]"
"457","(458) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsa narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash from a man from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet (ﷺ), when he needed to relieve himself, would not raise his garment until he drew close to the ground.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb narrated it from al-Aʿmash from Anas ibn Mālik."
"458","(459) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr al-ʿAdl narrated to us; Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad al-Rāzī narrated to us; Sahl ibn Naṣr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, and he mentioned it with the same meaning as Abū Dāwūd, except that he said: \Until he reached the ground.\""\n\n(T) And ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated it from ʿAbd al-Salām"," saying: \""Until he drew close to the ground.\"" [Ḥasan through other chains.]"""
"459","(460) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Khusrūjirdī informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Muslim, from the original of his book, narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Rajāʾ al-Miṣṣīṣī, a venerable shaykh, narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he intended to relieve himself, would move away and would not raise his garments until he drew close to the ground."
"460","(461) Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Ṭalq ibn Ghannām narrated to us; Isrāʾīl ibn Yūnus ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated from Yūsuf ibn Abī Burda from his father from ʿĀʾisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he came out from relieving himself, would say: \Ghufraṇaka\"" (Your forgiveness). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 30.]"""
"461","(462) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — who is al-Aṣamm — narrated to us; he said: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; he said: Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us; he said: Isrāʾīl ibn Yūnus narrated it in the same manner. [Ḥasan. Al-Ḥākim narrated it, 1/261]"
"462","(463) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī in Marw informed us; he said: Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us; he said: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us; he said: Isrāʾīl ibn Yūnus narrated it in a similar manner. And he mentioned therein the hearing of Abū Burdah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). [Ḥasan. Al-Ḥākim narrated it, 1/261]"
"463","(464) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; he said: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr narrated to us; he said: Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated to us; he said: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us; he said: Isrāʾīl narrated it in a similar manner. [Ḥasan. Al-Ḥākim narrated it, 1/261]"
"464","(465) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us; he said: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us; he said: Abū Mūsā Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; he said: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated it with its chain of narration and added upon it: \Ghufraānaka Rabbanā wa ilayka al-maṣīr\"" (Your forgiveness"," our Lord"," and to You is the return).\n\nIbn Khuzaymah said: And Muḥammad ibn Aslam informed us; he said: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us from Isrāʾīl with this same chain of narration"," similar to it.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This addition in this hadith I did not find except in the narration of Ibn Khuzaymah"," and he is an imam. However"," I saw it in an old copy of the book of Ibn Khuzaymah in which this addition was not present; then it was appended in the margin in another handwriting. Thus"," it is most likely that it was appended to his book without his knowledge. And Allah knows best.\n\nAnd the Imam Abū ʿUthmān al-Ṣābūnī informed us; he said: Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us; he said: My grandfather narrated it to us without this addition. Thus"," the falsity of this addition in the hadith was confirmed by that."""
"465","(466) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ in Naysābūr and Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Bazzāz in Baghdād informed us; both said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Fākihī in Makkah informed us; he said: Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrah narrated to us; he said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to us; he said: al-Layth narrated—\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me; he said: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Imām narrated to us; he said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; he said: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he forbade urinating in stagnant water.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it, 281]"
"466","(467) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī (may Allah, the Most High, have mercy upon him) informed us by dictation; he said: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Ibrāhīh ibn Bālawayh al-Muzakkī narrated to us; he said: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; he said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; he said: Maʿmar narrated from Hammām ibn Munabbih; he said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Let no one urinate in stagnant water that does not flow"," and then perform ghusl from it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 282]"""
"467","(468) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; he said: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; he said: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; he said: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; he said: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from his father from Abī Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Beware of the two things that bring curses.\"" They said: \""And what are the two things that bring curses"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""The one who relieves himself in the pathway of the people or in their shade.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Ḥasan. Muslim narrated it"," 269]"""
"468","(469) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us; he said: My grandfather narrated to us; he said: Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; he said: Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd informed me; he said: Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ informed me that Abū Saʿīd al-Ḥimyarī narrated to him from Muʿādh ibn Jabal; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Beware of the three things that bring curses: defecating at the water sources"," in the middle of the road"," and in the shade.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 26]"""
"469","(470) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; he said: Abū al-Muthannā informed us; he said: Kāmil ibn Ṭalḥah narrated to us; he said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Anṣārī narrated to us; he said: Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated to us; he said: A man said to Abū Hurayrah: \You have given us fatwā on everything"," until you are about to give us fatwā on excrement.\"" Abū Hurayrah said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Whoever aims his blade at a frequented pathway of the pathways of the Muslims"," upon him is the curse of Allah"," the angels"," and all of mankind.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 1/296]"""
"470","(471) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; he said: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; he said: ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us; he said: Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us; he said: Hiql narrated to us; he said: al-Awzāʿī narrated from Ḥassān ibn ʬāṭiyyah; he said: \It is disliked for a man to urinate in open air"," and to defecate atop a mountain as though he were a bird alighting.\""\n\nThis is how the narration is from al-Awzāʿī. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"471","(472) It has been narrated by Yūsuf ibn al-Safar — and he is abandoned (matrūk) — from al-Awzāʿī, from Yaḥyā, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked urinating in open space.\n\nAbū Saʿd narrated to us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdiyy narrated to us, Ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿImrān narrated to us, Yūsuf narrated it with its chain of narration. Abū Aḥmad said: It is fabricated (mawḍūʿ). [Bāṭil (False)]"
"472","(473) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, my father narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar informed me, Ashʿath informed me, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Mughaffal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \None of you should urinate in his place of bathing and then perform ghusl or wuḍūʾ in it"," for indeed the majority of waswās (devilish whisperings) comes from it.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd recorded it in the Sunan from Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 27]"""
"473","(474) It was narrated to us by Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal and al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī both said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, and he mentioned it, except that in the ḥadīth of al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī he said: from Ashʿath ibn ʿAbdillāh.\n\n(b) And it has reached me from Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī that he said: This ḥadīth is not known except from this chain. And it is said that this Ashʿath is Ibn Jābir al-Ḥuddānī. And Maʿmar narrated, saying: Ashʿath ibn ʿAbdillāh from al-Ḥasan. The Shaykh said: And it is also said that he is Ashʿath ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Jābir, and al-Bukhārī mentioned him in al-Tārīkh. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 27]"
"474","(475) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʔbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Tamtām — Muḥammad ibn Ghālib — narrated to us, Abū ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Qatādah narrated to us, from Saʿīd, from al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Mughaffal: that he used to dislike urinating in the place of bathing and said: \Indeed"," from it comes the waswās (devilish whisperings).\"" This is how Yazīd ibn Ibrāhīm al-Tustarī narrated it. [Weak]"""
"475","(476) Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from ʿUqbah ibn Ṣuhbān, from Ibn Mughaffal, who said: He was forbidden — or rebuked — from urinating in the place of bathing.\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us, Saʿīd narrated it with something similar to it. [Ṣaḥīh through other chains]"
"476","(477) Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah that he heard ʿUqbah ibn Ṣuhbān from ʿAbdullāh ibn Mughaffal: that he was asked about a man who urinates in his place of bathing. He said: \The waswās (devilish whisperings) is feared from it.\""\n\nIt was narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miqrīʾ al-Mihrājānī"," al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us"," Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us"," ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us"," Shuʿbah narrated it. [Ṣaḥīh]"""
"477","(478) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Dāwūd ibn ʿAbdillāh, from Ḥumayr al-Ḥimyarī — and he is Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — who said: I met a man who accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) just as Abū Hurayrah accompanied him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that any of us should comb his hair every day or urinate in his place of bathing. [Ṣaḥīh. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 28]"
"478","(479) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Zakariyyā — Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī — narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm, ʿUbaydullāh ibn Saʿīd, Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā, Muḥammad ibn Bashshār, ʿAbbās al-ʿAnbarī, and Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr narrated to us. Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm said: \He informed us","\"" and the others said: \""He narrated to us.\"" Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us"," he said: My father narrated to me"," from Qatādah"," from ʿAbdullāh ibn Sarjis"," that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""None of you should urinate in a hole. And when you sleep"," extinguish the lamps"," for indeed the mouse may take the wick and burn down the household. And tie up the waterskins"," cover the vessels"," and close the doors.\""\n\nIt was said to Qatādah: \""What is disliked about urinating in a hole?\"" He said: \""They are the dwellings of the jinn.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 29]"""
"479","(480) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, Azhar ibn Saʿd al-Sammān narrated to us, from Ibn ʿAwn, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, who said: It was said to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her): \They say that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) made a bequest to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him).\"" She said: \""What bequest did he make to ʿAlī? I saw him call for a basin to urinate in it"," while I was supporting him against his chest. Then he bent over — or she said"," 'I bent over' — and he passed away"," and I did not notice. So what do these people mean when they say he made a bequest to ʿAlī?\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdillāh ibn Muḥammad"," from Azhar. And Muslim narrated it through another chain from Ibn ʿAwn. And this Ibrāhīm is said to be Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd ibn Sharīk al-Taymī. [Ṣaḥīh. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 4190]"""
"480","(481) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl the jurist in Rayy — narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj al-Azraq narrated to us, Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ḥikmah bint Umaymah bint Ruqayqah, from her mother, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had a vessel of wood beneath his bed in which he would urinate at night. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 24]"
"481","(482) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; al-Firyābī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from al-Ḍaḥḥābk ibn ʿUthmān from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that a man greeted the Prophet ﷺ while he was urinating, and he did not return the greeting.\n\nIt is recorded in the book of Muslim from the ḥadīth of al-Thawrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim, 115]"
"482","(483) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Mayṣarah informed us; Ibn Mahdī narrated to us; ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Hilāl ibn ʿIyāḍ; Abū Saʿīd narrated to me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \Two men should not go out to relieve themselves"," exposing their nakedness while conversing with one another"," for Allah"," the Most High"," despises that.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 15]"""
"483","(484) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥafīd narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Bajalī narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm al-Warrāq narrated to us; ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from ʿIyāḍ ibn Hilāl, and he mentioned it with the same wording.\n\n(b) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah said after these two narrations: This is the correct one — this narrator is ʿIyāḍ ibn Hilāl, from whom Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated more than one ḥadīth, and I consider the error to be from ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār when he said \from Hilāl ibn ʿIyāḍ.\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us"," saying: Abū Dāwūd said: No one narrated it with a complete chain except ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 1/260]"""
"484","(485) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: I heard ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh say: I heard Mūsā ibn Hārūn say: Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us; al-Walīd narrated from al-Awzāʿī from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, who narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a mursal ḥadīth.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ḥākim, 1/260]"
"485","(486) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī informed us; Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; al-Aʿmash narrated from Abū Wāʾil from Ḥudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a heap of garbage belonging to a people and urinated while standing. I moved away from him, and he said: \Come closer.\"" So I came near"," and then he performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his khuffayn.\n\nIt is recorded in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 222]"""
"486","(487) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Musaddad ibn Qaṭan narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrated from Manṣūr ibn al-Muʿtamir from Abū Wāʾil Shiqīq ibn Salamah from Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān, who said: I saw myself and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walking together. He came to a heap of garbage belonging to a people behind a wall and urinated as one of you stands. I moved away, and he gestured to me, so I came and stood at his heels until he finished.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 223]"
"487","(488) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from ʢāṣim, who said: I heard Abū Wāʾil narrate from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a heap of garbage belonging to a people and urinated while standing. I met Manṣūr and asked him about it, and he narrated it to me from Abū Wāʾil from Ḥudhayfah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a heap of garbage belonging to a people and urinated while standing.\n\nThus did ʢāṣim ibn Bahdalah and Ḥammād ibn Abī Sulaymān narrate it from Abū Wāʾil from al-Mughīrah.\n\nThe correct narration is what Manṣūr and al-Aʿmash narrated from Abū Wāʾil from Ḥudhayfah. Thus said Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī and a group of the ḥuffāẓ. And there has been narrated regarding the reason for his urinating while standing a ḥadīth whose like cannot be established. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim, 1/295]"
"488","(489) Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Mihrānī informed us; Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Mudhakkir narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Māhān al-Hamdānī al-Karābīsī narrated to us.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿImrān Mūsā ibn Saʿīd al-Ḥanẓalī in Hamadān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Māhān al-Karābīsī narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Ghassān al-Juʿfī narrated to us; Maʿn ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Abū al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet ﷺ urinated while standing due to a wound he had in his knee.\n\n(b) Imam Aḥmad, may Allah have mercy on him, said: It has been said that the Arabs used to seek a cure for back pain by urinating while standing. Perhaps he had back pain at that time. Al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, mentioned something to that effect. And it has been said: He did so only because he could not find a place to sit. And Allah knows best."
"489","(490) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal al-Māsarjisī informed us; Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated from Zayd ibn Wahb from ʿAbd ibn Ḥasanah, who said: I and ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ were sitting when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us with a shield in his hand. He urinated while sitting. We spoke among ourselves and said: \He urinates as a woman urinates.\"" He came to us and said: \""Do you not know what befell the companion of the Children of Israel? When urine touched them"," they would cut off that part. He forbade them"," so they left it"," and he was punished in his grave.\""\n\nIbn ʿUyaynah and others added in it: \""He screened himself with it and urinated while sitting.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 22]"""
"490","(491) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Usayd ibn ʢāṣim narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us; Sufyān narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from al-Miqdām ibn Shurayḥ from his father from ʢāʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never urinated while standing since al-Furqān was revealed upon him.\n\nIn the narration of al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ: \Sūrah al-Furqān.\"" And some of them narrated it"," saying: \""al-Qurʾān\"" or \""al-Furqān.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 6/113]"""
"491","(492) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī in Marw informed us: Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd informed us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā informed us: Isrāʾīl narrated from al-Miqdām ibn Shurayḥ from his father, who said: I heard ʿĀʾishah swearing by Allah that she had not seen anyone urinate while standing since the Furqān was revealed upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\n\n[Saḥīḥ. Al-Ḥākim narrated it, 1/295]"
"492","(493) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī in Baghdād informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: ʿAbd al-Karīm informed me from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: ʿUmar said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me urinating while standing"," so he said: 'O ʿUmar"," do not urinate while standing.'\"" He said: \""So I never urinated standing after that.\""\n\nThis ʿAbd al-Karīm is Ibn Abī al-Mukhāriq. A group narrated from ʿAbd al-Razzāq and attributed the name to him.\n\n(b) ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn Abī al-Mukhāriq is ḍaʿīf (weak).\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Mājah narrated it"," 8/3]"""
"493","(494) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Mālik ibn Anas informed me from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār that he saw ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar urinating while standing.\n\nThis weakens the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Karīm.\n\n(t) And we have narrated reports of urinating while standing from ʿUmar, ʿAlī, Sahl ibn Saʿd, and Anas ibn Mālik.\n\n[Saḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it, 1310]"
"494","(495) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me by way of ijāzah: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad informed us: Isḥāq informed us: Sufyān narrated from Muṭarrif from Saʿīd ibn ʿAmr ibn Saʿīd, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Urinating while standing is more protective of the back (i.e."," the posterior).\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"495","(496) ʿAdī ibn al-Faḍl narrated — and he is weak — from ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥakam from Abū Naḍrah from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from urinating while standing.\n\nAbū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated it to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us: Ibn Ṣāʿid informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Mukharramī and Abū al-Faḍl al-Khiraqī both said: Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī narrated to us: ʿAdī ibn al-Faḍl narrated it.\n\n[Very weak (ḍaʿīf jiddan)]"
"496","(497) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Ibn ʿAjlān from al-Qaʿqāʿ ibn Ḥakīm from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abī Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I am to you like a father. When one of you goes to relieve himself"," let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back towards it"," whether for defecation or urination"," and let him clean himself with three stones.\"" And he forbade using dung and bone"," and he forbade a man from cleaning himself with his right hand.\n\n[Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 8]"""
"497","(498) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad al-Raqāshī informed us: Umayyah ibn Bisṭām informed us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ informed us: Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, mentioning the same meaning with its chain of narration, except that he said: \And he forbade dung and bone"," and he commanded the use of three stones.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Ibn Mājah narrated it"," 313]"""
"498","(499) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Rajāʾ and al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān both said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah and Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash from Ibrāhīm from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, who said: They said to Salmān: \Your Prophet has taught you everything"," even the manner of defecation.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," yes. He forbade us from facing the qiblah with defecation or urination"," and he forbade any one of us from cleaning himself with fewer than three stones"," and he forbade us from cleaning ourselves with dung or bone.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Shaybah.\n\n(b) Al-Thawrī narrated it from al-Aʿmash and Manṣūr from Ibrāhīm"," mentioning it"," and in it: \""Let none of you clean himself with fewer than three stones.\""\n\n[Saḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 262]"""
"499","(500) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq ibn Yazīd al-ʿAṭṭār al-Baghdādī informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated in al-Kūfah: Yaʿqūb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Zuhrī narrated from Abī Ḥāzim from Muslim ibn Qurṭ from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you goes to relieve himself"," let him take with him three stones with which to clean himself"," for they will suffice him.\""\n\n[Saḥīḥ through other chains (ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrih). Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 4]"""
"500","(501) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Nufaylī informed us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from ʿAmr ibn Khuzaymah from ʿUmārah ibn Khuzaymah from Khuzaymah ibn Thābit, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about cleaning oneself after relieving (al-istiṭābah), so he said: \With three stones"," in which there is no dung.\""\n\n(t) Abū Dāwūd said: Thus Abū Usāmah and Ibn Numayr narrated it from Hishām. The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And likewise Muḥammad ibn Bishr al-ʿAbdī"," Wakīʿ"," and ʿAbdah ibn Sulaymān narrated it from Hishām. And Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it from Hishām from Abī Wajzah from ʿUmārah. And ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī used to say: The correct narration is that of the group from Hishām from ʿAmr ibn Khuzaymah.\n\n[Saḥīḥ through other chains (ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrih). Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 41]"""
"501","(502) The Shaykh, may Allah, the Most High, have mercy upon him, said: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated it once from Hishām, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd, from ʿAmr ibn Khuzaymah. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\n(b) Abū ʿĪsā said: al-Bukhārī said: Abū Muʿāwiyah erred in this hadith when he added therein \from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd.\""\n\n(c) al-Bukhārī said: The correct chain is what ʿAbdah and Wakīʿ narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," from Abī Khuzaymah"," from ʿUmārah ibn Khuzaymah"," from Khuzaymah.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy upon him"," said: And Abū Khuzaymah is ʿAmr ibn Khuzaymah. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"""
"502","(503) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shīrūyah narrated to us: Isḥāq, meaning al-Ḥanẓalī, informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, from Maʿmar, from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to bring him three stones. So I brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and discarded the dung and said: \Bring me a stone.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"503","(504) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abī Idrīs al-Khawlānī, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever performs wuḍūʾ should sniff water into the nose [for istinshāq]"," and whoever cleanses with stones [for istijmār] should do so in an odd number.\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Yūnus ibn Yazīd from al-Zuhrī.\n\n(t) A similar narration is established from al-Aʿraj"," from Abū Hurayrah"," from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nAnd from Abū al-Zubayr"," from Jābir"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," a similar narration regarding istijmār. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 160]"""
"504","(505) In the narration of Abū Sufyān, from Jābir, from the Prophet ﷺ: \When any one of you cleanses with stones [for istijmār]"," let him do so three times.\"" Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Jarīr narrated"," from al-Aʿmash"," from Abū Sufyān"," from Jābir"," who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""When any one of you cleanses with stones [for istijmār]"," let him do so three times.\""\n\n(q) In this [narration] there is an indication that His command to perform istijmār in an odd number refers to the odd number that exceeds one. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Aḥmad narrated it"," 3/400]"""
"505","(506) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus and ʿAmr ibn al-Walīd both said: Thawr ibn Yazīd narrated to us, from Ḥuṣayn al-Ḥubrānī, from Abī Saʿd al-Khayr, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever cleanses with stones [for istijmār] should do so in an odd number. Whoever does this has done well"," and whoever does not"," there is no blame upon him.\""\n\n(q) And if this [narration] is authentic"," then what is intended—and Allah knows best—is an odd number that comes after three. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 35]"""
"506","(507) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qāḍī in Marw narrated to us: al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbadah narrated to us: Abū ʿĀmir al-Khazzāz narrated, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \When any one of you cleanses with stones [for istijmār]"," let him do so in an odd number"," for Allah is Odd [al-Witr] and loves the odd. Do you not see: the heavens are seven"," the earths are seven"," and the circuits of ṭawāf are seven?\"" And he mentioned other things. [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it"," 77]"""
"507","(508) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ in Naysābūr and Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-ʿAlawī in Kūfah both informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Ḥuḥaym al-Shaybānī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAbsī narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated, from al-Aʿmash. He said: I heard Mujāhid narrating from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by two graves and said: \Indeed"," they are being punished"," and they are not being punished for anything major. As for one of them"," he used to walk about with namīmah [tale-bearing]. As for the other"," he used not to protect himself from his urine.\"" Wakīʿ said: \""He used not to guard against it.\"" He said: \""Then he called for a fresh palm frond and split it in two. He planted one piece on this grave and one on that grave"," then said: 'Perhaps it will be lightened for them as long as they do not dry out.'\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Mūsā and others"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Kurayb and others"," all of them from Wakīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 213]"""
"508","(509) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī in Marw narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated.\n\nAnd Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated, from al-Aʿmash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥasanah, who said: I set out with ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣī, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out with a shield or something like a shield. He sat and screened himself with it and urinated while sitting. I and my companion said: \Look at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—how he urinates as a woman urinates"," while he is sitting!\"" He came to us and said: \""Do you not know what befell the companion of the Children of Israel? When any of them was afflicted with something of urine"," he would cut it off with scissors. So he was forbidden from that"," and he was punished in his grave.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 22]"""
"509","(510) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Maymūnah.\n\nHe said: I heard Anas say: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come to the place of relieving himself"," and I"," along with a young boy of the Anṣār"," would follow him with a vessel of water"," and he would cleanse himself with it.\"" [It is] narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 149]"""
"510","(511) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām narrated, from Yūnus ibn al-Ḥārith, from Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Maymūnah, from Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \This verse was revealed concerning the people of Qubāʾ: {In it are men who love to purify themselves} [al-Tawbah:108].\"" He said: \""They used to cleanse themselves with water [for istinjāʾ]"," so this verse was revealed concerning them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 44]"""
"511","(512) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khalliyy narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding the verse: **{In it are men who love to purify themselves}** (Qur'an 9:108). He said: When this verse was revealed, Rasul Allah ﷺ sent for 'Uwaym ibn Sa'idah and said: *\What is this purification for which Allah has praised you?\""* He said: \""O Prophet of Allah"," no man or woman among us who answers the call of nature but washes his posterior\"" — or he said"," \""his sitting place.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: *\""It is concerning this.\""*\n\n(T) And it has been narrated from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman that he would perform istinja' (cleansing with water) when he urinated. And from 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her: that it is Sunnah for a woman to wash her front private part. [Sahih by other than him. Al-Hakim reported it (1/299)]"""
"512","(513) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sadiq Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fawaris al-'Attar informed us — they both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Maz'id al-Bayruti narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to me — 'Utban ibn Abi Hakim narrated to me — Talhah ibn Nafi' narrated to me.\n\nHe said: Abu Ayyub, Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, and Anas ibn Malik, the Ansari companions, narrated to me: When this verse was revealed — **{In it are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves}** (Qur'an 9:108) — Rasul Allah ﷺ said: *\O company of Ansar"," indeed Allah has praised you greatly regarding purification. What is this purification of yours?\""* They said: \""O Rasul Allah"," we perform wudu' for Salah and we bathe from janabah (major ritual impurity).\"" Rasul Allah ﷺ said: *\""Is there anything besides that?\""* They said: \""No"," except that when one of us answers the call of nature"," he prefers to perform istinja' with water.\"" He ﷺ said: *\""That is it — so adhere to it.\""* [Sahih by other than him. Ibn Majah reported it (355)]"""
"513","(514) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — al-Hasan ibn Ya'qub ibn Yusuf narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us — 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata' narrated to us — Sa'id narrated from Qatadah, from Mu'adhah, from 'A'ishah, that she said: *\Command your husbands to wash away the traces of excrement and urine"," for I feel shy of them.\""* And Rasul Allah ﷺ used to do so. [Sahih. Ahmad reported it (6/95)]"""
"514","(515) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umari al-Muqri' in Baghdad informed us — Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih narrated to us — Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir narrated to us — 'Affan narrated to us — Hammam and Abu 'Awanah both narrated to us — Qatadah narrated, mentioning it with the same meaning.\n\n(T) Abu Qilabah and others narrated it from Mu'adhah al-'Adawiyyah, but he did not trace it back to the action of the Prophet ﷺ. (J) Qatadah is a hafiz (preserver of hadith). [Sahih by other than him]"
"515","(516) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi, and Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Susi informed us — they said: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us — al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid informed us — 'Uqbah ibn 'Alqamah narrated to me — al-Awza'i narrated to me — Abu 'Ammar narrated from 'A'ishah: Women from the people of Basrah came to her, and she commanded them to perform istinja' with water. She said: *\Command your husbands to do this"," for Rasul Allah ﷺ used to do it.\""* And she said: *\""It is a cure for hemorrhoids (al-basur).\""*\n\nImam Ahmad"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: *\""This is mursal (disconnected).\""* (J) Abu 'Ammar is Shaddad — I do not think he met 'A'ishah. [Da'if. Ahmad reported it (6/93)]"""
"516","(517) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us — Sa'id ibn 'Uthman al-Ahwazi narrated to us — 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us — Zaidah narrated from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, who said: 'Ali ibn Abi Talib said: *\They used to pass solid dung like camels"," and you pass soft excrement. So follow the stones with water.\""*\n\n(T) Mis'ar followed him in narrating from 'Abd al-Malik. He said: *\""This is not from the older narrations of 'Abd al-Malik"," for 'Abd al-Malik narrates from the young (al-shabab).\""* [Da'if. Ibn Abi Shaybah reported it (1634)]"""
"517","(518) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us — Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us — Mis'ar narrated from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, who said: 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: *\We used to pass solid dung"," and you today pass soft excrement.\""* [Da'if]"""
"518","(519) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu Hamid ibn Bilal narrated to us — Yahya ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us — Sufyan narrated from Isma'il.\n\n(H) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — and the wording is his — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah, father of Dawud ibn al-Munadi, narrated to us — Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated from Isma'il, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Sa'd ibn Malik, who said: *\I have seen myself as the seventh of seven with Rasul Allah ﷺ"," and we had no food except the leaves of al-hablah (a type of tree) or al-hublah\""* — thus Shu'bah narrated — *\""to the extent that one of us would pass dung like a sheep passes its droppings.\""* Then Banu Asad began to reproach me for Islam: *\""I would indeed have lost"," and my effort would have been in vain.\""*\n\nIn the narration of Ibn 'Uyunah: *\""except the leaves of trees or al-hublah"," to the extent that one of us would pass dung like a sheep passes its droppings"," without any mixture.\""* And the remainder has the same meaning.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad from Wahb ibn Jarir"," and Muslim reported it from another route from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari reported it (5096)]"""
"519","(520) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us — Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us — Sharik narrated.\n\nAbu Dawud said: And Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah informed us — Waki' narrated from Sharik, from Ibrahim ibn Jarir, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: *\When the Prophet ﷺ came to the privy"," I would come to him with water in a small vessel (tawr) or a waterskin (rakwah)"," and he would perform istinja'. Then he would rub his hand on the earth. Then I would come to him with another vessel"," and he would perform wudu'.\""*\n\nAbu Dawud said: *\""And the hadith of Aswad ibn 'Amir is more complete.\""* [Hasan by other than him. Abu Dawud reported it (45)]"""
"520","(521) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah, Abu 'Uthman al-Kufi, narrated to us — Aban ibn 'Abd Allah al-Bajali narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Jarir ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us — Jarir ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to me, who said: *\I came to Rasul Allah ﷺ with water for wudu'"," and he performed istinja'. Then he rubbed his hand on the earth. Then he performed wudu' and wiped over his leather socks (khuffayn).\""* I said: *\""O Rasul Allah"," your feet?\""* He said: *\""I had put them on while they were in a state of purity (tahirayn).\""*\n\n(T) Thus Abu Nu'aym and Shu'ayb ibn Harb narrated it from Aban ibn 'Abd Allah.\n\nAbu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i said: *\""This is more likely to be correct than the hadith of Sharik"," and Allah knows best.\""* The Shaykh"," may Allah the Most High have mercy on him"," said: And it has been said regarding Aban ibn 'Abd Allah that he narrated from a mawla (freed slave) of Abu Hurayrah"," from Abu Hurayrah. [Hasan by other than him. Al-Nasa'i reported it (50)]"""
"521","(522) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us; Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri informed us; Aban ibn 'Abdillah informed us. He said: A client of Abu Hurayrah narrated to me — and I think he said it was Abu Wahb — who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: \Bring me water for ablution.\"" So I brought him water for ablution"," and he performed istinja' (cleansing after relieving himself). Then he placed his hand in the earth and wiped it with it"," then washed it. Then he performed wudu' and wiped over his khuffs (leather socks). I said: \""You performed wudu' but did not wash your feet.\"" He said: \""I put them on while they were both pure.\"" [Hasan due to supporting narrations. Reported by Ahmad (2/358)]"""
"522","(523) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad informed us; Yahya ibn Ma'in informed us; Ibn Abi 'Adiyy narrated from Ibn 'Awn, from Anas ibn Sirin, that Anas ibn Malik used to have water and ashnan (a cleansing plant) placed before him — meaning for the purpose of istinja'. [Sahih]"
"523","(524) Abu 'Abdillah — Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz — informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah informed us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us; Suwayd ibn Sa'id informed us; 'Amr ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn 'Amr al-Qurashi narrated from his grandfather Sa'id ibn 'Amr, who said: Abu Hurayrah used to follow the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) carrying a vessel for his wudu' and his need (for relieving himself). He said: One day he caught up with him and said: \Who is this?\"" He said: \""I am Abu Hurayrah.\"" He said: \""Bring me stones with which I may cleanse myself"," and do not bring me a bone or dung.\"" So I brought him stones in my garment and placed them beside him. When he finished and stood up"," I followed him and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what is the matter with bones and dung?\"" He said: \""A delegation from the tribe of Naseeb came to me and asked me for provisions. So I supplicated to Allah for them that they would not pass by any dung or bone except that they would find food upon it.\"" [Sahih. Reported by al-Bukhari (3647)]"""
"524","(525) Abu Hazim al-'Abdawi al-Hafiz informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Isma'il al-Muqri' informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini in Basrah informed us; 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi informed us; 'Amr ibn Yahya narrated from his grandfather Sa'id ibn 'Amr, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) carrying my vessel, and I found him when he intended to relieve himself. He mentioned the hadith with the same meaning. Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Makki from 'Amr ibn Yahya, in an abbreviated form, without the question of Abu Hurayrah and without the mention of the jinn from Naseeb. [Sahih]"
"525","(526) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Qadi informed us; Abu Nu'aim al-Fadl ibn Dukayn and Ahmad ibn Yunus both said: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiya narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, who said: Abu 'Ubaydah did not mention it, but rather 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated from his father that he heard 'Abdillah say: The Prophet (ﷺ) went to relieve himself and commanded me to bring him three stones. He said: I found two stones and searched for the third but could not find it. So I took a piece of dung and brought it to the Prophet (ﷺ). He took the two stones and discarded the dung, saying: \This is impure (riks).\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Nu'aim. This is a hadith over which there is disagreement regarding its chain from Abu Ishaq al-Sabi'i. Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiya narrated it in this manner"," and al-Bukhari relied upon it and placed it in his Jami'. (T) Ma'mar narrated it from Abu Ishaq"," from 'Alqamah"," from 'Abdillah"," and added at the end: \""Bring me a stone.\"" (J) Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated it from Abu Ishaq"," from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd"," from 'Abdillah. (J) Isra'il narrated it from Abu Ishaq"," from Abu 'Ubaydah"," from 'Abdillah. (J) Abu 'Isa al-Tirmidhi said: The hadith of Isra'il is"," in my view"," more established and more accurate"," because Isra'il is more reliable in narrating from Abu Ishaq than these others"," and Qays ibn al-Rabi' followed him in that. He said: Zuhayr is not like that in narrating from Abu Ishaq"," because his hearing from Abu Ishaq was towards the end"," and Abu Ishaq's memory had deteriorated towards the end of his life. [Sahih. Reported by al-Bukhari (100)]"""
"526","(527) The Shaykh said: Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Walid al-Faqih informed us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah informed us; 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated from Layth, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Abdillah, who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for his need, and he said: \Bring me something with which I may perform istinja'"," and do not bring me dung or regurgitated matter (raji').\"" This narration"," if authentic"," strengthens the narration of Abu Ishaq from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad. (J) However"," Layth ibn Abi Sulaym is weak (da'if). [Da'if. Reported by Ahmad (1/426)]"""
"527","(528) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Nadr, Muhammad ibn Nu'aym, and Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us; 'Abd al-A'la ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated from Dawud, from 'Amir, who said: I asked 'Alqamah: \Was Ibn Mas'ud with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the Night of the Jinn?\"" 'Alqamah said: \""I asked Ibn Mas'ud: 'Did any of you witness with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) the Night of the Jinn?' He said: 'No. However"," we were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) one night and we lost him. We searched for him in the valleys and mountain paths and said: \""He has been carried away or seized.\"" We spent the worst night that any people have ever spent. When morning came"," he approached us from the direction of Hira'. We said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," we lost you and searched for you but could not find you"," and we spent the worst night that any people have ever spent.\"" He said: \""A caller of the jinn came to me"," so I went with him and recited the Qur'an to them.\"" He said: \""He then took us and showed us their traces and the traces of their fires. They asked him for provisions"," and he said: 'Every bone upon which the name of Allah has been mentioned will fall into your hands with more flesh than it ever had"," and every piece of dung is fodder for your animals.'\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Do not perform istinja' with them (bones and dung)"," for they are the food of your brothers.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna in this manner. [Sahih. Reported by Muslim (450)]"""
"528","(529) It was narrated from 'Ali ibn Hujr, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, with this chain of narration up to his words: \and the traces of their fires.\"" Al-Sha'bi said: \""They asked him for provisions"," and they were from the jinn of the island (jazirah).\"" This is the end of the hadith from the words of al-Sha'bi"," separated from the hadith of 'Abdillah. Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu al-Walid informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq and Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr said: 'Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. [Sahih. Reported by Muslim (1/45)]"""
"529","(530) Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adiyy narrated from Dawud up to his words: \and the traces of their fires.\"" Then he said: Dawud said: \""I do not know whether it was in the hadith of 'Alqamah or in the hadith of 'Amir that they asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for provisions that night","\"" and he mentioned it. Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr informed us; Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adiyy narrated from Dawud"," and he mentioned it. A group narrated it from Dawud"," incorporated into the hadith without any doubt. [Sahih]"""
"530","(531) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dassah informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi narrated; Ibn 'Ayyash narrated from Yahya ibn Abi 'Amr al-Saybani, from 'Abdillah ibn al-Daylami, from 'Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, who said: A delegation of the jinn came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \O Muhammad"," forbid your ummah from performing istinja' with a bone"," a piece of dung"," or coal"," for Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has made provision for us in them.\"" He said: The Prophet (ﷺ) forbade it. [Sahih. Reported by Abu Dawud (39)]"""
"531","(532) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, he said: it was read to Ibn Wahb: Mūsā ibn ʿAlī narrated to you from his father, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade performing istinjāʾ with a bone that has no flesh on it, or with dung, or with coal.\n\n(b) The hearing of ʿAlyy ibn Rabbāḥ from Ibn Masʿūd is not established. The first chain is Syrian and not strong. And Allah knows best.\n\n(t) In this chapter there are narrations from Abū ʿUthmān ibn Sanntah al-Khuzāʿī and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Rāfiʿ al-Tanūkhī from Ibn Masʿūd, except that in their narrations there is no mention of coal. [Ṣaḥīgh for something other than it. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it (1/55, 56).]"
"532","(533) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us, Zakariyyā ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade us from performing tammassuh (wiping for blessing) with a bone or with droppings.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Rūḥ.\n\n(t) And it has been narrated in this regard from Salmān al-Fārisī and Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (263).]"
"533","(534) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Khālid ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Mawhab al-Hamdānī narrated to us, al-Mufaḍḍal, meaning Ibn Faḍālah al-Miṣrī, narrated to us, from ʿAyyāsh ibn ʿAbbās al-Qitbānī, that Shuʿaym ibn Baytān al-Qitbānī informed him from Shaybān al-Qitbānī, from Ruwayfiʿ ibn Thābit, who said: Indeed, one of us in the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would take his brother's camel on the condition that he would receive half of what was gained, and we would receive half. And indeed, one of us would have the arrowhead and feathers, and the other would have the wooden shaft. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: \O Ruwayfiʿ"," perhaps life will be prolonged for you after me"," so inform the people that whoever ties a knot in his beard"," or wears a bowstring"," or performs istinjāʾ with the droppings of an animal or with a bone"," then Muḥammad is free of him.\""\n\n(gh) al-Niḍw: a lean camel. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (36).]"""
"534","(535) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Burshān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī al-Razzāz narrated to us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us, from Misʿar, from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd, from his brother, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding the skins of dead animals: \Indeed"," their tanning has removed their impurity"," or their filth"," or their uncleanness.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Aḥmad narrated it (1/237).]"""
"535","(536) As for the narration that ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Mūsā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Anṣārī, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from a man from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) from the Anṣār, who informed him from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): that he forbade anyone from performing istinbāṭ (cleaning oneself) with a bone, or dung, or skin.\n\nAbū Bakr al-Ḥārithī informed us of it, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Nuṣayr narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, Abū Ṭāhir and ʿAmr ibn Sawwād said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith, and he mentioned it. ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar said: This chain is not established. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Ṭaḥāwī narrated it in Sharh al-Maʿānī (1/133).]"
"536","(537) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr, meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah, narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abū Bishr informed us, from Ṭāwūs.\n\n(ḥ) And Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-ʿUmarī in Kūfah narrated to us, Abū Kurayb narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abū Bishr, from Ṭāwūs, who said: Istinjāʾ is with three stones or three sticks. I said: What if I do not find them? He said: Three handfuls of earth. This is what is authentic from Ṭāwūs as his own statement. (t) And Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it in the same manner from Salamah ibn Wahram from Ṭāwūs. And Zamaʿah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated it from Salamah and raised it as a mursal narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it (1639).]"
"537","(538) Abū Bakr al-Ḥārithī al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbbād narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, from Zamaʿah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from Salamah ibn Wahram, who said: I heard Ṭāwūs say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you comes to relieve himself"," let him honor the qiblah of Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," so let him not face it nor turn his back to it. Then let him perform istinbāṭ with three stones"," or three sticks"," or three handfuls of earth. Then let him say: 'All praise is due to Allah"," Who removed from me what harms me and retained for me what benefits me.'\""\n\nThis is how Ibn Wakīʿ narrated it"," and others narrated it from Zamaʿah.\n\nAnd Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥaḍarī narrated it — and he is a liar"," abandoned — from Abū ʿĀṣim"," from Zamaʿah"," from Salamah"," from Ṭāwūs"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and its being connected (waṣl) and its being raised (rafʿ) are not authentic.\n\nʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: I asked Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah: \""Did Zamaʿah used to raise it?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So I asked Salamah about it"," and he did not know it — meaning he did not raise it. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it (1/57).]"""
"538","(539) Mubashshir ibn ʿUbayd narrated from al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: Surāqah ibn Mālik came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and asked him about defecation. So he commanded him to seek elevated ground, and to avoid the qiblah — neither facing it nor turning his back to it — and to perform istinjāʾ with three stones in which there is no dung, or three sticks, or three handfuls of earth.\n\nAbū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū ʿUtbah narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn ʿUbayd narrated to me, al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh narrated, and he mentioned it.\n\n(b) Abū Bakr al-Ḥārithī informed us, he said: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: No one narrated it other than Mubashshir ibn ʿUbayd, and he is abandoned in hadith.\n\n(t) The Sheikh said: And it has been narrated in this regard from Anas ibn Mālik as a marfūʿ narration, and that is rejected. [Very weak. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it (1/56).]"
"539","(540) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī in Baghdad informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Tarqafī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿlā narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ghaylān, from Abū Isḥāq, from the mawlā of ʿUmar, Yasār ibn Numayr, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say when he urinated: \Give me something with which I may perform istinjāʾ.\"" He said: \""So I would give him a piece of wood and a stone"," or he would come to a wall and wipe himself with it"," or touch the earth"," and he would not wash it.\"" And this is the most authentic narration in this chapter and the highest in chain. [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"540","(541) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us of it, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, al-Khaḍir ibn Aḥmad ibn Umayyah narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Khālid narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, meaning al-Ṭarāʾifī, narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Mālik say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Istinjāʾ is with three stones"," and with earth if one does not find a stone"," and one should not perform istinjāʾ with something that has already been used for istinjāʾ once.\""\n\n(b) ʿUthmān al-Ṭarāʾifī: they spoke critically of him; he narrates from unknown people. And Allah knows best. And it has been narrated from another route from Anas"," but it is not authentic. [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn ʿAdī narrated it (1/202"," 271).]"""
"541","(542) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdīy informed us; Aḥmad ibn Hārūn ibn Mūsā al-Baladī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ḥumayd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Abī Dāwūd narrated to us; Muʿān ibn Rifāʿah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Bukht narrated from Anas, who said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Istinjāʾ is to be performed with three stones"," and with earth if one cannot find stones. And one should not perform istinjāʾ with something that has already been used for istinjāʾ once.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdīy said: Most of what Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ḥumayd narrated of this kind is not corroborated by anyone else.\n\n[Very weak. Narrated by Ibn ʿAdīy (1/202)]"""
"542","(543) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us from the original of his book; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān al-Tannūkhī narrated to us; Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī narrated. Abū al-ʿAbbās said, and al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd informed us; my father narrated to me; al-Awzāʿī narrated. He said, and al-ʿAbbās informed us; ʿUqbah ibn ʿAlqamah narrated from al-Awzāʿī — and the hadith belongs to al-ʿAbbās — he said: Yaḥyā, meaning Ibn Abī Kathīr, narrated to me; he said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah narrated to me; my father narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \When any of you urinates"," let him not touch his private part with his right hand"," and let him not breathe into the vessel"," and let him not perform istinjāʾ with his right hand.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf from al-Awzāʿī"," and Muslim narrated it through various chains from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr. In some of its routes: \""Let none of you hold his private part with his right hand while urinating.\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (153)]"""
"543","(544) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Hishām narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah from his father that the Prophet ﷺ said: \When any of you comes to the privy"," let him not perform istinjāʾ with his right hand"," and let him not touch his private part with his right hand.\""\n\nIt is recorded in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the hadith of Hishām al-Dastawāʾī.\n\nAnd we narrated it from the hadith of Salmān and Abū Hurayrah.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (152)]"""
"544","(545) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Ṣaydalānī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Sufyān from al-Aʿmash and Manṣūr from Ibrāhīm from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd from Salmān, who said: The polytheists said to him: \We see your companion teaching you even how to defecate!\"" He said: \""Indeed! He has forbidden us from performing istinjāʾ with the right hand"," and from facing the qiblah"," and he has forbidden us from using dung and bones"," and he said: 'Let none of you perform istinjāʾ with fewer than three stones.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Muslim (262)]"""
"545","(546) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Ibn ʿAjlān; al-Qaʿqāʿ ibn Ḥakīm narrated to me; from Abī Ṣāliḥ; from Abū Hurayrah; from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \I am to you like a father — I teach you. So when any of you goes to the privy"," let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it"," and let him not perform istinjāʾ with his right hand.\"" And he used to command the use of three stones and prohibit the use of dung and bone.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1)]"""
"546","(547) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-Ṣaydalānī informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Khallān informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah informed us; Abū Ayyūb, meaning al-Afrīqī, informed us; from ʿĀṣim; from al-Musayyib ibn Rāfiʿ and Maʿbad; from Ḥārithah ibn Wahb al-Khuzāʿī, who said: Ḥafṣah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to dedicate his right hand for his food, drink, and clothing, and his left hand for other than that.\n\n[Sahih in other than this chain. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (32)]"
"547","(548) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Sharqī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bazīʿ narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ al-Khaffāf narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Abī Maʿshar from Ibrāhīm from al-Aswad ibn Yazīd from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The right hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was for his purification and his food, and the left hand was for his privy and whatever was impure.\n\nThus Abū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim ibn Bazīʿ from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb."
"548","(549) ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah, but he did not mention al-Aswad ibn Yazīd in its chain. Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Abū Tawbah narrated to us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah, and he mentioned it.\n\n[Sahih in other than this chain. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (33)]"
"549","(550) Ibn Abī ʿAdīy narrated from Saʿīd from a man from Abī Maʿshar from Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī, who said: ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said. Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Mihrajānī al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Khaṭṭāb narrated to us; Ibn Abī ʿAdīy narrated it.\n\n[Sahih in other than this chain]"
"550","(551) Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā narrated to me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Mulaykah narrated to me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us; Fahd ibn Ḥayyān al-Qaysī narrated to us; Abū Yaʿqūb al-Ḍabbī — and he is ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā — narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah from his mother from ʿĀʾishah: that the Prophet ﷺ urinated, and ʿUmar brought him a vessel of water. He said: \What is this"," O ʿUmar?\"" He said: \""Perform wuḍūʾ with it.\"" He said: \""I have not been commanded to perform wuḍūʾ every time I urinate. Had I done so"," it would have become a sunnah.\"" The wording is that of the hadith of Fahd ibn Ḥayyān.\n\n[Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (42)]"""
"551","(552) Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Khalīl al-Ṣūfī informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAdiyy al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ḥamzah al-Aṣbahānī informed us, ʿAlī ibn Sahl ibn al-Mughīrah informed us, Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah informed us, Zakariyyā ibn Isḥāq and Zamʿah both said: ʿĪsā ibn Yazdād informed us from his father that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to, when he urinated, shake his penis three times.\n\n(b) ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAdiyy said: The narration of ʿĪsā ibn Yazdād from his father is mursal. Zamʿah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from him, and it is not authentic. I heard Ibn Ḥammād mention it from al-Bukhārī.\n\nʿAbdullāh said: It is also said ʿĪsā ibn Azdād, and he is not known except through this hadith. [Weak. Narrated by Ibn ʿAdiyy 5/254]"
"552","(553) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam al-Qaṭrī informed us, ʿAtīq ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Ubayy ibn al-ʿAbbās ibn Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī informed us from his father, from Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about istijmār (cleaning with stones), so he said: \Cannot one of you find three stones: two stones for the two sides and one stone for the outlet?\"" Thus it was in his book. [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī 1/56]"""
"553","(554) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed it to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥulwānī informed us, ʿAtīq mentioned it with its chain and its meaning, except that he said: \Two stones for the two sides and one stone for the outlet.\""\n\nAbū Bakr al-Ḥārithī informed us"," he said: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: Its chain is ḥasan"," meaning the chain of this hadith. [Weak]"""
"554","(555) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr and others informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān informed us, al-Zuhrī informed us, ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm informed me from his uncle ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd, who said: A complaint was made to the Prophet (ﷺ) about a man who imagines something during the prayer, so he said: \He should not turn away until he hears a sound or finds an odor.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah be pleased with him) said in the narration of Abī Saʿīd: When the Sunnah indicated that a man should break his prayer due to wind"," the wind was of the same category as passing stool"," and passing stool was more prevalent than it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī and others"," and Muslim narrated it from ʿAmr al-Nāqid and others"," all of them from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. [Authentic. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 137]"""
"555","(556) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us, Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbdillāh and ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Farrāʾ and Qaṭan ibn Ibrāhīm said: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us, he said: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān informed me from Sulaymān al-Aʿmash from Ibrāhīm from Hammām.\n\n(h) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us, Abū Muʿāwiyah informed us, al-Aʿmash informed us from Ibrāhīm from Hammām, who said: Jarīr urinated, then performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his leather socks. It was said to him: \Do you do this when you have urinated?\"" He said: \""Yes"," I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) urinate"," perform wuḍūʾ"," and wipe over his leather socks.\""\n\nIbrāhīm said: This hadith pleased them because the Islam of Jarīr came after the revelation of al-Māʾidah.\n\nThe wording is that of Abī Muʿāwiyah. In the hadith of Ibn Ṭahmān"," from Jarīr ibn ʿAbdillāh: He urinated"," then performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his leather socks. We said to him: \""What is this that you have done?\"" He said: \""I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) do the same as I have done.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others from Abī Muʿāwiyah"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through other chains from al-Aʿmash. [Authentic. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 380]"""
"556","(557) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd al-Bayrūtī informed us, Ibn Shuʿayb informed me, Shaybān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed me from ʿĀṣim ibn Bahdalah, who is Ibn Abī al-Najūd, who informed them from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh, who said: I came to Ṣafwān ibn ʿAssāl and said to him: \You were a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and something has been troubling my chest regarding wiping over the leather socks after urination and stool. Inform me of something"," if you heard it from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" He said: \""He used to command us"," when we were on a journey or traveling"," not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights"," except from janābah"," but from urination"," stool"," and sleep.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī 3535]"""
"557","(558) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Shirawayh informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Hāshim informed us, Wakīʿ informed us from Miʿsar from ʿĀṣim ibn Abī al-Najūd from Zirr.\n\nFrom Ṣafwān ibn ʿAssāl, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted us permission regarding wiping over the leather socks for the traveler for three days, except from janābah, but from stool, urination, or wind. Abū al-Walīd said: No one said \or wind\"" other than Miʿsar. [Ḥasan]"""
"558","(559) And Abū Bakr al-Ḥārithī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Mubashshir and Abū ʿUbaydillāh Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān in Wāsiṭ said: Aḥmad ibn Sinān informed us.\n\nʿAlī said: And Abū al-Ṭayyib Yazīd ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Yazīd al-Bazzāz informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ḥasanī informed us, they said: Wakīʿ informed us, Miʿsar informed us, mentioning it similarly. ʿAlī said: No one said in this hadith \or wind\"" other than Wakīʿ from Miʿsar. [Ḥasan]"""
"559","(560) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī in Kūfah informed us, and Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī in Naysābūr informed us, they said: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh al-ʿAbsī informed us, Wakīʿ informed us from al-Aʿmash from Mundhir, Abū Yaʿlā, from Ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah, from ʿAlī, who said: \I was a man who experienced frequent madhī (pre-seminal fluid)"," so I felt too shy to ask the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) because of his daughter (being my wife). So I ordered al-Miqdād ibn al-Aswad"," and he asked him"," and he said: 'He should wash his penis and perform wuḍūʾ.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Wakīʿ"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through other chains from al-Aʿmash. [Narrated by al-Bukhārī 132]"""
"560","(561) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Shuʿbah informed us from al-Aʿmash. He said: I heard Mundhir al-Thawrī narrating from Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah from ʿAlī, who said: \I felt too shy to ask the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about madhī because of Fāṭimah"," so I ordered a man"," and he asked him"," and he said: 'Wuḍūʾ is required for it.'\""\n\nIt is recorded in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the hadith of Shuʿbah. [Authentic]"""
"561","(562) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us. He said: And Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was recited to Ibn Wahb: \Mālik ibn Anas informed you that Abū al-Naḍr narrated to him from Sulaymān ibn Yasār from al-Miqdād ibn al-Aswad that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālli — may Allah be pleased with them both — instructed him to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about what is incumbent upon one of us when madhy (pre-seminal fluid) comes out"," for he had the Prophet's daughter with him and felt too shy to ask. So al-Miqdād said: I asked him"," and he said: 'When any of you finds that (madhy)"," let him wash his private part and perform wuḍūʾ as he would for the prayer.'\""\n\nThus narrated Abū al-Naḍr from Sulaymān.\n\nAnd Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ashajj narrated it from Sulaymān from Ibn ʿAbbās"," in a connected (mawṣūl) chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"562","(563) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, Ibn Wahb said: Makhrama ibn Bukayr informed me from his father, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \I sent al-Miqdād ibn al-Aswad to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he asked him about the madhy that comes out of a person and what one should do regarding it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Perform wuḍūʾ and sprinkle water on your private part.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 303]"""
"563","(564) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Usayd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Manṣūr, from Mujāhid, from Muwarriq, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Regarding maniyy (semen)"," madhy (pre-seminal fluid)"," and wady (urethral discharge): from maniyy"," ghusl (ritual bath) is required; and from these two (madhy and wady)"," wuḍūʾ is required — one washes his private part and performs wuḍūʾ.\""\n\n(T) And Ibrāhīm narrated it from Ibn Masʿūd"," who said: \""Wady is what occurs after urination"," and wuḍūʾ is required for it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it"," 973]"""
"564","(565) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed me, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, Hishām ibn ʿUrwa narrated to us, from his father, from ʿĀʾisha, that Fāṭima bint Abī Ḥubaysh asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: \I experience istiḥāḍa (irregular bleeding) and never become pure — should I abandon the prayer?\"" He said: \""That is from a vein"," not menstruation (ḥayḍ). When it comes"," leave the prayer. When it ceases"," wash the traces of blood from yourself"," perform wuḍūʾ"," and pray"," for that is from a vein"," not menstruation.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Khalaf ibn Hishām from Ḥammād"," without her saying \""and perform wuḍūʾ.\"" Then Muslim said: \""In the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Zayd there is an additional word which we have not mentioned"," because this addition is not preserved (maḥfūẓa). What is preserved is what Abū Muʿāwiya and others narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwa — this ḥadīth — and at the end of it Hishām said: His father said: 'Then perform wuḍūʾ for every prayer until that time comes again.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"565","(566) Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Isfarāʾinī narrated to us therein, Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Bashr narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-Dhuhlī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: I read to Sharīk, from Abū al-Yaqẓān, from ʿAdī ibn Thābit, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The woman experiencing istiḥāḍa should leave the prayer during the days of her ḥayḍ"," then perform ghusl"," perform wuḍūʾ for every prayer"," fast"," and pray.\""\n\nAnd this ḥadīth — we shall mention some of what has been said about it"," if Allah the Most High wills"," in the book of Ḥayḍ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"566","(567) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-ʿAlawī narrated to us in Kūfa, Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAbsī narrated to us, Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ẓabyān, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that wuḍūʾ from food was mentioned in his presence — al-Aʿmash said once: and cupping for the fasting person — and he said: \Wuḍūʾ is only from what exits"," not from what enters. And breaking the fast (fiṭr) is only from what enters"," not from what exits.\""\n\n(T) And it was also narrated from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib as his own statement. And it was narrated from the Prophet ﷺ"," but it is not established. [Ṣaḥīḥ as a statement of others. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it"," 653]"""
"567","(568) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Munqidh narrated to us, Idrīs ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, al-Faḍl ibn al-Mukhtār narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, from Shuʿba — the mawlā of Ibn ʿAbbās — from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Wuḍūʾ is from what exits"," not from what enters.\""\n\n(Q) And we have narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ that he said regarding the one who performs wuḍūʾ and then a worm comes out of his anus: \""Wuḍūʾ is incumbent upon him.\"" And al-Ḥasan and a group said likewise. [Mawḍūʿ. Abū Nuʿaym narrated it in al-Ḥilya]"""
"568","(569) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī and Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us, saying: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, Maʿmar narrated to us, from Hammām ibn Munabbih, that he heard Abū Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The prayer of the one who has a ḥadath (nullification of wuḍūʾ) is not accepted until he performs wuḍūʾ.\"" A man from Ḥaḍramawt asked: \""What is a ḥadath"," O Abū Hurayra?\"" He said: \""Passing wind silently or with a sound.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ"," all of them from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 135]"""
"569","(570) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān narrated to us in Baghdad, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī al-Razzāz narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us, Shuʿba narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, from Abū Hurayra, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \There is no wuḍūʾ (required) except from a sound or an odor.\"" This is an abridged version"," and its complete form is in what follows. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it"," 74]"""
"570","(571) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Salama narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Jarīr narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abū Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When any of you feels something in his abdomen and is uncertain whether something has come out or not"," he should not leave the mosque until he hears a sound or detects an odor.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Jarīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 362]"""
"571","Allah, the Most High, said: {When you rise to perform the Salah, wash your faces} [Al-Ma'idah: 6].\n\n(572) Al-Shafi'i said: \I heard someone whose knowledge of the Qur'an I trust claim that this verse was revealed concerning those who rise from sleep.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""This is also narrated by Malik ibn Anas from Zayd ibn Aslam"," that this (when you rise to perform the Salah) refers to rising from the sleeping places"," meaning sleep.\"" [Al-Qurtubi transmitted it in his Tafsir"," 6/78]"""
"572","(573) Abu al-Mihrajan informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik narrated it.\n\n(q) Al-Shafi'i used as evidence in his earlier position that the verse was revealed concerning a specific circumstance, that the Prophet ﷺ performed multiple Salahs with a single wudu'. [Sahih. Malik transmitted it, 39]"
"573","(574) Abu al-Husayn ibn Burhan al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us: Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn al-Misri narrated to us: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Al-Firyabi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from 'Alqamah ibn Murthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: \The Prophet ﷺ"," on the Day of the Conquest"," performed all of his Salahs with a single wudu'"," and wiped over his leather socks. 'Umayr ibn Maymun said to him: 'I saw you do something today that you had not done before.' He ﷺ said: 'I did it deliberately"," O 'Umayr.'\""\n\nMuslim transmitted it in his Sahih from the hadith of Sufyan al-Thawri.\n\n(sh) Al-Shafi'i said: \""And in the Sunnah there is evidence that one who rises from his sleep should perform wudu'.\"" [Sahih. Muslim transmitted it"," 277]"""
"574","(575) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Nusayr al-Khuldi narrated to us: Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Al-Mughirah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \When one of you awakens from his sleep"," let not his hand enter the wudu' water until he washes it"," for he does not know where his hand spent the night.\"" Muslim transmitted it in his Sahih from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id. [Sahih. Muslim transmitted it"," 278]"""
"575","(576) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Makhlad ibn Ja'far al-Baqarhi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jarir narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us: Al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you rises from sleep to perform wudu'"," let him pour water over his hands"," for he does not know where his hand spent the night.\""\n\nMuslim transmitted it in his Sahih from Abu Kurayb. [Sahih]"""
"576","(577) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us: Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us: Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from 'Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zir ibn Hubaysh, who said: \I came to Safwan ibn 'Assal al-Muradi and said: 'Something has been troubling my chest regarding wiping over the leather socks after passing stool and urine"," and you were a companion of the Prophet ﷺ"," so I have come to ask you: did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning that?' He said: 'Yes"," he used to command us"," when we were on a journey or were travelers"," not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights"," except due to janabah"," but not after stool"," urine"," or sleep.'\"" [Hasan]"""
"577","(578) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Abu 'Utbah narrated to us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated from al-Wadin ibn 'Ata', from Mahfuz ibn 'Alqamah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'A'idh al-Azdadi, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \The eye is the sphincter (wikā') of the anus; so whoever sleeps"," let him perform wudu'.\"" [Hasan li-ghayrihi. Abu Dawud transmitted it"," 203]"""
"578","(579) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahmuyah al-'Askari narrated to us: Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Bahrani narrated to us: Yazid ibn 'Abd Rabbih narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from 'Ata' ibn Qays, from Mu'awiyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The eye is the sphincter of the anus; when the eye sleeps"," the sphincter is released.\"" [Hasan li-ghayrihi. Ahmad transmitted it"," 4/96]"""
"579","(580) Marwan ibn Janah narrated from 'Ata' ibn Qays, from Mu'awiyah, who said: \The eye is the sphincter of the anus\"" — and he stopped there (i.e."," as a mawquf narration).\n\nAbu Sa'd al-Sufi informed us: Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us: Salih ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Asad narrated to us: Al-Walid narrated to us: Marwan ibn Janah narrated it as mawquf.\n\n(j) Al-Walid ibn Muslim said: \""And Marwan is more reliable than Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam.\"" [Da'if. Malik transmitted it"," 38]"""
"580","(581) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Nasr 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Qatadah informed us, saying: Abu 'Amr ibn Nujayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab said: \When one of you sleeps lying down"," let him perform wudu'.\"" This is a mursal narration. [Munkar. Al-Harith transmitted it in his Musnad"," 89]"""
"581","(582) Al-Husayn ibn Bashran informed us in Baghdad: Abu Ja'far al-Razzaz narrated to us: Ahmad ibn al-Khalil narrated to us: al-Waqidi narrated to us: Usamah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated from his father, from his grandfather, from Umayr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \When any one of you lies down on his side"," let him perform wudu.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Abi Shaybah"," 1412]"""
"582","(583) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Asid ibn 'Asim narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated from Sufyan, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \Wudu is obligatory upon every sleeper"," except one who merely nods his head once.\""\n\nThus a group narrated it from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad as a mawquf narration"," and it was also narrated as marfu'"," but its being marfu' is not established. [Weak]"""
"583","(584) Abu Hazim al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Qasim 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Baghawi informed us in Baghdad: 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd informed us: Shu'bah narrated from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Khalid ibn Ghilaq, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: \Whoever is overcome by sleep"," wudu has become obligatory upon him.\"" [Weak. Narrated by 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd"," 1452]"""
"584","(585) Abu Hazim informed us: Abu Ahmad informed us: Abu al-Qasim informed us: Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us: Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated from al-Jurayri with his chain of narration, the same.\n\nIsma'il said: al-Jurayri said: \We asked him about what constitutes being 'overcome by sleep","' and he said: 'It is when one places his side down.'\""\n\nAnd this was narrated as marfu'"," but its being marfu' is not authentic. [Weak]"""
"585","(586) Abu Bakr al-Harithi al-Isbahani informed us: Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan informed us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: Abu 'Amir Musa ibn 'Amir narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, and Abu 'Amr informed me from Nafi' that Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to sleep lightly in al-Masjid al-Haram and then perform wudu. [Hasan due to supporting narrations]"
"586","(587) With his chain of narration, al-Walid narrated to us, saying: 'Umar ibn Muhammad informed me from his father, from his grandfather, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar that when sleep overcame him during the night prayer, he would go to his bed and lie down, sleeping the sleep of a bird, then he would spring up, perform wudu, and return to the prayer. [Hasan]"
"587","(588) With his chain of narration, al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Amr informed me from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata' and Mujahid, who both said: \Whoever sleeps while in ruku' or sujud should perform wudu.\"" [Hasan]"""
"588","(589) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Walid al-Faqih narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Bakr narrated to us: Ibn Idris narrated from Hisham, from al-Hasan that he used to hold the view that wudu is required for one who sleeps while sitting.\n\n(al-Thawri narrated it from Hisham, from al-Hasan, who said: \If one sleeps while sitting or standing"," wudu is required upon him.\"")\n\nAnd al-Muzani (may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy upon him) held this opinion. [Weak]"""
"589","(590) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shadh ibn Fayyad narrated to us: Hammad al-Dustawa'i narrated from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: \The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to wait for the late 'Isha prayer until their heads would nod from sleep"," then they would pray without performing wudu.\""\n\nAbu Dawud said: Shu'bah added in it from Qatadah: \""During the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 386]"""
"590","(591) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdah informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us: Tamtam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: \The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to sleep and then stand up and pray without performing wudu"," during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Yahya ibn Habib from Khalid ibn al-Harith from Shu'bah"," without his words \""during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\"" [Sahih. Narrated by al-Daraqutni"," 1/130]"""
"591","(592) Abū Ḥāẓim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us; Ibn Ḥumayd, meaning Muḥammad, narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us; Maʿmar narrated from Qatādah, from Anas, who said: \I saw the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) being woken for prayer"," to the point that I could hear the snoring of one of them. Then they would stand and pray without performing ablution.\""\n\n(Q) Ibn al-Mubārak said: \""This"," according to us"," was while they were seated.\""\n\nIt was upon this that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī and al-Shāfiʿī relied"," and their two narrations on this matter are recorded in the *Khilāfiyāt*.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 616.]\n\n---"""
"592","(593) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl and Dāwūd ibn Shabīb both said: Ḥammād narrated to us from Thābit al-Bunānī that Anas ibn Mālik said: \The ʿIshā' prayer was commenced"," whereupon a man stood and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I have a need.' So he stood and spoke with him privately until the people—or some of them—became drowsy. Then he led them in prayer and did not mention ablution.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Salamah"," without his words \""and did not mention ablution.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"," 40.]\n\n---"""
"593","(594) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us.\n\nAnd Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: \Mālik ibn Anas"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"," Yūnus ibn Yazīd"," al-Layth ibn Saʿd"," and Ibn Samʿān informed you from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to sleep while seated"," then pray and not perform ablution.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah.]\n\n---"""
"594","(595) Abū Ḥāẓim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated from Mughīrah ibn Ziyād, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās—he did not raise it (to the Prophet)—who said: \Whoever sleeps while seated"," there is no ablution upon him; but if he lies down"," then ablution is upon him.\""\n\n(T) And we have narrated something similar from Zayd ibn Thābit"," Abū Hurayrah"," and Abū Umāmah.\n\nSome of our companions used this as evidence.\n\n[Ḥasan.]\n\n---"""
"595","(596) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAbdān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Ḥisāb narrated to us; Qazʿah ibn Suwayd narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Kanīz al-Saqqāʾ narrated to me; Maymūn al-Khayyāṭ narrated from Abī ʿIyāḍ, from Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān, who said: \I was sitting in the mosque of Madīnah"," nodding (with drowsiness)"," when a man embraced me from behind. I turned"," and lo"," it was the Prophet (ﷺ). I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," has ablution become obligatory upon me?' He said: 'No"," until you lay down your side.'\""\n\nThis ḥadīth is narrated uniquely by Baḥr ibn Kanīz al-Saqqāʾ. (J) He is weak"," and his narration cannot be used as evidence.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn ʿAdī"," 2/54.]\n\n---"""
"596","(597) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Jawharī narrated to us; Zakariyyā ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb narrated from Yazīd al-Dālānī, from Qatādah, from Abū al-ʿĀliyah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slept in his prostration until he snored and breathed heavily. I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," you have slept!\"" He said: \""Ablution is only obligatory upon one who lays down his side"," for when he lays down his side"," his joints become loose.\""\n\nThus did a group narrate it from ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb. And some of them said in the ḥadīth: \""Ablution is only upon one who sleeps lying down"," for when he lies down"," his joints become loose.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr"," 12748.]\n\n---"""
"597","(598) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr al-Salūlī narrated from ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb, and he mentioned it with his chain, saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Ablution is not obligatory upon one who sleeps while seated"," standing"," or in prostration"," until he lays down his side"," for when he lays down his side"," his joints become loose.\""\n\nYazīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," Abū Khālid al-Dālānī"," is the only one who narrated this ḥadīth in this particular form.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: \""I asked Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī about this ḥadīth"," and he said: 'This is nothing.'\""\n\n(T) Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated it from Qatādah"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," as his own statement"," and he did not mention Abū al-ʿĀliyah in it. (J) And I do not know of Abū Khālid al-Dālānī having heard (directly) from Qatādah.\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us"," saying: Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī said: His statement—\""Ablution is upon one who sleeps lying down\""—is a reprehensible (munkar) ḥadīth"," narrated only by Yazīd al-Dālānī from Qatādah.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: Shuʿbah said: \""Qatādah only heard four aḥādīth from Abū al-ʿĀliyah: the ḥadīth of Yūnus ibn Mattá"," the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar regarding prayer"," the ḥadīth 'Judgments are three","' and the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbbās—he narrated to me by reliable men among them"," ʿUmar"," and the one most pleasing to me among them is ʿUmar—regarding 'There is no prayer after the ʿAṣr.'\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: He also heard the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbbāth regarding what is said at the time of distress"," and his ḥadīth regarding the vision of the Prophet (ﷺ) of Mūsā and others on the night of the Isrāʾ.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: \""I mentioned the ḥadīth of Yazīd al-Dālānī to Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," and he said: 'What has Yazīd al-Dālānī to do with inserting himself among the companions of Qatādah?'\""\n\nThe Sheikh said"," meaning by this what al-Bukhārī mentioned"," that it is not known that Abū Khālid al-Dālānī heard (directly) from Qatādah.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: \""And a group narrated its beginning from Ibn ʿAbbās without mentioning any of this.\""\n\n(T) And ʿIkrimah said: \""The Prophet (ﷺ) was protected (maḥfūẓ).\""\n\nAnd ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""My eyes sleep"," but my heart does not sleep.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf.]\n\n---"""
"598","(599) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ayyūb, Ḥumayd, and Ḥammād al-Kūfī, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slept until his snoring was heard. Then he stood and prayed and did not perform ablution. ʿIkrimah said: \Indeed"," the Prophet (ﷺ) was protected (maḥfūẓ).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 138.]\n\n---"""
"599","(600) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; al-Firyābī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Kurayb, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet (ﷺ) slept until he breathed heavily (snored), then stood and prayed and did not perform ablution.\n\nIt is narrated in the two *Ṣaḥīḥs* from the ḥadīth of al-Thawrī, without the addition that Abū Khālid al-Dālānī narrated uniquely.\n\n(T) And likewise, Saʿīd ibn Jubayr and others narrated it from Ibn ʿAbbāth in the ḥadīth of overnight stay, without that addition.\n\n(Q) This sleep of his was while he was lying down, and he (ﷺ) would leave ablution from it as a special dispensation. What indicates this is what...\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]\n\n---"
"600","(601) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed me; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us; Sufyān said: ʿAmr heard Kurayb narrating from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \I spent a night with my aunt Maymūnah. When part of the night had passed"," the Prophet (ﷺ) stood and performed ablution from a hanging water-skin"," a light ablution—ʿAmr would demonstrate it"," making it very minimal—then he stood to pray. So I stood and performed ablution similar to what he had performed"," then I stood to his left. He turned me and placed me to his right. Then he prayed as Allah willed"," then he lay down and slept until he snored. Then the caller came and announced the prayer to him.\""\n\nAnd Sufyān said on another occasion: \""Then he stood for the prayer and prayed with us and did not perform ablution.\""\n\nSufyān said: \""We said to ʿAmr: 'Some people say that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sleeps with his eyes but his heart does not sleep.'\"" ʿAmr said: \""I heard ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr say: 'The dreams of the Prophets are revelation (waḥy).' And he recited: {Indeed"," I see in a dream that I am sacrificing you} [al-Ṣāffāt: 102].\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim and Ibn Abī ʿUmar"," from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah"," except that they both said: Sufyān said: \""This is specific to the Prophet (ﷺ)"," because it has reached us that the Prophet (ﷺ) sleeps with his eyes but his heart does not sleep.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 117.]"""
"601","(602) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdūs informed us; ʿUthmān al-Dārimī narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us — from what he recited to Mālik — from Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿĀʾishah, in a mention she made regarding the night prayer, she said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allāh"," do you sleep before you pray Witr?' He said: 'O ʿľishah"," my two eyes sleep"," but my heart does not sleep.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik.\n\n(T) And it has been narrated to us from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," from Abū Hurayrah"," and from Anas ibn Mālik"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," that which indicates that his eyes would sleep but his heart would not sleep.\n\nAnas ibn Mālik said: \""Such is the case with the Prophets — the blessings of Allāh be upon them — their eyes sleep but their hearts do not sleep.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (9/19).]"""
"602","(603) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh — that is, Ibn al-Mubārak — narrated to us; Ḥaywah ibn Shurayḥ informed us; Abū Ṣakhr informed me that he heard Yazīd ibn Qusayṭ say:\n\nHe heard Abū Hurayrah say: \There is no wuḍūʾ upon one who sleeps while sitting cross-legged"," nor upon one who sleeps while standing"," nor upon one who sleeps in prostration"," until he lies down. When he lies down"," he should perform wuḍūʾ.\"" And this is mawqūf.\n\n[Ḥasan.]"""
"603","(604) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūnus narrated to us.\n\n(H) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Abī ʿĀʾishah narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, who said: I entered upon ʿĀʾishah — may Allāh be pleased with her — and said: \Will you not narrate to me about the illness of the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ?\"" She said: \""Yes. The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ became heavy [with illness] and said: 'Have the people prayed?' We said: 'No"," O Messenger of Allāh; they are waiting for you.' He said: 'Place water for me in the vessel.' We did so"," and he performed ghusl. Then he tried to stand up"," but he lost consciousness. Then he regained consciousness and said: 'Have the people prayed?' We said: 'No"," they are waiting for you"," O Messenger of Allāh.' He said: 'Place water for me in the vessel.' We did so"," and he performed ghusl. Then he tried to stand up"," but he lost consciousness. Then he regained consciousness and said: 'Have the people prayed?' We said: 'No"," they are waiting for you"," O Messenger of Allāh.' He said: 'Place water for me in the vessel.' We did so"," and he performed ghusl. Then he tried to stand up"," but he lost consciousness. Then he regained consciousness and said: 'Have the people prayed?' We said: 'No"," and they are waiting for you"," O Messenger of Allāh.' She said: The people were dozing in the mosque"," waiting for the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ for the last ʿIshāʾ prayer. She said: So the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ sent to Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\""\n\nHe mentioned the hadith. The wording of both is the same. The remainder of the hadith is in the book of Ṣalāh. Al-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus.\n\n(Q) And performing ghusl during unconsciousness is something the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ considered recommended"," though wuḍūʾ is sufficient"," if Allāh the Most High wills.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (655).]"""
"604","(605) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us; my grandfather narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān — from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from Ibn ʿUmar, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allāh be pleased with him — said: \Indeed"," kissing is from touching (al-lams)"," so perform wuḍūʾ from it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ḥākim narrated it (1/229).]"""
"605","(606) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, from Shuʿbah, from Mukhāriq, from Ṭāriq ibn Shihāb, that ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Ibn Masʿūd — said regarding the words of the Most High: \Or you touched women\"" (al-Māʾidah 5:6): \""It means words [referring to] other than intercourse.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ḥākim narrated it (1/221).]"""
"606","(607) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Bālawayh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Jawharī narrated to us; Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from Abū ʿUbaydah, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \Kissing is from touching (al-lams)"," and wuḍūʾ is required for it. And al-lams is other than intercourse.\""\n\n(T) Thus narrated al-Thawrī and Shuʿbah from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ from other than him.]"""
"607","(608) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us.\n\nAnd Abū Aḥmad al-ʿAdl informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim, from his father, who said: \A man's kissing of his wife and touching her body with his hand are from al-mulāmasah (touching). So whoever kisses his wife or touches her with his hand"," wuḍūʾ is incumbent upon him.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of al-Shāfiʿī — may Allāh be pleased with him. And in the narration of Ibn Bukayr: \""Then wuḍūʾ has become obligatory upon him.\""\n\n(Q) This is the position of ʿUmar"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar. Ibn ʿAbbās opposed them and interpreted al-mulāmasah mentioned in the Noble Book as referring to intercourse"," and he did not consider wuḍūʾ to be required for kissing.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it (95).]"""
"608","(609) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us, from Shuʿbah, from Abū Bishr, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: \We discussed al-lams (touching)"," and some of the mawālī said: 'It is not from intercourse.' And some of the Arabs said: 'It is from intercourse.' I mentioned that to Ibn ʿAbbās"," and he said: 'With which of them were you?' I said: 'With the mawālī.' He said: 'The mawālī are mistaken. Indeed"," al-lams and al-mubāsharah (physical contact) are from intercourse. However"," Allāh"," the Mighty and Majestic"," employs allusion (kināyah) as He wills with what He wills. And the statement of the one whose view accords with the apparent meaning of the Book is more deserving.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"609","(610) Some of our companions cited as evidence what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Mūsā informed me; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā and Yaḥyā ibn al-Mughīrah both said: Jarīr narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Muʿādh ibn Jabal, that he was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came to him and said: \O Messenger of Allāh"," what do you say about a man who has been with a woman who is not lawful for him"," and he did not leave anything that a man does with his wife except that he did it with her"," except that he did not have intercourse with her?\"" He said: \""Perform wuḍūʾ"," a good wuḍūʾ"," then stand and pray.\""\n\nHe said: Then Allāh"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed this verse: \""Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the approaches of the night\"" (Hūd 114). He said: \""Is it specifically for him"," or for the Muslims in general?\"" He said: \""Rather"," it is for the Muslims in general.\""\n\n(T) And thus narrated Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah and Abū ʿĀwānah from ʿAbd al-Malik"," and in it there is irsāl. (J) ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā did not meet Muʿādh ibn Jabal. [Ṣaḥīḥ"," without the command to perform wuḍūʾ. Al-Ḥākim narrated it (1/229).]"""
"610","(611) As for the hadith which Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī narrated to us in al-Kūfah; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAbsī narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, that the Prophet ﷺ kissed one of his wives and then went out to pray and did not perform wuḍūʾ.\n\n(J) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, and the hadith of al-Aʿmash from Ḥabīb from ʿUrwah was mentioned to him. He said: \Indeed"," Sufyān al-Thawrī was the most knowledgeable of people about this. He claimed that Ḥabīb did not hear anything from ʿUrwah.\""\n\nAnd Abū Bakr informed us; ʿAlī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Ṣāliḥ ibn Aḥmad narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us"," saying: I heard Yaḥyā"," and the hadith of al-Aʿmash from Ḥabīb from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah was mentioned — regarding praying even if blood drips onto the mat"," and regarding kissing. Yaḥyā said: \""Narrate from me that they are both virtually nothing.\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Makhlad al-Ṭālaqānī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Maghrāʾ narrated to us; al-Aʿmash informed us; some of our companions informed us"," from ʿUrwah al-Muzanī"," from ʿĀʾishah"," with this hadith.\n\n(J) Abū Dāwūd said: It was narrated from al-Thawrī that he said: \""Ḥabīb did not narrate to us except from ʿUrwah al-Muzanī\"" — meaning he did not narrate to them from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr anything. The Shaykh said: Thus the hadith reverts to the narration of ʿUrwah al-Muzanī"," and he is unknown (majhūl).\n\n[Ḥasan from other than him. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (178).]"""
"611","(612) As for the hadith narrated to us by Abu Tahir al-Faqih, who was informed by Abu Bakr al-Qattan, who was informed by Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami, who was informed by Abd al-Razzaq, who was informed by Sufyan, from Abu Rawq, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from A'ishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would kiss after performing ablution and then would not repeat the ablution. She said: \Then he would pray.\"" This is a mursal hadith.\n\n(b) Ibrahim al-Taymi did not hear from A'ishah"," as stated by Abu Dawud al-Sijistani and others.\n\n(c) And Abu Rawq is not strong; Yahya ibn Ma'in and others deemed him weak.\n\n(d) And Abu Hanifah narrated it from Abu Rawq"," from Ibrahim"," from Hafsah. (c) And Ibrahim did not hear from A'ishah nor from Hafsah"," as stated by al-Daraqutni and others.\n\n(e) And we have narrated all that has been narrated on this topic and have explained its weaknesses in al-Khilafiyat.\n\n(f) And the authentic hadith from A'ishah concerns kissing while fasting"," so the weak narrators applied it to the matter of not repeating ablution. Had its chain been sound"," we would have acted upon it"," if Allah the Most High wills. [Hasan due to supporting evidence. Narrated by al-Daraqutni"," 1/141]"""
"612","(613) Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan informed us, who was informed by Ahmad ibn Ubayd al-Saffar, who was informed by Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Milhan, who was informed by Yahya, who was informed by al-Layth.\n\n(h) And Abu Sa'd Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Uthman al-Zahid narrated to us by dictation, and Abu Salih ibn Abi Tahir al-Anbari said: Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi informed us, who was informed by Ahmad ibn Salamah, who was informed by Qutaybah ibn Sa'id al-Thaqafi, who was informed by al-Layth, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zurqi, that he heard Abu Qatadah say: \While we were sitting in the mosque"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out to him carrying Umamah bint Abi al-As ibn al-Rabi'"," whose mother was Zainab bint Rasul (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and she was a young girl. He carried her on his shoulder. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed while she was on his shoulder; he would set her down when he bowed"," and would lift her up when he stood"," until he completed his prayer"," doing this with her.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Walid"," and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah"," both from al-Layth ibn Sa'd. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 494]"""
"613","(614) Abu al-Hafiz Abu Abdullah and Abu Uthman Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdan and Abu Sadiq Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fawaris al-Attar said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, who was informed by al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan al-Amiri, who was informed by Abu Usamah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from A'ishah, who said: \I missed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) one night"," so I searched for him with my hand"," and my hand fell upon his two feet while they were placed upright and he was in prostration"," and he was saying: 'O Allah"," I seek refuge in Your well-being from Your punishment"," and I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your displeasure"," and I seek refuge in You from You. I cannot enumerate praise upon You; You are as You have praised Yourself.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from Abu Usamah"," without his words: \""and he was in prostration.\"" (t) And Wuhaib"," al-Mu'tamir"," and Ibn Numayr narrated it from Ubayd Allah without mentioning Abu Hurayrah in its chain. [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 486]"""
"614","(615) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri informed us, who was informed by al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who was informed by Yusuf ibn Ya'qub, who was informed by Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, who was informed by Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ubayd Allah, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad. He said: A'ishah said.\n\n(h) And Abu al-Hafiz Abu Abdullah informed me, who was informed by Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Bindar al-Zahid, who was informed by Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Bujayr, who was informed by Amr ibn Ali, who was informed by Yahya ibn Sa'id, who was informed by Ubayd Allah, who was informed by al-Qasim, from A'ishah, who said: \Evil is what you have compared us to dogs and donkeys! I have seen myself while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was praying and I was lying between him and the qiblah. When he intended to prostrate"," he would nudge my legs"," and I would draw them in.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of Amr. And in the hadith of al-Muqaddami: \""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) praying while I was lying across. When he intended to prostrate"," he nudged me"," and I drew in my legs.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it from Amr ibn Ali.\n\n(t) And in the narration of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father: \""Until when he intended to pray the Witr"," he touched me with his leg.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of Abu Salamah from A'ishah: \""When he prostrated"," he nudged me"," and I drew in my legs.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of Urwah from A'ishah: \""When he intended to pray the Witr"," he woke me"," and I prayed the Witr.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 489]"""
"615","(616) Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Muzaki narrated to us, who was informed by Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who was informed by al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman, who was informed by al-Shafi'i, who was informed by Malik, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr say: \I entered upon Marwan ibn al-Hakam"," and we discussed what necessitates ablution. Marwan said: 'Ablution is required from touching the private part.' Urwah said: 'I did not know that.' Marwan said: 'Busrah bint Safwan informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \""When any one of you touches his private part"," let him perform ablution.\""'\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Malik"," 89]"""
"616","(617) And Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated it from Malik and added: \Let him perform his ablution for prayer.\""\n\nAbu al-Mihrajani informed us"," who was informed by Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzaki"," who was informed by Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Abdi"," who was informed by Ibn Bukayr"," who was informed by Malik"," and he mentioned it. [Sahih. Narrated by Ibn Hibban"," 1116]"""
"617","(618) Abu Zakariyya and Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and others said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, who was informed by Bahr ibn Nahr, who said: It was recited to Ibn Wahb: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman informed you, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Busrah bint Safwan, who said: \She had accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)\"": that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""When any one of you touches his private part"," let him not pray until he performs ablution.\"" (t) And thus Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated it from Hisham ibn Urwah"," from his father"," from Busrah"," and he mentioned Hisham's audition from his father. [Hasan due to supporting evidence. Narrated by al-Daraqutni"," 1/46]"""
"618","(619) And Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, who was informed by Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Qattan, who was informed by Abu Yahya Abd al-Karim ibn al-Haytham, who was informed by Abu al-Yaman, who informed me: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed me, from al-Zuhri, who informed me: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm informed me that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr say: \Marwan ibn al-Hakam"," during his governorship over Madinah"," mentioned that ablution is required from touching the private part when a man's hand reaches it. I rejected that and said: 'There is no ablution upon the one who touches it.' Marwan said: 'Busrah bint Safwan informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mention what ablution is required from.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'And ablution is required from touching the private part.'\"" Urwah said: \""I continued to argue with Marwan until he sent one of his guards to Busrah to ask her about what she had narrated. Busrah sent back to him the same as what Marwan had narrated to me about her.\""\n\nAnd Hisham ibn Urwah narrated it from his father"," from Marwan"," from Busrah. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Nasa'i"," 164]"""
"619","(620) Abu al-Hafiz Abu Abdullah and Abu Tahir al-Imam and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi Amr said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, who was informed by Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam, who was informed by Anas ibn Iyad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Marwan, from Busrah bint Safwan, who had accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When any one of you touches his private part"," let him not pray until he performs ablution.\""\n\n(t) And Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated it from Hisham"," from his father"," from Busrah"," and he mentioned Hisham's audition from his father. As for his father's audition from Busrah and his direct conversation with her about the hadith after hearing it from Marwan"," that is another matter. [Sahih]"""
"620","(621) Abu al-Hafiz Abu Abdullah informed us, who was informed by Abu al-Walid Hassan ibn Muhammad al-Faqih, among others, who said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, who was informed by Muhammad ibn Rafi', who was informed by Ibn Abi Fudayk, who was informed by Rabi'ah ibn Uthman, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, from Busrah bint Safwan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever touches his private part"," let him perform ablution.\"" Urwah said: \""So I asked Busrah"," and she confirmed it.\"" [Hasan due to supporting evidence. Narrated by Abu Dawud"," 181]"""
"621","(622) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Muḥammad Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Nuṣayr al-Khawwāṣ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Abān narrated to us: ʿAnbasah ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from Marwān, from Busrah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever touches his private part should not perform prayer until he performs wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nHe (the narrator) said: \""So I went to Busrah and she narrated to me just as Marwān had narrated to me from her"," that she heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say that.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 1/232]"""
"622","(623) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Shuʿayb ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah informed me, from his father, that Marwān narrated to him from Busrah bint Ṣafwān — who had accompanied the Prophet (ﷺ) — that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \When any one of you touches his private part"," let him not perform prayer until he performs wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nHe (the narrator) said: \""ʿUrwān denied that"," so he asked Busrah"," and she confirmed it with what he had said.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains]"""
"623","(624) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, both saying: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Shuʿayb ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, and he mentioned the hadith with its chain, similar to it.\n\n(T) ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ said: Rabiʿah ibn ʿUthmān, al-Mundhir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, ʿAnbasah ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid, and Ḥumayd ibn al-Aswad followed him in narrating it, reporting it from Hishām, from his father, from Marwān, from Busrah. ʿUrwah said: \So I asked Busrah after that"," and she confirmed it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains]"""
"624","(625) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Baghdādī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us. He said: I heard ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī, and he mentioned the hadith of Shuʿayb ibn Isḥāq from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah in which ʿUrwah's hearing from Busrah is mentioned. ʿAlī said: \This is among the things that indicate that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd has preserved from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," from his father"," that he said: 'Busrah informed me.'\""\n\nʿAlī said: \""Abū al-Aswad Ḥumayd ibn al-Aswad narrated to me"," from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," from his father"," from Marwān"," from Busrah bint Ṣafwān — who had accompanied the Prophet (ﷺ) — that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'When any one of you touches his private part"," let him not perform prayer until he performs wuḍūʾ.'\""\n\nʿUrwah denied that and asked Busrah"," and she confirmed it.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: My father informed me: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us"," saying: Al-Shāfiʿī used to obligate wuḍūʾ from touching the private part"," following the report of Busrah bint Ṣafwān"," not by analogy (qiyās).\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī says: \""I say this because ʿUrwah has heard the hadith of Busrah from her.\""\n\n(J) The Shaykh said: Busrah bint Ṣafwān ibn Nawfal ibn Asad was among the women who gave the pledge of allegiance (al-mubāyiʿāt)"," and Waraqah ibn Nawfal was her paternal uncle. She was the wife of Muʿāwiyah ibn al-Mughīrah ibn Abī al-ʿĀṣ — this was stated by Muṣʿab al-Zubayrī. And she was the grandmother of ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān"," the mother of his mother — this was stated by Mālik ibn Anas.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains]"""
"625","(626) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Ḥumayd narrated to us, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Ḥārith, from Makḥūl, from ʿAnbasah ibn Abī Sufyān, from Umm Ḥabībah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), that she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever touches his private part should perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥamdān al-Jallāb narrated to us: Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us: Abū Mushir ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Mushir narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Ḥumayd narrated to us"," and he mentioned it similarly.\n\nAnd it has reached me from Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī"," who said: \""I asked Abū Zurʿah about the hadith of Umm Ḥabībah"," and he considered it good (istaḥsanahu)"," and I saw him counting it among the preserved (maḥfūẓ) narrations.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains. Ibn Mājah narrated it"," 481]"""
"626","(627) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Baghdādī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us: Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad al-Farwī informed us: Yazīd ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Nawfalī narrated to us, from al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever touches his private part"," wuḍūʾ is incumbent upon him.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains. Ibn ʿAdī narrated it"," 2/413]"""
"627","(628) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī al-ʿAdl informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us, from Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn Saʿd ibn Abī Wāqqāṣ, from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, that he said: \I was holding the muṣḥaf for Saʿd ibn Abī Wāqqāṣ"," and I experienced an itch. Saʿd said: 'Perhaps you have touched your private part?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Get up and perform wuḍūʾ.' So I got up and performed wuḍūʾ"," then I returned.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it"," 90]"""
"628","(629) And with his chain, he said: Mālik narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that he used to say: \When a man touches his private part"," wuḍūʾ becomes obligatory upon him.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it"," 91]"""
"629","(630) And with his chain, he said: Mālik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that he said: \I saw ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar performing ghusl and then performing wuḍūʾ. I said to him: 'O father"," does the ghusl suffice you from wuḍūʾ?' He said: 'Yes"," indeed"," but sometimes I touch my private part"," so I perform wuḍūʾ.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it"," 93]"""
"630","(631) And with his chain, he said: Mālik narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that he said: \I was with ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar on a journey"," and I saw him after the sun had risen perform wuḍūʾ and then pray. I said to him: 'This is a prayer that you did not use to perform.' He said: 'After I had performed wuḍūʾ for the morning prayer"," I touched my private part"," and then I forgot to perform wuḍūʾ. So I performed wuḍūʾ and then returned to my prayer.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it"," 94]"""
"631","(632) And by his isnad, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Hisham ibn `Urwah, from his father, that he used to say: \Whoever touches his penis"," then wudu' has become obligatory upon him.\""\n\n(T) And we have been narrated in that regard from `A'ishah and Abu Hurayrah"," and al-Shafi`i narrated in al-Qadim from Muslim and Sa`id"," from Ibn Jurayj"," from Ibn Abi Mulaykah: that `Umar ibn al-Khattab"," while he was leading the people in prayer"," his hand slipped upon his penis"," so he gestured to the people: \""Remain where you are.\"" Then he went out"," performed wudu'"," and returned"," and completed for them what remained of the prayer. [Sahih. Malik narrated it (92)]"""
"632","(633) Abu Bakr informed us: Ahmad ibn `Ali al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri' informed us: Abu Ja`far ibn Salamah, that is al-Tahawi, narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Shu`ayb narrated to us: `Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Shu`bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, that Ibn `Umar and Ibn `Abbas used to say regarding a man who touches his penis: \He must perform wudu'.\"" Shu`bah said: I said to Qatadah: \""From whom is this?\"" He said: \""From `Ata'.\"" [Da`if. Al-Tahawi narrated it in Sharh al-Ma`ani (1/76)]"""
"633","(634) Abu Sa`d informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sufi informed us: Abu Ahmad ibn `Adi al-Hafiz informed us: al-Qasim ibn al-Layth and `Abd al-Samad ibn `Abd Allah said: Hisham ibn `Ammar narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: `Abd al-Rahman ibn Namir al-Yahsubi narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from `Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that he heard Marwan ibn al-Hakam saying: Busrat bint Safwan al-Asadiyyah informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanding wudu' for touching the penis, and the woman is the same as that.\n\nAbu Ahmad ibn `Adi said: And this hadith, with this addition in its matn — \and the woman is the same as that\"" — no one other than Ibn Namir narrates it from al-Zuhri.\n\n(T) The Sheikh said: And thus it was narrated by Harun ibn Ziyad al-Hanna'i from al-Walid ibn Muslim"," and Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated it from al-Walid ibn Muslim"," correctly in both the isnad and the matn. [Da`if]"""
"634","(635) Abu al-Hasan ibn `Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn `Ubayd narrated to us: `Ubayd ibn Sharik narrated to us: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, from `Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, that he said: `Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm informed me that he heard `Urwah ibn al-Zubayr saying: Marwan ibn al-Hakam mentioned during his governorship over al-Madinah that wudu' is performed when one touches his penis with his hand and reaches it. I rejected that and said: \There is no wudu' for the one who touches it.\"" Marwan said: \""Nay"," Busrat bint Safwan informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioning what wudu' is performed for","\"" and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""And wudu' is performed for touching the penis.\"" `Urwah said: \""I continued to dispute with Marwan until he called a man from his guards and sent him to Busrat to ask her about what she had narrated regarding that"," and Busrat sent to him the same as what Marwan had narrated to me about her.\"" This is the correct version from the hadith of al-Zuhri. [Sahih. Al-Nasa'i narrated it (164)]"""
"635","(636) Abu Sa`id ibn Abi `Amr informed us: Abu `Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya`qub al-Shaybani narrated to us: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from `Abd al-Rahman ibn Namir, who said: I asked al-Zuhri about a woman touching her vulva — must she perform wudu'? He said: `Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr informed me, from `Urwah, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, from Busrat bint Safwan, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you reaches with his hand to his private part"," let him perform wudu'.\"" He said: \""And the woman is likewise.\""\n\nThe apparent meaning of this indicates that his statement \""and the woman is likewise\"" is the statement of al-Zuhri"," and what indicates this is that all other narrators narrated it from al-Zuhri without this addition.\n\n(T) And that was narrated in the hadith of Isma`il ibn `Ayyash from Hisham ibn `Urwah from his father"," but it is not preserved. [Sahih li-ghayrihi. Al-Nasa'i narrated it (445)]"""
"636","(637) Abu `Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa`id ibn Abi `Amr and Abu Bakr ibn Raja' al-Adib and Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn `Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Nawqani — in Harat — they said: Abu al-`Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya`qub narrated to us: Abu `Utbah Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Hijazi al-Himsi narrated to us: Baqiyyat ibn al-Walid narrated to me: al-Zubaydi narrated to me: `Amr ibn Shu`ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Any man who touches his private part"," let him perform wudu'"," and any woman who touches her private part"," let her perform wudu'.\""\n\n(T) And Ishaq al-Hanzali narrated it from Baqiyyah"," from al-Zubaydi Muhammad ibn al-Walid. (J) And Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi is thiqah.\n\n(T) And thus it was narrated by `Abd Allah ibn al-Mu'mal from `Amr"," and it was narrated from another direction from `Amr. [Sahih li-ghayrihi. Al-Daraqutni narrated it (1/147)]"""
"637","(638) Abu Sa`d al-Malini informed us: Abu Ahmad ibn `Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us: Ibn Qutaybah and Ahmad ibn `Umayr said: Idris, that is Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us: Damrat ibn Rabi`ah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Rashid narrated to us: `Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, from his father, from `Amr ibn Shu`ayb — and he mentioned it with its isnad and its meaning.\n\nAbu Ahmad said: This is, from the hadith of Ibn Thawban from his father from `Amr, gharib.\n\nThe Sheikh said: And al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabah contradicted them regarding `Amr in his isnad, and he is not strong. [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"
"638","(639) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-`Alawi informed us: Abu al-`Abbas `Abd Allah ibn Ya`qub al-Kirmani, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ya`qub al-Kirmani — narrated to us: `Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us: al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabah, from `Amr ibn Shu`ayb, from Sa`id ibn al-Musayyib, from Busrat bint Safwan, one of the women of Banu Kinanah, that she said: \O Messenger of Allah"," what do you say about one of us who touches her private part"," and the man who touches his penis after having performed wudu'?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to her: \""She must perform wudu'"," O Busrat bint Safwan.\""\n\n`Amr said"," and Sa`id ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me: that Marwan sent to her to ask her"," and she said: \""Leave me"," I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while so-and-so and so-and-so and `Abd Allah ibn `Umar were with him"," and he commanded me to perform wudu'.\""\n\nAbu `Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu `Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Buttah al-Isbahani narrated to us from the original of his book. [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"""
"639","(640) `Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Zakariyyah al-Isbahani narrated to us: Muhriz ibn Salamah al-`Adani narrated to us: `Abd al-`Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from `Ubayd Allah ibn `Umar, from al-Qasim, from `A'ishah, who said: \If a woman touches her private part"," she must perform wudu'.\""\n\n(T) And thus it was narrated by `Abd Allah al-`Umari from his brother `Ubayd Allah. [Sahih li-ghayrihi. Al-Hakim narrated it (1/223)]"""
"640","(641) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Ashnani informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn `Abdus al-Tarafi`i narrated to us: `Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us: `Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Yazid ibn `Abd al-Malik al-Nawfali, from Sa`id ibn Abi Sa`id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever reaches with his hand to his private part"," with no barrier between them"," the wudu' of prayer has become obligatory upon him.\""\n\n(T) And thus it was narrated by Ma`n ibn `Isa and a group of thiqat from Yazid ibn `Abd al-Malik"," except that they spoke critically of Yazid.\n\n(J) And Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us: `Abd Allah ibn Ja`far al-Nahwi narrated to us: Ya`qub ibn Sufyan narrated to me: al-Fadl ibn Ziyad said: I asked Abu `Abd Allah"," that is Ahmad ibn Hanbal"," about Yazid ibn `Abd al-Malik al-Nawfali"," and he said: \""A shaykh from the people of al-Madinah"," there is no harm in him.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: And for Abu Hurayrah there is an origin for it. [Hasan li-ghayrihi. Al-Tabarani narrated it in al-Awsat (110)]"""
"641","(642) Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Fārsiyy informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Aṣbahāniyy informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn Fāris narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī narrated to us; Ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad narrated to us; he heard ʿUmar ibn Abī Wahb; he heard Jamīl ibn Bashīr.\n\nFrom Abū Hurayrah: Whoever touches his private part with his hand, let him perform wuḍūʾ.\n\nThis is reported as a mawqūf (stopped) narration. It is also said that Jamīl reported from Abū Wahb, from Abū Hurayrah.\n\n[Weak. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Tārīkh al-Kabīr 2/216]"
"642","(643) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Hārūn ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us; from ʿUmar ibn Abī Wahb; from Jamīl al-ʿIjlī; from Abū Wahb al-Khuzāʿī.\n\nFrom Abū Hurayrah, who said: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform wuḍūʾ. And whoever touches it — meaning through the garment — there is no wuḍūʾ upon him.\n\n[Weak. Abū Nuʿaym narrated it in al-Ḥilyah 9/44]"
"643","(644) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Nāfiʿ and Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated to us; from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb; from ʿUqbah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān; from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you touches his private part with his hand"," let him perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nIbn Nāfiʿ added: from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān"," from Jābir"," from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: I heard more than one of the ḥuffāẓ narrate it without mentioning Jābir in it.\n\nAbū Saʿīd added in his hadith:\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""Al-ifḍāʾ (touching) with the hand refers specifically to the palm"," just as it is said 'he extended his hand in pledge' and 'he extended his hand to the ground in prostration' and 'he extended his hand to his knees in rukūʿ.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it"," 35]"""
"644","(645) As for the hadith which Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us of; Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Mulāzim ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥanafī narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Badr narrated to us; from Qays ibn Ṭalq; from his father Ṭalq ibn ʿAlī, who said: We went out to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ as a delegation until we came to him. We gave him our pledge of allegiance and prayed with him. Then a man came who seemed to be a Bedouin and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," what do you say about a man touching his private part after he has performed wuḍūʾ?\"" He said: \""It is but a piece or a morsel of your own body.\""\n\nThis is the hadith as narrated by Mulāzim ibn ʿAmr.\n\nAbū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣibghī said: \""There is a question regarding Mulām.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Muḥammad ibn Jābir al-Yamāmiyy and Ayyūb ibn ʿUtbah narrated it from Qays ibn Ṭalq"," and both of them are weak.\n\nʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār narrated from Qays that Ṭalq asked the Prophet ﷺ"," and he sent it as a mursal narration.\n\nʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār is the best of those who narrated from Qays.\n\nThere is disagreement regarding the grading of ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār. Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān and Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal criticized him"," and al-Bukhārī declared him very weak.\n\nAs for Qays ibn Ṭalq"," al-Zaʿfarānī narrated from al-Shāfiʿī that he said: \""We asked about Qays but did not find anyone who knew him in a manner that would make us accept his report.\""\n\nThis hadith has been opposed by those whose reliability"," soundness in hadith"," and firmness we have described.\n\nIn what Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us of — Abū Bakr informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Naqqāsh narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā al-Qāḍī al-Sarakhsī narrated to us; Rajāʾ ibn Murajjā al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us"," mentioning a story in which he said: Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn said: \""The people have spoken much about Qays ibn Ṭalq"," but his hadith is not used as a proof.\""\n\nAbū Bakr al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Ibn Abī Ḥātim said: \""I asked my father and Abū Zurʿah about the hadith of Muḥammad ibn Jābir"," and they said: 'Qays ibn Ṭalq is not one through whom a proof is established.' They weakened him and did not confirm him.\""\n\nFurthermore"," if this hadith is authentic"," it dates to the beginning of the Hijrah when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was building his mosque. The hearing of Abū Hurayrah and others from whom we have narrated on this topic came after that"," and it is in that context.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 182]"""
"645","(645) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ al-Mihrajānī narrated to us therein; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us; from Muḥammad ibn Jābir, who said: Qays ibn Ṭalq narrated to me from his father, who said: \I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was building the mosque"," and he said: 'Mix the clay"," for you know best how to mix it"," O Yamāmī.' Then I asked him — or a man asked him — 'What do you say about a man who performs wuḍūʾ and then touches his private part?' He said: 'It is only from you (i.e."," part of your body).'\""\n\nSome of our companions interpreted this as referring to touching it with the back of the hand. And in that.\n\n[Weak]"""
"646","(647) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to us; Hammām narrated to us.\n\nMuḥammad ibn Jābir narrated to us; he said: A shaykh of ours from the people of al-Yamāmah, called Qays ibn Ṭalq, narrated to me from his father, who said: He asked the Prophet ﷺ — or he heard a man asking him — he said: \While I was praying"," I began to scratch my thigh"," and my hand touched my private part.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""It is only from you (i.e."," part of your body).\""\n\nThe apparent meaning of the condition of one who scratches his thigh and his hand touches his private part is that he touches it with the back of his hand. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Ḥasan through other chains. Ibn Mājah narrated it"," 483]"""
"647","(648) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Jarrāḥī al-ʿAdl al-Ḥāfiẓ in Marw narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā al-Qāḍī al-Sarakhsī narrated to us; Rajāʾ ibn Murajjā al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: We gathered in the Mosque of al-Khayf — I, Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī, and Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn — and they debated the matter of touching the private part. Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn said: \Wuḍūʾ is required from it.\"" ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī adopted the position of the Kūfans and said the same.\n\nIbn Maʿīn used as evidence the hadith of Busrah bint Ṣafwān"," and ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī used as evidence the hadith of Qays ibn Ṭalq. He said to Yaḥyā: \""How can you accept the chain of Busrah when Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam sent a policeman to her who returned her response to him?\"" Yaḥyā said: \""Then ʿUrwah was not satisfied until he came to Busrah and asked her directly and spoke to her face to face about the hadith.\"" Then Yaḥyā said: \""The people have spoken much about Qays ibn Ṭalq"," and his hadith is not used as a proof.\""\n\nAḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: \""Both matters are as you have said.\"" Yaḥyā said: \""Mālik from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: wuḍūʾ is required from touching the private part.\""\n\nʿAlī said: \""Ibn Masʿūd used to say: 'There is no wuḍūʾ from it; it is but a piece of your body.'\"" Yaḥyā said: \""This is from whom?\"" He said: \""From Sufyān"," from Abū Qays"," from Huzayl"," from ʿAbdullāh.\"" Yaḥyā said: \""When Ibn Masʿūd and Ibn ʿUmar are both present and they differ"," Ibn Masʿūd is more deserving of being followed.\""\n\nAḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: \""Yes"," but Abū Qays al-Awdī — his hadith is not used as a proof.\"" ʿAlī said: \""Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Misʿar narrated to me; from ʿUmayr ibn Saʿīd; from ʿAmmār"," who said: 'I do not care whether I touch it or my nose.'\"" Yaḥyā said: \""Between ʿUmayr ibn Saʿīd and ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir there is a great distance (i.e."," a gap in the chain).\""\n\n[Weak. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 1/234]"""
"648","(649) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Naqqāsh narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā al-Qāḍī al-Sarakhsī narrated to us, and he mentioned it with its chain and part of its meaning.\n\nHe said at the end of it, regarding the hadith of ʿUmayr ibn Saʿīd from ʿAmmār: Aḥmad said: \ʿAmmār and Ibn ʿUmar are equal (in rank). Whoever wishes may take this"," and whoever wishes may take that.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: We have narrated from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī that he said regarding the hadith of Busrah and ʿUrwah's hearing from her"," just as Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn had said. It is as though he retracted on this point to the position of Yaḥyā and adopted the hadith of Busrah.\n\n[Weak. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 1/234]"""
"649","(650) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; he said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm said: ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: \Sufyān and Ibn Jurayj met and discussed touching the private part. Ibn Jurayj said: 'Wuḍūʾ is required from it.' Sufyān said: 'Wuḍūʾ is not required from it.' Sufyān said: 'Tell me"," if a man were to hold semen in his hand"," what would be upon him?' Ibn Jurayj said: 'He would wash his hand.' He said: 'Which is greater — semen or touching the private part?' He said: 'The devil has not placed this on your tongue.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: What Ibn Jurayj intended is that the Sunnah cannot be opposed by analogy (qiyās).\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī mentioned in the narration of al-Zaʿfarānī from him that what was said from the Companions — that there is no wuḍūʾ in it — was said based on personal opinion (raʾy)"," and whoever makes wuḍūʾ obligatory in it does so only by way of following (ittibāʿ). As for the hadith which.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it"," 439]"""
"650","(651) Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿImrān narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ibn Abī Laylā narrated to us; from ʿĪsā; from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā; from Abī Laylā, who said: \We were with the Prophet ﷺ when al-Ḥasan came and began to rub against him. He lifted him from his shirt and kissed his uvula.\""\n\nThis chain is not strong"," and it does not contain the fact that he touched him with his hand and then prayed without performing wuḍūʾ.\n\n[Weak]"""
"651","(652) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Tusi al-Faqih informed us: Abu Bishr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hadir informed us: Abu Bakr, companion of Abu Sakhrata, informed us: Ali, meaning ibn Muslim, informed us —\n\nAnd Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us: Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz informed us: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Wakil narrated to us: Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Busrata bint Safwan, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \Whoever touches his male organ"," or his testicles"," or his pubic region"," let him perform wudu.\""\n\nIn the narration of al-Tusi: \""or his pubic region"," let him perform wudu\"" — his wudu being for prayer.\n\nAli ibn Umar al-Hafiz said: Thus did Abd al-Himid ibn Ja'far narrate it from Hisham"," and he erred in mentioning the testicles and the pubic region"," and in incorporating that into the hadith of Busrata from the Prophet ﷺ. What is correctly preserved is that this is from the statement of Urwah"," not raised (as a prophetic hadith).\n\nLikewise"," the trustworthy narrators transmitted it from Hisham"," among them Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and Hammad ibn Zayd"," and others besides them.\n\n[Weak. Al-Hakim recorded it (1/229).]"""
"652","(653) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu al-Hasan al-Sarraj narrated to us: Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Basri al-Anbari narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us —\n\nAnd Abu Bakr al-Harithi informed us: Ali ibn Umar informed us: Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Mubashshir, and al-Husayn ibn Isma'il, and Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Sarraj said: Abu al-Ash'ath narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Busrata bint Safwan, that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \Whoever touches his male organ"," let him perform wudu.\""\n\nHe said: And Urwah used to say: \""If he touches his pubic region"," or his testicles"," or his male organ"," let him perform wudu.\""\n\n[Hasan. Al-Daraqutni recorded it (1/148).]"""
"653","(654) And Abu Bakr informed us: Ali informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: My father used to say: \If a man touches his pubic region"," or his testicles"," or his private parts"," let him not pray until he performs wudu.\""\n\nAnd this was narrated from Hisham ibn Urwah from another route"," incorporated into the hadith"," and it is an error. The correct position is that it is from the statement of Urwah.\n\nAnd the qiyas (analogical reasoning) is that there is no wudu for touching (the private parts) through clothing. Rather"," we follow the Sunnah in its obligation through touching the private part itself — so it is not obligatory for anything other than that.\n\n[Sahih. Al-Daraqutni recorded it (1/148).]"""
"654","(655) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Darastawayh narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Humaydi said: I heard Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan asking Sufyan, meaning ibn Uyaynah, about this hadith: \We performed tayammum with the Prophet ﷺ up to the shoulders.\""\n\nSufyan said: I was present when Isma'il ibn Umayyah came to al-Zuhri and said: \""O Abu Bakr"," the people reject two of your hadiths.\"" He asked: \""Which are they?\"" He said: \""We performed tayammum with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ up to the shoulders.\""\n\nAl-Zuhri said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah informed me about it"," from his father"," from Ammar"," who said: \""We performed tayammum with the Prophet ﷺ up to the shoulders.\"" Isma'il said: \""And the hadith of Ubayd Allah concerns touching the armpit.\""\n\nIt was as though al-Zuhri fell silent regarding it"," as though he rejected it or disavowed it. So I went to Amr ibn Dinar and informed him"," having heard him narrate it from al-Zuhri. Amr said: \""Yes"," al-Zuhri narrated to me from Ubayd Allah that Umar commanded a man to perform wudu from touching the armpit.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And the hadith of touching the armpit is mursal (disconnected). Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah did not meet Umar ibn al-Khattab"," and al-Zuhri rejected it after having narrated it.\n\nAnd perhaps he (Umar) ordered washing the hand from it for the purpose of cleaning"," and Allah knows best.\n\nAnd it was narrated from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas"," each one of them contradicting his companion in that.\n\n[Weak. Al-Humaydi recorded it in his Musnad (143).]"""
"655","(656) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us: Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: \When a man performs wudu and touches his armpit"," he should repeat the wudu.\""\n\nHe said: And Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us"," from Abi Sinan"," from Sa'id ibn Jubayr"," from Ibn Abbas"," who said: \""There is no repetition (i'adah) required upon him.\""\n\nAnd something in agreement with the position of Ibn Abbas was narrated from Ibn Umar.\n\n[Weak.]"""
"656","(657) Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukkari in Baghdad informed us: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Razi, from Yahya al-Bakka', who said: I saw Ibn Umar insert his hand into his armpit while he was in prayer, and then he continued with his prayer.\n\n[Weak.]"
"657","(658) And Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar narrate from Nafi', that Abd Allah ibn Umar used to perform wudu in the heat and pass his hands over his armpits, and that did not invalidate his wudu.\n\nAnd from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, and Yazid ibn Abi Habib, and Layth ibn Sa'd, and Malik ibn Anas, who said: \There is no wudu for touching the armpit.\"" Ibn Wahb used to say that.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And this is the position of al-Hasan al-Basri and al-Harith al-Ukli among the Tabi'in"," and it is the position of al-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," and our position is in agreement with theirs.\n\n[Weak.]"""
"658","(659) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi Amr said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Sufyan informed us, from Hisham, from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir, who said: I heard my grandmother Asma' say: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about menstrual blood that gets on clothing. He said: \Scrape it off"," then rub it with water"," then sprinkle water on it"," then pray in it.\""\n\nAbu Sa'id added in his narration that al-Shafi'i said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that menstrual blood be washed by hand and did not order wudu for it — and blood is more impure (najis) than the male organ — then anything that is touched by whatever is najis"," the qiyas regarding it is that there should be no wudu from it. And if this is the case with something that is najis"," then that which is not najis is even more deserving of not obligating wudu"," except for that which has a specific text (khabar) concerning it.\n\n[Sahih.]"""
"659","(660) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us: Musa ibn al-Hasan informed us: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by the market, entering from one of the elevated areas, with people on either side of him. He passed by a dead, earless young goat. He picked it up, taking it by its ear, and said: \Which of you would like to have this for a dirham?\"" They said: \""We would not like to have it for anything. What would we do with it?\"" He said: \""Would you like it to be yours?\"" They said: \""By Allah"," even if it were alive"," it would be a defect in it because it is earless — so how about when it is dead?\"" He said: \""Then by Allah"," the world is more insignificant to Allah than it is to you.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from al-Qa'nabi. [Sahih. Muslim recorded it (2957).]"""
"660","(661) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us —\n\nAnd Abu Abd Allah informed us: Ali ibn Isa narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib narrated to us: Ibn Abi Umar narrated to us —\n\nThey both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abi Wa'il, from Abd Allah, who said: We used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ and we would not perform wudu from filth (mastiy') that had been trodden upon.\n\nAnd thus did Abd Allah ibn Idris, and Sharik, and Jarir narrate it from al-A'mash, except that they did not say \with the Prophet ﷺ.\""\n\nAnd Abu Mu'awiyah narrated it in one of his two narrations from him.\n\n[Sahih. Ibn Khuzaymah recorded it (37).]"""
"661","(662) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Shaqīq — or he narrated it from him — who said:\n\nʿAbdullāh said: \We used to pray without tucking up our hair or our garments"," and we would not perform wuḍūʾ from [impurity caused by] treading [on something impure].\""\n\nAnd thus Hannād ibn al-Sarī narrated it from Abū Muʿāwiyah. And Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Muʿāwiyah narrated it"," as Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Hannād ibn al-Sarī and Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Muʿāwiyah narrated to us from Abū Muʿāwiyah from al-Aʿmash from Shaqīq from Masrūq — or he narrated it from him — who said: Abdullāh said. And Hannād said: from Shaqīq — or he narrated it from him — who said: Abdullāh said.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 204]"""
"662","(663) Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Ṣadaqah ibn Yasār narrated to me from ʿAqīl ibn Jābir,\n\nfrom Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: \We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Dhāt al-Riqāʿ"," [during the season] of palm trees. A man from among the Muslims came upon the wife of a man from among the polytheists. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned back [returning]"," her husband came — and he had been absent. When he was informed of the matter"," he swore that he would not cease until he had shed blood among the Companions of Muḥammad. So he set out"," following the tracks of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted at a campsite and said: 'Who is a man who will guard us this night?' A man from the Muhājirūn and a man from the Anṣār volunteered and said: 'We [will]"," O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Then be at the mouth of the valley.'\n\nWhen they went out to the mouth of the valley"," the Anṣārī said to the Muhājirī: 'Which part of the night would you prefer that I cover for you — its beginning or its end?' He said: 'Rather"," cover the first part for me.' So the Muhājirī lay down and slept"," and the Anṣārī stood up to pray.\n\nThe husband of the woman came. When he saw the figure of the man"," he recognized that he was the sentry of the people. He shot an arrow at him"," and it struck him. He [the Anṣārī] pulled it out and placed it [aside]"," and remained standing"," praying. Then he shot another arrow at him"," and it struck him. He pulled it out and placed it [aside]"," and remained standing"," praying. Then he returned to him a third time"," and it struck him. He pulled it out and placed it [aside]. Then he bowed and prodded his companion"," saying: 'Sit"," for you have been struck.' So he sprang up.\n\nWhen the man saw them both"," he realized that they had been alerted"," so he fled. When the Muhājirī saw what had befallen the Anṣārī of blood"," he said: 'Subḥān Allāh! Why did you not alert me the first time he shot at you?' He said: 'I was in a sūrah that I was reciting"," and I did not wish to cut it short until I had completed it. When he persisted in shooting at me"," I bowed and alerted you. By Allah"," were it not that I would be neglecting a post that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to guard"," I would have preferred to have my soul taken before cutting it short or completing it.'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 198]"""
"663","(664) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Abū Tawbah al-Rabīʿ ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, who said: Ṣadaqah ibn Yasār narrated to me from ʀAqīl ibn Jābir from Jābir, and he mentioned it with the same meaning, in abbreviated form. And at the end of it:\n\nWhen the Muhājirī saw what had befallen the Anṣārī of blood, he said: \Subḥān Allāh! Why did you not alert me the first time he shot at you?\"" He said: \""I was in a sūrah that I was reciting"," and I did not wish to cut it short.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 198]"""
"664","(665) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, that when he performed cupping (ḥijāmah), he would wash the sites of the cupping.\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī narrated this in al-Qadīm.\n\nAnd from a man from Layth from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Wash the traces of the cupping from yourself"," and that is sufficient for you.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Anas ibn Mālik from the Prophet ﷺ"," except that in its chain there is weakness.\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"665","(666) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed it; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād narrated to us; Ṣāliḥ ibn Muqātil narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd, Abū Ayyūb al-Qurashī in al-Raqqah, narrated to us; Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed cupping, then prayed and did not perform wuḍūʾ, and did not do more than wash the sites of his cupping.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī 1/151]"
"666","(667) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr — meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah — narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated from al-Taymī from Bakr — meaning Ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Muzanī — who said:\n\nI saw Ibn ʿUmar squeeze a pimple on his face, and some blood came out. He scratched it between his two fingers, then prayed and did not perform wuḍūʾ.\n\nAnd it has been narrated with the meaning of this from Ibn Masʿūd, and from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, and from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh, and from al-Ḥasan, and from Ṭāwūs, and from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad: \There is no wuḍūʾ upon the one who performs cupping.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah 1469]"""
"667","(668) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Zāṭiyā narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us; Muṭarrif ibn Māzin narrated to me; Isḥāq ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī al-Mujālid narrated to me from Abū al-Ḥakam al-Dimashqī that ʿUbadah ibn Nusī narrated to him from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ghanm al-Ashʿarī from Muʿādh ibn Jabal, that he said:\n\n\Wuḍūʾ is not obligatory from nosebleed (ruʿāf)"," vomiting"," touching the private part"," or that which fire has touched.\""\n\nIt was said to him: \""Indeed"," some people say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Perform wuḍūʾ from that which fire has touched.'\"" He said: \""A people heard but did not retain. We used to call washing the hands and the mouth 'wuḍūʾ","' and it is not obligatory. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only commanded the believers to wash their hands and their mouths from that which fire has touched"," and it is not obligatory.\""\n\nMuṭarrif ibn Māzin — they spoke concerning him. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr 134]"""
"668","(669) As for the hadith which Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Ibn Jurayj; ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Mulaykah informed me from ʿĀʾishah from the Prophet ﷺ, who said:\n\n\When one of you vomits"," or has a regurgitation (qalas)"," or has a nosebleed during his prayer"," let him perform wuḍūʾ"," then let him build upon what has passed of his prayer"," so long as he has not spoken.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: \""This hadith was narrated by Ibn ʿAyyāsh once thus"," and once he said: from Ibn Jurayj from his father from ʿĀʾishah — and neither of the two is preserved.\""\n\nAnd Abū Saʿd informed us; Abū Aḥmad narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Abī ʿIṣmah narrated to us; Abū Ṭālib Aḥmad ibn Ḥumayd narrated to us; he said: I heard Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal say: \""Whatever Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from the Syrians is sound"," and whatever he narrated from the people of the Ḥijāz is not sound.\""\n\nHe said: \""And I asked Aḥmad about the hadith of Ibn ʿAyyāsh from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abī Mulaykah from ʿĀʾishah that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever vomits or has a nosebleed…' the hadith.\"" He said: \""Thus did Ibn ʿAyyāsh narrate it. However"," Ibn Jurayj narrated it from his father"," and he did not narrate it as a musnad [continuous] chain from his father; ʿĀʾishah is not in it.\""\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 1221]"""
"669","(670) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and Ibrāhīm ibn Hāniʾ both said: Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us. And Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yazīd ibn Ṭayfūr and Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq both said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Abū al-Azhar and al-Ḥasan ibn Yaḥyā both said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us. All of them [narrated] from Ibn Jurayj from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\When one of you vomits"," or has a regurgitation (qalas)"," or finds madhy [pre-seminal fluid] while he is in prayer"," let him turn away and perform wuḍūʾ"," then let him return and build upon his prayer"," so long as he has not spoken.\""\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan said: Abū Bakr said to us: I heard Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā say: \""This is the sound [narration] from Ibn Jurayj"," and it is mursal [discontinuous].\""\n\nAs for the hadith of Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abī Mulaykah from ʿĀʾishah"," which Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrates — it is nothing [i.e."," it is not established].\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said regarding the hadith of Ibn Jurayj from his father: \""This narration is not firmly established from the Prophet ﷺ.\""\n\nAnd he interpreted it"," along with what has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar and others"," as referring to washing some of the limbs.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated it once thus as mursal"," just as the group narrated it"," and it is the preserved [narration] from Ibn Jurayj"," and it is mursal.\n\nAl-Zaʿfarānī said: Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Shāfiʿī said regarding what has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar and Ibn al-Musayyib — that they would have a nosebleed and perform wuḍūʾ and build upon what they had prayed — \""We have narrated from Ibn ʿUmar and Ibn al-Musayyib that they did not consider wuḍūʾ to be required from blood. The meaning of their 'wuḍūʾ","' according to us"," is the washing of the blood and whatever has soiled the body — not the wuḍūʾ of prayer.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Ibn Masʿūd that he washed his hands from food"," then wiped his face with the moisture of his hands"," and said: \""This is the wuḍūʾ of one who has not broken his wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nAnd this is known in the speech of the Arabs — they would call washing some of the limbs \""wuḍūʾ","\"" not the complete wuḍūʾ of prayer. This is the meaning of what has been narrated from Ibn Jurayj from his father from the Prophet ﷺ regarding wuḍūʾ from nosebleed"," according to us. And Allah knows best.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""This narration is not firmly established from the Prophet ﷺ.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And upon this basis is interpreted what has been narrated from Thawbān from the Prophet ﷺ regarding vomiting"," if the narration concerning it is authentic.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī 1/153]"""
"670","(671) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAmr al-Awzāʿī narrated to us; Yaʿīsh ibn al-Walīd ibn Hishām narrated to us from his father, who said: Maʿdān ibn Ṭalḥah narrated to me from Abū al-Dardāʾ that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ vomited and broke his fast.\n\nI met Thawbān in the mosque of Damascus and mentioned that to him. He said: \It was I who poured his wuḍūʾ water for him.\""\n\nThe chain of this hadith is confused (muḍṭarib)"," and they differed concerning it greatly. And Allah knows best. It is mentioned along with the rest of what has been narrated on this topic in the works on jurisprudential differences.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 2381]"""
"671","(672) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-Ḥusaynī informed us in Kūfah: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Sufyān, who said: Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh was asked about a man who laughs during the prayer. He said: He should repeat the prayer but need not repeat the wuḍūʾ. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā, 12313]"
"672","(673) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Sufyān, from Jābir, who said: If a man laughs during the prayer, he should repeat the prayer but need not repeat the wuḍūʾ. [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī, 1/172]"
"673","(674) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated from Sufyān — that is, al-Thawrī — from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Sufyān, from Jābir, who said: He should repeat the prayer but need not repeat the wuḍūʾ. And Yazīd ibn Khālid narrated it similarly from Abū Sufyān. [Weak]"
"674","(675) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī both informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Yazīd Abī Khālid, who said: I heard Abū Sufyān narrate from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh that he said regarding laughing during the prayer: There is no need to repeat the wuḍūʾ.\n\nAnd from Yazīd Abī Khālid, from al-Shaʿbī, a similar report. And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī and Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated it similarly from Shuʿbah. And Ibn Jurayj narrated it from Yazīd Abī Khālid. And Abū Shaybah Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUthmān narrated it from Yazīd Abī Khālid and raised it (to the Prophet). (j) Abū Shaybah is weak. (t) The correct view is that it is mawqūf (a statement of the Companion). And Ḥabīb al-Muʿallim narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir, as his own statement. [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī, 1/173]"
"675","(676) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Wakīl narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah narrated to us: Hushaym narrated from Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah, from Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl, from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī: He was leading the people in prayer when they saw something, and some of those who were with him laughed. Abū Mūsā said when he had finished the prayer: Whoever among you laughed should repeat the prayer.\n\nAnd Abū Nuʿaym narrated it similarly from Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah, and in none of its versions is there any command to repeat the wuḍūʾ. [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī, 1/174]"
"676","(677) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn Fāris narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl — that is, al-Bukhārī — said: Zakariyyā narrated to me: al-Ḥakam ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah, from a mawlā of Abī Umāmah, from Abī Umāmah, who said: The ḥadath (nullification of wuḍūʾ) is what comes from the lower half (of the body)."
"677","(678) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Raffā informed us: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, who said: Among the jurists whom I met and whose opinions are followed were Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, and Sulaymān ibn Yasār, along with other eminent elders besides them. They said regarding the one who experiences a nosebleed: He should wash off the blood and need not perform wuḍūʾ. And regarding the one who laughs during the prayer: He should repeat the prayer but need not repeat his wuḍūʾ.\n\nAnd we have narrated a statement similar to theirs regarding laughing from al-Shaʿbī, ʿAṭāʾ, and al-Zuhrī. [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī, 1/165]"
"678","(679) As for the ḥadīth: Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣūfī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us: Ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Hishām narrated from Ḥafṣah, from Abū al-ʿĀliyah: A blind man came while the Prophet ﷺ was in the prayer, and he fell into a well. Groups of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ laughed, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered those who had laughed to repeat the wuḍūʾ and the prayer.\n\nThis is a mursal ḥadīth. The mursal narrations of Abū al-ʿĀliyah are not considered reliable, as he did not care from whom he took his ḥadīth — thus said Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī, Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī, and al-Zuhrī in mursal form. [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī, 1/162]"
"679","(680) As for the ḥadīth of al-Ḥasan: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Muqriʾ informed us in Baghdād: Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us: Hishām — meaning Ibn Ḥassān — narrated from al-Ḥasan: The Prophet ﷺ was leading the people in prayer when a blind man entered and fell into a well that was in the mosque. Groups of those who were behind the Prophet ﷺ in their prayer laughed. When the Prophet ﷺ gave the salām, he ordered those who had laughed to repeat their wuḍūʾ and to repeat their prayer.\n\nAnd Abū Ḥanīfah narrated it from Manṣūr ibn Zādhān, from al-Ḥasan, from Maʿbad al-Juhanī, from the Prophet ﷺ, in mursal form.\n\nBut Ghaylān ibn Jāriy differed and narrated it from Manṣūr ibn Zādhān, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Maʿbad.\n\nThis Maʿbad was not a Companion, and he was the first to speak about al-qadar (divine decree) in Baṣrah.\n\nAnd Hushaym narrated it from Manṣūr, from Ibn Sīrīn, in mursal form. [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī, 1/165]"
"680","(681) As for the ḥadīth of Ibrāhīm: Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated from Ibrāhīm, who said: A blind man came while the Prophet ﷺ was in the prayer. He stumbled and fell into a well, so they laughed. The Prophet ﷺ ordered those who had laughed to repeat the wuḍūʾ and the prayer. [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī, 1/171]"
"681","(682) As for the hadith of al-Zuhrī, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: al-Thiqah informed us from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb from Ibn Shihāb that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded a man who had laughed during the prayer to repeat the wuḍūʾ and the ṣalāh.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: We do not accept this, for it is mursal.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: Then al-Thiqah informed us from Maʿmar from Ibn Shihāb from Sulaymān ibn Arqam from al-Ḥasan from the Prophet (ﷺ) with this hadith.\n\nThe Shaykh said: All these narrations trace back to Abū al-ʿĀliyah al-Riyāḥī.\n\nThat which indicates this is what Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ibn Ṣāʿid informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq said: I heard ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī said to me: The hadith about laughing in prayer — that the Prophet (ﷺ) commanded that one repeat the wuḍūʾ and the ṣalāh — all of it revolves around Abū al-ʿĀliyah. ʿAlī said: I said: al-Ḥasan narrated it from the Prophet (ﷺ) as a mursal narration. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd informed us from Ḥafṣ ibn Sulaymān: I narrated it to al-Ḥasan from Ḥafṣah from Abū al-ʿĀliyah. I said to him: Ibrāhīm narrated it from the Prophet (ﷺ). ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: Sharīk informed us from Abū Hāshim: I narrated it to Ibrāhīm from Abū al-ʿĀliyah. ʿAlī said: I said to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: al-Zuhrī narrated it from the Prophet (ﷺ) as a mursal narration.\n\nʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: I read this hadith in the book of the nephew of al-Zuhrī, from al-Zuhrī from Sulaymān ibn Arqam from al-Ḥasan. And I heard ʿAlī saying: The most knowledgeable person regarding this hadith is ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī.\n\nImām Aḥmad (may Allah, the Most High, have mercy on him) said: Had al-Zuhrī or al-Ḥasan possessed a sound hadith regarding this, they would not have deemed it permissible to hold an opinion contrary to it. It has been authentically reported from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan that he did not consider wuḍūʾ to be required due to laughing in the prayer.\n\nAnd from Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah and others from al-Zuhrī that he said: Due to laughing, one repeats the ṣalāh but does not repeat the wuḍūʾ.\n\nAbū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, saying: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī said: The most criticized narration against Abū al-ʿĀliyah is this hadith, and all those who narrated it other than him — their source and point of reference is Abū al-ʿĀliyah; the hadith belongs to him and through him it is known. It is on account of this hadith that they spoke critically of Abū al-ʿĀliyah, while the rest of his narrations are upright and sound.\n\nAbū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān al-Fārisī informed us, saying: I heard Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb mention the hadith of Abū al-ʿĀliyah — that a man laughed in the prayer and the Prophet (ﷺ) commanded him to repeat the wuḍūʾ and the ṣalāh — and he declared it weak.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us, saying: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn saying: The mursal narrations of Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab are better than the mursal narrations of al-Ḥasan, and the mursal narrations of Ibrāhīm are sound except for the hadith of the merchant of al-Baḥrayn and the hadith of laughing in the prayer, and the mursal of al-Zuhrī is nothing.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This has also been narrated through connected chains, but they are weak; I have explained their weakness in al-Khilāfiyyāt.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muṭarriz informed us, saying: I heard Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā — that is, al-Dhuhlī — saying: No report has been established from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding laughing in the prayer.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: I read in the handwriting of Abū ʿAmr al-Mustamlī: I heard Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā, and he was asked about the hadith of Abū al-ʿĀliyah and its supporting narrations regarding laughing, and he said: Wāh! It is weak.\n\nAnd in the narration of al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī regarding the hadith of laughing in the prayer: Had the hadith been established with us regarding that, we would have ruled according to it. And the one who claims that wuḍūʾ is required due to loud laughter claims that analogy (qiyās) dictates that it does not break it, but he followed the āthār. Had he followed the sound and well-known narrations among them, that would have been praiseworthy in our view; however, he rejects the sound, connected, well-known narrations and accepts the weak, disconnected ones.\n\n[Weak. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī, 5/12]"
"682","(683) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf al-Ṭāʾī informed us: Abū al-Mughīrah ʿAbd al-Quddūs ibn al-Ḥajjāj informed us: al-Awzāʿī informed us from al-Zuhrī from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever among you swears an oath and says in his oath"," 'By al-Lāt and al-ʿUzzā","' let him say"," 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh.' And whoever says to his companion"," 'Come"," let me gamble with you","' let him give charity.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq from Abū al-Mughīrah"," and Muslim narrated it from Suwayd ibn Saʿīd from al-Walīd from al-Awzāʿī.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 4579]"""
"683","(684) Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibrāhīm — meaning Ibn Saʿd — informed us from Ibn Shihāb from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever swears an oath by al-Lāt and al-ʿUzzā"," let him say"," 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh.'\""\n\nIbn Shihāb said: It has not reached me that he mentioned wuḍūʾ in that.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 1647]"""
"684","God said: And when Abraham was tried by his Lord with words, he responded to them. [The Quran, 124]

Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Zakariyya al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam informed us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us from Abd Allah bin Tawus from his father from Ibn Abbas, that he said: God tried Abraham with words, and he responded to them. He said: God tried Abraham with words, and he responded to them. He said: God tried Abraham with words, and he responded to them.

He said: God tried Abraham with words, and he responded to them. He said: God tried Abraham with words, and he responded to them. He said: God tried Abraham with words, and he responded to them.

