He said: God tried Abraham with words, and he responded to them. He said: God tried Abraham with words, and he responded to them. He said: God tried Abraham with"," and he fulfilled them.\"" [Sūrah al-Baqarah: 124]\n\n(685) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Zakariyyā al-ʿAnbarī informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṭāwūs from his father from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the words of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: \""And when his Lord tried Ibrāhīm with certain words\"" — he said: Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," tried him with matters of purification: five pertaining to the head and five pertaining to the body. Those pertaining to the head are: trimming the moustache"," rinsing the mouth"," sniffing water into the nose"," using the siwāk"," and parting the hair. Those pertaining to the body are: clipping the nails"," shaving the pubic area"," circumcision"," plucking the armpit hair"," and washing the place of excrement and urine with water.\n\nThere has already passed in this book the hadith of Ibn al-Zubayr from ʿĀʾishah from the Prophet (ﷺ): \""Ten are from the fiṭrah\"" — and he mentioned them"," except that he mentioned growing the beard and washing the knuckles"," but did not mention circumcision or parting the hair.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 2/293]"""
"685","(686) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Isfarāʾinī informed us, all saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū Yaḥyā Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā ibn Asad informed us: Sufyān informed us from al-Zuhrī from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab from Abū Hurayrah, narrating it up to the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The fiṭrah consists of five things — or five things are from the fiṭrah: circumcision"," shaving the pubic area with a blade"," plucking the armpit hair"," trimming the moustache"," and clipping the nails.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"," all from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 555]"""
"686","(687) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — dictation — Ḥāmid ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqrīʾ informed us: Isḥāq ibn Sulaymān informed us: Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān informed us from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \From the Sunnah are: trimming the moustache"," plucking the armpit hair"," and clipping the nails.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Abī Rajāʾ from Isḥāq ibn Sulaymān.\n\n[Sahih]"""
"687","(688) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Let the beards grow and trim the moustaches.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from ʿUbayd Allāh.\n\nAnd ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad ibn Zayd added in it from Nāfiʿ: \""Differ from the polytheists.\""\n\n[Sahih]"""
"688","(689) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb informed us: Abū al-Muthannā informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl informed us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ informed us: ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Differ from the polytheists; let the beards grow and trim the moustaches.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl"," and Muslim narrated it from Sahl ibn ʿUthmān from Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ. And Abū Hurayrah narrated it from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," except that he said: \""And differ from the Magians.\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 5553]"""
"689","(690) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us: al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed us from his father from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Trim the moustaches"," let the beards grow"," and differ from the Magians.\""\n\nIt is recorded in the book of Muslim from the hadith of Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar from al-ʿAlāʾ.\n\n[Hasan. Narrated by Muslim"," 260]"""
"690","(691) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ informed us: Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Shādhān informed us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān informed us from Abū ʿImrān al-Jawnī from Anas ibn Mālik.\n\nAnas said: \A time was appointed for us regarding trimming the moustache"," clipping the nails"," plucking the armpit hair"," and shaving the pubic area — that we should not leave any of it for more than forty nights.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah.\n\n[Sahih li-ghayrihi. Narrated by Muslim"," 258]"""
"691","(692) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Muḥāribī in al-Kūfah informed us; Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunayn narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ṣadaqah ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Abū ʿImrān al-Jawnī narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) set for us a time limit of forty days for shaving the pubic hair"," trimming the moustache"," clipping the nails"," and plucking the armpit hair.\"" [Ṣaḥīh by other than him]"""
"692","(693) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; Ayyūb ibn Suwayd narrated to us; ʿĪsā narrated from Sulaymān al-Taymī from Abī Mijlaz, who said: \I saw Ibn ʿUmar clip his nails"," so I said: 'Will you not perform wuḍūʾ?' He said: 'From what should I perform wuḍūʾ? You consider yourself more intelligent than the one whose family named him al-Kayyis (the intelligent one).'\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from al-Shaʿbī that he said regarding a man who clips his nails after performing wuḍūʾ: \""It is his purification (ṭahūr).\""\n\nAnd from al-Ḥasan: \""There is no wuḍūʾ required for it.\"" And from ʿAṭāʾ: \""Touch it with water.\"" And from Ibrāhīm: likewise. And from al-Zuhrī: \""If he wishes"," he may wipe over it with water"," and if he wishes"," he may leave it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"693","(694) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; Abū ʿĀmir Mūsā ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from al-Awzāʿī from al-Zuhrī regarding one who clips his nails, trims his moustache, or cuts his hair: \If he wishes"," he may wipe over it with water"," and if he wishes"," he may leave it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"694","(695) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; al-Masʿūdī narrated to me; Abū ʿAwn al-Thaqafī Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh narrated from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a man with a long moustache, so he called for a siwāk and a blade. He placed the siwāk beneath the moustache and trimmed it against it. [Ḍaʿīf. al-Ṭayālisī narrated it as 698]"
"695","(696) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us; al-Nufaylī narrated to us, saying: I read to Maʿqil ibn ʿUbayd Allāh from Maymūn ibn Mihrān from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned the Magians and said: 'Indeed"," they let their moustaches grow and shave their beards"," so oppose them.'\"" He said: \""So Ibn ʿUmar used to take his moustache broadly and cut it as a sheep or a camel is shorn.\"" [Ḥasan. al-Ṭabarānī narrated it in al-Awsaṭ (51/1)]"""
"696","(697) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; al-Firyābī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ, who said: \I saw Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," Ibn ʿUmar"," Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj"," Abū Usayd al-Anṣārī"," Ibn al-Akwaʿ"," and Abū Rāfiʿ trimming their moustaches extensively"," up to the point of shaving.\""\n\nImām Aḥmad said: \""This is how I found it.\"" Others narrated from ʿUthmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ"," and it was said: \""Ibn Rāfiʿ.\"" [Ḥasan. al-Ṭabarānī narrated it in al-Kabīr (668)]"""
"697","(698) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Najdah narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us; Sharḥbīl ibn Muslim al-Khawlānī narrated to us, saying: \I saw five of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) trimming their moustaches"," letting their beards grow"," and dyeing them: Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn Busr"," ʿUtbah ibn ʿAbd al-Sulamī"," al-Ḥajjāj ibn ʿĀmir al-Thumālī"," and al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdīkarib al-Kindī. They used to trim their moustaches in line with the edge of the lip.\"" [Ḥasan. al-Ṭabarānī narrated it in al-Kabīr (3218)]"""
"698","(699) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Kāmil ibn Khalaf al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Uwaysī narrated to us, saying: \Mālik ibn Anas mentioned some people's practice of shaving their moustaches completely"," and Mālik said: 'Whoever does that deserves to be struck. The ḥadīth of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) does not refer to shaving (iḥfāʾ)"," but rather to revealing the edge of the two lips and the mouth.'\"" Mālik ibn Anas said: \""Shaving the moustache is an innovation (bidʿah) that has appeared among the people.\"" Thus he said. [Ṣaḥīh]"""
"699","(700) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed me; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Bakr ibn Quraysh informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated from Mālik ibn Anas from Abī Bakr ibn Nāfiʿ from his father from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he commanded the trimming of the moustaches and the letting grow of the beards. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Qutaybah. And in the ḥadīth of al-Qaʿnabī: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded the trimming of the moustache and the letting grow of the beard.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd.\n\nAnd we narrated it from the ḥadīth of ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad ibn Zayd from Nāfiʿ.\n\nIt is as though he (Māhimah Allāh taʿālā) understood the commanded trimming (iḥfāʾ) mentioned in the report to mean cutting the moustache by clipping (al-jazʿ) rather than shaving (al-ḥalq)"," and his objection was directed at shaving specifically"," not at trimming in general. The error occurred on the part of the narrator from him regarding the categorical rejection of trimming. And Allah knows best. Those who held the view of shaving claimed that it falls under the general meaning of His command to trim. [Ṣaḥīh. Muslim narrated it (259)]"""
"700","(701) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Kāmil Abū al-ʿAlāʾ narrated from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit from Umm Salamah that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to remove his pubic hair and would attend to his private parts with his own hand.\n\nKāmil Abū al-ʿAlāʾ narrated it with a complete chain (asnadahu), while one who is more reliable than him narrated it as a mursal report. [Munkar. Ibn Mājah narrated it (3752)]"
"701","(702) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Hārūn ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Sufyān, from Manṣūr, from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) would trim his pubic hair with his own hand. [Weak. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq (1127)]"
"702","(703) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sufyān al-Thawrī informed me, from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) applied depilatory (nūr), he would attend to his pubic hair himself. [Weak]"
"703","(704) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Jarrāḥī in Marw narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Shāsawayh narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Sukkari narrated to us, Wahb ibn Zamʿah narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ʿAbd al-Malik said: ʿAbdullāh, meaning Ibn al-Mubārak, said: \I do not know who informed me from Qatādah that the Prophet (ﷺ) did not use depilatory (nūr).\"" ʿAbdullāh said: \""And this is more likely of the two possibilities — that he did not do so.\"" And he mentioned the other hadith: \""That the Prophet (ﷺ) attended to his pubic hair himself.\"" He said: \""This is weak.\"" The Shaykh said: \""The hadith contains what I have previously stated"," and it has been narrated through another isnad"," not well-known"," some of its narrators being unknown.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Saʿd in al-Ṭabaqāt (1/442)]"""
"704","(705) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdad, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Salamah al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Nāshirah al-Alhānī said: I heard Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Alhānī say: Thawbān was a neighbour of ours, and he used to enter the bathhouse (ḥammām). I asked him, and he said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) used to enter the bathhouse and use depilatory (nūr).\"" [Baseless (Bāṭil)]"""
"705","(6) Abū Dāwūd narrated in al-Marāsīl from Abū Kāmil al-Jaḥdarī, from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid, from Ṣāliḥ ibn Ṣāliḥ, from Abī Maʿshar: A man applied depilatory (nūr) to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and when he reached the pubic region, the man withdrew his hand, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) applied the depilatory to himself. [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Saʿd in al-Ṭabaqāt (1/442)]"
"706","(707) From ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāh al-Adhramī, from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from Saʿīd, from Qatādah: The Prophet (ﷺ) did not use depilatory (nūr), nor did Abū Bakr, nor ʿUmar, nor ʿUthmān. Both chains are mursal (disconnected). Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī narrated to us, Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated both of them. [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Saʿd in al-Ṭabaqāt (1/442)]"
"707","(708) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah narrated to us, Abū ʿAlī al-Raffāʾ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṭāʾī in Baghdad narrated to us, Abū ʿAmmār al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥurayth al-Marwazī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq narrated to us, from Abī Ḥamzah al-Sukkari, from Muslim al-Malāʾī, from Anas, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) did not use depilatory (nūr). When his hair became abundant"," he would shave it.\"" Muslim al-Malāʾī is weak in hadith. If he preserved it"," it is possible that Qatādah also took it from Anas. And Allah knows best. It has also been narrated regarding this from Ibn ʿUmar. [Weak]"""
"708","(709) Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Usāmah ibn Zayd al-Laythī informed me, from Nāfiʿ: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar used to apply oil (ṭalā) to his body, and he would instruct me to apply it to him. When he reached his lower region, he would attend to it himself. [Ḥasan]"
"709","(710) Through this same isnad, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to me, from Nāfiʿ: Ibn ʿUmar did not enter the bathhouse (ḥammām). He would use depilatory (nūr) at home, wearing a lower garment (izār), and he would instruct me to apply depilatory to what was visible of his body. Then he would instruct me to withdraw, and he would attend to his private parts himself. [Weak]"
"710","(711) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, Mālik narrated. (Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ate the shoulder of a sheep, then he prayed and did not perform wuḍūʾ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf, and Muslim narrated it from al-Qaʿnabī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (48)]"
"711","(712) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, who said: Wahb ibn Kaysān narrated to me from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās.\n\nHishām said: and al-Zuhrī narrated to me: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated to me from his father, Ibn ʿAbbās.\n\nHishām said: and Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī narrated to me from his father from Ibn ʿAbbās: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ate a shoulder [of meat] or some meat, then he prayed and did not rinse his mouth nor did he touch water.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it, 354.]"
"712","(713) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, who said: I was with Ibn ʿAbbās in the house of Maymūnah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), in the mosque, and he expressed astonishment at those who claim that wuḍūʾ is required from that which has been touched by fire, and he cited examples regarding it and said: \We used to bathe with heated water and perform wuḍūʾ with it"," and we used to anoint ourselves with cooked oil.\"" He mentioned other things that people come into contact with that have been touched by fire. Then he said: \""I myself saw in this house"," in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," that he performed wuḍūʾ"," then put on his garments. The muʾadhdhin came"," and he went out to the prayer. When he was in the ḥujrah outside the house"," a gift was brought to him — a portion of a sheep — and he ate from it one or two morsels"," then he prayed and did not touch water.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Kurayb from Abī Usāmah. In it is evidence that Ibn ʿAbbās witnessed that from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 359.]"""
"713","(714) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl narrated to us in Baghdād: Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAlī ibn Mukram narrated to us: ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAmr ibn Umayyah narrated to me that his father ʿAmr ibn Umayyah informed him: that he saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cutting from a shoulder of sheep in his hand. He was called to prayer, so he cast it aside — and the knife with which he was cutting — then he stood and prayed and did not perform wuḍūʾ.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī narrated it, 5092.]"
"714","(715) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: ʿImrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā al-Miṣrī informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me from Ibn Shihāb from Jaʿfar ibn ʿAmr ibn Umayyah al-Ḍamrī from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cutting from a shoulder of sheep and eating from it. He was called to prayer, so he stood, cast aside the knife, then prayed and did not perform wuḍūʾ.\n\nIbn Shihāb said: and ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated to me from his father from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding that.\n\nʿAmr said: Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to me from Kurayb, the mawlā of Ibn ʿAbbās, from Maymūnah: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ate a shoulder [of meat] in her presence, then prayed and did not perform wuḍūʾ.\n\nʿAmr said: and Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah narrated to me from Yaʿqūb ibn al-Ashajj from Kurayb from Ibn ʿAbbās from Maymūnah from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding that.\n\nʿAmr said: and Saʿīd ibn Abī Hilāl narrated to me from ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUbaydillāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ from Abī Ghaṭafān from Abī Rāfiʿ, who said: I bear witness that I used to roast the belly of a sheep for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), then he would stand and pray and not perform wuḍūʾ.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā, except that he said in the ḥadīth of Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah from Yaʿqūb from Kurayb from Maymūnah — and this is the correct version — and the mention of Ibn ʿAbbāth in it is an erroneous addition.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated the ḥadīth of Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj from Aṣbagh ibn al-Faraj from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it, 357.]"
"715","(716) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdillāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī by recitation, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿlā ibn al-Ḥārith al-Muḥāribī narrated to us: Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ narrated from ʿIkrimah and ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī Maysarah, both saying: We heard ʿĀʾishah mentioning that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would pass by the cooking pot, take from it a bone with meat, eat from it, then proceed to prayer without performing wuḍūʾ and without rinsing his mouth. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"716","(717) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdillāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī narrated to us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed me that ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār informed him that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), informed him: that she presented a roasted side [of meat] to the Prophet (ﷺ) and he ate it, then he stood for prayer and did not perform wuḍūʾ.\n\nSimilarly, al-Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad and Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated it from Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Tirmidhī narrated it, 1829.]"
"717","(718) ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated it from Ibn Jurayj from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf from Sulaymān ibn Yasār from Umm Salamah from the Prophet (ﷺ) in a similar manner.\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of it: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar informed us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nIt has also been narrated from ʿAbdillāh ibn Shaddād and Zaynab bint Umm Salamah from Umm Salamah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Yaʿlā narrated it, 6985.]"
"718","(719) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdād from the original of his book: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb al-Ṭāʾī narrated to us: Abū Jaddī ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jābir: that the Prophet (ﷺ) ate meat, then prayed and did not perform wuḍūʾ.\n\nIn this chapter [there are narrations] from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, ʿAbdillāh ibn Masʿūd, Suwayd ibn al-Nuʿmān, Muḥammad ibn Muslimah, Abū Hurayrah, ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Jazʾ al-Zubaydī, Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, and others from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAl-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī said: Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Shāfiʿī said: And it has been narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ): \Wuḍūʾ is from that which has been touched by fire.\"" But he only intended [something specific]. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it"," 3/307.]"""
"719","(720) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to me: al-Layth ibn Saʿd —\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Walīd — and the wording is his — narrated to us: ʿAbdillāh ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us: my father narrated to me from my grandfather from ʿUqayl. Ibn Shihāb said: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām informed me that Khārijah ibn Zayd al-Anṣārī informed him that his father Zayd ibn Thābit said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Wuḍūʾ is from that which has been touched by fire.\""\n\nIbn Shihāb said: and ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed me that ʿAbdillāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Qāriẓ informed him: that he found Abū Hurayrah performing wuḍūʾ in the mosque"," and he said: \""I am only performing wuḍūʾ from pieces of dried yogurt (athwār aqīṭ) that I ate"," because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Perform wuḍūʾ from that which has been touched by fire.'\""\n\nIbn Shihāb said: Saʿīd ibn Khālid ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān informed me — and I was narrating this ḥadīth to him — that he asked ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr about wuḍūʾ from that which has been touched by fire. ʿUrwah said: I heard ʿĀʾishah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Perform wuḍūʾ from that which has been touched by fire.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb. In this chapter [there are narrations] from Umm Ḥabībah the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ)"," Umm Salamah the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ)"," Abū Ṭalḥah"," Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī"," Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," and others from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAl-Zaʿfarānī said: Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Shāfiʿī said: And we only said that wuḍūʾ is not to be performed from it because in our view it is abrogated (mansūkh). Do you not see that ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbbās — who only became his companion after the Conquest — narrates from him that he saw him eating from a shoulder of sheep"," then he prayed and did not perform wuḍūʾ? In our view"," this is among the clearest proofs that wuḍūʾ from it is abrogated"," or that his command to perform wuḍūʾ from it was merely for the purpose of washing for cleanliness. What is established from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) is that he did not perform wuḍūʾ from it"," and likewise from Abū Bakr"," ʿUmar"," ʿUthmān"," ʿAlī"," Ibn ʿAbbās"," ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah"," Ubayy ibn Kaʿb"," and Abū Ṭalḥah — none of them performed wuḍūʾ from it.\n\nThe Shaykh said: As for the first approach"," a group of scholars adopted it"," and they argued with what al-Shāfiʿī argued from the narration of Ibn ʿAbbās"," and then from the narration of Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī"," Muḥammad ibn Muslimah"," and Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 351.]"""
"720","(721) As for the ḥadīth of Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us: Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: The last of the two matters from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was the abandonment of wuḍūʾ from that which has been touched by fire. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it, 192.]"
"721","(722) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us — and he mentioned its chain of narration similarly, saying: The last of the two matters from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was that he ate bread and meat, then he performed Ṣalāh and did not perform Wuḍūʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"722","(723) As for the Ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn Maslamah — Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us, Quraysh ibn Ḥayyān al-ʿIjlī narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Abī Khālid narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Maslamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate something that had been changed by fire, then he performed Ṣalāh and did not perform Wuḍūʾ, and that was the last of his two commands.\n\nAnd someone other than Yūnus ibn Abī Khālid narrated it. From Muḥammad ibn Maslamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate…\n\n[Weak. Al-Ṭabarānī narrated it in al-Dāwsiyyah [1208]]"
"723","(724) As for the Ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah — Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdah al-Ḍabbī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī narrated to us from Suhayl, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, that he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing Wuḍūʾ from a piece of dried curd (aqīṭ), then he saw him eat from the shoulder of a sheep, then he performed Ṣalāh and did not perform Wuḍūʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other routes. Aḥmad narrated it 1/366]"
"724","(725) ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muslim narrated it from Suhayl, and he said in the Ḥadīth: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a piece of dried curd and performed Wuḍūʾ, and he ate a shoulder and did not perform Wuḍūʾ.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Abū al-Nuʿmān narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muslim narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nSome of the people of knowledge held the second view, and they claimed that the Ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah is defective (maʿlūl), and that his fatwā regarding Wuḍūʾ from it was given after the death of the Prophet ﷺ, and that the narration of Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadar is an abridgement of the Ḥadīth which Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us.\n\nAnd Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Usāmah ibn Zayd and Ibn Jurayj informed you, from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadar, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to a woman of the Anṣār, and his Companions were with him. She brought him a roasted sheep. He said: So he ate, and we ate. Then the time for Ẓuhr came, so he performed Wuḍūʾ, then he performed Ṣalāh. Then he returned to the remainder of his food, so he ate. Then the time for ʿAṣr came, so he performed Ṣalāh and did not perform Wuḍūʾ.\n\nThus did a group narrate it from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadar, and they held that the \last of his two commands\"" was intended in this narration. Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī and others said this. And they likewise held the Ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn Maslamah.\n\nAnd it has been narrated in another Ḥadīth what may suggest that it abrogates the obligation of Wuḍūʾ from it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"725","(726) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated it to us, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me, Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to me, Zayd ibn Jubayrah ibn Maḥmūd ibn Abī Jubayrah al-Anṣārī, from Banī ʿAbd al-Ashhal, narrated to me, from his father Jubayrah ibn Maḥmūd, from Salamah ibn Salāmah ibn Waqsh — and he was the last of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, apart from Anas ibn Mālik, for he outlived him — that the two of them entered upon a wedding feast, and Salamah was in a state of Wuḍūʾ. They ate, then they went out. So Salamah performed Wuḍūʾ. Jubayrah said to him: Were you not in a state of Wuḍūʾ? He said: Yes, but I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when we came out from a feast to which we had been invited, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a state of Wuḍūʾ. He ate, then he performed Wuḍūʾ. So I said to him: Were you not in a state of Wuḍūʾ, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \Yes"," but new matters occur"," and this is among what has newly occurred.\""\n\nAnd al-Zuhrī held a similar view to this"," and he was firm in it. [Very weak. Al-Ḥākim narrated it 3/473]"""
"726","(727) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Abū Yaḥyā ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, Abū al-Yamān informed me, Shuʿayb informed me, from al-Zuhrī, who said: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAmr ibn Umayyah informed me that his father ʿAmr ibn Umayyah informed him: He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cutting from the shoulder of a sheep in his hand. Then he was called to Ṣalāh, so he cast it down along with the knife with which he was cutting, then he stood and performed Ṣalāh and did not perform Wuḍūʾ.\n\nAl-Zuhrī said: That practice spread among the people. Then men from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and women from among his wives informed that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Perform Wuḍūʾ from that which has been touched by fire.\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us"," Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us"," and he said: Abū Saʿīd — meaning ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī — said:\n\nThese Ḥadīths have differed"," and there is disagreement regarding which is the earlier and which is the later among them. We have not come upon a clear"," definitive indication of the abrogating and the abrogated among them by which we may rule to the exclusion of anything else. So we looked to that upon which the Rightly Guided Caliphs and the prominent figures among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ agreed"," and we followed their consensus regarding the dispensation (rukhṣah) in the matter. And the Ḥadīth in which the dispensation is narrated from the Prophet ﷺ is [Ṣaḥīḥ]."""
"727","(728) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, Mālik narrated to us, from Abū Nuʿaym Wahb ibn Kaysān, that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh say: I saw Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) eat meat, then he performed Ṣalāh and did not perform Wuḍūʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it 54]"
"728","(729) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Muḥammad narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿĀʾishah narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār and Abū al-Zubayr together, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh: That Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq and ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb ate bread and meat, then they performed Ṣalāh and did not perform Wuḍūʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ṭaḥāwī narrated it 1/41]"
"729","(730) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr al-Miṣrī narrated to us, Mālik narrated to us, from Ḍamrah ibn Saʿīd al-Māzinī, from Abān ibn ʿUthmān: That ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān ate bread and meat, then he rinsed his mouth, washed his hands, and wiped his face with them, then he performed Ṣalāh and did not perform Wuḍūʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it 51]"
"730","(731) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Kathīr al-ʿAbdī informed us, Isrāʾīl informed us, from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, from Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): That he ate bread and meat, and it was said to him: Will you not perform Wuḍūʾ? He said: \Wuḍūʾ is from what comes out"," not from what enters.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"731","(732) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, i.e. ibn ʿAṭāʾ, narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf, the client of ʿUthmān, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, who said: I stood by Abū Hurayrah while he was performing wuḍūʾ, when Ibn ʿAbbās came to him and said: \O Ibn ʿAbbās"," do you know why I have performed wuḍūʾ?\"" He said: \""No.\"" Abū Hurayrah said: \""I ate a piece of dried yogurt (aqīṭ).\"" Ibn ʿAbbās then said: \""I do not care why you performed wuḍūʾ. By Allah"," I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) eat bread and meat"," then he stood up for the prayer and did not perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 1/361]"""
"732","(733) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Yaḥyā narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said: \There is no wuḍūʾ required for that which has been touched by fire. Fire is merely a blessing"," and fire does not render anything lawful or unlawful.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 653]"""
"733","(734) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us, from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd al-Anṣārī, that Anas ibn Mālik came from Iraq and visited Abū Ṭalḥah and Ubayy ibn Kaʿb. Food that had been touched by fire was brought near to them, and they ate from it. Then Anas stood up and performed wuḍūʾ. Abū Ṭalḥah and Ubayy ibn Kaʿb said to him: \What is this"," O Anas? Is this an Iraqi practice?\"" Anas said: \""I wish I had not done it.\"" Then Abū Ṭalḥah and Ubayy ibn Kaʿb stood up and prayed"," and they did not perform wuḍūʾ.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik 56]"""
"734","(735) With the same chain of narration, he said: Mālik narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, that he asked ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah about a man who performs wuḍūʾ for the prayer and then eats food that has been touched by fire — should he perform wuḍūʾ? ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah said: \I saw my father do that and then not perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik 53]"""
"735","(736) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, i.e. ibn ʿAṭāʾ, narrated to us: Dāwūd narrated to us, from ʿĀmir, from ʿAlqamah and al-Aswad, that both of them ate bread and meat with Ibn Masʿūd and did not perform wuḍūʾ.\n\n[Ḥasan]"
"736","(737) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Abū ʿUmar, Musaddad, and al-Ḥajabī narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Kāmil narrated to us. They said: Abū ʿAwanah narrated to us, from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mawhab, from Jaʿfar ibn Abī Thawr, from Jābir ibn Samurah, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \Should I perform wuḍūʾ from the meat of sheep?\"" He said: \""If you wish"," perform wuḍūʾ"," and if you wish"," do not perform wuḍūʾ.\"" He said: \""Should I perform wuḍūʾ from the meat of camels?\"" He said: \""Yes"," perform wuḍūʾ from the meat of camels.\"" He said: \""May I pray in the sheepfolds?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""May I pray in the resting places of camels?\"" He said: \""No.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū Kāmil. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kāmil"," and he also narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ashʿath ibn Abī al-Shaʿthāʾ and Simāk ibn Ḥarb"," from Jaʿfar ibn Abī Thawr.\n\nAnd ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī held the view that this Jaʿfar ibn Abī Thawr is unknown (majhūl).\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Isfarāʾinī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Barāʾ narrated to us"," saying: ʿAlī said: \""This Jaʿfar is unknown.\"" Thus said ʿAlī.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn Fāris informed us"," from Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī"," who said: \""Jaʿfar ibn Abī Thawr — his grandfather is Jābir ibn Samurah.\""\n\nSufyān"," Zakariyyā"," and Zāʾidah said"," from Simāk"," from Jaʿfar ibn Abī Thawr ibn Jābir"," from Jābir"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," regarding meats.\n\nThe people of genealogy said: \""The children of Jābir ibn Samurah are: Khālid"," Ṭalḥah"," and Maslamah"," and he is Abū Thawr.\""\n\nShuʿbah said"," from Simāk"," from Abī Thawr ibn ʿIkrimah ibn Jābir ibn Samurah"," from Jābir ibn Samurah.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said"," as it reached me from him: \""The ḥadīth of al-Thawrī is more authentic than the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah"," and Shuʿbah erred in it"," for he said: 'From Abī Thawr","' when in fact it is Jaʿfar ibn Abī Thawr. And Jaʿfar ibn Abī Thawr is a well-known man"," and he is from the descendants of Jābir ibn Samurah. Simāk ibn Ḥarb"," ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mawhab"," and Ashʿath ibn Abī al-Shaʿthāʾ narrated from him.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah said: \""These three are among the most eminent of the narrators of ḥadīth.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""Whoever has such narrators reporting from him is no longer considered unknown. For this reason"," Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj included it in his Ṣaḥīḥ book.\""\n\nAnd Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit"," who said: \""Someone who heard Jābir ibn Samurah informed me"," saying: 'We used to rinse our mouths from the milk of camels but did not rinse our mouths from the milk of sheep"," and we used to perform wuḍūʾ from the meat of camels but did not perform wuḍūʾ from the meat of sheep.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim 360]"""
"737","(738) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: I heard Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Karābīsī, i.e. Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh, saying: I heard Aḥmad ibn Ḥamdūn al-Aʿmashī saying: I heard ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Afṭas saying: \I saw Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan performing wuḍūʾ from the meat of camels.\"" And it has been narrated through other chains from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"738","(739) The Ustādh Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAbd Allāh, a client of Quraysh, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) was asked about wuḍūʾ from the meat of camels, and he commanded it. He was asked about praying in the resting places of camels, and he forbade it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than its chain. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 493]"
"739","(740) With the same chain of narration, he said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh, a client of Quraysh, from Ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, that the Prophet (ﷺ) was asked about wuḍūʾ from the meat of sheep, and he gave permission regarding wuḍūʾ from it. He was asked about praying in their sheepfolds, and he gave permission regarding it.\n\nThus a group narrated it from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Rāzī.\n\nAnd al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr.\n\nAnd al-Ḥajjāj is weak (ḍaʿīf). Abū ʿĪsā said: \The ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash is more authentic.\""\n\nHe said: And ʿUbaydah al-Ḍabbī narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā"," from Dhī al-Ghurrah"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and it is nothing (i.e."," it is not valid).\n\nAnd Dhī al-Ghurrah — it is not known who he is. And the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash is more authentic.\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And ʿUbaydah al-Ḍabbī is not strong (qawī). And it has reached me from Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal and Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī that they both said: 'Two authentic ḥadīths have been established in this topic from the Prophet (ﷺ): the ḥadīth of al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib and the ḥadīth of Jābir ibn Samurah.'\""\n\nAnd Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us"," saying: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah said: \""We have not seen any disagreement among the scholars of the people of ḥadīth that this report is authentic from the standpoint of transmission"," due to the integrity of its narrators.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And it has been narrated from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib and Ibn ʿAbbās: 'Wuḍūʾ is required for what comes out (of the body)"," not for what enters it.' And they said this regarding the abandonment of wuḍūʾ for that which has been touched by fire.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than its chain]"""
"740","(741) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Mihrajānī narrated to us in it: Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Jumān al-Rāzī narrated to us in it: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us, from ʿImrān ibn Sulaym, from Abī Jaʿfar, who said: A bowl containing liver and hump — the meat of a camel — was brought to Ibn Masʿūd, and he ate and did not perform wuḍūʾ. This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected) and mawqūf (stopped).\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Abī ʿUbaydah, who said: \ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd used to eat from various kinds of food and would not perform wuḍūʾ from it.\"" And with such a narration"," that which is established from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cannot be abandoned.\n\nAnd some of the fuqahāʾ have interpreted the wuḍūʾ mentioned in the report as referring to wuḍūʾ in the sense of cleanliness and the removal of greasiness.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"741","(742) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūs al-Sūsī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿĀṣim al-Nabīl narrated to us, from al-Awzāʿī, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet (ﷺ) drank milk, then rinsed his mouth and said: \Indeed"," it has fat (dasam) in it.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū ʿĀṣim"," and it was narrated by Muslim from another route from al-Awzāʿī."""
"742","(743) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed you, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) drank milk, then he called for water and rinsed his mouth with it, then he said: \Indeed"," it has fat (dasam) in it.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā from Ibn Wahb."""
"743","(744) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us, saying: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, saying: Abū Khalīfah narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh — meaning al-Qaʿnabī — narrated to us, from Mālik, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Bushayr ibn Yasār, that Suwayd ibn al-Nuʿmān informed him that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the year of Khaybar, until when they reached al-Ṣahbāʾ, the nearest part of Khaybar, he prayed ʿAṣr, then he called for the provisions, but nothing was brought except sawīq (parched barley). He ordered it to be moistened, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ate and we ate with him. Then he stood up for Maghrib and rinsed his mouth, and we rinsed our mouths, then he prayed and did not perform wuḍūʾ.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī and others."
"744","(745) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us, saying: Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from Wahb ibn Kaysān, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, who reported from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās, that he said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) eating a bone from a sheep"," then he prayed"," and he did not rinse his mouth nor did he touch water.\""\n\nIt is recorded in the book of Muslim from the ḥadīth of Hishām ibn ʿUrwah."""
"745","(746) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, saying: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, saying: ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb, from Muṭīʿ ibn Rāshid, from Tawbah al-ʿAnbarī, that he heard Anas ibn Mālik say: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) drank milk"," and he did not rinse his mouth"," nor did he perform wuḍūʾ"," and he prayed.\""\n\nZayd said: Shuʿbah directed me to this shaykh.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿIkrimah"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," that he said: \""Were it not for the act of picking food from between the teeth (talammuẓ)"," I would not mind not rinsing my mouth.\"""""
"746","(747) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan — I read to him — narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, saying: Ādam narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated to us, saying: ʿAmr ibn Murrah narrated to us, saying: I heard Saʿīd ibn Jubayr say: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: \If I were to eat bread and meat and drink the milk of camels"," I would not mind praying without performing wuḍūʾ"," except that I would rinse my mouth and wash my fingers from the grease of the meat.\"""""
"747","(748) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, saying: Maʿmar informed us, from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The prayer of any one of you is not accepted when he has broken his wuḍūʾ (i.e."," experienced ḥadath) until he performs wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq"," and it was narrated by Muslim from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ"," both from ʿAbd al-Razzāq."""
"748","(749) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, saying: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, saying: Sufyān informed us, saying: al-Zuhrī informed us, saying: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm informed me from his (ʿAbbād's) paternal uncle, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd, who said: \A complaint was brought to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about a man who imagines something during the prayer.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""He should not turn away (from his prayer) until he hears a sound or finds an odour.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī and others"," and it was narrated by Muslim from ʿAmr al-Nāqid and others"," all from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah."""
"749","(750) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, saying: Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, saying: Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, saying: Suhayl narrated to me from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When any one of you finds wind in his belly and it is suggested to him that something has come out of him"," he should not leave until he hears a sound or finds an odour.\""\n\nIt is recorded in the book of Muslim from the ḥadīth of Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ"," and he said in the ḥadīth: \""He should not leave the mosque.\"""""
"750","(751) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us, from Ashʿath, from al-Ḥasan, that he said: \If you are in doubt about the breaking of wuḍūʾ (ḥadath) but are certain about your wuḍūʾ"," then you are still in a state of wuḍūʾ. And if you are in doubt about your wuḍūʾ but are certain about the breaking of wuḍūʾ (ḥadath)"," then perform wuḍūʾ.\"""""
"751","(752) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahbubi informed us that Ahmad ibn Sayyar narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us that Sufyan narrated from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Sufyan ibn al-Hakam or al-Hakam ibn Sufyan, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) urinated"," he would perform wudu and sprinkle (water).\"" (T) Thus narrated al-Thawri"," Ma'mar"," and Zaidah from Mansur. [Sahih (authentic) through other chains. Abu Dawud reported it as no. 166.]"""
"752","(753) And Shu'bah narrated it, as Abu al-Hasan al-Muqr'i informed us that al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us that Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that Hafs ibn 'Umar narrated to us that Shu'bah narrated from Mansur, from Mujahid, from a man called al-Hakam or Abu al-Hakam from Thaqif, from his father, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform wudu, then take a handful of water and sprinkle with it.\n\n(T) And thus narrated Wahib from Mansur. And Abu 'Awanah, Ruh ibn al-Qasim, and Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated from Mansur, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam or Abu al-Hakam ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi, as a musnad narration, except that they did not mention his father.\n\nAnd Isra'il, Salam ibn Abi Mu'ti', and Zakariyya narrated from Mansur, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam ibn Sufyan — they did not express doubt, nor did they mention his father.\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: \I asked Muhammad"," meaning Ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari"," about this hadith"," and he said: 'The correct narration is what Shu'bah and Wahib reported"," and they said: \""from his father.\"" And Ibn 'Uyaynah sometimes said in this hadith: \""from his father.\""'\""\n\nImam Ahmad said: \""Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated it from Mansur; once he mentioned his father in it and once he did not.\"" [Sahih through other chains. Al-Nasa'i reported it as no. 134.]"""
"753","(754) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us that 'Isa narrated to us that Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib narrated to us that Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us that Sufyan narrated from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from a man from Thaqif, from his father, who said: \I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) urinate"," then sprinkle water on his private part.\""\n\nAnd Abu 'Isa al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ibn Abi 'Umar"," from Ibn 'Uyaynah"," from Mansur and Ibn Abi Najih"," thus"," and he said in the hadith: \""Then he performed wudu and sprinkled water on his private part.\"" [Sahih through other chains. Abu Dawud reported it as no. 167.]"""
"754","(755) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us that 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us that Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us that Abu Dawud narrated to us that Shu'bah narrated from Mansur, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam or Abu al-Hakam, a man from Thaqif, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed wudu and sprinkled water on his private part. [Sahih through other chains. Abu Dawud reported it as no. 168.]"
"755","(756) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us in Baghdad that 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Darastawayh narrated to us that Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us that 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us that Ibn Luhai'ah narrated to us that 'Uqayl informed us from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Usamah ibn Zaid ibn Harithah, from his father, that Jibril came down to the Prophet (ﷺ) at the time when revelation was first sent down to him and taught him wudu. The Prophet (ﷺ) performed wudu, and when he finished, the Prophet (ﷺ) took water in his hand and sprinkled it on his private part. [Sahih through other chains. Ahmad reported it, 3/2.]"
"756","(757) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that al-'Abbas al-Duri narrated to us that Qabisah narrated to us that Sufyan narrated from Zaid ibn Aslam, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called for water and performed wudu"," washing each limb once"," and sprinkled (water).\""\n\nImam Ahmad said: \""His statement 'and sprinkled' — Qabisah is alone in narrating it from Sufyan. A group narrated it from Sufyan without this addition. And Allah knows best.\"" [Sahih through other chains. Al-Darimi reported it as no. 711.]"""
"757","(758) Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Ubayd al-Harfi informed us in Baghdad that Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us that Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham narrated to us that Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us that al-Furat narrated from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that a man came to Ibn 'Abbas and said: \I find moisture when I stand to pray.\""\n\nIbn 'Abbas said: \""Sprinkle (water) with a cup of water"," and if you find anything of that"," say: 'It is from it.'\"" The man left and stayed as long as Allah willed"," then came after that and claimed that what he used to find of that had gone. [Da'if (weak)]"""
"758","(759) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us that Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us. And Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, saying: It was recited to Ibn Wahb: Sufyan al-Thawri informed you from 'Alqamah ibn Murthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet (ﷺ), that he prayed on the day of the Conquest of Makkah multiple prayers with a single wudu, and wiped over his leather socks. 'Umar ibn al-Khattab said: \I saw you do something you did not use to do.\"" He said: \""I did it deliberately"," O 'Umar.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Hatim from Yahya al-Qattan from al-Thawri. [Sahih. Muslim reported it as no. 277.]"""
"759","(760) Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bishran al-'Adl informed us in Baghdad that Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Bakhtari al-Razzaz informed us that Yahya ibn Ja'far informed us that al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad informed us that Sufyan al-Thawri narrated, mentioning its chain similarly: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed wudu, wiped over his leather socks, and prayed five prayers with a single wudu. Then he mentioned the remainder with the same meaning. [Sahih]"
"760","(761) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl informed us in Baghdad that Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated us that Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us that al-Firyabi narrated to us that Sufyan narrated from 'Amr ibn 'Amir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to perform wudu for every prayer"," and one wudu sufficed any of us so long as he had not broken it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari reported it as no. 211.]"""
"761","(762) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Fāris narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ said — and Abū Dāwūd also narrated from Musaddad, who narrated from ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus, and both said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād narrated from Abī Ghuṭayf al-Hudhalī, who said:\n\nI was with ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar when the call for Ẓuhr was given, so he performed wuḍūʾ and prayed. When the call for ʿAṣr was given, he performed wuḍūʾ again. I asked him about that, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: \Whoever performs wuḍūʾ while already in a state of purity"," Allah records for him ten good deeds.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: This is the ḥadīth of Musaddad"," and it is the more complete version"," though I find the ḥadīth of Ibn Yaḥyā more precise.\n\nThe Shaykh said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād al-Afrīqī is not strong"," and this is a munkar ḥadīth. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 62]"""
"762","(763) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Khaṭṭāb al-Anṣārī narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Hishām narrated.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated.\n\nAnd Abū al-Khayr Jāmiʿ ibn Aḥmad al-Wakīl informed us; Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Hishām and Shuʿbah narrated to us; both said: Qatādah narrated from al-Ḥasan from Abī Rāʿif from Abī Hurayrah from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said:\n\n\When he sits between her four parts and the two circumcised parts meet"," then ghusl becomes obligatory.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm. In the ḥadīth of Wahb ibn Jarīr it reads: \""When he sits between her four parts"," then exerts himself"," ghusl becomes obligatory.\"" And in the ḥadīth of Abū Nuʿaym: \""Then he exerts himself.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from Wahb ibn Jarīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 216]"""
"763","(764) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Qatāda and Maṭar narrated from al-Ḥasan from Abī Rāʿif from Abī Hurayrah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\n\n\When he sits between her four parts"," then exerts himself"," ghusl becomes obligatory.\""\n\nIn the ḥadīth of Maṭar there is the addition: \""Even if he does not ejaculate.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and others from Muʿādh ibn Hishām. Abān ibn Yazīd"," Hammām ibn Yaḥyā"," and Ibn Abī ʿArūbah also narrated the additional wording mentioned by Maṭar from Qatādah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 287]"""
"764","(765) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us; ʿAffān narrated to us; Abān ibn Yazīd al-Aṭṭār and Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; both said: Qatādah narrated from al-Ḥasan from Abī Rāʿif from Abī Hurayrah from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said:\n\n\When he sits between her four parts"," then exerts himself"," ghusl becomes obligatory — whether he ejaculates or does not ejaculate.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"""
"765","(766) Jāmiʿ ibn Aḥmad al-Wakīl narrated to us; Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan from Abī Rāʿif from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\When the two circumcised parts meet"," ghusl becomes obligatory — whether he ejaculates or does not ejaculate.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 2/347]"""
"766","(767) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥām al-Muzakkī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Kāmil narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sulamī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī narrated.\n\nAnd Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us; Abū Mūsā Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us; Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us; Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl narrated from Abī Burdah from Abī Mūsā that they were sitting together and they discussed what necessitates ghusl.\n\nAbū Mūsā added in his ḥadīth that one of those present from among the Muhājirīn said: \When the circumcised part touches the circumcised part"," ghusl becomes obligatory.\"" And one of those present from among the Anṣār said: \""Not until it flows\"" — then they agreed on the meaning. Abū Mūsā said: \""I will bring you the report.\"" So he went to ʿĀʾishah"," greeted her"," and said: \""I wish to ask you about something"," and I feel shy before you.\"" She said: \""Do not feel shy to ask me about something you would have asked your mother who bore you — I am your mother.\"" He said: \""What necessitates ghusl?\"" She said: \""You have come to one who is well-informed. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'When he sits between her four parts and the circumcised part touches the circumcised part"," ghusl becomes obligatory.'\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Sulamī. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from al-Anṣārī.\n\nYaḥyā ibn Saʿīd also narrated it from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab from Abī Mūsā"," except that he did not raise it to the Prophet (ﷺ). And ʿAlī ibn Zayd ibn Judʿān raised it from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab. ʿAlī ibn Zayd is not used as a proof in his ḥadīth. The narration that Muslim extracted in al-Ṣaḥīḥ is a sound"," musnad narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 227]"""
"767","(768) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb narrated. And Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: ʿIyāḍ ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Qurashī and others informed you from Abī al-Zubayr al-Makkī from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: Umm Kulthūm informed me from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), that a man asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about a man who has intercourse with his wife and then becomes limp — is ghusl obligatory upon him? ʿĀʾishah was sitting there. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I do that"," myself and this one (ʿĀʾishah)"," and then we perform ghusl.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 346]"""
"768","(769) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd informed us; my father informed me; I heard al-Awzāʿī say: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad narrated to me from his father from ʿĀʾishah that she was asked about a man who has intercourse with his wife and does not ejaculate water. She said: \I and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did that"," and we both performed ghusl.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/111]"""
"769","(770) As for the ḥadīth that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us; Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, who said: My father informed me; Abū Ayyūb informed me; Ubayy ibn Kaʿb informed me that he said: \O Messenger of Allah"," when a man has intercourse with his woman and does not ejaculate?\"" He said: \""He should wash what touched the woman of him"," then perform wuḍūʾ and pray.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it through other routes from Hishām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 289]"""
"770","(771) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us; Abū Qilābah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated.\n\nAnd Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿĪsā al-Bisṭāmī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to me; my father narrated to me; al-Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated to me; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to me that Abū Salamah narrated to him that ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār narrated to him that Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī narrated to him that he asked ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān about a man who has intercourse but does not ejaculate. He said: \There is no ghusl upon him.\"" Then he said: \""I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" He said: \""After that I asked ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām"," Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydillāh"," and Ubayy ibn Kaʿb"," and they all said the same from the Prophet (ﷺ).\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Bisṭāmī. Abū Qilābah said in his ḥadīth: \""There is nothing upon him except purification (ṭahūr).\"" He did not mention Ubayy or the ḥadīth of ʿUrwah from Abī Ayyūb.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Maʿmar from ʿAbd al-Wārith ibn Saʿīd. And Muslim narrated it from ʿAbd al-Wārith ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad and others from ʿAbd al-Ṣamad"," except that he did not mention the statement of ʿAlī and those with him. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 288]"""
"771","(772) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Muqriʾ informed us in Baghdad: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghrazah informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us: Shaybān Abū Muʿāwiyah informed us, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, that ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār informed him that Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī informed him: \I asked ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān. I said: 'What is your opinion regarding a man who has intercourse with his wife but does not ejaculate?' ʿUthmān said: 'He should perform wuḍūʾ as he does for ṣalāh and wash his private parts.' And he mentioned that he heard this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""\n\n\""So I asked ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām"," and Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbayd Allāh about that"," and they instructed him to do so.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Ḥafṣ from Shaybān"," and he mentioned Ubayy ibn Kaʿb among them. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"772","(773) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us: Shuʿbah informed us, from al-Ḥakam, from Dhakwān Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Saʿīd: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man from the Anṣār and sent a message to him. He came out while his head was dripping with water. He ﷺ said: 'Perhaps we hastened you.' He said: 'Yes"," O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If you are hastened or do not ejaculate"," then there is no ghusl upon you; upon you is wuḍūʾ.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq from al-Naḍr ibn Shuʿayl from Shuʿbah"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr and others from Ghundar from Shuʿbah. This ruling is abrogated by the narrations we have previously mentioned. The evidence for its abrogation is what follows. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 178]"""
"773","(774) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Shādhān informed us in Baghdad from his original: Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar informed us, from Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī, from al-Zuhrī: \A group of the Anṣār"," among them Abū Ayyūb and Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," used to give the fatwā that 'water is from water' (al-māʾ min al-māʾ)"," and that there is no ghusl upon the one who approaches his wife but does not ejaculate. When this was mentioned to ʿUmar"," Ibn ʿUmar"," and ʿĀʾishah"," they rejected it and said: 'When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part"," then ghusl becomes obligatory.'\""\n\n\""Sahl ibn Saʿd"," who had met the Prophet ﷺ during his lifetime and was then fifteen years of age"," narrated to me that Ubayy ibn Kaʿb informed him: 'The fatwā of \""water is from water\"" was a concession (rukhṣah) that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted at the beginning of Islam"," and then He commanded ghusl.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than him]"""
"774","(775) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us in Naysābūr, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿUmar ibn Burhān al-Ghazzāl, and Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān, and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī in Baghdad, all said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us, from Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī, from al-Zuhrī, from Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, from Ubayy ibn Kaʿb, who said: \The fatwā of 'water is from water' was a concession at the beginning of Islam"," and then it was prohibited.\""\n\n\""This ḥadīth was not heard by al-Zuhrī directly from Sahl; rather"," he heard it from some of his companions from Sahl.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than him. Ibn Ḥibbān narrated it"," 1173]"""
"775","(776) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed him: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: ʿAmr, meaning Ibn al-Ḥārith, informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: \Some of those I approve of narrated to me that Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī informed him that Ubayy ibn Kaʿb informed him: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only made that a concession for the people at the beginning of Islam due to the scarcity of clothing"," and then He commanded ghusl and prohibited it.'\""\n\n\""We have also narrated it through another connected"," sound chain from Sahl ibn Saʿd.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than him. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 214]"""
"776","(777) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Muqriʾ informed us in Baghdad: Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād informed us: Mūsā ibn Hārūn informed us: Muḥammad ibn Mihrān al-Jammāl informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Muḥammad ibn Mihrān al-Rāzī informed us: Mubashshir al-Ḥalabī informed us, from Muḥammad ibn Abī Ghassān, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Sahl ibn Saʿd, who said: \Ubayy ibn Kaʿb narrated to me: 'The fatwā that they used to give"," that \""water is from water","\"" was a concession that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted at the beginning of Islam"," and then He commanded ghusl thereafter.'\""\n\nIn the ḥadīth of Mūsā ibn Hārūn: \""Then He commanded us to perform ghusl thereafter.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 215]"""
"777","(778) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Kaʿb, the mawlā of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, that Maḥmūd ibn Labīd al-Anṣārī asked Zayd ibn Thābit about a man who has intercourse with his wife but then becomes slack and does not ejaculate. Zayd said: \He should perform ghusl.\"" Maḥmūd ibn Labīd said to him: \""Ubayy ibn Kaʿb did not consider ghusl to be obligatory.\"" Zayd ibn Thābit said to him: \""Ubayy retracted from that before he died.\""\n\n\""The statement of Ubayy ibn Kaʿb"," 'water is from water","' and his subsequent retraction from it"," indicates that it was confirmed for him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it and then abrogated it. This is also the position of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and others.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it"," 5/1]"""
"778","(779) Abū Aḥmad al-ʿAdl informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, and ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, used to say: \When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part"," then ghusl becomes obligatory.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it"," 102]"""
"779","(780) Ibn Bukayr said: And al-Dārawardī narrated to me, from Jaʿfar, from his father, that ʿAlī used to say: \Whatever necessitates the ḥadd (prescribed punishment) necessitates ghusl.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"780","(781) Through his chain, he said: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from Abū al-Naḍr, the mawlā of ʿUmar ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: \I asked ʿĀʾishah"," the Mother of the Believers"," may Allah be pleased with her: 'What necessitates ghusl?' She said: 'Do you know what your example is"," O Abū Salamah? Your example is like the young chick that hears the rooster crowing and crows along with it. When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part"," then ghusl becomes obligatory.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it"," 77]"""
"781","(782) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he used to say: \When the circumcised part meets the circumcised part"," ghusl becomes obligatory.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"782","(783) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated from Sufyān, from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ and Hishām, from Ibn Sīrīn, who said: \I asked ʿUbaydah what necessitates ghusl?\"" He said: \""The ejaculation (dafq) and the meeting (khilāṭ).\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"783","(784) And with his chain of narration, from Sufyān, from Jābir, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, a similar narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"784","(785) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUqayl al-Khuzāʿī narrated to us from his book, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Jābir, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \When the circumcised part passes beyond the circumcised part"," ghusl has become obligatory.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"785","(786) And from him, from al-Shaʿbī, from al-Ḥārith al-Aʿwar, from ʿAlī, a similar narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"786","(787) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, ʿAmr — meaning Ibn al-Ḥārith — informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Water is from water (al-māʾu min al-māʾ).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd"," from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 345]"""
"787","(788) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Zāʾidah narrated from Rukayn ibn al-Rabīʿ, from Ḥuṣayn ibn Qabīṣah al-Fazārī, from ʿAlī, who said: \I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about madhī (pre-seminal fluid)"," and he said: 'When you see madhī"," perform wuḍūʾ and wash your private part. And when you see the gushing of water (naḍḥ al-māʾ)"," then perform ghusl.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 206]"""
"788","(789) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Kūfī al-Muṭayyan narrated to us, ʿAmr al-Nāqid narrated to us, Ḥumayd al-Ruʾāsī narrated to us, al-Ḥasan — meaning Ibn Ṣāliḥ — narrated from Bayān, from Ḥuṣayn ibn Ṣafwān, from ʿAlī, who said: \I was a man who experienced abundant madhī. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to know that the water had caused me distress"," he said: 'Ghusl is only from the ejaculating water (al-māʾ al-dāfiq).'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Yaʿlā narrated it"," 362]"""
"789","(790) Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿUrbah al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī Maʿshar al-Sulamī informed us in Ḥarrān, Abū Kurayb narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Khālid narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from his brother ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from al-Qāsim, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about a man who sees wetness in his sleep but does not recall a wet dream. He said: 'He should perform ghusl. And if he sees that he had a wet dream but does not see any wetness"," then there is no ghusl upon him.'\""\n\n[Ḥasan for other than him. Abū Yaʿlā narrated it"," 4694]"""
"790","(791) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, Mālik narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Khwārizmī informed us in Baghdād, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad — meaning Ibn Ḥamdān al-Naysābūrī — narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Ibn Abī Uways informed me, Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that she said: \Umm Sulaym"," the wife of Abū Ṭalḥah al-Anṣārī"," came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," indeed Allah is not shy from the truth. Is there ghusl upon a woman when she experiences a wet dream?' He said: 'Yes"," when she sees the water (al-māʾ).'\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Uways. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf and Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"," and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah.\n\nAmong them is: [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 278]"""
"791","(792) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Ka'bi narrated to us that Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us that Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us that Waki' narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah — he mentioned it with its chain of narration and its meaning, and added: \I said to her: You have exposed the women! Does a woman experience wet dreams?\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""May your right hand be dusted — by what means"," then"," would her child resemble her?\""\n\nMuslim transmitted it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. Thus said Hisham"," but al-Zuhri contradicted him"," saying: from 'Urwah"," from 'A'ishah."""
"792","(793) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us that Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us that 'Ubayd — meaning ibn Sharik — narrated to us that Yahya — meaning ibn Bukayr — narrated to us that al-Layth narrated from 'Uqayl from Ibn Shihab from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she related to him: Umm Sulaym, mother of the sons of Abi Talhah, went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," indeed Allah is not shy of the truth. Tell me"," if a woman sees in her sleep what a man sees"," should she perform ghusl?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" 'A'ishah said: \""Shame on you! Does a woman see that?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to her and said: \""May your hands be dusted — from where"," then"," would the resemblance come?\""\n\nMuslim transmitted it in his Sahih from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth"," from his father"," from his grandfather.\n\nAnd similarly it was transmitted by Yunus ibn Yazid"," al-Zubaydi"," and the brother of al-Zuhri from al-Zuhri"," and Malik sent it as a mursal report from him in most of the narrations"," except that Ibn Abi al-Wazir transmitted from Malik and connected its chain thus.\n\nAnd Musafi' al-Hajabi transmitted from 'Urwah in a manner similar to the narration of al-Zuhri."""
"793","(794) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us that Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us that Isma'il ibn Khalil narrated to us that Yahya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us —\n\nAND — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us that 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us that Abu Kurayb narrated to us that Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated from his father, from Mus'ab ibn Shaybah, from Musafi' ibn 'Abd Allah, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah: that a woman said: \O Messenger of Allah"," should a woman perform ghusl if she experiences a wet dream or sees water?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" 'A'ishah said to her: \""May your hands be dusted.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Leave her — for resemblance only comes from that. When her fluid overrides the man's fluid"," the child resembles the maternal uncles; and when the man's fluid overrides her fluid"," the child resembles the paternal uncles.\""\n\nMuslim transmitted it in his Sahih from Abu Kurayb and others from Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah."""
"794","(795) Abu 'Abd Allah narrated to us that Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that 'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali and Ahmad ibn Sahl and Husayn ibn Muhammad said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us that Salih ibn 'Umar narrated to us that Abu Malik al-Ash'ani narrated from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A woman asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees in his dream. He said: \If that which happens to a man happens to her"," let her perform ghusl.\""\n\nMuslim transmitted it from Dawud ibn Rushayd."""
"795","(796) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us that Abu Dawud narrated to us that Qutaybah narrated to us that Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us that 'Abd Allah al-'Umari narrated from 'Ubayd Allah from al-Qasim from 'A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who finds moisture but does not recall a wet dream — he said: \He must perform ghusl.\"" And about a man who sees that he has had a wet dream but finds no moisture — he said: \""There is no ghusl upon him.\"" Umm Sulaym said: \""If a woman sees that"," is there ghusl upon her?\"" He said: \""Yes — indeed women are the counterparts of men.\"""""
"796","(797) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us that Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us that Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us that Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us —\n\nAND — Abu 'Abd Allah narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that 'Imran ibn Musa and Ahmad ibn al-Nadr ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab both narrated to us that al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us that Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated to us that Sa'id narrated from Qatadah that Anas ibn Malik narrated to them that Umm Sulaym related: that she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees in his dream. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \If a woman sees that"," let her perform ghusl.\"" Umm Sulaym said — and she was shy about that: \""Does that happen?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""From where"," then"," would the resemblance come? The man's fluid is thick and white"," and the woman's fluid is thin and yellow. Whichever of the two prevails or precedes — from that comes the resemblance.\""\n\nThe wording of the hadith of al-'Abbas — Muslim transmitted it in his Sahih from al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi."""
"797","(798) Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us that Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Qattan narrated to us that Abu Yahya 'Abd al-Karim ibn al-Haytham al-Dayraquli informed us that Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us that Mu'awiyah ibn Salam narrated from Zayd ibn Salam that he heard Abu Salam narrate that Abu Asma' al-Rahabi narrated that Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said: I was standing by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a scholar from among the Jewish rabbis came and said: \Peace be upon you"," O Muhammad.\"" I pushed him with a push that nearly caused him to fall. The Jewish man said: \""Why did you push me?\"" I said: \""Why do you not say"," 'O Messenger of Allah'?\"" The Jewish man said: \""We only call him by the name which his family gave him.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Indeed"," the name by which my family named me is Muhammad.\"" The Jewish man said: \""I have come to ask you about a matter.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Will it benefit you anything if I narrate to you?\"" He said: \""I will listen with my two ears.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew lines with a stick that was with him and then said: \""Ask.\"" The Jewish man said: \""Where will the people be on the day when the earth is changed into other than the earth and the heavens?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""They will be in darkness"," before the bridge.\"" He said: \""Who will be the first people to cross?\"" He said: \""The poor among the Muhajirun.\"" The Jewish man said: \""What will be their greeting when they enter Paradise?\"" He said: \""The increase of the liver of the whale.\"" He said: \""What will be their food after that?\"" He said: \""The bull of Paradise will be slaughtered for them — the one that used to eat from its sides.\"" He said: \""What will be their drink upon that?\"" He said: \""From a spring therein called Salsabil.\"" He said: \""You have spoken the truth.\"" He said: \""I have come to ask you about a matter which no one on the people of the earth knows except a prophet"," or one or two men.\"" He said: \""Will it benefit you if I narrate to you?\"" He said: \""I will listen with my two ears.\"" He said: \""I have come to ask you about the child.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""The man's fluid is white"," and the woman's fluid is yellow. When the man's semen overrides the woman's semen"," they produce a male child"," by the permission of Allah the Most High; and when the woman's semen overrides the man's semen"," they produce a female child"," by the permission of Allah.\"" He said: \""You have spoken the truth"," and indeed you are a prophet.\"" Then he departed. The Prophet ﷺ said: \""This one asked me about that which I asked me"," and I had no knowledge of it whatsoever until Allah brought it to me.\""\n\nMuslim transmitted it in his Sahih from al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Hulwani from Abu Tawbah."""
"798","(799) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us that Abu Dawud narrated to us that Qutaybah narrated to us that 'Ubaydah ibn Humayd al-Hadda' narrated from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi' from Husayn ibn Qabisah from 'Ali, who said: I was a man who experienced frequent madhy (pre-seminal fluid), so I would perform ghusl until my back cracked. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ — or it was mentioned to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do not do that. When you see madhy"," wash your private parts and perform wudu as you would for the prayer. When you ejaculate water (i.e."," semen)"," then perform ghusl.\"""""
"799","(800) Abu Nasr 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us that Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Shayban al-Baghdadi al-Harawi informed us that Mu'adh ibn Najdah narrated to us that Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us that Malik ibn Mighwal narrated from Zur'ah Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: \Al-maniyy (semen)"," al-madhy (pre-seminal fluid)"," and al-wady (post-urinary fluid) — as for al-maniyy"," it is that which necessitates ghusl; and as for al-wady and al-madhy"," he said: 'Wash your private parts and perform wudu as you would for the prayer.'\""\n\nAnd we have received from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar regarding al-madhy something similar to that."""
"800","(801) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb narrated from Malik and others.\n\nAND — Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-'Adl narrated to us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abdi narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Malik narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father, from Zayd ibn al-Salt, who said: I went out with 'Umar ibn al-Khattab to al-Jurf. He looked and saw that he had experienced a wet dream, yet he had prayed without performing ghusl. He said: \By Allah"," I do not think I have had a wet dream without realizing it"," and I have prayed without performing ghusl.\"" He then performed ghusl"," washed what he saw on his garment"," and sprinkled water on what he had not seen. He then gave the adhan and the iqamah"," and prayed after the sun had risen"," settling himself fully. This is the wording of Ibn Bukayr."""
"801","(802) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us — Ibn Bukayr informed us — Mālik from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Sulaymān ibn Yasār: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb led the people in the morning prayer, then went to his land at al-Jurfs, and found traces of a wet dream (iḥtilām) upon his garment. He said: \When the wadak (a type of perfume) reaches us"," the veins soften.\"" He then performed ghusl (ritual bath)"," washed what he saw of the wet dream on his garment"," and repeated the prayer. [Ṣaḥīḥ in its own right. Reported by Mālik"," 113.]"""
"802","(803) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī — Yazīd ibn Hārūn — Ibn Abī Dhīb from al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah and ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from ʿĀʾishah: that Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh experienced istiḥāḍah (irregular bleeding) for seven years, and she was the wife of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf. She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said: \It is merely a vein (ʿirq) and not menstruation (ḥayḍah). Perform ghusl and pray.\"" She would therefore perform ghusl for every prayer. [Authenticated in the Ṣaḥīḥ of al-Bukhārī from the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Dhīb"," and in the Ṣaḥīḥ of Muslim from the ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith from al-Zuhrī from both of them. Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"803","(804) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh: Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī — both of them said — Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd — my father — al-Awzāʿī — al-Zuhrī — ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr and ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd ibn Zurārah: that ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: \Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh experienced istiḥāḍah while she was married to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf"," for seven years. She complained of that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'It is not menstruation; it is merely a vein. When the menstruation comes"," leave the prayer. When it departs"," perform ghusl and then pray.'\"" ʿĀʾishah said: \""Umm Ḥabībah would sit in a vessel belonging to her sister Zaynab bint Jaḥsh"," to the point that the redness of the blood would rise above the water.\"" The Shaykh said: His statement \""When the menstruation comes\"" in this ḥadīth — none of the companions of al-Zuhrī mentioned it other than al-Awzāʿī. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"804","(805) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us — Abū Ḥāmid: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ, in the year twenty-five and three hundred — Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī and Abū al-Azhar: Aḥmad ibn al-Azhar — both of them said — ʿAbd al-Razzāq ibn Hammām — ʿUbayd Allāh and ʿAbd Allāh, the two sons of ʿUmar — from Saʿīd al-Maqburī from Abū Hurayrah: that Thumāmah ibn Uthāl al-Ḥanafī was captured. The Prophet ﷺ would go to him and say: \What do you have to say"," O Thumāmah?\"" He would say: \""If you kill"," you kill one with blood (i.e."," one whose people will seek vengeance); if you show favor"," you show favor upon one who is grateful; and if you desire wealth"," we will give you whatever you wish.\"" The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ loved ransoming and said: \""What would we gain by killing this man?\"" One day the Prophet ﷺ passed by him and he accepted Islam"," so he released him and sent him to the garden of Abū Ṭalḥah"," commanding him to perform ghusl. He performed ghusl and prayed two rakʿahs"," and the Prophet ﷺ said: \""Your brother has indeed become a good Muslim.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 253.]"""
"805","(806) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — Baḥr ibn Naṣr al-Khawlānī — he said: It was recited to Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth: \Your father informed you\"" — from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī"," that he heard Abū Hurayrah saying: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent cavalry toward Najd"," and they brought a man from Banū Ḥanīfah called Thumāmah ibn Uthāl"," the chief of al-Yamāmah. They tied him to one of the pillars of the mosque.\"" He mentioned the ḥadīth"," and in it the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Release Thumāmah.\"" So he went to a palm tree near the mosque and performed ghusl"," then entered the mosque and said: \""I bear witness that there is no god but Allah"," and I bear witness that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah.\"" He mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from al-Layth. In this narration"," the ghusl precedes the shahādah (declaration of faith). It is also possible that he accepted Islam in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ"," then performed ghusl"," entered the mosque"," and then made the declaration of faith — harmonizing between the two narrations. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by al-Bukhārī"," 450.]"""
"806","(807) And Abū al-Ḥasan: ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār — al-Ḥasan ibn Sahl al-Mujawwiz — Abū ʿĀṣim — Sufyān from al-Agharr from Khalīfah ibn Ḥuṣayn from Qays ibn ʿĀṣim: that he came to the Prophet ﷺ and accepted Islam, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to perform ghusl with water and lote-tree leaves (sidr). And thus did Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrate it from Sufyān al-Thawrī. And Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated it similarly. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by al-Tirmidhī, 605.]"
"807","(808) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān — both of them said — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār — Saʿdān ibn Naṣr — Wakīʿ — Sufyān — al-Agharr — Khalīfah ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, that his grandfather Qays ibn ʿĀṣim: came to the Prophet ﷺ wishing to accept Islam, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to perform ghusl with water and lote-tree leaves. And Muḥammad ibn Kathīr and a group narrated its meaning, except that most of them said: \From his grandfather"," Qays ibn ʿĀṣim.\"" And Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah narrated it and added to its isnād. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"808","(809) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān — Qabīṣah — Sufyān — al-Agharr, who is Ibn al-Ṣabāḥ, a mawlā of Banī Minqar — from Khalīfah ibn Ḥuṣayn from his father: that his grandfather Qays ibn ʿĀṣim came to the Prophet ﷺ and accepted Islam, and he was commanded to perform ghusl with water and lote-tree leaves. [Munkar al-Isnād.]"
"809","(810) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh — Muʿādh ibn Najdah al-Qurashī — Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah, and he mentioned it thus. [Munkar al-Isnād.]"
"810","(811) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah — Abū Dāwūd — Makhlad ibn Khālid — ʿAbd al-Razzāq — Ibn Jurayj — he said: I was informed from ʿUthaym ibn Kulayb from his father from his grandfather: that he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \I have accepted Islam.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \""Remove from yourself the hair of disbelief (shaʿr al-kufr)\"" — meaning"," shave it. He said: And another narrator informed me that the Prophet ﷺ said to another man who was with him: \""Remove from yourself the hair of disbelief and be circumcised (ikhtatin).\"" [Ḥasan in its own right. Reported by Abū Dāwūd"," 356.]"""
"811","(812) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from his original source: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us by dictation, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr informed us, Muʿāwiya ibn ʿAmr informed us, Zāʾida narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwa, from his father, from ʿĀʾisha that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he performed ghusl from janāba, would begin by washing his hands from the vessel before placing his hand into the vessel, then he would perform wuḍūʾ similar to his wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr al-Nāqid from Muʿāwiya ibn ʿAmr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it, no. 245.]"
"812","(813) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Qutayba informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shayba informed us, Wakīʿ narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwa, from his father, from ʿĀʾisha that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ghusl from janāba and began by washing his palms three times, then he performed his wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh, then he placed his hand and ran his fingers through the roots of his hair until it seemed to me that he had reached the skin, then he poured water over his head, then he poured water over the rest of his body.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shayba. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it, no. 316.]"
"813","(814) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us. Baḥr ibn Naṣr said: it was read to Ibn Wahb: Makhrama, meaning Ibn Bukayr, informed you from his father, from Abū Salama ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: ʿĀʾisha said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he performed ghusl, would begin with his right hand and pour water over it, then wash it, then pour water over the impurity that was upon it with his right hand, and wash it away with his left hand, until he finished that. I think he added: he poured water over his head.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn al-Aylī from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it, no. 321.]"
"814","(815) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Abū ʿAmr al-Mustamlī informed us, ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr informed us, ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd, from Kurayb, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: My aunt Maymūna narrated to me, saying: I brought the water for the ghusl of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from janāba. He washed his palms two or three times, then he placed his right palm in the vessel and poured water over his private parts, washing them with his left hand, then he struck the ground with his left hand and rubbed it vigorously, then he performed his wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh, then he poured three handfuls, filling both his palms, over his head, then he washed the rest of his body, then he moved away from that spot and washed his feet. Then I brought him a cloth (mandīl), but he refused it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it, no. 317.]"
"815","(816) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us, Abū Muʿāwiya narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Sālim, from Kurayb, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from Maymūma, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: The Prophet ﷺ, when he performed ghusl from janāba, would begin by pouring the vessel over his hand and washing it three times, then he would pour with his right hand over his left hand, then over his private parts, then he would strike the ground with his hand and wipe it, then he would wash it, then he would perform his wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh, then he would pour water over his head and the rest of his body, then he would move away and wash his feet.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others from Abī Muʿāwiya. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it, no. 317.]"
"816","(817) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us, al-Ḥumaydī informed us, Sufyān informed us, al-Aʿmash narrated it with his chain of narration that the Prophet ﷺ performed ghusl from janāba and washed his private parts with his hand, then rubbed it against the wall, then washed it, then performed his wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh, and when he finished his ghusl, he washed his feet.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it, no. 257.]"
"817","(818) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsa informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Shawkar informed us, Hushaym narrated from ʿUrwa al-Hamdānī, al-Shaʿbī informed us, saying: ʿľʾisha said: If you wish, I can show you the trace of the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the wall where he used to perform ghusl from janāba.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it, no. 1244.]"
"818","(819) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, Hishām narrated from his father that ʿĀʾisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would begin by washing his hands, then perform his wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh, then place his palms in the water and run his fingers through the roots of his hair, until when it seemed to him that he had reached the skin, he would scoop water with his hand in three scoops and pour them over his head, then he would perform ghusl.\n\nExtracted in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of Hishām ibn ʿUrwa. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it, no. 245.]"
"819","(820) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad and Ismāʿīl ibn Qutayba said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Abū Muʿāwiya narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwa, from his father, from ʿľʾisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he performed ghusl from janāba, would begin by washing his hands, then pour with his right hand over his left hand, wash his private parts, then perform his wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh, then take water and insert his fingers into the roots of the hair, until when he saw that he had reached the skin, he would scoop three handfuls over his head, then pour water over the rest of his body, then wash his feet.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. His statement at the end of this ḥadīth: \then he washed his feet\"" — this is a ṣaḥīḥ gharīb wording preserved by Abū Muʿāwiya alone from among the trustworthy companions of Hishām. And that was for the purpose of cleaning"," if Allah the Most High wills. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 316.]"""
"820","(821) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated from Sufyān, from al-Aʿmash, from Sālim, from Kurayb, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from Maymūna bint al-Ḥārith, who said: I screened the Prophet ﷺ while he was performing ghusl from janāba. He began by washing his hands, then poured with his right hand over his left hand, washed his private parts and whatever had soiled them, then struck the wall with his hand, then performed his wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh, except for his feet, then poured water over himself, then moved his feet aside and washed them.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Firyābī from Sufyān al-Thawrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it, no. 246.]"
"821","(822) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed ghusl from janābah"," he would begin by washing his hands. Then he would take water with his right hand and pour it over his left hand"," and wash his private parts until he had cleansed them. Then he would rinse his mouth three times"," snuff water into his nose three times"," and wash his face three times and his arms three times each. Then he would pour water over his head and his body. When he had finished"," he would wash his feet.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for others. Al-Ṭayālīsī narrated it (1474)]"""
"822","(823) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik narrated from Hishām from his father from ʿĀʾishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he performed ghusl from janābah, would begin by washing his hands, then perform wuḍūʾ as he would perform it for ṣalāh, then insert his fingers into the water and therewith part the roots of his hair, then pour three handfuls of water over his head with his two hands, then pour the water over his entire body. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (245)]"
"823","(824) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qāsim ibn al-Qāsim al-Sayyārī in Marw informed us that Abū al-Muwajjah Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Muwajjah al-Fazārī informed us that ʿAbdān informed us that ʿAbdullāh narrated to us that Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated from his father from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," when he performed ghusl from janābah"," would wash his hands and perform his wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh"," then part his hair with his hand until"," when he deemed that he had moistened his skin"," he would pour water over it three times"," then wash the rest of his body.\"" She said: \""I and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would perform ghusl from a single vessel"," both of us taking handfuls from it together.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (269)]"""
"824","(825) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Muslim narrated to us that Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us that Ḥammād, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would perform wuḍūʾ from janābah, then insert his right hand into the water, then part the right side of his head therewith, following it through to the roots of the hair, then do the same to the left side of his head with his left hand, until he had thoroughly moistened the skin, then pour water over his head three times. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (255)]"
"825","(826) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us that Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Jaʿfar al-Muqrīʾ in the year thirty-three and three hundred narrated to us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Warrāq narrated to us that Ḥajjāj, ʿAffān, and ʿUbaydullāh narrated — and the wording is that of ʿAffān — who said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us that ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated from Zādhān that ʿAlī said: \I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: 'Whoever leaves a hair's breadth of his body from janābah untouched by water"," such and such will be done to him in the Fire.'\"" ʿAlī said: \""It is because of that that I came to despise my head.\"" ʿUbaydullāh said in his hadith: \""And he used to shave his hair.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (349)]"""
"826","(827) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Naṣr ibn ʿAlī and Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr said: al-Ḥārith ibn Wajīh al-Rāsibī narrated to us that Mālik ibn Dīnār narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Beneath every hair is janābah; therefore wash the hair and cleanse the skin.\"" Al-Ḥārith ibn Wajīh is alone in narrating it in connected form"," and al-Ḥārith ibn Wajīh has been spoken about by the scholars. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (248)]"""
"827","(828) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us that al-Asfāṭī, meaning al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl, Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Wāsiṭī, and al-Ḥasan ibn Sahl said: Abū al-Walīd Hishām ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated to us that Quraysh ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Farrūkh said: \I met Abū Ayyūb and shook his hand"," and he found my nails to be long.\"" He said: \""A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and asked him about the news of the heavens. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'One of you asks about the news of the heavens while he leaves his nails like the talons of birds"," in which janābah and filth accumulate.'\"" The wording is that of al-Asfāṭī. A group narrated it from Quraysh. Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālīsī also narrated it. [Ḍaʿīf. Aḥmad narrated it (417)]"""
"828","(829) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Quraysh ibn Ḥayyān narrated from Wāʾil ibn Sulaym, who said: \I came to Abū Ayyūb al-Azdī and shook his hand"," and he saw that my nails were long. He said: 'A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and asked him. He said: \""One of you asks me about the news of the heavens while he leaves his nails like the talons of birds"," in which janābah and filth accumulate.\""'\"" This is a mursal narration. Abū Ayyūb al-Azdī is other than Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Ṭayālīsī narrated it (596)]"""
"829","(830) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated. (H) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us that al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," when he intended to perform ghusl from janābah"," would begin by washing his hands before placing them into the vessel"," then wash his private parts"," then perform his wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh"," then saturate his hair with water"," then pour three handfuls over his head.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said in his chain from Hishām"," and he said in the hadith: \""He would wash his hand before placing it into the vessel.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it (242)]"""
"830","(831) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk informed us that Abū Qalābah ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad al-Raqāshī informed us that Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Makhūl from Abū Jaʿfar from Jābir, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," when he performed ghusl from janābah"," would pour water over his head three times.\"" A man said: \""My hair is abundant.\"" Jābir said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had more hair than you and it was finer.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Ghundar from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (256)]"""
"831","(832) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān informed us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir, that the Prophet ﷺ would pour water over his head three times while he was in a state of janābah. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Jaʿfar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim, 329]"
"832","(833) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed me: ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ghusl from janābah"," he would pour three handfuls of water over his head.\"" Al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad said: \""My hair is thick.\"" Jāfir said: I said to him: \""O son of my brother"," the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more abundant and finer than yours.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 329]"""
"833","(834) Abū Ḥāzim ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-ʿAdl informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Ṣaffār narrated to us in the year 296 AH: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ informed us, from Abī Isḥāq, from Sulaymān ibn Ṣurad, from Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, who said: \They disputed regarding ghusl in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Some of the people said: 'As for me"," I wash my head such and such.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'As for me"," I pour three handfuls over my head.'\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 327]"""
"834","(835) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: ʿAmr ibn Marzūq informed us: Zuhayr informed us, from Abī Isḥāq, who said: Sulaymān ibn Ṣurad narrated to me, from Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, who said: \We mentioned ghusl from janābah in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'As for me"," I pour water over my head three times.'\"" Zuhayr described it and said: \""He placed the inner side of his palms toward the sky and their outer side toward the earth.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym"," from Zuhayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 251]"""
"835","(836) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Sālim, from Kurayb, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from Maymūnah, who said: \I placed water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ghusl from janābah. He poured water onto his right hand and washed it"," then poured with his right hand onto his left hand and washed it"," then poured with his right hand onto his left and washed his private parts. Then he struck his hand on the earth"," then performed wuḍūʾ as he would for ṣalāh"," then poured water over his head with his hand three times"," then over the rest of his body. Then he moved away from where he had bathed and washed his feet. I brought him a cloth but he did not take it; rather he shook the water off with his hand.\"" Ḥafṣ said: al-Aʿmash said: \""I mentioned this to Ibrāhīm"," and he said: 'They only disliked that out of fear that it would become a habit (ʿādah).'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ"," from his father. And we have narrated something similar from ʿUrwah"," from ʿĀʾishah"," from the Prophet ﷺ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 270]"""
"836","(837) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Fasawī informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar informed us: Muʿādh ibn Hishām informed us: my father narrated to me, from Qatādah, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \When he performed ghusl from janābah"," he would sprinkle water into his eyes and insert his finger into his navel.\"" Mawqūf. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr"," 7/14]"""
"837","(838) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that when he performed ghusl from janābah, he would sprinkle water into his eyes. Mālik said: \There is no practice established upon this.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""He is not required to sprinkle water into his eyes"," because they are not external parts of his body.\"" The Shaykh said: \""It has also been narrated as marfūʿ"," but its chain is not sound.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"," 54]"""
"838","(839) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Wakīʿ informed us: al-Aʿmash informed us, from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd, from Kurayb, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās informed us, from his maternal aunt Maymūnah, who said: \I placed water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he performed ghusl from janābah. He tilted the vessel with his left hand onto his right hand"," washed his palms three times"," then poured water over his private parts and washed them. Then he placed his hand on the wall or the earth and rubbed it. Then he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose"," washed his face and his forearms"," poured water over his head"," then poured water over the rest of his body. Then he moved away and washed his feet. I brought him a garment"," and he gestured with his hand thus"," meaning he refused it.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ through various routes from al-Aʿmash"," and he used it as evidence for the one who performs wuḍūʾ from janābah and then washes the rest of his body without rewashing the places of wuḍūʾ. Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others"," from Wakīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 254]"""
"839","(840) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah informed us, from Abī Isḥāq, who said: I heard Sulaymān ibn Ṣurad; I heard Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim say: \Ghusl from janābah was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'As for me"," I pour water over my head three times.'\"" It is recorded in the book of Muslim from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"840","(841) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth informed us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir, that some people came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about ghusl from janābah, saying: \We live in a cold land.\"" He said: \""It is sufficient for one of you to scoop three handfuls of water over his head.\"" It is recorded in the Ṣaḥīḥ of Muslim from the ḥadīth of Jaʿfar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 328]"""
"841","(842) Abū Bakr ibn Furak informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Hushaym narrated from Abū Bishr from Abū Sufyān from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh that the people of Ṭāʾif said: \O Messenger of Allah"," our land is a cold land. What will suffice us for the ghusl of janābah?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""As for me"," I pour water over my head three times.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others from Hushaym. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"842","(843) Abū ʿAbdullāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us that Sufyān — time after time — narrated from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī from ʿAbdullāh ibn Rāfiʿ, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: I said, \O Messenger of Allah"," I am a woman who braids the hair of my head tightly. Should I undo it for the ghusl of janābah?\"" He said: \""No. It will suffice you to pour three handfuls of water over it"," then pour water over yourself and you will become pure.\"" Or he said: \""Then you will have become pure.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and a group from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 330]"""
"843","(844) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar from his father, that he used to say: \What wuḍūʾ is more complete than the ghusl when the private parts are washed (in the course of it)?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 1038]"""
"844","(845) Through this isnād, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, who said: They asked Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib about a man who performs ghusl from janābah — will that suffice him for wuḍūʾ? He said: \Yes"," but let him wash his feet.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī that he said regarding one who forgets to rinse the mouth and sniff water into the nose during ghusl of janābah: \""He does not repeat the ṣalāh.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"845","(846) Abū ʿAbdullāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb al-ʿAdl informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us that ʿAwf ibn Abī Jamīlah narrated from Abū Rajāʾ al-ʿUṭāridī from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said: We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)… and he mentioned the hadith. He said: He called for the ṣalāh and led the people in prayer. When he turned away from the prayer, he saw a man sitting apart who had not prayed with the people. He said: \What prevented you"," O so-and-so"," from praying with the people?\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I have been afflicted with janābah and there is no water.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Then use the clean earth"," for it will suffice you.\"" And he mentioned the hadith. He said: The last of that was that he gave the one afflicted with janābah a vessel of water and said: \""Go and pour it over yourself.\""\n\nIt is recorded in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of ʿAwf ibn Abī Jamīlah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"846","(847) Abū Bakr ibn Furak informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah and Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb from Abū Qilābah from a man of Banī ʿĀmir, who said: I saw Abū Dharr… and he mentioned the hadith regarding janābefalling upon him when there was no water. He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O Abū Dharr"," the clean earth is sufficient for you"," even if you do not find water for ten years. And when you find water"," then let it touch your skin.\""\n\nYūnus ibn Ḥabīb said: And Abū Ḥafṣ informed us that Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ from Abū Qilābah from ʿAmr ibn Budjān"," who said: I heard Abū Dharr"," meaning this very narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"847","(848) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Ayyūb ibn Jābir narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿIṣmah from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: The ṣalāh was fifty, the ghusl from janābah was seven times, and washing urine from clothing was seven times. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) continued to ask until the ṣalāh was made five, the ghusl from janābah was made once, and washing urine from clothing was made once.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said, as was narrated from him: As for what has been narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ): \Under every hair is janābah"," so wet the hair and clean the skin\"" — it is not established. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 247]"""
"848","(849) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAdī informed us that al-Faḍl ibn Ḥubāb informed us that Abū ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī narrated to us that al-Ḥārith ibn Wajīh narrated from Mālik ibn Dīnār from Ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Under every hair is janābah"," so wet the hair and clean the skin.\""\n\nAl-Ḥārith ibn Wajīh is alone in narrating it in this manner.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdullāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad said: I asked Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn about al-Ḥārith ibn Wajīh"," and he said: \""His ḥadīth is nothing.\""\n\nOthers among the scholars of ḥadīth also rejected it — al-Bukhārī"," Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī"," and others. It is only narrated from al-Ḥasan from the Prophet (ﷺ) as a mursal narration"," and from al-Ḥasan from Abū Hurayrah as a mawqūf narration"," and from al-Nakhaʿī: \""It used to be said…\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," in the narration of al-Zaʿfarānī and others from him"," interpreted it to mean the apparent and the hidden — the interior of the nose and the mouth being among the hidden parts"," comparable to the interior of the eyes and the interior of the ears. So those who spoke about this matter alongside al-Shāfiʿī said: \""Analogy dictates that he should not repeat"," but we take from the athar of Ibn ʿAbbās.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"849","(850) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Asbāṭ narrated to us that Abū Ḥanīfah narrated from ʿUthmān ibn Rāshid from ʿĀʾishah bint ʿAjarad from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \He does not repeat (the ghusl) unless he is junub — meaning (he must repeat) the rinsing of the mouth and sniffing of water into the nose.\""\n\nAnd likewise al-Thawrī narrated it from ʿUthmān. ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar said: ʿĀʾishah bint ʿAjarad has no narration other than this ḥadīth.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: The athr upon which ʿUthmān ibn Rāshid relies is from ʿĀʾishah bint ʿAjarad from Ibn ʿAbbās"," and he claims that this athr is established"," for which analogy is abandoned. And he reproaches us for taking the ḥadīth of Busrah bint Ṣafwān from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nʿUthmān and ʿĀʾishah are not known in their land"," and how can it be permissible for anyone who knows to establish a weak"," unknown narrator and weaken a strong"," well-known one?\n\nThe Shaykh said: And al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh narrated it from ʿĀʾishah bint ʿAjarad. And al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh is not a valid authority. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/115]"""
"850","(851) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that al-Asfāṭī narrated to us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Zuhayr narrated from Abū Isḥāq from al-Aswad from ʿĀʾishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to perform ghusl and then pray the two rakʿahs of Fajr, and I do not think he performed a fresh wuḍūʾ after the ghusl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 250]"
"851","(852) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaydalānī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us; Abū Nuʿaym informed us; Sharīk narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Aswad, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not perform wuḍūʾ after taking the ghusl of janābah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī"," 107]"""
"852","(853) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh informed us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-Bakhtarī informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh informed us; my father informed us; Shuʿbah narrated from Ibrāhīm — who is ibn Muhājir — from Ṣafiyyah bint Shaybah, from ʿĀʾishah, that Asmāʾ — i.e., the daughter of Shakal — asked the Prophet ﷺ about ghusl from ḥayḍ (menstruation). He said: \Let one of you take her water and her lotus leaves"," purify herself"," and perform purification well. Then she should pour water over her head and rub it vigorously until it reaches the roots of her hair. Then she should pour water over herself. Then she should take a piece of cloth scented with musk and purify herself with it.\"" She said: \""How shall I purify myself with it?\"" He said: \""Subḥān Allāh! Purify yourself with it.\"" And he turned away. ʿĀʾishah said: \""She should apply it to the traces of blood.\"" And she asked him about ghusl from janābah. He said: \""Take your water and purify yourself with the best and most thorough purification. Then pour water over your head"," then rub it until it reaches the roots of your hair"," then pour water over yourself.\"" ʿĀʾishah said: \""Excellent indeed are the women of the Anṣār — modesty did not prevent them from asking about religion and seeking understanding in it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh. Thus it is in our book: \""shuʾūn.\"" The scholars of language say \""sūr\"" or \""shawā","\"" and they said: \""sūruhu\"" means its highest part"," and \""shawāhu\"" means its skin. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 332]"""
"853","(854) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Hārūn ibn Sulaymān informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī informed us; Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah narrated from Ṣadaqah; Jumayʿ ibn ʿUmayr — the brother of Banī Taym Allāh ibn Thaʿlabah — informed us. He said: \I entered upon ʿĀʾishah with my mother and my maternal aunt"," and one of them asked her: 'How did you used to perform ghusl?' ʿĀʾishah said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would perform the wuḍūʾ he performed for ṣalāh"," then pour water over his head three times. And we would pour water over our heads five times on account of the braids (al-ḍufur).'\"" [Very weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 241]"""
"854","(855) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh informed me; Muḥammad ibn Yūnus informed us; Rūḥ informed us; Shuʿbah narrated from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām, from Ḥudhayfah, that he said: \Part it with water; do not part it with fire"," for its remaining traces are little.\""\n\nAnd al-Thawrī narrated it from Manṣūr with his isnād"," from Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān"," that he said to his wife: \""Part your head with water; do not part it with fire"," for its remaining traces upon it are little.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Dārimī"," 1148]"""
"855","(856) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; al-Thawrī narrated from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rāfiʿ — the freed slave of Umm Salamah — from Umm Salamah, who said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I am a woman who binds the braids of her head tightly' — or she said: 'the coils of my head' — 'Should I undo them for janābah and ḥayḍ?' He said: 'No. It is sufficient for you to pour three handfuls of water over yourself"," and then you have become pure.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 330]"""
"856","(857) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Umm Salamah, who said: \A woman from the Anṣār came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was with him"," and she said: 'I am a woman who binds the braids of my head tightly. What should I do when I perform ghusl from janābah?' He said: 'Pour three handfuls of water over your head"," then squeeze after each handful.'\""\n\nUsāmah ibn Zayd shortened the chain of narration in the narration of Ibn Wahb from him"," that Saʿīd heard it from Umm Salamah"," and that is in what… [Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains. Narrated by al-Dārimī"," 1157]"""
"857","(858) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us. And Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Usāmah ibn Zayd al-Laythī informed you that Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī informed him that he heard Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, say: \A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I am a woman who binds the braids of my head tightly. What should I do when I perform ghusl?' He said: 'Pour three handfuls of water over your head"," then squeeze it after each handful — that will suffice you.'\""\n\nThe narration of Ayyūb ibn Mūsā is more authentic than the narration of Usāmah ibn Zayd"," and he preserved in his isnād what Usāmah ibn Zayd did not preserve. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains]"""
"858","(859) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah informed us.\n\n(Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us and said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī informed us, and the wording is his: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from Ayyūb, from Abī al-Zubayr, from ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr, who said: \It reached ʿĀʾishah that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr used to command women"," when they performed ghusl"," to undo their heads. She said: 'How astonishing is Ibn ʿAmr! Why does not he command them to shave their heads? Indeed"," I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl from a single vessel"," and I would not do more than pour three pourings over my head.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 331]"""
"859","(860) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us; Naṣr ibn ʿAlī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dāwūd narrated from ʿUmar ibn Suwayd, from ʿĀʾishah bint Ṭalḥah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \We used to perform ghusl while we were wearing head-coverings (al-ḍimād)"," and we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," both in the state of iḥlāl and iḥrām.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 254]"""
"860","(861) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Hārūn ibn Sulaymān informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Bakkār ibn Yaḥyā, from his grandmother, who said: \I entered upon Umm Salamah","\"" then she mentioned the hadith. Umm Salamah said: \""As for the woman who used to comb her hair (al-mumtashiṭah)"," one of us would be combed"," and when she performed ghusl she would not undo that. Rather"," she would pour three handfuls over her head"," and when she saw moisture at the roots of the hair"," she would rub it"," then pour water over the rest of her body.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 359]"""
"861","(862) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz reported to us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Bayhaqi reported to us; my grandfather narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, who said: \I entered into ihram with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for 'Umrah during the Farewell Pilgrimage.\"" She then mentioned the hadith concerning her menses"," and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," this is the Day of 'Arafah and I have not yet become pure"," and I had performed Tamattu' with the 'Umrah.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to her: \""Undo your head"," comb your hair"," enter into ihram for Hajj"," and leave aside your 'Umrah.\"" She said: \""So I did that.\""\n\nAnd the hadith is recorded in the two Sahihs. As for her ghusl for the ihram of Hajj"," it was a Sunnah ghusl"," and she was commanded therein to undo her head and comb her hair"," as though she was commanded to do so as a recommended act"," just as Asma' bint 'Umays was commanded to perform ghusl for ihram during her postpartum bleeding as a recommended act. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 310.]"""
"862","(863) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz reported to us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq reported to us; Muhammad ibn Yunus narrated to us; Muslim ibn Subayh narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a woman performs ghusl from her menses"," she should undo her hair and wash it with al-khitmi (marshmallow plant) and al-ushnan (soda/lye). And when she performs ghusl from janabah"," she should not undo her head nor wash it with al-khitmi and al-ushnan.\"" [Da'if.]"""
"863","(864) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari reported to us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Ziyad narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from Qays ibn Wahb, from a man from Sawā', from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), that he used to wash his head with al-khitmi (marshmallow plant) while in a state of janabah, and that sufficed him, and he would not pour water over it.\n\nAnd if this is established, it is understood to mean that the water was predominant over the al-khitmi, and that his washing of the head was with the intention of purification from janabah. And likewise what follows. [Da'if. Narrated by Abu Dawud, 256.]"
"864","(865) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas reported to us; al-Rabi' said: al-Shafi'i said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith ibn al-Azma', who said: I heard Ibn Mas'ud say: \When the person in a state of janabah washes his head with al-khitmi (marshmallow plant)"," it does not count as a ghusl for him.\""\n\nAnd its meaning was narrated by al-Thawri and Shu'bah from Abu Ishaq. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Tabari in al-Kabir"," 9257.]"""
"865","(866) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad reported to us; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us; 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Shayban, from al-A'mash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Sariyyah ibn 'Abdullah, who said:\n\n'Abdullah said: \Whoever washes his head with al-khitmi (marshmallow plant) while in a state of janabah"," it suffices him"," and let him wash the rest of his body.\""\n\nBut Abu 'Awanah contradicted him"," narrating it from al-A'mash"," from Salim"," from Thabit ibn Qutbah al-Thaqafi"," from Ibn Mas'ud. The correct narration is that of Shayban. Likewise"," Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from al-A'mash. Ya'qub said: 'Ali ibn al-Madini said: \""The hadith is the hadith of Sufyan.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i that he said: \""They used to wash their heads with al-sidr (lote tree leaves) from janabah"," then one of them would wait a while"," then perform ghusl from janabah.\"" [Da'if. Narrated by al-Bukhari in his Tarikh"," 4/207.]"""
"866","(867) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani reported to us; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi reported to us. And Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari in Naysabur, Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran, and Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yahya al-Sukkari in Baghdad reported to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us; Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Safiyyah, from his mother, from 'A'ishah, that a woman asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about her ghusl from menses. He instructed her how to perform ghusl and said: \Take a piece of musk-scented cloth and purify yourself with it.\"" She said: \""How shall I purify myself with it?\"" He said: \""Purify yourself with it.\"" She said: \""How shall I purify myself with it?\"" She said: \""Then he concealed himself from me thus\"" — and Abu 'Uthman"," meaning Sa'dan"," gestured with his four fingers. He said: \""And Sufyan gestured and said: 'Subhan Allah"," purify yourself with it.'\"" 'A'ishah said: \""So I pulled her towards me and said: 'Apply it to the traces of blood.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Bishran and al-Rudhbari"," and the others did not mention the narration of Abu 'Uthman.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Yahya ibn Ja'far"," and Muslim narrated it from 'Amr al-Naqid and Ibn Abi 'Umar"," from Sufyan. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 308.]"""
"867","(868) Abu Tahir al-Faqih reported to us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us; Ibn Tahman narrated to us; Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm 'Atiyyah al-Ansariyyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: \A woman should not mourn over a deceased person for more than three days"," except over her husband"," for she mourns for four months and ten days. She should not wear a dyed garment except a garment of 'asb (undyed cloth). She should not apply kohl"," nor apply henna"," nor touch perfume"," except when she becomes pure from her menses — then she may use a small piece of qust (costus) or azhfar (a type of fragrant plant).\""\n\nIt is recorded in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Hisham ibn Hassan. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 307.]"""
"868","(869) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Faqih al-Shirazi reported to us, saying: Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us; Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us; Ayyub narrated to us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm 'Atiyyah, who said: \We were forbidden to mourn over a deceased person for more than three days"," except over a husband — four months and ten days. We were not to apply kohl"," nor wear perfume"," nor wear a dyed garment except a garment of 'asb (undyed cloth). And permission was granted at the time of purification: when one of us performed ghusl from her menses"," she could use a small piece of qust (costus) or azhfar (a type of fragrant plant).\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from al-Hajjabi"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani"," both from Hammad ibn Zayd. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 307.]"""
"869","(870) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' reported to us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated to us; Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from 'Amr ibn Bujdan, who said: I heard Abu Dharr mention the hadith concerning his Bedouin state and his janabah, until he said, from the Prophet (ﷺ): \The pure earth is the wudu' of the Muslim"," even if for ten years. But when he finds water"," let him touch his skin with the water"," for that is better.\"" [Sahih in meaning.]"""
"870","(871) Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Saydalani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan, from al-Qasim, from 'A'ishah, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed ghusl from janabah"," he would call for something resembling a large vessel (al-hilab)"," take it in his hand"," and begin with the right side of his head"," then the left side. Then he would take water in both his palms and pour it over his head.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it in the Sahih from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna.\n\nAnd al-hilab refers to the vessel — it is that in which milk is collected"," and it is called hilab. Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us of that from Shaykh Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili. And what confirms that is what follows. [Sahih.]"""
"871","(872) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us in *Ziyādāt al-Fawā'id*: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Abū ʿĀṣim al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Makhlad narrated to us from Ḥanẓalah from al-Qāsim from ʿĀ'ishah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl (ritual bath) with a vessel of this size.\n\nAbū ʿĀṣim showed us the size of the vessel with his hand, and it was equivalent to a mug holding eight arṭāl (a unit of measure). He would then pour water over the right side of his head, then over the left side of his head, and then he would take both hands and pour water over the middle of his head.\n\n[Sound. Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān (1197)]"
"872","(873) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Ḥayyān, known as Abū al-Shaykh, narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Khalf al-Dūrī narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Mūsā al-Anṣārī narrated to us: ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Zayd ibn Qunfudh al-Sahmī narrated to us from Jābir ibn Sīlān from Ibn Masʿūd that a man asked the Prophet ﷺ about a person who performs ghusl from janābah (major ritual impurity) and water misses a part of his body. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \He should wash that place and then pray.\""\n\nʿĀṣim ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," Abū ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Ashjaʿī — al-Bukhārī said regarding him: \""There is discussion about him.\""\n\n[Weak. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr (56/1)]"""
"873","(874) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghayāth narrated to us from al-Aʿmash from Sālim from Kurayb from Ibn ʿAbbās from Maymūnah, who said: \I placed water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ghusl from janābah.\"" She then mentioned the hadith regarding the Prophet's ﷺ ghusl. She said: \""I handed him a cloth (mandīl)"," but he did not take it; rather"," he began shaking off the water with his hands.\"" Al-Aʿmash said: \""I mentioned this to Ibrāhīm"," and he said: 'They only disliked that out of fear of it becoming a habit (ʿādah).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ from his father"," without the statement of al-Aʿmash. [Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (270)]"""
"874","(875) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Abū ʿAwanah narrated to us from al-Aʿmash from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from Kurayb from Ibn ʿAbbās from Maymūnah that the Prophet ﷺ performed ghusl at her place, and she brought him a cloth (mandīl), but he threw it aside. Al-Aʿmash said: \I mentioned it to Ibrāhīm"," and he said: 'The hadith is as such"," and there is no harm in wiping with a cloth; it is merely a matter of habit (ʿādah).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl from Abī ʿAwanah with the same meaning"," without the statement of al-Aʿmash to Ibrāhīm. [Sound. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī (1628)]"""
"875","(876) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us from Manṣūr from Hilāl, meaning Ibn Yisāf, from ʿAṭā' from Jābir, who said: \Do not use a cloth (mandīl) after performing wuḍū' (ablution).\""\n\nIt has been narrated from ʿUthmān and Anas that they saw no harm in it. And from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī that he used to do it. [Sound. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq (708)]"""
"876","(877) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us: Abū Muʿādh narrated to us from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUrwah from ʿĀ'ishah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a piece of cloth with which he would dry himself after wuḍū'.\n\nThis Abū Muʿādh is Sulaymān ibn Arqam, and he is matrūk (abandoned in hadith).\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated to us from Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ.\n\n(ḥ) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated to us from Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ.\n\nThis has been narrated with a chain that is not strong. [Very weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (53)]"
"877","(878) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ṣūfī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Shīrāzī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Naḥwī narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAynā' Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim narrated to us: Abū Zayd al-Naḥwī narrated to us: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAlā' narrated to us from Anas ibn Mālik from Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq that the Prophet ﷺ had a piece of cloth with which he would dry himself after wuḍū'.\n\nThe Shaykh said: \It is only narrated by Abū ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAlā' from Iyās ibn Jaʿfar"," that a man narrated to him that the Prophet ﷺ had a piece of cloth or a handkerchief"," and when he performed wuḍū'"," he would wipe his face and hands with it.\"" [Very weak]"""
"878","(879) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh narrated it to us: Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarā'inī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Ṣūfī narrated to us: al-Qawārīrī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us from Abī ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAlā' from Iyās ibn Jaʿfar, and he mentioned it.\n\nThis is the preserved (maḥfūẓ) version from the hadith of ʿAbd al-Wārith. [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Saʿd in al-Ṭabaqāt]"
"879","(880) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl narrated to us in Baghdad: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū Maʿmar ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: \I asked ʿAbd al-Wārith about the hadith of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb from Anas that the Prophet ﷺ had a handkerchief or a piece of cloth"," and when he performed wuḍū'"," he wiped his face with it.\"" He said: \""It was in a cotton garment"," and Ibn ʿUlayyah took it"," and I do not narrate it.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""Had ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated it from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz from Anas"," it would have been a sound chain; however"," he refrained from narrating it. It is possible that he only had it with the first chain"," and Allah knows best.\""\n\nIt has been narrated from Muʿādh ibn Jabal: \""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — when he performed wuḍū'"," he wiped his face with the edge of his garment.\""\n\nIt is weak"," and we have mentioned it in the chapter on the purity of used water. [Weak]"""
"880","(881) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us from al-Awzāʿī from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Asʿad ibn Zurārah from Qays ibn Saʿd that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited them, and they placed water for him, so he performed ghusl. Then they brought him a dyed blanket (milḥafah) colored with saffron or wars (a yellow dye), and he wrapped himself in it.\n\nThus Abū Dāwūd narrated it in *Kitāb al-Sunan* from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and others from al-Walīd ibn Muslim.\n\nAnd Ibn Abī Laylā narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Asʿad ibn Zurārah from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Sharḥbīl from Qays ibn Saʿd, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us"," and we placed water for him"," so he performed ghusl. Then we brought him a blanket dyed with wars"," and he wrapped himself in it"," and it is as though I can still see the trace of the wars on his armpits.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (5185)]"""
"881","(882) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Surayy ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated from Malik, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'Aishah, who said: \I used to comb the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was menstruating.\"" al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Ibn Yusuf from Malik"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Hisham.\n\nAl-Shafi'i also cited as evidence the established command of the Prophet ﷺ that a menstruating woman should wash the blood of menstruation from her garment"," and he did not command washing the entire garment. There is no doubt about the abundance of sweat in it"," and this hadith has been mentioned in several places.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 291]"""
"882","(883) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from al-A'mash, from Thabit ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from 'Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \Hand me the cloth (khumrah).\"" She said: \""I am menstruating.\"" He said: \""Your menstruation is not in your hand.\"" So she handed it to him.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 298]"""
"883","(884) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Walid informed me; Ibrahim ibn 'Ali narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from al-A'mash, and he mentioned it with its chain, similar to it, except that he added: \Hand me the cloth from the mosque.\"" And he did not say: \""So she handed it to him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih]"""
"884","(885) Abu Tahir al-Faqih and Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us. Abu 'Abdullah said: \He informed us","\"" and Abu Tahir said: \""He narrated to us.\"" Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu al-Muthanna narrated to us; al-Qa'nabi narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Birti narrated to us; al-Qa'nabi informed us; Aflah ibn Humayd narrated from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad"," from 'Aishah"," who said: \""I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel"," our hands dipping into it in turn"," from the state of major ritual impurity (janabah).\""\n\nal-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it together from al-Qa'nabi.\n\nIbn Wahb narrated from Aflah and added in the hadith: \""and they would meet.\"" And Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi said from Aflah"," meaning \""and they would meet.\""\n\nIn my view"," the meaning of his words \""our hands dipping into it in turn\"" is that both of them would insert their hands into it to take water. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 258]"""
"885","(886) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Hashimi narrated in Halab; Adam ibn Iyas narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mu'adah al-'Adawiyyah, from 'Aishah, Mother of the Believers, that she was asked about a man who puts his hand into a vessel while he is in a state of major ritual impurity (junub) before performing ghusl. She said: \Water is not rendered impure by anything. However"," let him begin by washing his hand. I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad"," 6/172]"""
"886","(887) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Hakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us. He said: I heard Malik saying: Nafi' narrated to me that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar used to sweat in his garment while he was in a state of major ritual impurity (junub), and then he would pray in it. [Sahih. Narrated by Malik, 118]"
"887","(888) Through this chain, Ibn Wahb informed us from Maslamah ibn 'Ali and al-Fudayl ibn 'Iyad, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from 'Ikrimah, the freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, that 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas said: \There is no harm in the sweat of a person in a state of major ritual impurity (junub) or a menstruating woman in the garment.\""\n\nIbn Wahb said: Malik ibn Anas said to me the same. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Darimi"," 1031]"""
"888","(889) Abu Zakariyya and Abu Bakr informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas informed us; Muhammad informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us. He said: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: 'Isa ibn Yunus informed you from Hurayth ibn Abi Matar, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from 'Aishah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would perform ghusl from janabah"," then come to me while I was in a state of major ritual impurity"," and he would seek warmth with me.\""\n\nHurayth ibn Abi Matar is alone in narrating it"," and there is some discussion regarding his being alone in it.\n\nIt has also been narrated through another weak chain from 'Alqamah"," from 'Aishah"," in an abridged form. [Da'if]"""
"889","(890) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz said among a group: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Ka'bi narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Sufyan narrated from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl from a vessel called al-qadah, which is al-faraq, and I and he used to bathe from a single vessel.\n\nThe wording is that of al-Shafi'i's hadith. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, and al-Bukhari narrated it through another chain from al-Zuhri. [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim, 319]"
"890","(891) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us. Abu Tahir said: \He narrated to us","\"" and Abu 'Abdullah said: \""He informed us.\"" Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Abu al-Muthanna"," Muhammad ibn Ghalib"," and 'Umar ibn 'Umar said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs"," from 'Urwah"," from 'Aishah"," who said: \""I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel from the state of major ritual impurity (janabah).\"" [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 260]"""
"891","(892) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us that Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq — informed us that Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, a similar narration.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd through both chains of narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 260]"
"892","(893) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us. Abū Ṭāhir said: narrated to us, and Abū ʿAbdullāh said: informed us — Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Abū Khaythamah narrated from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal from Muʿādhah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform ghusl from a single vessel between us"," and he would hasten (to take the water) before me"," so I would say: 'Leave some for me"," leave some for me.' She said: And we were both in a state of janābah.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Narrated by Muslim"," 321]"""
"893","(894) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us that Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from ʿĀṣim from Muʿādhah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform ghusl from a single vessel. He would hasten and I would hasten"," until I would say: 'Leave some for me"," leave some for me.' Thus she said.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 239]"""
"894","(895) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us that Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us that Abān narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \I and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform ghusl from a single vessel"," and he would begin before me.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"895","(896) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Ibn Jurayj informed me that Ibn ʿUrwah narrated from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and she used to perform ghusl from a single vessel, taking handfuls from it, while both were in a state of janābah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭaḥāwī in Sharḥ al-Kabīr, 1/26]"
"896","(897) Through his chain of narration, Ibn Jurayj said: ʿAṭāʾ informed me from ʿĀʾishah that she informed him about the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and herself, that they both began together while in a state of janābah from a single vessel. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad, 6/168]"
"897","(898) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Ḥāmid — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl al-Bazzār — narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Aḥmasī narrated to us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Jābir ibn Zayd, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that Maymūnah informed him: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and I performed ghusl from a single vessel.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and others from Ibn ʿUyaynah"," and it was narrated by al-Bukhārī from Abū Nuʿaym from Ibn ʿUyaynah without mentioning Maymūnah.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: \""Ibn ʿUyaynah used to say in his later years: from Ibn ʿAbbās from Maymūnah.\""\n\nAnd the correct narration is what Abū Nuʿaym narrated. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 250]"""
"898","(899) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to him that Abū ʿAbdullāh — Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Jawharī — in Baghdād narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf ibn al-Ṭabbāʿ narrated to us that Abū Nuʿaym narrated it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"899","(900) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh — informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me that my father narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq and Muḥammad ibn Bakr both narrated to us that Ibn Jurayj informed me that ʿAmr ibn Dīnār informed me. He said: \To my knowledge and what comes to my mind"," Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ informed me that Ibn ʿAbbās informed him: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform ghusl with the leftover water of Maymūnah.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others from Muḥammad ibn Bakr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 323]"""
"900","(901) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah informed us that ʿUbaydullāh, who is Ibn Mūsā, narrated from Sufyān from Simāk from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to one of his wives"," and there was some water left over from her ghusl. He intended to perform wuḍūʾ with it"," so she said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I performed ghusl from it for janābah.' He said: 'Water does not become impure.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr"," 1037]"""
"901","(902) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us; Simāk narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: One of the wives of the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed ghusl (ritual bath) in a vessel. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) came to perform wuḍūʾ (ablution) from it or to perform ghusl. She said to him: \O Messenger of Allah"," I was in a state of janābah (major ritual impurity).\"" He said: \""Water does not become impure.\""\n[Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 68]"""
"902","(903) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to me; my father narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, who said: Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me that Zaynab bint Umm Salamah narrated to him that Umm Salamah narrated to her: She and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to perform ghusl from janābah from a single vessel.\n[Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from Muʿādh. Sound. Narrated by Muslim, 324]"
"903","(904) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jabr from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) and one of his wives used to perform ghusl from a single vessel.\n[Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd. Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 261]"
"904","(905) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Yazīd ibn Kaysān, who said: Abū Ḥāzim narrated to me, who said:\nAbū Hurayrah said: While the Prophet (peace be upon him) was in the mosque, he said: \O ʿĀʾishah"," hand me the cloth (khumrah).\"" She said: \""I am menstruating (ḥāʾiḍ).\"" He said: \""That is not in your hand.\"" So she handed it to him.\n[Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kāmil and others from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd. Sound. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī"," 1430]"""
"905","(906) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Yazīd narrated to us; Abū Badr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Ghanīyah narrated from Thābit ibn ʿUbayd from al-Qāsim from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) commanded me to hand him the cloth (khumrah) from the mosque. I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I am menstruating.\"" He said: \""Hand it to me"," for menstruation is not in your hand.\""\n[Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Malik. Sound. Narrated by Muslim"," 298]"""
"906","(907) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Qabīṣah narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr from Ibrāhīm from al-Aswad from ʿĀʾishah, who said: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to perform ghusl from a single vessel, both of us being in a state of janābah. He would bring his head out of the mosque while he was in iʿtikāf (spiritual retreat) and I was menstruating, and I would wash his head. He would command me, so I would wrap a waist-cloth (izār), and he would lie with me (yubāshirunī) while I was menstruating.\n[Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah. Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 295]"
"907","(908) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; and Abū al-Khayr Jāmiʿ ibn Aḥmad al-Wakīl informed us; Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; both said: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from Ḥumayd from Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Abī Rāʿif from Abī Hurayrah: The Prophet (peace be upon him) met him on one of the roads of Madīnah while he was in a state of janābah. He slipped away and went to perform ghusl. The Prophet (peace be upon him) missed him, and when he came, he said: \Where were you"," O Abā Hurayrah?\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," you met me while I was in a state of janābah"," and I disliked to sit with you until I performed ghusl.\"" He said: \""Subḥān Allāh! Indeed"," the believer does not become impure.\""\n[Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from another chain from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl. Sound. Narrated by Muslim"," 371]"""
"908","(909) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī narrated to us; Abū Kurayb narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated from Miṣwar from Wāṣil from Abī Wāʾil from Ḥudhayfah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) met him while he was in a state of janābah. He turned away from him, performed ghusl, then came and said: \I was in a state of janābah.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," the believer does not become impure.\""\n[Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb and others. Sound. Narrated by Muslim"," 371]"""
"909","(910) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us.\nAnd Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, Mālik ibn Anas, Yūnus ibn Yazīd, and others informed you from Nāfiʿ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar: Indeed, men and women during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to perform wuḍūʾ together from a single vessel.\n[Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik ibn Anas. Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 190]"
"910","(911) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yaḥyā narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh, who said: Nāfiʿ narrated to me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: We and the women used to perform wuḍūʾ from a single vessel during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), dipping our hands into it.\n[Sound. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 80]"
"911","(912) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us. And Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Usāmah ibn Zayd al-Laythī informed you from Sālim ibn al-Nuʿmān from Umm Ṣubayyah al-Juhaniyyah, who said: My hand and the hand of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came into contact in a single vessel during wuḍūʾ.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: This Sālim is Ibn Sarj, and he is also called Ibn Kharbūdh Abū al-Nuʿmān. Some said: Ibn al-Nuʿmān.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: He is the freed slave of Umm Ṣubayyah, and her name is Khawlah bint Qays.\n\nMuḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us with it: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn Fārīs narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī, and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīgh in other than his collection. He narrated it as 78.]"
"912","(913) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Ziyād ibn al-Khalīl narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Abū ʿAwwānah narrated to us from Dāwūd ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Awdī from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Ḥimyarī, who said: I met a man who had accompanied the Prophet (ﷺ) for as long as Abū Hurayrah had accompanied him—four years. He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade that any of us comb his hair every day, or urinate in his place of bathing, or that a woman bathe with the leftover water of a man, or that a man bathe with the leftover water of a woman; rather, let them both scoop water together.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Dāwūd ibn ʿAbdullāh, and he mentioned something similar, except that he did not say: \rather"," let them both scoop water together.\""\n\nThe narrators of this hadith are trustworthy"," except that Ḥumayd did not name the Companion who narrated to him"," so it is in the meaning of a mursal hadith"," though it is a sound mursal"," were it not for its contradiction of the established"," connected hadiths that precede it.\n\nDāwūd ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Awdī was not used as a proof by the two Shaykhs"," al-Bukhārī and Muslim—may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy on them both. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 38.]"""
"913","(914) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, who said: I heard Abū Ḥājib narrating from a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade performing wuḍūʾ with the leftover water of a woman's wuḍūʾ. Yūnus said: Thus Abū Dāwūd narrated it to us. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 82.]"
"914","(915) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī narrated to us: Ibn Bashshār narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abū al-Ḥasan ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ibn Bashshār narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd, meaning al-Ṭayālisī, narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us from ʿĀṣim from Abī Ḥājib from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAmr, who is al-Aqraʿ, that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade a man from performing wuḍūʾ with the leftover water of a woman's wuḍūʾ.\n\nMaḥmūd ibn Ghaylān narrated it from Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī in the same manner, except that he said: \or he said"," with her leftover drink (suʾrihā).\""\n\nWahb ibn Jarīr narrated it from Shuʿbah likewise. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī 1252.]"""
"915","(916) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal from Abī Ḥājib from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAmr al-Ghifārī that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade the leftover drink (suʾr) of a woman. And ʿĀṣim did not know whether it referred to the leftover water of her wuḍūʾ or the leftover of her drinking.\n\nShuʿbah narrated it from Sulaymān al-Taymī likewise. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 4/213.]"
"916","(917) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: Abū Qilābah narrated to us: Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us from Sulaymān al-Taymī, who said: I heard Abū Ḥājib narrating from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade a man from performing wuḍūʾ with the leftover water of a woman's wuḍūʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"917","(918) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ibrāhīm al-Ḥarbī narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Zuraʿī narrated to us from Sulaymān from Abī Ḥājib from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) from Banī Ghifār that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) forbade a man from purifying himself with the leftover water of a woman's wuḍūʾ.\n\nHushaym narrated it from Sulaymān al-Taymī likewise.\n\nAbū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī said: Sawādah ibn ʿĀṣim Abū Ḥājib al-ʿAnazī is counted among the Baṣrans, and he is also called al-Ghifārī, and I do not consider his narration from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAmr to be authentic.\n\nIt has reached me from Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī that he said: I asked Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl, meaning al-Bukhārī, about this hadith, and he said: \It is not authentic","\"" meaning the hadith of Abū Ḥājib from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAmr.\n\nAbū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ said: Abū Ḥājib's name is Sawādah ibn ʿĀṣim. There is disagreement concerning him. ʿImrān ibn Ḥudayr and Ghazwān ibn Ḥujayr al-Sadūsī narrated from him a mawqūf narration from the statement of al-Ḥakam"," not raised to the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"918","(919) Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us: Ibrāhīm al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Ibn Fāris narrated to us: Muḥammad informed us: ʿAbdān informed us: ʿAbdullāh informed us: ʿImrān ibn Ḥudayr narrated to us from Sawādah al-ʿAnazī, who said: The people gathered around al-Ḥakam at al-Mirbad, and he forbade them from it. [Ḥasan.]"
"919","(920) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Sarrāj narrated to us: Muṭayyin narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Mukhtār narrated to us from ʿĀṣim from ʿAbdullāh ibn Sarjis, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade the leftover water of a woman's wuḍūʾ.\n\nMuʿallā ibn Asad narrated it from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Mukhtār likewise, but Shuʿbah contradicted him from ʿĀṣim. [Shādh.]"
"920","(921) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed it to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us from ʿĀṣim from ʿAbdullāh ibn Sarjis, who said: A woman may perform wuḍūʾ and bathe from the leftover water of a man's bathing and his purification, but a man may not perform wuḍūʾ with the leftover water of a woman's bathing or her purification.\n\nʿAlī said: This is mawqūf, and it is more correct.\n\nThe Shaykh said: It has reached me from Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī from Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī that he said: The authentic hadith of ʿAbdullāh ibn Sarjis in this topic is mawqūf, and whoever raised it made an error. [Ṣaḥīḥ Mawqūf.]"
"921","(922) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us in his latter narrations — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Malik informed us.\n\n(Chain variant) And Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Maslamah narrated to us — from Malik — from Ishaq ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah — from Anas ibn Malik, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the time of the 'Asr prayer arrived"," and the people sought water for ablution but could not find it. Then water was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he placed his hand in that vessel and commanded the people to perform ablution from it.\"" He said: \""I saw the water gushing out from beneath his fingers"," and the people performed ablution until the last of them had done so.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi and others"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Malik.\n\nIt was also narrated by 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud"," Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah"," and al-Bara' ibn 'Azib from the Prophet ﷺ."""
"922","(923) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Mahruyah ibn 'Ayyash al-Razi informed us — Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us — 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us — Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us — from his father — from 'A'ishah, who said: \I used to bathe"," I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," from a single vessel.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it through another chain from Hisham."""
"923","(924) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us — Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us — from al-Zuhri — from 'Urwah — from 'A'ishah, who said: \I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel"," and that drinking cup at that time was called al-Faraq.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Adam ibn Abi Iyas from Ibn Abi Dhi'b"," and he said: \""From a cup called al-Faraq.\"""""
"924","(925) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us — Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us — Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim informed us — al-Layth narrated to us — from Ibn Shihab — from 'Urwah — from 'A'ishah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe in the cup"," which was al-Faraq"," and I used to bathe"," I and he"," from a single vessel.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id and others from al-Layth.\n\nAnd Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated it from al-Zuhri in the same manner."""
"925","(926) Ma'mar narrated from al-Zuhri, and he said in the hadith that she said: \I used to bathe"," I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," from a single vessel containing the measure of al-Faraq.\""\n\nAbu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed it to us — Hajjib ibn Ahmad informed us — Muhammad ibn Hammad narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us — from Ma'mar and Ibn Jurayj — from al-Zuhri"," and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd Malik narrated it from al-Zuhri as an addition to it"," without the other chain."""
"926","(927) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi informed us through dictation — Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us — Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us — he said: I read to Malik — from Ibn Shihab — from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr — from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe from a vessel which was al-Faraq, for the major ablution (janabah).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya."
"927","(928) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us — Abu Muslim informed us — Abu 'Umar informed us — Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us — he said: I heard Ibn Shihab narrating from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad — from 'A'ishah, who said: \I used to bathe"," I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," from a single vessel"," and it was al-Faraq.\""\n\nHe said: Al-Zuhri said: \""I reckon it was five aqsat.\""\n\nHe said: Abu 'Amr said: \""A qasrt is four ratls.\""\n\nOthers also narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd in the same manner.\n\nAnd Abu Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us — Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sufyan informed us — Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj informed us — he said: Qutaybah said — Sufyan"," meaning Ibn 'Uyaynah"," said: \""Al-Faraq was three sa's.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of Harmalah from al-Shafi'i"," that he said it.\n\nAnd Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us — Abu Dawud informed us — he said: I heard Ahmad ibn Hanbal saying: \""Al-Faraq is sixteen ratls.\"" He said: And I heard him saying: \""The sa' of Ibn Abi Dhi'b is five ratls and a third.\"" It was said: \""Then what of the one who said eight ratls?\"" He said: \""That is not preserved (mahfuz).\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: \""And it has reached us that the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution with a mudd and bathed with a sa'.\"""""
"928","(929) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz — read to him — and Abu Tahir al-Faqih and 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf — through dictation — they said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq informed us — Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn al-Harith narrated to us — Abu Nu'aym narrated to us — Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us — from Ibn Jabr — he said: Abu 'Abd Allah, in his hadith, said: A sheikh from the Ansar, known as Ibn Jabr, narrated to me — he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: \The Prophet ﷺ used to bathe with a sa' up to five mudds"," and he used to perform ablution with a mudd.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Nu'aym"," and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Waki' from Mis'ar."""
"929","(930) And Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us — Ishaq al-Harbi narrated to us — 'Affan narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Jabr narrated to us — from Anas ibn Malik, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution with a makkuk and bathe with five maka'k.\"""""
"930","(931) And with its meaning, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh and others narrated it from Shu'bah, and Muslim narrated it from their hadith from him in his Sahih.\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: \In this there is evidence that there is no fixed measure for it except its completion (kamaluhu)"," and Allah knows best.\"" Along with this"," it has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said regarding the person in a state of janabah: \""When you find water"," then let it touch your skin"," without specifying any particular amount of it.\"" The Shaykh said: \""This hadith has already passed"," and it will be mentioned again"," if Allah the Most High wills.\"""""
"931","(932) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Ka'bi informed us; Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated from Abu Rayhanah, from Safinah, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would perform ghusl with a sa' and would perform wudu' with a mudd.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. [Sahih through other chains. Muslim reported it"," 326.]"""
"932","(933) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Hammad Abu al-Nazzar al-Bazzaz narrated to us; Hafs al-Fallas narrated to us; Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us; Abu Rayhanah narrated from Safinah, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, who said: \A mudd sufficed the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) for wudu'"," and a sa' sufficed him for ghusl.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from 'Amr ibn 'Ali Abi Hafs and others. [Sahih. Muslim reported it"," 325.]"""
"933","(934) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Muqri' in Baghdad informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir narrated to us; 'Affan narrated to us; Aban narrated to us; Qatadah narrated, saying: Safiyyah narrated to me that 'A'ishah said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would perform wudu' with a mudd and would perform ghusl with a sa'.\"" [Sahih. Abu Dawud reported it"," 92.]"""
"934","(935) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi both informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us; Ibn Fudayl narrated from Husayn and Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \A mudd suffices for wudu'"," and a sa' suffices for ghusl from janabah.\"" [Sahih through other chains. al-Nasa'i reported it"," 230.]"""
"935","(936) Abu 'Awanah and others narrated it from Yazid alone, through his chain, saying: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would perform wudu' with a mudd and would perform ghusl with a sa'.\""\n\nAbu Bakr ibn Furak informed us of it; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Abu 'Awanah narrated it and mentioned it. [Sahih through other chains. al-Tayalisi reported it"," 1732.]"""
"936","(937) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us; Salih ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to me; Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated.\n\nAbu Bakr said: And 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad informed us; Ishaq, meaning al-Hanzali, narrated to us; Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Abu Ishaq narrated to us; Abu Ja'far narrated that he was in the company of Jabir, and there were some people with him. They asked him about ghusl from janabah, and he said: \A sa' suffices you.\"" A man among them said: \""By Allah"," that does not suffice me"," nor such-and-such.\"" Jabir said: \""It used to suffice one who had more hair than you","\"" or he said: \""who was better than you.\""\n\nal-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad"," from Yahya ibn Adam. [Sahih. al-Bukhari reported it"," 249.]"""
"937","(938) Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us; Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hamdan al-Sayrafi in Marw narrated to us; al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah al-Baghdadi narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abu Salamah, from 'A'ishah, who said: Her brother from nursing asked her about the ghusl of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) from janabah. So she called for water amounting to a sa', performed ghusl, and poured water over her head three times.\n\nal-Bukhari narrated it from the hadith of 'Abd al-Samad from Shu'bah, then he said: And Yazid ibn Harun said from Shu'bah: \Amounting to a sa'.\""\n\nAnd Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Mu'adh from Shu'bah"," and he added in the hadith: \""And there was a screen between us and her.\"" [Sahih. al-Bukhari reported it"," 248.]"""
"938","(939) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali narrated to us; Abu al-Walid narrated to us; al-Layth narrated. He said: And Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to me, and the wording is his: 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Rafi' narrated to us; Shabbabah narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from 'Irak, from Hafsah bint 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, who was married to al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr, that 'A'ishah informed her: \She and the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to perform ghusl from a single vessel"," which held three mudds or close to that.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Rafi'. [Sahih. Muslim reported it"," 321.]"""
"939","(940) Abu Tahir al-Faqih narrated to us; Abu Tahir al-Muhammadabathi narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-'Adani narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us; Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki narrated from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr al-Makki, who said: It reached 'A'ishah that 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr was issuing a fatwa that a woman should undo her hair at the time of ghusl from janabah. She said: \He has indeed placed a burden upon women! I have seen myself performing ghusl with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) from this\"" — and there was a vessel placed before them"," like a sa' or less — \""and I would pour water over my head three times altogether.\"" [Sahih. al-Nasa'i reported it"," 416.]"""
"940","(941) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Ibn Bashshar narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'hab narrated from Habib al-Ansari, who said: I heard 'Abbad ibn Tamim narrate from my grandmother, who was Umm 'Umarah, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed wudu', and a vessel was brought to him containing water amounting to two-thirds of a mudd.\n\nThus did Muhammad ibn Ja'far Ghundar narrate it from Shu'bah, and others contradicted him in its chain. [Sahih. Abu Dawud reported it, 94.]"
"941","(942) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā al-Rāzī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Ḥabīb ibn Zayd from ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd: that the Prophet ﷺ was brought two-thirds of a mudd of water, and he performed wuḍūʾ and began rubbing his arms."
"942","(943) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar al-Muqriʾ in Baghdād informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd narrated to us that Abū Khālid al-Aḥmar narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Ḥabīb ibn Zayd al-Anṣārī from ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm from Ibn Zayd al-Anṣārī: that the Prophet ﷺ performed wuḍūʾ with approximately two-thirds of a mudd.\n\nAnd Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh similarly narrated it from Shuʿbah. Abū Zurʿah al-Rāzī said: The authentic one, in my view, is the ḥadīth of Ghundar."
"943","(944) And it is narrated from al-Ṣalt ibn Dīnār from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab from Abī Umāmah: that the Prophet ﷺ performed wuḍūʾ with half a mudd.\n\nAbū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated it to us; he said Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; he said ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Baghawī narrated to us; he said Surayj ibn Yūnus narrated to us; he said ʿAlī ibn Thābit al-Jazarī narrated to us from al-Ṣalt… and he mentioned it.\n\nAl-Ṣalt ibn Dīnār is abandoned (matrūk); one does not rejoice in his ḥadīth.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from him in this ḥadīth that he said on another occasion: \With a qist (measure) of water.\"""""
"944","(945) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us; he said Abū Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; he said Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; he said Surayj ibn Yūnus narrated to us… and he mentioned it with its chain, similar to the ḥadīth of al-Mālinī, and he added that he said on another occasion: \With a qist of water.\""\n\nAnd it has been said from him in this ḥadīth: \""With less than a mudd.\"""""
"945","(946) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated it to us; he said Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; he said Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Nāqid narrated to us; he said Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Abī Madhʿūr narrated to us; he said ʿAlī ibn Thābit al-Jazarī narrated to us from al-Ṣalt ibn Dīnār… and he mentioned it."
"946","(947) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Abī Khalaf al-Ṣūfī al-Mihrajānī informed us therein that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Yazdād ibn Masʿūd narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us that Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us that Saʿīd al-Jurayrī narrated from Abī Naʿāmah: that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mughaffal heard his son saying: \O Allah"," I ask You for the white palace on the right side of Paradise when I enter it.\"" He said: \""O my son"," ask Allah for Paradise and seek His protection from the Fire"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Indeed"," there will be in this ummah a people who will transgress in purification and supplication.'\"""""
"947","(948) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Khārijah ibn Muṣʿab narrated to us that Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd narrated from al-Ḥasan from ʿUttayy al-Saʿdī from Ubayy ibn Kaʿb from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \Indeed"," for wuḍūʾ there is a shayṭān called al-Walhān"," so beware of him.\"" Or he said: \""So guard against him.\""\n\nAnd others besides him narrated from Abū Dāwūd in this ḥadīth: \""So beware of him"," and guard against the waswās (whispering) of water.\"""""
"948","(949) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us; he said ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; he said Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Jamīl narrated to us; he said ʿAbdah ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār both said: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us… and he mentioned it in its like.\n\nAnd he said in its chain: from ʿUttayy ibn Ḍamrah. And this ḥadīth is muʿallal (defective) due to the narration of al-Thawrī from Bayān from al-Ḥasan, part of which is from his own words and not marfūʿ (elevated), and the remainder from Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd from his own words and not marfūʿ. And Allah knows best."
"949","(950) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us that Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Bayān from al-Ḥasan who said: \The shayṭān of wuḍūʾ is called al-Walhān; he makes people laugh during wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nAnd from Sufyān from Yūnus who said: \""It used to be said that water has waswās"," so guard against the waswās of water.\""\n\nAnd from Sufyān from Ḥuṣayn from Hilāl ibn Yasāf who said: \""It used to be said that there is excess in everything"," even in purification"," even if one is on the bank of a river.\""\n\nThus narrated it other than Khārijah ibn Muṣʿab from al-Ḥasan and Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd.\n\nKhārijah is alone in narrating it musnad (with a connected chain)"," and he is not strong in narration. And Allah knows best.\n\nAnd it has been narrated through another weak chain from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn as marfūʿ"," meaning what we narrated from Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd."""
"950","(951) Abū Saʿd ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī ʿUthmān al-Zāhid and Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Isfarāyinī both said: Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad ibn Bishr al-Tamīmī narrated to us; he said ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Nājiyah narrated to us; he said Muḥammad ibn Ḥuṣayn al-Aṣbaḥī narrated to us; he said Yaḥyā ibn Kathīr narrated to us from Sulaymān al-Taymī from Abī al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Shikhkhīr from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Guard against the waswās of water"," for indeed water has waswās and a shayṭān.\"""""
"951","(952) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas al-Qasim ibn al-Qasim al-Sayyari in Marw informed us; Abu al-Muwajjih informed us; 'Abdan informed us; 'Abdullah informed us; Sufyan informed us, from al-A'mash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Maymunah, who said: \I screened the Prophet ﷺ while he was performing ghusl from janabah. He began by washing his hands"," then he poured water with his right hand over his left"," washed his private parts and whatever had soiled him"," then wiped his hands against the wall or the ground"," then performed wudu as for prayer except for his feet"," then poured water over his body"," then moved aside and washed his feet.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from 'Abdan. Abu 'Awanah"," Zaidah"," and Ibn Fudayl followed him from al-A'mash regarding the screening. Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Zaidah. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari 277]"""
"952","(953) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr informed us; Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr informed us; Zaidah informed us, from al-A'mash, and he mentioned it with his isnad. She said: \I placed water for the Prophet ﷺ…\"" and she mentioned it. She said: \""And I screened him until he completed his ghusl.\"" Muslim narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim"," from Musa al-Qari"," from Zaidah. [Sahih]"""
"953","(954) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus informed us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi informed us; al-Qa'nabi informed us, from what he read to Malik. And Abu 'Abdullah informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Isma'il ibn Qutaybah informed us; Yahya ibn Yahya informed us. He said: I read to Malik, from Abu al-Nadr, that Abu Murrah, the freed slave of Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, informed him that he heard Umm Hani bint Abi Talib say: \I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the Conquest and found him performing ghusl"," and his daughter Fatimah screening him with a garment.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from al-Qa'nabi"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari 276]"""
"954","(955) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Harithi narrated to us; Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-Walid, meaning Ibn Kathir, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, that Abu Murrah, the freed slave of 'Aqil ibn Abi Talib, narrated to him that Umm Hani bint Abi Talib narrated to him: \Ali ibn Abi Talib came to her while they were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the campaign of the Conquest of Makkah.\"" Then he mentioned the hadith. She said: \""Then water was poured for him for ghusl"," and his daughter Fatimah screened him with a garment. When he had completed his ghusl"," he took it and wrapped himself with it"," then he stood and performed eight prostrations (rak'ahs)"," and that was in the forenoon (duha).\"" Muslim narrated it in the Sahih from Abu Kurayb"," from Abu Usamah. [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim 336]"""
"955","(956) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Ibn Nufayl narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman al-'Arzami, from 'Ata', from Ya'la, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man performing ghusl in the open. He ascended the minbar, praised Allah and glorified Him, then said: \Verily Allah—exalted be His praise—is modest and concealing; He loves modesty and concealment. When one of you performs ghusl"," let him conceal himself.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Abu Dawud 4012]"""
"956","(957) And Abu 'Ali informed us; Abu Bakr informed us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khalaf narrated to us; al-Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from 'Ata', from Safwan ibn Ya'la, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, with this hadith. Abu Dawud said: The first narration is more complete. [Shadhdh. Narrated by Abu Dawud 4013]"
"957","(958) Abu Tahir al-Faqih and Abu Ya'la Hamzah ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Muhallabi both said: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar informed us, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abu Hurayrah narrated to us. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \While Ayub was performing ghusl naked"," a swarm of locusts of gold fell upon him. Ayub began gathering them into his garment. His Lord called out to him: 'O Ayub"," have I not enriched you from what you see?' He said: 'Yes"," O my Lord"," but I cannot do without Your blessing.'\"" [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari 275]"""
"958","(959) And with their isnad, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The Children of Israel used to perform ghusl naked"," looking at one another's private parts"," while Musa"," peace be upon him"," used to perform ghusl alone. They said: 'By Allah"," nothing prevents Musa from performing ghusl with us except that he has a scrotal hernia.' He said: So one day he went to perform ghusl and placed his garment on a rock. The rock fled with his garment. Musa ran after it"," saying: 'My garment"," O rock! My garment"," O rock!' until the Children of Israel saw the private parts of Musa and said: 'By Allah"," there is nothing wrong with Musa.' He said: Then the rock stopped after they had looked at it. He took his garment and began striking the rock.\"" Abu Hurayrah said: \""By Allah"," there are marks on the rock—six or seven strikes from Musa's hitting the rock.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated both in the Sahih from Ishaq ibn Nasr"," from 'Abd al-Razzaq. Muslim narrated the second hadith from Muhammad ibn Rafi'"," from 'Abd al-Razzaq. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari 274]"""
"959","(960) 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us; Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Basri in Makkah informed us; Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbaḥ al-Za'farani informed us; Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh and Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah informed us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, that he said: \O Prophet of Allah"," what of our 'awrah should we conceal and what should we expose?\"" He said: \""Guard your 'awrah except from your wife or what your right hand possesses.\"" I said: \""What if the people are of one kind (i.e."," all men)?\"" He said: \""If you can ensure that no one sees it"," then let no one see it.\"" He said: I said: \""What if one of us is alone?\"" He said: \""Allah has more right that one should be modest before Him than before people.\"" Al-Bukhari mentioned it in the translation in an abbreviated form"," and he said: Bahz narrated from his father"," from his grandfather"," from the Prophet ﷺ: \""Allah has more right that one should be modest before Him than before people.\"" [Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawud 4017]"""
"960","(961) Abu Dawud narrated in al-Marasil from Qutaybah, from al-Layth, from 'Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do not perform ghusl in the open desert unless you cannot find a place of concealment. If you cannot find a place of concealment"," let one of you draw a line like a circle"," then invoke the name of Allah the Most High and perform ghusl within it.\"" Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad informed us; Abu al-Husayn al-Fasawi informed us; Abu 'Ali al-Lu'lu'i informed us; Abu Dawud narrated to us… and he mentioned it. [Da'if. Narrated by the author in Shu'ab al-Iman 7785]"""
"961","(962) And with this chain of narration from al-Zuhrī: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Let none of you bathe except near a person who does not look at him and who is close enough to speak to him.\""\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"962","(963) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr — narrated to us; Ḥammād — narrated to us, from Burd. And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah — narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal — narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm — narrated to us; Burd ibn Sinān — narrated to us, from ʿUbadah ibn Nusayy, from Ghuḍayf ibn al-Ḥārith, who said: I said to ʿĀʾishah: \Tell me"," did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ghusl from janābah at the beginning of the night or at the end of it?\"" She said: \""Sometimes he would perform ghusl at the beginning of the night"," and sometimes he would perform ghusl at the end of it.\"" I said: \""Allah is the Greatest! All praise is due to Allah"," Who has placed ease in the matter.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (226)]"""
"963","(964) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq — informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah — narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā — narrated to us. He said: I read before Mālik, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he would be afflicted with janābah during the night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Perform wuḍūʾ"," wash your private part"," and then sleep.\""\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\nAnd al-Thawrī and Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār in this ḥadīth: \""Wash your private part and perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (286)]"""
"964","(965) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us; and Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ — informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd — narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that a man said: \O Messenger of Allah"," may one of us sleep while in a state of janābah?\"" He said: \""Yes"," if he performs wuḍūʾ.\""\nIt is recorded in the two Ṣaḥīḥs"," with the naming of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb in the question.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (283)]"""
"965","(966) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī — informed us; and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam — informed us; Ibn Wahb — informed us. And Baḥr ibn Naṣr — narrated to us; he said: It was read before Ibn Wahb: Yūnus ibn Yazīd and al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed you, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to sleep while in a state of janābah"," he would perform wuḍūʾ — the wuḍūʾ of ṣalāh — before sleeping.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (284)]"""
"966","(967) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq — informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah — narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā — informed us; al-Layth ibn Saʿd — narrated to us, and he mentioned it… in similar wording.\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā, and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Abū Salamah.\nAnd in the narration of ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah, she said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to sleep while in a state of janābah"," he would wash his private part and perform the wuḍūʾ of ṣalāh"," and then he would sleep.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"967","(968) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Abū Usāmah al-Kalbī narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, saying: ʿAththām, meaning Ibn ʿAlī, narrated from Hishām, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in a state of janābah and wished to sleep"," he would perform wuḍūʾ or tayammum.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"968","(969) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qays, who said: \I asked ʿĀʾishah about the witr of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) — how did he perform witr"," at the beginning of the night or at the end of it?\"" She said: \""He would do all of that; sometimes he would perform witr early and sometimes he would delay it.\"" I said: \""All praise is due to Allah Who has made the matter flexible.\"" I said: \""How was his recitation during the night — would he recite quietly during the night or would he recite aloud?\"" She said: \""He would do all of that; sometimes he would recite quietly and sometimes he would recite aloud.\"" He said: I said: \""All praise is due to Allah Who has made the matter flexible.\"" I said: \""How would he deal with janābah — would he perform ghusl before sleeping"," or would he sleep before performing ghusl?\"" She said: \""He would do all of that; sometimes he would perform ghusl and then sleep"," and sometimes he would perform wuḍūʾ and then sleep.\"" He said: I said: \""All praise is due to Allah Who has made the matter flexible.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from al-Layth"," except that he abridged the hadith and mentioned only the account of the ghusl without what preceded it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"969","(970) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAttāb al-ʿAbdī narrated to us in Baghdad, saying: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Saʿīd ibn Kathīr ibn ʿUfayr and Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bukayr both narrated to us, saying: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qays, who said: \I asked ʿĀʾishah how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would deal with janābah — would he perform ghusl before sleeping"," or would he sleep before performing ghusl?\"" She said: \""He would do all of that; sometimes he would perform ghusl and then sleep"," and sometimes he would perform wuḍūʾ and then sleep.\"" I said: \""All praise is due to Allah Who has made the matter flexible.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it as 307]"""
"970","(971) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, when he wished to eat or to sleep while in a state of janābah, would wash his face and his hands up to the elbows, wipe over his head, and then eat or sleep. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it as 109]"
"971","(972) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Rafi' and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr both narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Razzāq narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; Nāfi' informed me from Ibn 'Umar: that 'Umar asked the Prophet ﷺ, \May one of us sleep while he is in a state of janābah?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Yes"," let him perform wuḍū' and then sleep"," and when he wishes"," he may perform ghusl.\"" He said: And when 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar intended to sleep while in a state of janābah"," he would pour water over his hands"," then wash his private parts with his left hand"," then wash the hand with which he had washed his private parts"," then rinse his mouth and sniff water into his nose"," sprinkle water into his eyes"," wash his face and his hands up to the elbows"," wipe over his head"," and then sleep. And when he intended to eat something while in a state of janābah"," he would do the same. Muslim narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rafi'"," without the action of Ibn 'Umar. The action of Ibn 'Umar"," who is the narrator of the report"," may resemble an explanation of the wuḍū' mentioned in the report"," except that 'Ā'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he performed the wuḍū' for ṣalāh. The wuḍū' for ṣalāh includes washing the feet along with the other limbs. And Allah knows best. What was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas: that the Prophet ﷺ rose at night"," relieved himself"," then washed his face and his hands"," and then slept — he did not mean by that intercourse; rather"," he meant thereby the hadath (minor impurity). The context of the hadith indicates that"," and its mention has passed"," and its completion will come"," if Allah the Most High wills. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzāq"," 1077]"""
"972","(973) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yūsuf narrated to us by dictation and recitation; Abu Sa'īd Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated to us in Makkah; Abu 'Alī al-Ḥasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Za'farānī narrated to us; Ya'qūb ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us from 'Alī ibn Mudrik from Abū Zur'ah from 'Abd Allah ibn Nujayy from his father, who said: I heard 'Alī say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image"," a person in a state of janābah"," or a dog.\"" [Ḍa'īf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 227]"""
"973","(974) Abu Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated to us from Abū Isḥāq from al-Aswad from 'Ā'ishah: that the Prophet ﷺ would sleep while in a state of janābah without touching water. [Ṣaḥīḥ, without his words \without touching water.\""]"""
"974","(975) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismā'īl ibn Qutaybah informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū Khaythamah informed us. And Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Zuhrī narrated to us. And Abu Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — and the wording is his — Ahmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān informed us; 'Amr ibn Khālid informed us; Zuḥayr narrated to us from Abū Isḥāq, who said: I asked al-Aswad ibn Yazīd — and he was a neighbor and a friend of mine — about what 'Ā'ishah narrated to him regarding the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: He would sleep at the beginning of the night and stay awake at its end. Then, if he had a need with his family, he would fulfill his need, then sleep before touching water. When the first call to prayer was given, she said: he would leap up. By Allah, she did not say: \He stood and took water.\"" And by Allah"," she did not say: \""He performed ghusl.\"" And I know best what she meant. And if he had no need"," he would perform wuḍū' as a man performs wuḍū' for ṣalāh"," then pray two rak'ahs. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Ahmad ibn Yūnus"," without his words: \""before touching water.\"" That is because the ḥuffāẓ criticized this expression"," imagining it to be taken from other than al-Aswad"," and that Abū Isḥāq sometimes practiced tadlīs"," so they considered it among his tadlīs. They cited as evidence for that the narration of Ibrāhīm al-Nakha'ī and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad from al-Aswad"," which differs from the narration of Abū Isḥāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"975","(975) As for the hadith of Ibrāhīm, Abu Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us of it; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Ḥakam from Ibrāhīm from al-Aswad from 'Ā'ishah, that she said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a state of janābah and intended to sleep or eat, he would perform wuḍū'. Muslim narrated it through various chains from Shu'bah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim, 5/3]"
"976","(977) As for the hadith of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr informed us, both saying: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us from Ibn Isḥāq from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad from his father, who said: I asked 'Ā'ishah: How was the wuḍū' of the Prophet ﷺ when he intended to sleep while in a state of janābah? She said: He would perform the wuḍū' for ṣalāh, then sleep. The Shaykh said: The hadith of Abū Isḥāq al-Sabī'ī is sound from the perspective of its chain of narration, because Abū Isḥāq explicitly stated his hearing from al-Aswad in the narration of Zuḥayr ibn Mu'āwiyah from him. When a mudallis explicitly states his hearing from the one he narrated from, and he is trustworthy, there is no ground for rejecting it. The manner of reconciling the two narrations is on a possible basis. Abū al-'Abbās ibn Surayj reconciled between them beautifully, and that is in what Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us of, saying: I asked Abū al-Walīd the jurist, saying: O master, the hadith of al-Thawrī from Abū Isḥāq from al-Aswad from 'Ā'ishah has reached us as sound: that the Prophet ﷺ would sleep while in a state of janābah without touching water. And likewise the hadith of Nāfi' and 'Abd Allah ibn Dīnār from Ibn 'Umar is sound: that 'Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, may one of us sleep while in a state of janābah? He said: \Yes"," if he performs wuḍū'.\"" Abū al-Walīd said to me: I asked Abū al-'Abbās ibn Surayj about the two hadiths"," and he said: The ruling applies to both of them together. As for the hadith of 'Ā'ishah"," she meant thereby that the Prophet ﷺ did not touch water for ghusl. And as for the hadith of 'Umar"," it is the explicatory one"," mentioning wuḍū'"," and upon it we act. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"977","(978) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abd Allah Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn 'Abd Allah informed us; Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us. And Abu 'Alī al-Ḥusayn ibn 'Alī al-Hafiz informed me — and the wording is his — al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Ibn 'Ulayyah, Wakī', and Ghundar narrated to us from Shu'bah from al-Ḥakam from Ibrāhīm from al-Aswad from 'Ā'ishah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a state of janābah and intended to eat or sleep, he would perform wuḍū'. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"978","(979) And Abu al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān al-Ahwāzī informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ibrāhīm al-Ḥarbī informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ informed us; Ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us from Yūnus from al-Zuhrī from Abū Salamah from 'Ā'ishah: that the Prophet ﷺ, when he intended to eat while in a state of janābah, would wash his hand. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 223]"
"979","(980) And Abu 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed it to us; Abu Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Bazzāz narrated to us… and he mentioned it with his chain and said: He would wash his hands. Abū Dāwūd said: And Ibn Wahb narrated it from Yūnus, making the matter of eating the statement of 'Ā'ishah exclusively. The Shaykh said: And likewise al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated it from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"980","(981) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed it to me; Abu 'Alī al-Hafiz informed me; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah informed us; Yazīd ibn Mawhab al-Ramlī informed us; al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed us from Ibn Shihāb from Abū Salamah from 'Ā'ishah: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he intended to sleep while in a state of janābah, would perform the wuḍū' for ṣalāh before sleeping. 'Ā'ishah said: And when he intended to eat or drink, he would wash his hands, then eat and drink if he wished. It has been said in this chain other than this, and the hadith of al-Aswad from 'Ā'ishah is more authentic. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad, 6/118]"
"981","(982) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak, the master, informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī, from Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmar, from ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir, who said: \I came to my family from a journey and they anointed me with saffron. When I went in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and greeted him"," he did not welcome me nor show me cheerfulness"," and he said: 'Go and wash this off yourself.' So I washed it off"," but some trace of it remained. I came to him and greeted him"," but he did not welcome me nor show me cheerfulness"," and he said: 'Go and wash this off yourself.' So I washed it again. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and greeted him"," and he returned my greeting and welcomed me. Then he said: 'Indeed"," the angels do not attend the funeral of a disbeliever with any good"," nor the one anointed with saffron"," nor the one in a state of janābah (major ritual impurity).'\"" And he granted concession to the one in a state of janābah"," when he intends to eat or sleep"," to perform wuḍūʾ (ablution). [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 4176]"""
"982","(983) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī informed us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us: Ḥammād narrated it with his chain of narration that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) granted concession to the one in a state of janābah, when he eats, drinks, or sleeps, to perform wuḍūʾ. He did not mention the story.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: \Between Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmar and ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir in this ḥadīth there is a man (i.e."," a missing narrator in the chain).\""\n\nHe also said: ʿAlī"," Ibn ʿUmar"," and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr said: \""The one in a state of janābah"," when he intends to eat"," should perform wuḍūʾ.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 4601]"""
"983","(984) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Farrāʾ informed us: Muḥāḍir informed us: ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī informed us — and the wording is his —: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim, from Abī al-Mutawakkil, from Abī Saʿīd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When one of you comes to his wife at night and then intends to return (to her again)"," let him perform wuḍūʾ between the two times.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 8/3]"""
"984","(985) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, from Abī al-Mutawakkil, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When one of you intends to return (to his wife)"," let him perform wuḍūʾ"," for it is more invigorating for the return.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb that he commanded performing wuḍūʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 1211]"""
"985","(986) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Shuʿayb al-Ḥarrānī informed us: My father informed us: Miskīn ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Shuʿbah, from Hishām ibn Zayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to visit his wives with a single ghusl (ritual bath).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Shuʿayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī, 263]"
"986","(987) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from the original of his book: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl informed us in the year twenty-five and three hundred: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ al-Zaʿfarānī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated to us, from Ḥumayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) visited his wives in a single night with one ghusl.\n\nAnd likewise Qatādah narrated it from Anas. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī, 263]"
"987","(988) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us: Abū Zakariyyā informed us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us: Ḥammād narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Rāfiʿ, from his aunt Salmā, from Abī Rāfiʿ, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) visited his wives one day, performing ghusl at each one's place. So I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," why do you not make it a single ghusl?\"" He said: \""This is purer"," more pleasant"," and cleaner.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: \""The ḥadīth of Anas is more authentic than this.\"" And in the narration of Abū Zakariyyā al-Saylaḥīnī: \""He visited all his wives in a single night"," performing a ghusl for each one of them"," and it was said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," why not a single ghusl?' He said: 'This is more pleasant and purer.'\"" [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 219]"""
"988","(989) Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us. He said: I read to Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, dictating: al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Mālik, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on some of his journeys until we reached al-Baydāʾ or Dhāt al-Jaysh. A necklace of mine broke (and was lost)"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stopped to search for it"," and the people stopped with him. They were not near any water"," and they had no water with them. The people came to Abū Bakr and said: 'Do you not see what ʿĀʾishah has done? She has detained the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and the people"," and they are not near any water"," and they have no water with them.' Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) came"," while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had placed his head on my thigh"," having fallen asleep. He said: 'You have detained the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and the people"," and they are not near any water"," and they have no water with them.' ʿĀʾishah said: \""Abū Bakr rebuked me and said whatever Allah willed him to say"," and he kept poking his hand into my side. Nothing prevented me from moving except the place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on my thigh. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) slept until morning without any water. Then Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed the verse of tayammum (dry ablution)"," and they performed tayammum. Usayd ibn al-Ḍuḥayr"," who was one of the chiefs"," said: 'This is not the first of your blessings"," O family of Abū Bakr.' ʿĀʾishah said: 'We sent the camel I was riding"," and we found the necklace beneath it.'\"" The wording is that of the narration of al-Qaʿnabī.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf and others"," from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 327]"""
"989","(990) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh, Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī, and Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us. Abū Bakr said: \informed us","\"" and the other two said: \""narrated to us\"": Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: al-Layth informed me: Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah narrated to me"," from al-Aʿraj"," from ʿUmayr"," the freed slave of Ibn ʿAbbās"," that he heard him say: \""I and ʿAbdullāh ibn Yasār"," the freed slave of Maymūnah"," the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," came to Abū al-Juhaym ibn al-Ḥārith ibn al-Ṣimmah. Abū al-Juhaym said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came towards the well of Jaml"," and a man met him and greeted him"," but he did not return the greeting until he came to the wall and wiped his face and his hands. Then he returned the greeting to him.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it"," saying: \""And al-Layth ibn Saʿd said.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 330]"""
"990","(991) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿUmar Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Abū Ṣāliḥ informed me: al-Layth narrated it with its chain of narration and its meaning, except that he said: \He wiped his face and his forearms"," then returned the greeting to him.\"" [Munkar. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/176]"""
"991","(992) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad informed us, from Abū al-Ḥuwayrith, from al-Aʿraj, from Ibn al-Ṣimmah, who said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was urinating, so I greeted him with salām, but he did not return my salām until he went to a wall and scraped it with a stick that he had with him. Then he placed his hands on the wall and wiped his face and his two forearms, after which he returned my salām.\n\nThis is a supporting testimony for the narration of Abū Ṣāliḥ, the scribe of al-Layth, except that this one is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). (j) ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Hurmuz al-Aʿraj did not hear it directly from Ibn al-Ṣimmah; rather, he heard it from ʿUmayr, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, from Ibn al-Ṣimmah. As for Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Yaḥyā al-Aslamī and Abū al-Ḥuwayrith ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muʿāwiyah, the ḥuffāẖ (hadith critics) have differed regarding their reliability (ʿādālah). However, their narration mentioning the two forearms therein has a supporting testimony from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar. [Very weak. Reported by al-Shāfiʿī, 31]"
"992","(993) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbbād informed us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm al-Azdī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Thābit al-ʿAbdī — and he was ṣadūq (truthful) — informed us. And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān al-Ahwāzī informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm al-Azdī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Thābit al-ʿAbdī informed us: Nāfiʿ said: I set out with Ibn ʿUmar on an errand to Ibn ʿAbbās. When he had fulfilled his need, among the things he related that day was: \While the Prophet (ﷺ) was in one of the lanes of Madīnah"," and the Prophet (ﷺ) had come from relieving himself of stool or urine"," a man greeted him with salām"," but he did not return his salām. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) struck with his two palms and wiped his face once. Then he struck with his two palms a second time and wiped his two forearms up to the two elbows"," and said: 'Nothing prevented me from returning your salām except that I was not in a state of wuḍūʾ — or he said: on a state of purity.'\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbdān. Some of the ḥuffāẓ have denied the marfūʿ (elevated) status of this ḥadīth as narrated by Muḥammad ibn Thābit al-ʿAbdī"," for a group have narrated it from Nāfiʿ as the action of Ibn ʿUmar. And what others have narrated from Nāfiʿ as the action of Ibn ʿUmar is tayammum only. As for this incident (qiṣṣah)"," it is well-known from the Prophet (ﷺ) through the narration of Abū al-Juhaym ibn al-Ḥārith ibn al-Ṣimmah and others.\n\nIt is also narrated from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān"," from Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," that a man passed by while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was urinating and greeted him"," but he did not return his salām — except that he shortened his narration. And Yazīd ibn al-Hād narrated it from Nāfiʿ more completely than that. [Munkar. Reported by Abū Dāwūd"," 330]"""
"993","(994) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Musāfir informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā, meaning al-Burlusī, informed us: Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ informed us, from Ibn al-Hād, that Nāfiʿ informed him, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came from relieving himself of stool, and a man met him at the well of Jamal and greeted him with salām, but the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not return his salām until he approached a wall. He placed his hand on the wall, then wiped his face and his two hands, after which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) returned the man's salām.\n\nThis narration is a testimony supporting the narration of Muḥammad ibn Thābit al-ʿAbdī, except that he preserved in it the mention of the two forearms, while others did not affirm it as he did. Both he and Ibn al-Hād narrated the ḥadīth mentioning his tayammum and then his returning the reply to the salām, even though al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān shortened it. The action of Ibn ʿUmar — performing tayammum on the face and the two forearms up to the elbows — is a testimony to the soundness of the narration of Muḥammad ibn Thābit, without negating it.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ushnānī informed us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us, saying: I heard ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī say: I asked Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn: \Muḥammad ibn Thābit al-ʿAbdī?\"" He said: \""There is nothing wrong with him.\"" Thus he said in the narration of al-Dārimī from him. And he is not deserving of criticism (nakīr) in this ḥadīth"," given the evidences I have mentioned. A group of the Imāms have narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Thābit"," such as Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr"," Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr"," and others"," and Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm praised him and narrated from him. And it is well-known from Ibn ʿUmar. [Ḥasan. Reported by Abū Dāwūd"," 331]"""
"994","(995) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzzakī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from Nāfiʿ, the freedman of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that he and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar came from al-Jurf, and when they were at al-Mirbad, ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar dismounted and performed tayammum with clean earth, wiping his face and his two hands up to the elbows, and then he prayed. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Mālik, 121]"
"995","(996) And with his chain of narration, he said: Mālik informed us, from Nāfiʿ, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to perform tayammum up to the elbows. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Mālik, 122]"
"996","(997) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl informed us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAmr informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar informed us: Nāfiʿ informed me, from Ibn ʿUmar.\n\nHe said: And al-Ḥusayn informed us: Ziyād ibn Ayyūb informed us: Hushaym informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and Yūnus informed us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to say: \Tayammum consists of two strikes: one strike for the face"," and one strike for the two palms up to the elbows.\""\n\nIt was narrated by ʿAlī ibn Ẓabyān from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"," and he raised it (as marfūʿ)"," but that is an error. The correct view is that with this wording it is from Ibn ʿUmar as a mawqūf (stopped) narration.\n\nIt was narrated by Sulaymān ibn Abī Dāwūd al-Ḥarrānī"," from Sālim and Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAnd it was narrated by Sulaymān ibn Arqam al-Taymī"," from al-Zuhrī"," from Sālim"," from his father"," from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nSulaymān ibn Abī Dāwūd and Sulaymān ibn Arqam are both ḍaʿīf (weak)"," and their narrations cannot be used as proof. The ṣaḥīḥ narration is that of Maʿmar and others"," from al-Zuhrī"," from Sālim"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," as his own action. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"997","(998) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl and Abū Bakr ibn Bālawayh informed us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥarbī informed us: Abū Nuʿaym informed us: ʿAzrah ibn Thābit informed us, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: A man came and said: \Janābah has afflicted me"," and I rolled about in the dust.\"" He said: \""Strike.\"" So he struck the earth with his two hands and wiped his face. Then he struck with his two hands and wiped his two hands up to the elbows.\n\nThus he said"," and its chain is ṣaḥīḥ"," except that he did not identify the one who commanded him to do so. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/182]"""
"998","(999) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh and Abū Bakr ibn Bālawayh informed us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad al-Anmāṭī informed us: Ḥarmiyyah ibn ʿUmarah informed us, from ʿAzrah ibn Thābit, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Tayammum is one strike for the face and one strike for the two hands up to the elbows.\"" [Shādh (irregular). Reported by al-Ḥākim"," 1/287]"""
"999","(1000) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Badr informed us, from his father, from his grandfather, from a man called al-Aslaʿ, who said: I used to serve the Prophet (ﷺ), and Jibrīl came to him with the verse of tayammum. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) showed me how the wiping for tayammum is done. So I struck the earth with my hand once and wiped my face with it. Then I struck the earth with them and wiped my hands up to the elbows.\n\nAl-Rabīʿ ibn Badr is ḍaʿīf (weak), except that he is not alone in narrating it. (t) And we have narrated this statement from the Tābiʿūn: from Sālib ibn ʿAbd Allāh, al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī, al-Shaʿbī, and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī. [Very weak. Reported by al-Dāraquṭnī, 1/179]"
"1000","(1001) The Ustādh Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh, from ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir, who said: A necklace of ʿĀʿishah, made from the beads of Ẓafār, was lost during one of the journeys of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and ʿĀʾishah was with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on that journey. So ʿĀʾishah searched for her necklace until the night was well advanced. Abū Bakr came and became angry with her and said: \You have detained the people at a place where there is no water.\"" He said: Then the verse of al-Ṣaʿīd (tayammum) was revealed. Abū Bakr came and said: \""By Allah"," O daughter"," I did not know how blessed you were.\"" ʿUbayd Allāh said: And ʿAmmār used to relate that the people began that day striking the earth with their palms and wiping their faces. Then they would return and strike another blow and wipe their hands up to the shoulders and the armpits"," and then they would pray.\n\nAnd similarly"," it was narrated by Maʿm ibn Rāshid"," Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī"," al-Layth ibn Saʿd"," the brother of al-Zuhrī"," and Jaʿfar ibn Burqān"," from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah"," from ʿAmmār. And Maʿm and Yūnus preserved in it the two strikes"," just as Ibn Abī Dhiʾb preserved them. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Abū Dāwūd"," 320]"""
"1001","(1002) It was narrated by Mālik ibn Anas, as Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, who said: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, who said: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abū Ṭāhir al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Salamah al-Kaʿbī in Hamadhān informed us, who said: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Barzah informed us, who said: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Ḥammād ibn Zayd al-Qāḍī narrated to us, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ narrated to us, who said: Juwayriyah narrated from Mālik, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah, that he informed him from his father, from ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir, who said: \We performed tayammum with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and we wiped our faces and our hands up to the shoulders.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbdān.\n\nAnd Abū Uways al-Madanī narrated it from al-Zuhrī. As for Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah"," he expressed doubt regarding the mention of his father in its isnād. He narrated it once from Ibn Dīnār from al-Zuhrī"," and once directly from al-Zuhrī himself.\n\nAnd Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUbaydullāh"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," from ʿAmmār. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1002","(1003) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him, who said: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, who said: my father narrated to us, who said: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, who said: my father narrated from Ṣāliḥ, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to me from Ibn ʿAbbās, from ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made a halt at Ulat al-Jaysh, and with him was his wife ʿĀʾishah. Her necklace, made from the beads of Ẓifār, was lost, and the people were detained on account of searching for her necklace, until the dawn broke and the people had no water with them. So Allah, the Most High, revealed to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) the dispensation of purification with clean soil (ṣaʿīd ṭayyib). The Muslims stood up with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and struck their hands upon the earth. Then they raised their hands without taking anything from the dust, and therewith they wiped their faces and their hands up to the shoulders, and from the inner sides of their hands up to the armpits.\n\nIbn Shihāb said: \The people do not give consideration to this.\"" And it reached us that Abū Bakr said to ʿĀʾishah: \""By Allah"," I did not know that you were so blessed.\""\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn Isḥāh ibn Yasār narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," and he mentioned Ibn ʿAbbās therein and mentioned two strikes"," as Ibn Abī Dhiʾb and Yūnus mentioned.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," who said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us"," who said: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said:\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy upon him) said: \""In this ḥadīth of ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir"," if their tayammum up to the shoulders was by the command of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," then it is abrogated (mansūkh)"," because ʿAmmār informed that this was the first tayammum that took place when the verse of tayammum was revealed. Every tayammum that the Prophet (ﷺ) performed after it that contradicted it is therefore abrogating (nāsikh) of it.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""And it has been narrated from ʿAmmār that the Prophet (ﷺ) commanded him to perform tayammum of his face and his palms.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (320)]"""
"1003","(1004) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him, who said: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, who said: my father narrated to us, who said: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, who said: my father narrated from Ṣāliḥ, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to me from Ibn ʿAbbās, from ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made a halt at Ulat al-Jaysh, and with him was his wife ʿĀʾishah. Her necklace, made from the beads of Ẓifār, was lost, and the people were detained on account of searching for her necklace, until the dawn broke and the people had no water with them. So Allah, the Most High, revealed to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) the dispensation of purification with clean soil. The Muslims stood up with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and struck their hands upon the earth. Then they raised their hands without taking anything from the dust, and therewith they wiped their faces and their hands up to the shoulders, and from the inner sides of their hands up to the armpits.\n\nIbn Shihāb said: \The people do not give consideration to this.\"" And it reached us that Abū Bakr said to ʿĀʾishah: \""By Allah"," I did not know that you were so blessed.\""\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," and he mentioned Ibn ʿAbbās therein and mentioned two strikes"," as Ibn Abī Dhiʾb and Yūnus narrated.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," who said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us"," who said: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said:\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy upon him) said: \""In this ḥadīth of ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir"," if their tayammum up to the shoulders was by the command of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," then it is abrogated"," because ʿAmmār informed that this was the first tayammum that took place when the verse of tayammum was revealed. Every tayammum that the Prophet (ﷺ) performed after it that contradicted it is therefore abrogating of it.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""And it has been narrated from ʿAmmār that the Prophet (ﷺ) commanded him to perform tayammum of his face and his palms.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (331)]"""
"1004","(1005) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him, who said: Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Asadī in Hamadhān informed us, who said: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, who said: Ādam narrated to us, who said: Shuʿbah narrated to us, who said: al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah narrated to me from Dharr, from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā, from his father, who said: \A man came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and said: 'I have had a seminal emission (ajnubtu) and I cannot find water.' So ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir said to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb: 'Do you not remember when we were on a journey and I had a seminal emission and so did you? As for you"," you did not pray"," and as for me"," I rolled in the dust and then I prayed. I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him"," and the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""It would have been sufficient for you to do thus.\"" Then the Prophet (ﷺ) struck his two palms upon the earth and blew into them"," and then wiped his face and his palms therewith.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās"," and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān and al-Naḍr ibn Shuʿmayl from Shuʿbah"," and he mentioned that al-Ḥakam heard the ḥadīth directly from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān himself. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1005","(1006) ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā narrated — al-Ḥakam said: then I heard it from Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā in Khurāsān — who said: \A man came to ʿUmar and said: 'I have had a seminal emission and I cannot find water.' So ʿAmmār said to him: 'Do you not remember when we were on a military expedition (sariyyah) during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and I had a seminal emission and so did you? As for you"," you did not pray"," and as for me"," I rolled in the dust and then I prayed. I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him"," and he said: \""It would have been sufficient for you to do thus.\"" Then he struck his hand upon the earth and blew into them"," and wiped his face and his palms"," and did not go beyond the elbows (kūʿayn).\""\n\nAnd Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated it from Dharr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Murhibī"," except that he expressed doubt in its text and was uncertain therein. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1006","(1007) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, who said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, who said: Baḥr ibn Naṣr ibn Sābiq al-Khawlānī informed us, who said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād informed us, who said: Shuʿbah informed us, who said: al-Ḥakam narrated to me from Dharr, from a son of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — al-Ḥakam said: then I heard it from Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā in Khurāsān — who said: \A man came to ʿUmar and said: 'I have had a seminal emission and I cannot find water.' So ʿAmmār said to him: 'Do you not remember when we were on a military expedition during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and I had a seminal emission and so did you? As for you"," you did not pray"," and as for me"," I rolled in the dust and then I prayed. I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him"," and he said: \""It would have been sufficient for you to do thus.\"" Then he struck his hand upon the earth and blew into them"," and wiped his face and his palms"," and did not go beyond the elbows.'\""\n\nAnd Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated it from Dharr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Murhibī"," except that he expressed doubt in its text and was uncertain therein. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1007","(1007) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, who said: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, who said: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, who said: Shuʿbah narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Dharr narrating from Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā, and he mentioned it.\n\nShuʿbah said: \Then Salamah expressed doubt and did not know whether it was up to the palms (kaffayn) or up to the elbows (mirfaqayn).\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn Jaʿfar Ghundar narrated it from Shuʿbah from Salamah thus"," and he said: \""I do not know whether it includes the elbows or the palms.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1008","(1008) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, who said: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, who said: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, who said: ʿAlī ibn Sahl al-Ramlī narrated to us, who said: Ḥajjāj narrated to us, who said: Shuʿbah narrated to me with his isnād this ḥadīth, and he said: \Then he blew into them and wiped therewith his face and his palms up to the elbows or the forearms.\"" Shuʿbah said: \""Salamah used to say: the palms"," the face"," and the forearms.\"" So Manṣūr said to him one day: \""Look at what you are saying"," for no one mentions the forearms apart from you.\""\n\nSalamah ibn Kuhayl narrated it from Abū Mālik Ḥabīb ibn Ṣahbān al-Kāhilī"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. [Shādh]"""
"1009","(1009) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him, who said: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, who said: Abū al-Muthannā informed us, who said: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us, who said: Sufyān narrated from Salamah, from Abū Mālik, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā, who said: \I was with ʿUmar","\"" and he mentioned the ḥadīth. And ʿAmmār said: \""I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him"," and he said: 'It would have been sufficient for you to do thus.' And he struck his two hands upon the earth"," then blew into them"," and then wiped his face and his hands up to half of the forearm.\""\n\nAnd Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Abū Mālik"," who said: \""I heard ʿAmmār delivering a sermon and he mentioned tayammum"," and he struck his palms upon the earth and wiped therewith his face and his palms.\"" And Ibrāhīh ibn Ṭaḥmān raised it from Ḥuṣayn. And al-Aʿmash narrated it once from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā"," and once from Salamah from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from his father. And he said once in its text: \""Then he wiped his face and his forearms up to half of the forearm"," and did not reach the elbows.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (322)]"""
"1010","(1010) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him, who said: Abū al-Faḍl al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf informed us, who said: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, who said: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬāʾiʾ informed us, who said: Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from ʿAzrah, from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā, from his father, from ʿAmmār, that he said: \I asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about tayammum"," and he commanded me to perform tayammum of the face and the palms with a single strike.\""\n\nQatādah used to issue fatwā according to it. And a group narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah. And ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah without mentioning ʿAzrah in its isnād. And Abān ibn Yazīd al-Aṭṭār likewise narrated it from Qatādah"," and there was disagreement regarding the mention of ʿAzrah in its isnād. And it was narrated from Abān from Qatādah with another isnād that it goes up to the elbows. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Ibn Ḥibbān narrated it (1303)]"""
"1011","(1012) And Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith the jurist — informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar the ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Qāḍīān — al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl and ʿUmar — Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf — both said: Ibrāhīm ibn Hānīʾ informed us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us: Abān said: Qatādah was asked concerning tayammum during travel, and he said: Ibn ʿUmar used to say, \Up to the elbows.\"" And al-Ḥasan and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī used to both say"," \""Up to the elbows.\""\n\nHe said: And a narrator informed me about al-Shaʿbī"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā"," from ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir"," that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Up to the elbows.\""\n\nAbū Isḥāq said: I mentioned it to Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," and he was astonished by it and said"," \""How excellent it is!\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: This discrepancy in the matn of the ḥadīth of Ibn Abzā from ʿAmmār occurred mostly from Salmah ibn Kuḥayl due to a doubt that arose in him. And al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtaybah — he is a ḥāfiậ and jurist — narrated it from Dharr ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," then he heard it directly from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and thus related the ḥadīth with affirmation"," without any doubt in it. And the ḥadīth of Qatādah from ʿAzrah concurs with it. Likewise"," the ḥadīth of Ḥuṣayn from Abī Mālik. As for the ḥadīth of Qatādah from an unnamed narrator from al-Shaʿbī"," it is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected); it is not known who narrated it to him"," so it is subject to further examination.\n\nAnd the ḥadīth has been established from another chain such that no doubt can be cast upon the soundness of its isnād. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1012","(1013) Abū al-Ḥusayn — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān the upright judge — in Baghdad, informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣāghānī informed us, in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year two hundred and sixty-eight: Yaʿlī ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭanāfisī informed us: al-Aʿmash informed us, from Shaqīq, who said: I was sitting with ʿAbd Allāh and Abū Mūsā, and Abū Mūsā said: \O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," a man becomes janbāʾ and finds no water — should he pray?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Have you not heard the statement of ʿAmmār to ʿUmar: 'Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me and you"," and I became janbāʾ"," so I rolled in the dust. Then we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him"," and he said: \""It would have sufficed you thus","\"" and he wiped his face and his two palms once.'\"" He said: \""I did not see ʿUmar accept that.\"" I said: \""Then how do you deal with this verse: {So perform tayammum with clean earth} [al-Nisāʾ: 43]?\"" He said: \""If we were to grant them concession in this"," any one of them"," upon finding cold water"," would wipe himself with earth.\"" Al-Aʿmash said: I said to Shaqīq: \""He only disliked it because of this.\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it through various chains from al-Aʿmash"," and al-Bukhārī alluded to the narration of Yaʿlī ibn ʿUbayd"," and he is the most precise of them in the context of the ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1013","(1014) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said: al-Shāfiʿī said, regarding the ḥadīth of ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir: It is not permissible for ʿAmmār, when he performed tayammum with the Prophet ﷺ at the time of the revelation of the verse, to go beyond the command of the Prophet ﷺ to the shoulders, unless it is abrogated, since he narrated that the Prophet ﷺ commanded tayammum of the face and the two palms, or that he only narrated a single tayammum from him.\n\nThus his narration from him varies. So the narration of Ibn al-Ṣimmah, which does not vary, is more established. And when it does not vary, it is more deserving of being adopted, because it is more consonant with the Book of Allah, Exalted is He, than the two varying narrations that have been reported. Or it may be that they only heard the verse of tayammum at the time of a prayer, so they performed tayammum and took precaution, reaching the furthest extent upon which the term \hand\"" (yad) may fall"," for that does not harm them"," just as it would not harm them if they did so in wuḍūʾ. When the matter reached the Prophet ﷺ"," he informed them that the least of what they had done sufficed them for tayammum. And this is the most appropriate meaning to me regarding the narration of Ibn Shihāb from the ḥadīth of ʿAmmār"," by virtue of the evidence I have described.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: What prevented us from adopting the narration of ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir regarding tayammum of the face and the two palms is the establishment of the report from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he wiped his face and his two forearms. And this is more consonant with the Qurʾān and with qiyās (analogical reasoning)"," for the substitute of a thing is only its like.\n\nAnd al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī narrated from al-Shāfiʿī the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar concerning tayammum: one strike for the face and one strike for the two hands up to the elbows.\n\nThen he said — meaning al-Shāfiʿī: \""And by this I have seen our companions take.\"" And something has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ regarding it. Had I known it to be firmly established"," I would not have abandoned it nor doubted it. And ʿAmmār said: \""We performed tayammum with the Prophet ﷺ up to the shoulders.\"" And it has been narrated from him"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," the face and the two palms.\n\nIt is as though his statement — \""We performed tayammum with the Prophet ﷺ up to the shoulders\"" — was not based on the command of the Prophet ﷺ. So if the face and the two palms are established from ʿAmmār from the Prophet ﷺ"," and the narration up to the elbows is not established from the Prophet ﷺ"," then what is established from the Prophet ﷺ is more deserving of being followed. And upon this was the fatwā of Saʿīd ibn Sālim. It is as though he"," in the earlier period"," doubted the establishment of both ḥadīths for what we have mentioned regarding each of them. And the wiping of the face and the two palms in the ḥadīth of ʿAmmār is more firmly established than the ḥadīth of wiping the forearms"," although the ḥadīth of wiping the forearms is also well-attested by the corroborating evidence we have mentioned"," and it is in another context. If the ḥadīth of ʿAmmār concerns the initial tayammum"," when the verse was revealed and they returned to the Prophet ﷺ"," and he informed them that the least of what they had done sufficed them for tayammum"," then the ḥadīth of wiping the forearms came after it"," and it is more deserving of being followed. And it is more consonant with the Book"," with qiyās"," and with the action of Ibn ʿUmar"," which is soundly reported from him. And wiping of the face and the two palms has been narrated from ʿAlī and Ibn ʿAbbās"," and a contrary narration has been reported from ʿAlī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1014","(1015) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us: Ibn al-Mubārak informed us: Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb informed us, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, that ʿAlī and Ibn ʿAbbās used to say regarding tayammum: \The face and the two palms.\"" And it has been narrated from ʿAṭāʾ"," from Ibn ʿAbbās. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1015","(1016) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith the jurist informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar the ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAlī informed us: Ibrāhīm al-Ḥarbī informed us: Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān and Shujāʿ informed us: Hushaym informed us: Khālid informed us, from Abī Isḥāq, from certain companions of ʿAlī, from ʿAlī, who said: \Two strikes: one for the face and one for the two forearms.\"" And both of these from ʿAlī are munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī transmitted it in the Kitāb of ʿAlī and ʿAbd Allāh as a balāgh (reach) from Hushaym"," from Khālid"," from Abī Isḥāq"," that ʿAlī said regarding tayammum: \""One strike for the face and one strike for the two palms.\""\n\nAnd the precaution is to wipe the face and to wipe the two hands up to the elbows"," in order to exit the difference of opinion. And by Allah lies success. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1016","(1017) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr — Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf the jurist — informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Nāṣir the jurist — informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Hushaym. Abū al-Naḍr said: And al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: Hushaym informed us: Sayyār informed us: Yazīd al-Faqīr informed us: Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I have been given five things which were not given to anyone before me: I was aided with terror (al-ruʿb) over a month's journey; the earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification (ṭahūr)"," so any man of my ummah whom the prayer overtakes"," let him pray; the spoils of war were made lawful for me and were not made lawful for anyone before me; I was given the right of intercession (shafāʿah); and a prophet would be sent to his people specifically"," whereas I have been sent to all of mankind generally.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Sinān and others"," from Hushaym. And Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," and he said in the ḥadīth: \""And the earth was made for me pure (ṭayyibah)"," a means of purification (ṭahūr)"," and a mosque.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 328]"""
"1017","(1018) Abū Ḥāzim the ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-Dhuhlī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Hushaym ibn Bashīr informed us, from Sayyār, from Yazīd al-Faqīr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — he mentioned it with the same meaning — and he mentioned this wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1018","(1019) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān the upright judge in Baghdad informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik informed us: Yazīd — meaning Ibn Hārūn — informed us: Sulaymān — meaning al-Taymī — informed us, from Sayyār, from Abī Umaymah, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \I have been distinguished by four things: the earth was made for my ummah a mosque and a means of purification (ṭahūr)"," so any man of my ummah whom the prayer overtakes and finds no water — he finds the earth a mosque and a means of purification; I have been sent to all people generally; I was aided with terror (al-ruʿb) over a month's journey"," marching before me; and the spoils of war were made lawful for my ummah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than it. Aḥmad narrated it"," 5/248]"""
"1019","(1020) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq the jurist informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā informed us: Ibn Zurayʿ informed us: Khālid informed us, from Abī Qilābah, from ʿAmr ibn Bujdān, from Abī Dharr, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \Pure earth (al-ṣaʿīd al-ṭayyib) is the wuḍūʾ of the Muslim"," even if ten years pass. So when he finds water"," let him let it touch his skin"," for that is better.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than it. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," no. 332]"""
"1020","(1021) Abū Ḥāzim the ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Aḥmad the ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿUrābah informed us: ʿAmr ibn Hishām and Aḥmad ibn Bakkār both informed us: Makhlad — and he is Yazīd — informed us, from Sufyān, from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī and Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from Abī Qilābah, from ʿAmr ibn Bujdān, from Abī Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Pure earth (al-ṣaʿīd al-ṭayyib) is the wuḍūʾ of the Muslim"," even if he finds no water for ten years.\"" Makhlad alone narrated it in this manner.\n\nAnd others narrate it from al-Thawrī"," from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī"," from Abī Qilābah"," from a man"," from Abī Dharr; and from Khālid"," from Abī Qilābah"," from ʿAmr ibn Bujdān"," from Abī Dharr"," as the rest of the people have narrated it.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Qabīṣah"," from al-Thawrī"," from Khālid"," from Abī Qilābah"," from Miḥjan or Abī Miḥjan"," from Abī Dharr. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than it]"""
"1021","(1022) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Musa ibn Harun informed us. In another transmission, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Ka'bi informed us; Isma'il ibn Qutaybah informed us. Both said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah informed us; Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i from Rabi'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I have been given preference over people in three respects: our rows have been made like the rows of the angels; the entire earth has been made a place of prostration for us; and its soil has been made a means of purification for us.\"" And he mentioned a third characteristic.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. And he added in the hadith: \""If we do not find water.\""\n\nAnd Abu 'Awanah narrated it from Abu Malik"," and he said: \""And its soil has been made a means of purification for us.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 522.]"""
"1022","(1023) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us in Baghdad; Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Qattan informed us; Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi informed us; 'Affan informed us; Abu 'Awanah informed us; Abu Malik al-Ashja'i informed us.\n\nIn another transmission, Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan al-Ahwazi informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us; 'Umar ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi informed us; Abu Kamil informed us; Abu 'Awanah informed us from Abu Malik from Rabi'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \We have been given preference over people in three respects: our rows have been made like the rows of the angels; the earth has been made a place of prostration for us; and its soil has been made a means of purification for us. And I was given this verse from the end of Surah al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne"," which no one was given before me and no one will be given after me.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of Abu Kamil"," and the hadith of 'Affan has the same meaning"," and he said: \""And its soil has been made a means of purification for us.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad"," 5/283.]"""
"1023","(1024) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Bakr al-Qattan informed us; Ibrahim ibn al-Harith informed us; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr informed us; Zuhayr ibn Muhammad informed us from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, who heard 'Ali ibn Abi Talib say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I was given what no prophet was given.\"" We said: \""What is it"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""I was helped through awe (cast into the hearts of enemies); I was given the keys of the earth; I was named Ahmad; the soil was made a means of purification for me; and my ummah was made the best of nations.\"" [Sahih through other chains. Narrated by Ahmad"," 1/98.]"""
"1024","(1025) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us; Muhammad ibn Shadhan al-Jawhari informed us; Mu'alla ibn Mansur informed us; Jarir informed us from Qabus from his father from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \The best of soil is the soil of cultivated land.\"" [Da'if. Narrated by Ibn Abi Shaybah"," 1702.]"""
"1025","(1026) Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi informed us; Abu 'Abd al-Malik — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid in Sur informed us; Ya'qub ibn Ka'b al-Halabi informed us; Ibn Idris informed us from Qabus ibn Abi Zabyan from his father from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \Al-sa'id is the cultivated soil of the earth.\"" [Narrated by Ibn Abi Shaybah"," 1702.]"""
"1026","(1027) Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn Furak informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us; Yunus ibn Habib informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Shu'bah informed us from al-Hakam, who heard Dharr ibn 'Abdullah narrate from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from his father, who said: A man came to 'Umar and mentioned the hadith, and in it from 'Ammar from the Prophet (ﷺ): \It would suffice you.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) struck his hand upon the earth unto the soil"," and said: \""Like this.\"" Then he blew into it and wiped his face and his hands up to the joints"," and the forearms are not mentioned in it.\n\nIt is narrated in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj. [Sahih.]"""
"1027","(1028) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abdullah — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed me; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Abu Kurayb informed us; Abu Usamah informed us from Hisham from his father from 'A'ishah, who said: She borrowed a necklace from Asma' and it was lost. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent some of his Companions to search for it. The time of prayer overtook them, so they prayed without wudu'. When they came to the Prophet (ﷺ), they complained of that to him. Then the verse of tayammum was revealed. Usayd ibn Hudayr said: \May Allah reward you with good. By Allah"," no matter has ever befallen you except that Allah made a way out for you from it"," and He placed blessing for the Muslims therein.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Ubayd ibn Isma'il from Abu Usamah"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu Kurayb.\n\nThese Companions — may Allah be pleased with them — when they found no water"," they performed tayammum with that which had been made a means of purification for them"," and they prayed at the proper time. They complained of that to the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he did not disapprove of it. Likewise"," others among them when they find no water and no soil. [Sahih.]"""
"1028","(1029) He said: And Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us; Abu Salamah al-Khuza'i informed us; Layth informed us from Yazid, meaning ibn al-Had, from Ibn Shihab from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whatever I have forbidden you"," avoid it; and whatever I have commanded you"," do of it as much as you are able. Indeed"," those who came before you were destroyed by the abundance of their questions and their disagreement with their prophets.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khalaf from Abu Salamah.\n\nAnd the implication of the position of 'Umar and Ibn Mas'ud regarding one who finds no water and no soil is that he should not pray"," for they did not consider any means of purification for the person in a state of major ritual impurity (junub) except water. So when he does not find it"," they said he should not pray. And likewise in other cases. [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 1327.]"""
"1029","(1030) Abu 'Amr — Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Adib informed us; Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Umar, Abu al-Husayn, meaning al-Jurjani, informed us; Bishr, meaning ibn Khalid al-Farid, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us from Shu'bah from Sulayman from Abu Wa'il, who said: Abu Musa said to 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: \If one does not find water"," should he not pray?\"" 'Abdullah said: \""Yes. If I do not find water for a month"," I will not pray. If I were to give them concession in this"," then whenever any of them felt the cold"," he would say"," 'Like this' — meaning tayammum — and pray.\"" I said: \""Then what of the statement of 'Ammar to 'Umar?\"" He said: \""I do not see that 'Umar was satisfied with the statement of 'Ammar.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Bishr ibn Khalid. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 339.]"""
"1030","(1031) Abu Muhammad — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Mu'ammili informed us; Abu 'Uthman al-Basri informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us; Sulayman ibn Harb al-Washiḥi, Abu Ayyub, informed us; Hammad ibn Zayd informed us.\n\nAnd Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Abi 'Ali al-Hafiz al-Mihrajanī, and Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Muqri' al-Mihrajanī, both said: Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi informed us; Abu al-Rabi' and Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr and Musaddad said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from 'Alqamah ibn Waqqas al-Laythi, who said: I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \O people"," actions are but by intentions"," and each person shall have only what he intended. So whoever's migration was to Allah and His Messenger"," his migration is to Allah and His Messenger; and whoever's migration was for some worldly gain he would acquire or a woman he would marry"," his migration is to that for which he migrated.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu al-Rabi'. The hadith of Sulayman ibn Harb does not contain \""O people","\"" and the rest is the same. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 338.]"""
"1031","(1032) Abū Bakr ibn Furak informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Thābit al-ʿAbdī narrated to us; and Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us that Muḥammad ibn Thābit, meaning al-ʿAbdī, narrated from Nāfiʿ, who said: I set out with Ibn ʿUmar to Ibn ʿAbbās regarding a need that Ibn ʿUmar had with Ibn ʿAbbās. When Ibn ʿUmar fulfilled his need from Ibn ʿAbbās, among the things he narrated that day was that he said: A man passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in one of the lanes, having just relieved himself of excrement or urine, and he greeted him with salām, but he did not return the salām. When the man was about to disappear from the lane, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) struck his hands upon the wall, wiped his face, then struck his hands another blow and wiped his arms, then returned the salām to the man and said: \Nothing prevented me from returning your salām except that I was not in a state of purity.\"" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and it is the more complete of the two. [Munkar]"""
"1032","(1033) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us that Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated. And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us that Abū ʿAmr al-Ḥawḍī narrated to us that Shuʿbah said: Ashʿath ibn Sulaym informed me, saying: I heard my father narrate from Masrūq, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) liked to begin with the right side in his sandals, his combing of his hair, his purification, and in all his affairs.\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of al-Ḥawḍī, and the ḥadīth of Bishr ibn ʿUmar carries the same meaning. He said: \from from\"" — and al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn ʿUmar"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1033","(1034) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me that al-Ḥasan, meaning ibn Sufyān, narrated to us that Ḥabbān narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh informed us that ʿAwf narrated from Abī Rajāʾ, who narrated that ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn al-Khuzāʿī narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a man who had separated himself and was not praying with the people. He said: \O so-and-so"," what prevented you from praying with the people?\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I have been afflicted with janābah and there is no water.\"" He said: \""Upon you is the clean earth (al-ṣaʿīd)"," for it will suffice you.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān"," from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 341]"""
"1034","(1035) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Dharr, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā, from his father, who said: I was present with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb when ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir said to him: \Do you remember when we were on a military expedition and we became junub"," so we rolled about in the dust? Then we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned that to him"," and he said: 'This would have sufficed you.'\"" And he described that"," meaning tayammum.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in most of the manuscripts from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1035","(1036) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us that Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadbādhī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from Nājiyah ibn Kaʿb, from ʿAmmār, who said: I became junub in a sandy place, so I rolled about like an animal rolls. Then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him, and he said: \Tayammum would have sufficed you from that.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"""
"1036","(1037) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us that Mālik ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Abū Badr Shuʿjāʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdillāh — and he is not al-Masʿūdī — narrated from al-Minhāl ibn ʿAmr, from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh, from ʿAlī, who said: This verse was revealed regarding the traveller: {Nor [when you are] junub, except while passing through [a place of prayer], until you have washed [your whole body]} (al-Nisāʾ, 4:43). He said: If a person becomes junub and does not find water, he should perform tayammum and pray until he finds water. When he finds water, he should perform ghusl. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"
"1037","(1038) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated from Sufyān, meaning al-Thawrī, from al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abī Hurayrah, who said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \We are in a sandy region"," and among us are menstruating women"," women in postpartum bleeding"," and those in a state of janābah. Four months may pass upon us without us finding water.\"" He said: \""Upon you is the earth (al-turāb)\"" — meaning tayammum.\n\nThis ḥadīth is known through al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ from ʿAmr. And al-Muthannā is not strong.\n\nAl-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāʾ narrated it from ʿAmr"," but he differed from him in the chain"," narrating it from ʿAmr"," from his father"," from his grandfather"," and he abbreviated the text"," making the question about a man who cannot find water: \""May he cohabit with his wife?\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\n[Weak. Abū Yaʿlā narrated it"," no. 5870]"""
"1038","(1039) Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Sammān — Ashʿath ibn Saʿīd — narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abī Hurayrah, that some Bedouins came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," we are in these sandy regions. We cannot find water"," and we may not see water for three or four months\"" — Abū al-Rabīʿ was uncertain — \""and among us are women in postpartum bleeding"," menstruating women"," and those in a state of janābah.\"" He said: \""Upon you is the earth.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Sammān narrated it. And Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Sammān is weak. [Very weak]"""
"1039","(1040) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated — he said: I heard ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh say: I said to Sufyān: \Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"," from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab"," from Abī Hurayrah regarding a man who is away with his camels.\""\n\nSufyān said: \""It was al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ who brought this from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb"," and ʿAmr ibn Dīnār only said: 'I heard Jābir ibn Zayd say it.'\"" ʿAlī said: I said to Sufyān: \""Shuʿbah narrated it in this manner from Jābir.\"" He said: \""Shuʿbah was among the people of precision and truthfulness"," and he was not among those who intended falsehood.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: It was also narrated from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah"," from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"," from Ibn al-Musayyab"," from Abī Hurayrah. And Ibn Abī ʿArūbah only heard it from Abū al-Rabīʿ"," from ʿAmr. Likewise"," Saʿd ibn al-Ṣalt narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah. And it was narrated through another weak chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn ʿAdī narrated it in al-Kāmil"," 1/378]"""
"1040","(1041) Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Khalīl al-Ṣūfī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that ʿUmar ibn Shabbah narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Salamah al-Afaṭṣ narrated from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abī Hurayrah, who said: Some Bedouins came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \We are in a sandy region"," and we may be deprived of water for two or three months"," and among us are those in a state of janābah and menstruating women.\"" He said: \""Upon you is the earth (al-turāb).\""\n\nʿAbdullāh ibn Salamah al-Afaṭṣ is weak"," and Allah knows best. [Very weak. Ibn ʿAdī narrated it"," 4/196]"""
"1041","(1042) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from a man of Banī ʿĀmir, who said: I entered Islam, and my religion preoccupied me, so I came to Abū Dharr. Abū Dharr said: I found the climate of Madīnah disagreeable, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered for me a herd of camels and some sheep, and he said to me: \Drink their milk.\"" Ḥammād said: I have doubt as to whether he said \""their urine\"" as well. Abū Dharr said: I was far from water while my wife was with me"," and I would experience janābah"," so I would pray without purification. I came to the Prophet ﷺ at midday while he was among a group of his Companions in the shade of the mosque. He said: \""Abū Dharr?\"" I said: \""Yes"," I am ruined"," O Messenger of Allah!\"" He said: \""What has ruined you?\"" I said: \""I was far from water while my wife was with me"," and I experienced janābah"," so I prayed without purification.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered water for me"," and a dark-skinned young woman came with a small water-skin"," the water sloshing within it though it was not full. I screened myself behind a camel and performed ghusl"," then I came. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""O Abū Dharr"," the pure earth is a means of purification for you"," even if you do not find water for ten years. But when you find water"," then let it touch your skin.\""\n\n[Authenticated by other narrators. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 333.]"""
"1042","(1043) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Maʿmard ibn Sulaymān narrated from al-Ḥajjāj, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \A man is in a place where he cannot find water — may he be intimate with his wife?\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nA similar narration is strengthened by corroborating reports. The established ḥadīth of ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir and ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn from both of them serves as a witness to these two.\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 2/225.]"""
"1043","(1044) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Abū ʿĀmir Mūsā ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us; al-Walīd, meaning Ibn Muslim, narrated to us; Saʿīd, meaning Ibn Bashīr, narrated from Qatādah, from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ḥakīm, from his paternal uncle, who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I am far from water and my wife is with me — may I be intimate with her?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I am absent for months.\"" He said: \""Even if you remain for three years.\""\n\nIt is said that his paternal uncle was Ḥakīm ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Numayrī.\n\n[Weak.]"""
"1044","(1045) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Jarīr narrated from Ashʿath, from Jaʿfar, from Saʿīd, from Ibn ʿAbbās: that he was intimate with his female slave and then performed tayammum and prayed while in a state of tayammum.\n\nAs for washing the private parts and the discussion regarding moisture in the woman's private parts, we have transmitted that in the Book of Prayer, in the chapter on Impurities.\n\n[Authenticated. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah, 1/36.]"
"1045","(1046) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf al-ʿAdl informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬāṭāʾ informed us; ʿAwf ibn Abī Jamīlah narrated from Abū Rajāʾ al-ʿUṭāridī, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said: We were on a journey with the Prophet ﷺ, and we traveled through the night until, when we were in the last part of the night, we made that stop — and there is no stop sweeter to a traveler than that. Nothing woke us except the heat of the sun. The first to awaken was so-and-so, then so-and-so — ʿAwf named them — then the fourth was ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb. The Prophet ﷺ, when he slept, would not be woken by anyone until he awoke on his own, because we did not know what might occur to him in his sleep. When ʿUmar awoke and saw what had befallen the people — and he was a stout, resolute man — he said the takbīr and raised his voice with takbīr. He continued saying takbīr and raising his voice until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ awoke from the sound of his voice. When he awoke, we complained to him about what had befallen us. He said: \No harm\"" — or \""No injury\"" — ʿAwf had doubt. He said: \""Move on.\"" The Prophet ﷺ moved on and traveled a short distance"," then stopped. He called for water and performed wuḍūʾ"," then called for the prayer and led the people in prayer. When he finished his prayer"," there was a man who had separated himself and had not prayed with the people. He said: \""O so-and-so"," what prevented you from praying with the people?\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I experienced janābah and there is no water.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Use the earth"," for it will suffice you.\""\n\nThe Prophet ﷺ continued"," and the people complained of thirst. He stopped and called for so-and-so — ʿAwf named him — and called for ʿAlī. He said: \""Go and seek water for us.\"" They set out and came upon a woman with two water-skins — or two vessels of water — on her camel. They said to her: \""Where is the water?\"" She said: \""I left the water at this time yesterday"," and my people are behind us\"" — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb said: meaning"," they are thirsty. They said to her: \""Then come along.\"" She said: \""To where?\"" They said: \""To the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" She said: \""The one they call al-Ṣābiʾ?\"" They said: \""The very one you mean"," so come along.\"" They brought her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him the story. He had her dismount from her camel. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a vessel and poured into it from the mouths of the two water-skins — or the two vessels — rinsed his mouth in the water and returned it to the mouths of the two water-skins — or the two vessels — then tied their mouths and opened the water-bags. He then said to the people: \""Drink and water your animals.\"" Whoever wished drank"," and whoever wished watered his animal.\n\nThe last of it was that he gave the one who had experienced janābah a vessel of water and said: \""Go and pour it over yourself.\"" She was standing"," watching what was being done with her water. By Allah"," he did not stop using it"," and it appeared to us that it was more full than when he began with it. The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Gather something for her.\"" They gathered for her from flour and parched barley flour until they gathered food for her"," placed it in her garment"," carried it"," and set it before her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""You know"," by Allah"," we have not diminished any of your water"," but it is Allah who gave us to drink.\"" She came to her family after having been delayed"," and they said to her: \""What kept you"," O so-and-so?\"" She said: \""Amazing! Two men came to me and took me to this al-Ṣābiʾ"," and he did such and such with my water — \"" she recounted what had happened. \""By Allah"," he is the greatest magician between these two\"" — gesturing — \""or he is truly the Messenger of Allah.\"" The Muslims used to raid those around her among the polytheists but would not attack the clan she was among. One day she said to her people: \""These people are deliberately leaving you alone. Would you not like to enter Islam?\"" They obeyed her"," and they all came and entered Islam.\n\n[Recorded in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of ʿAwf.]"""
"1046","(1047) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Khwārizmī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us in Baghdād; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Naysābūrī — and he was the brother of Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥamdān — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Salm ibn Zarīr narrated: I heard Abū Rajāʾ say: ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn narrated to us: that he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. They traveled through their night until, when it was near dawn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made camp, and their eyes overcame them until the sun had risen. The first to awaken from his sleep was Abū Bakr. No one would wake the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from his sleep until the Prophet ﷺ awoke on his own. Then ʿUmar awoke and sat at his head, and he began saying takbīr and raising his voice until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ awoke. When he awoke and saw the sun had risen, he said: \Move on.\"" He traveled with us until the sun had turned white"," then he stopped and prayed. A man from the people had separated himself and had not prayed with us. When the Prophet ﷺ finished"," he said: \""O so-and-so"," what prevented you from praying with us?\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I experienced janābah.\"" He commanded him to perform tayammum with the earth and then pray. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me ahead on a mount to search for water"," and we had become severely thirsty. While we were traveling"," we came upon a woman letting her legs hang down between two water-skins. We said to her: \""Where is the water?\"" She said: \""Oh dear"," oh dear"," there is no water!\"" We said: \""How far are your people and the water?\"" She said: \""A day and a night.\"" We said: \""Come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" She said: \""And what is the Messenger of Allah?\"" We did not dissuade her from her matter until we brought her before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She told him the same as she had told us"," except that she told him she had dependents waiting. He commanded regarding her water-skins and spat into the two upper water-bags. We drank — forty thirsty men — until we were satisfied. We filled every waterskin and vessel we had with us"," and washed our companion"," but we did not water a single camel. The water-skins were nearly overflowing from the abundance. Then he said to us: \""Bring what you have.\"" We gathered for her pieces of bread and dates until we made a bundle for her. He said to her: \""Go and feed this to your family"," and know that we have not diminished any of your water.\"" When she came to her family"," she said: \""I have met the most sorcerous of people — or he is a prophet as they claim.\"" Allah guided that clan through that woman"," so she embraced Islam and they embraced Islam.\n\n[Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd"," and Muslim narrated it from Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd from Salm ibn Zarīr.]"""
"1047","(1048) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Abū ʿAmr Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-ʿUṭāridī narrated to us; Yūnus, that is Ibn Bukayr, narrated from ʿAbbād ibn Manṣūr al-Nājī, who said: Abū Rajāʾ al-ʿUṭāridī narrated to me, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the man: \What prevented you from praying?\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I experienced janābah.\"" He said: \""Perform tayammum with the earth"," and when you have finished"," pray. And when you find water"," then perform ghusl.\"" They mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth.\n\n[Authenticated.]"""
"1048","(1049) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Mihrān ibn Khālid informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us; Isrāʾīl narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from Nājiyah ibn Kaʿb, who said: Ibn Masʿūd and ʿAmmār disputed regarding a man who experiences janābah and does not find water. Ibn Masʿūd said: \He should not pray until he finds water.\"" ʿAmmār said: \""I was among the camels and experienced janābah. I could not find water"," so I rolled in the dust as the beasts roll. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: 'Indeed"," tayammum with the pure earth would have sufficed you. Then when you find water"," perform ghusl.'\""\n\n[Authenticated by other narrators.]"""
"1049","(1050) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Khālid narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ, from Abū Qilābah, from ʿAmr ibn Bijdān, from Abū Dharr, who said: A small flock gathered near the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \O Abū Dharr"," go out among them.\"" So I went out to al-Rabadhah"," and I would experience janābah and remain for five or six days. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he said: \""Abū Dharr.\"" I remained silent. He said: \""May your mother be bereaved of you"," Abū Dharr — woe to your mother!\"" He called for a young woman"," and she came with a small water-skin of water. He screened me with my garment"," and I screened myself behind the mount and performed ghusl"," as though I had cast a mountain off myself. He said: \""The pure earth is the wuḍūʾ of the Muslim"," even if it be for ten years. But when you find water"," then let it touch your skin"," for that is better.\""\n\n[Authenticated by other narrators.]"""
"1050","(1051) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us; Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ narrated… and he mentioned it similarly, and said: I heard Abū Dharr say: Sheep from the ṣadaqah gathered near the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He did not mention camels or \woe","\"" and the rest carries the same meaning.\n\n[Authenticated by other narrators.]"""
"1051","(1052) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, ʿAmr ibn Marzūq informed us, Shuʿbah narrated from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet ﷺ said: \There is no [requirement of] wuḍūʾ except from a sound or an odour.\""\n\nThe use of this ḥadīth as evidence in this issue is not valid"," nor is the ḥadīth of Abū Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1052","(1053) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʔbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, Ḥabbān ibn ʿAlī narrated from Abī Sinān — Ḍirār ibn Murrah al-Shaybānī — from Ḥuṣayn, from ʿAlī, that he said upon the minbar: \Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Nothing invalidates the ṣalāh except al-ḥadath.' And I am not shy before you of that from which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not shy.\"" And al-ḥadath is that one passes wind silently or with a sound.\n\nḤabbān ibn ʿAlī al-ʿAnazī is the sole narrator of it. [Ḍaʿīf. ʿAbd Allāh narrated it in Zawāʾid al-Musnad 1/138]"""
"1053","(1054) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us, Ibn al-Mubārak informed us, ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated from ʿĀmir — meaning al-Aḥwal — from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \One performs tayammum for every prayer"," even if one has not broken one's wuḍūʾ.\"" Its isnād is ṣaḥīḥ. (T) And it has been narrated from ʿAlī"," from ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"," and from Ibn ʿAbbās. [Ḥasan. The author narrated it in al-Maʿrifah 337]"""
"1054","(1055) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, Abū Bakr — meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah — informed us, Hushaym narrated from Ḥajjāj, from Abī Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \One performs tayammum for every prayer.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it 1/184]"""
"1055","(1056) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Ibn Muḥammad — informed us, Isḥāq — meaning al-Ḥanẓalī — informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmar, from Qatādah, that ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ used to perform tayammum for every prayer when he broke his wuḍūʾ. And Qatādah used to take this as a proof. And this is a mursal narration. [Ḍaʿīf. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it 833]"
"1056","(1057) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh — informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī informed us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah, from al-Ḥakam, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \It is from the Sunnah that a man should not pray with tayammum except one prayer"," then he should perform tayammum for the next prayer.\""\n\nʿAlī said: \""Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah is weak.\""\n\nI say: And likewise Abū Yaḥyā al-Ḥimmānī narrated it from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah. [Bāṭil]"""
"1057","(1058) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us, and Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: \Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim informed you from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah"," from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah"," from Mujāhid ibn Jabr"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās"," that he said: 'One should not pray with tayammum except one prayer.'\""\n\nAnd likewise Ibn Zanjawayh narrated it from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," from al-Ḥasan. And al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah is not to be used as a proof. [Bāṭil]"""
"1058","(1059) Abū al-Fatḥ — Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār — in Baghdād informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Abū al-Ashʿath informed us, Yazīd ibn Zuraʿy informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Abū al-Muthannā informed us, Musaddad informed us, Yazīd ibn Zuraʿy informed us, Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated from Sayyār, from Abī Umaymah, that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," has given me preference over the prophets\"" — or he said: \""My ummah over the nations — with four things: He sent me to all of mankind; He made the entire earth for me and my ummah a means of purification and a place of prostration"," so wherever the time of prayer overtakes a man of my ummah"," his place of prayer and his means of purification are there; I was aided with terror"," which was cast into the hearts of my enemies"," travelling a distance of one month ahead of me; and the war spoils were made lawful for me.\"" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abī al-Ashʿath. [Ḥasan. Al-Ṭabarānī narrated it in al-Kabīr 1/8]"""
"1059","(1060) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ibn Milḥān informed us, Yaḥyā — meaning Ibn Bukayr — informed us, al-Layth narrated from Ibn al-Hād, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, during the year of the expedition of Tabūk, stood at night to pray, and he mentioned the ḥadīth. He said: \I was given five things during the night that no one before me was given.\"" He mentioned the ḥadīth"," and in it he said: \""The earth was made for me a place of prostration and a means of purification; wherever the time of prayer overtakes me"," I perform tayammum and pray.\"" He said: \""And the fifth: it was said to me"," 'Ask","' for every prophet has asked"," so I have deferred my request to the Day of Resurrection"," and it shall be for you and for whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah.\"" [Ḥasan. Aḥmad narrated it 2/222]"""
"1060","(1061) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us, Abū Isḥāq — Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī — informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥabīb ibn al-Shahīd informed us, Ibn Fuḍayl narrated from Abī Mālik al-Ashjaʿī, from Ribʿī ibn Ḥirāsh, from Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \We have been given preference over people with three things: the entire earth has been made for us a place of prostration; its soil has been made for us a means of purification when we do not find water; our rows have been made like the rows of the angels; and I was given these verses from the end of Sūrat al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne"," which was not given to anyone before me and will not be given to anyone after me.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," from Ibn Fuḍayl"," except that he said regarding the third: \""And he mentioned another trait but did not explain it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it 522]"""
"1061","(1062) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Maḥmūd ibn Muḥammad al-Wāsiṭī informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā al-Miṣrī informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim narrated to him from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, that she said: \A necklace of mine fell at al-Baydāʾ while we were entering Madīnah. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stopped"," and while his head was resting in my lap as he slept"," my father came and struck me a severe blow and said"," 'You have detained the people over a necklace!' Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) awoke and the time of Ṣalāh arrived. They searched for water but none was found"," and the verse was revealed: {O you who believe"," when you rise for Ṣalāh…} up to the mention of Tayammum.\"" Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr said: \""May Allah bless the people through you"," O family of Abū Bakr! You are nothing but a blessing.\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1062","(1063) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād informed us; Ibn Abī Uways informed us; Mālik narrated to me from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \We went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on one of his journeys until we were at al-Baydāʾ or Dhāt al-Jaysh"," when my necklace broke. The Prophet (ﷺ) stopped to search for it"," and the people stopped with him"," though they were not near water and had no water with them. The people came to Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq and said"," 'Do you not see what ʿĀʾishah has done? She has detained the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and the people"," though they are not near water and have no water with them.' Abū Bakr came while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sleeping on my thigh. He said"," 'You have detained the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and the people"," though they are not near water and have no water with them.' He rebuked me and said whatever Allah willed him to say"," and he kept poking me with his hand in my side. Nothing prevented me from moving except the place of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on my thigh. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slept until morning without water. Then Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," revealed the verse of Tayammum: {So Tayammum upon clean surface (ṣaʿīd ṭayyib)}. Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr said"," 'This is not the first of your blessings"," O family of Abū Bakr.' She said: 'We sent the camel I was riding"," and we found the necklace beneath it.'\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"," and narrated by Muslim from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1063","(1064) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Ibn ʿAjlān, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he came from al-Jurf and when he was at al-Mirbad, he performed Tayammum, wiped his face and his hands, and prayed ʿAṣr. Then he entered Madīnah while the sun was still high, and he did not repeat the Ṣalāh.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \Al-Jurf is near Madīnah.\""\n\nAl-Shaykh said: It has also been narrated as a Musnad hadith from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," but it is not preserved (as such). [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm 1/46]"""
"1064","(1065) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us in al-Fawāʾid al-Kabīr; and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī; and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī by dictation; and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr by recitation; and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī verbatim — they all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Razīn narrated to us; Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us from ʿUbaydullāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet (ﷺ) performed Tayammum while looking at the houses of Madīnah from a place called Mirbad al-Naʿam. [Munkar. Narrated by al-Ḥākim 1/288]"
"1065","(1066) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us.\n\nAnd Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us; Yūsuf ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Jarīr narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who raised it (to the Prophet), regarding the words of Allah the Most High: {Or if you are ill or on a journey}, he said: \When a man has wounds in the path of Allah"," or sores"," or smallpox"," and he becomes junub"," and fears that if he performs Ghusl he may die"," then let him perform Tayammum.\""\n\nThe wording is from the hadith of Abū Bakr ibn ʿAlī.\n\nSimilarly"," Jaʿfar al-Shāmātī narrated it from Yūsuf ibn Mūsā"," and similarly Isḥāq al-Ḥanẓalī narrated it from Jarīr. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah 272]"""
"1066","(1067) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Muqriʾ in Baghdād informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us; ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the man who is afflicted with Janābah and has wounds, and fears that if he performs Ghusl he may die: he said, \Let him perform Tayammum and pray.\""\n\nIbrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān and others also narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ as a Mawqūf hadith"," and similarly ʿAzrah narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr as Mawqūf. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1067","(1068) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated — he said: I asked Qatādah about the one afflicted with smallpox (al-majdūr). He said: al-Shaʿbī was asked about it, and he said, \Its horsemen have departed.\"" He said: Saʿīd ibn Jubayr said something"," but he (Qatādah) did not retain it. Shuʿbah said: And ʿĀṣim — meaning al-Aḥwal — informed me from Qatādah"," from ʿAzrah"," from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," that he said regarding the one afflicted with smallpox: \""He should perform Tayammum.\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Hāshimī in Ḥalab narrated to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal"," from Qatādah"," from ʿAzrah"," from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," regarding the one afflicted with smallpox and the like"," when he becomes junub: he said"," \""He should perform Tayammum with clean surface (ṣaʿīd).\""\n\nAnd al-Thawri and ʿAbdah ibn Sulaymān narrated it from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal with his chain from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: \""Tayammum with clean surface was permitted for the sick person.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 1070]"""
"1068","(1069) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān informed us; Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Fever is from the heat of Jahannam; extinguish it with water.\"" Nāfiʿ said: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar used to say: \""O Allah"," remove from us the torment (al-rijz).\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān from Ibn Wahb"," and narrated by Muslim from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd.\n\nAnd ʿĀʾishah and Asmāʾ"," the two daughters of al-Ṣiddīq"," narrated it"," and Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj narrated it — all of them from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 5391]"""
"1069","(1070) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh in Baghdād informed us — he said: It was recited to ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad while I was listening; Wahb ibn Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us; my father narrated to me — he said: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrating from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from ʿImrān ibn Abī Anas, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Jubayr, from ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, who said: \I experienced a wet dream on a cold night during the expedition of Dhāt al-Salāsil. I feared that if I performed Ghusl I would perish"," so I performed Tayammum and then led my companions in the Fajr prayer. They mentioned that to the Prophet (ﷺ)"," who said: 'O ʿAmr"," did you lead your companions in prayer while you were junub?' I informed him of what had prevented me from performing Ghusl"," and I said: 'Indeed"," I heard Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," say: {And do not kill yourselves; indeed"," Allah is Merciful to you.}' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) laughed and said nothing.\""\n\nAnd ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated it from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb"," but he contradicted him in both the Isnad and the Matn entirely. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 334]"""
"1070","(1071) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith and another man — I think him to be Ibn Lahiʿah — informed me from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from ʿImrān ibn Abī Anas, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Jubayr, from Abū Qays, the freedman of ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, that ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ was on a military expedition and severe cold befell them the like of which had never been seen. He came out for the Fajr prayer and said: \By Allah"," I experienced a wet dream last night"," but by Allah"," I have never seen cold like this. Has the like of it ever come upon you?\"" They said: \""No.\"" So he washed his joints and performed Wudūʾ as for Ṣalāh"," then led them in prayer. When he came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked: \""How did you find ʿAmr and his companions?\"" They praised him well and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," he led us in prayer while he was junub.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent for ʿAmr and asked him. He informed him of that and of what he had suffered from the cold. He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," indeed Allah the Most High said: {And do not kill yourselves.} Had I performed Ghusl"," I would have died.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) laughed at ʿAmr.\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated both of them in the Sunan"," then he said: And this story was narrated from al-Awzāʿī from Ḥassān ibn ʿAṭiyyah"," in which he said: \""So he performed Tayammum.\""\n\nAl-Shaykh said: It is possible that he did what was narrated in both reports — he washed what he was able to wash and performed Tayammum for the rest. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1071","(1072) Shu'ayb reported: I was sitting with Abdullah and Abu Musa. Abu Musa said, \O Abu Abd al-Rahman! A man becomes janabah and finds no water — should he pray?\"" He said"," \""No.\"" He said"," \""Have you not heard the statement of Ammar to Umar: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me and you"," and I became janabah"," so I rolled in the dust. We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him"," and he said: 'It is sufficient for you thus.' And he wiped his face and his hands with a single wipe.\"" He said"," \""I did not see Umar accept that.\"" He said"," \""What do you do with this verse: {And you find no water"," then seek clean earth [for tayammum]}?\"" He said"," \""If we were to grant them concession in this matter"," whenever one of them found cold water"," he would resort to wiping with dust.\"" Al-A'mash said"," \""I said to Shu'ayb: He only disliked it for this reason.\""\n\nNarrated in the two Sahihs.\n\nHafs ibn Giyath narrated from al-A'mash regarding the hadith: Abdullah did not know what to say. He said"," \""If we were to grant them concession in this matter"," it is likely that when the water became cold for any of them"," he would abandon it and perform tayammum.\"" I said to Shu'ayb"," \""Abdullah disliked it only for this reason?\"" He said"," \""Yes.\"" [Sahih]"""
"1072","(1073) Abu Abd al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' narrated to us: al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Giyath narrated to us: my father narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rabah narrated to us: Ata' narrated to us from Ibn Abbas: A man became janabah in winter and was asked about it. He was ordered to perform ghusl, so he bathed and died. This was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \What is the matter with them? They killed him — may Allah destroy them\"" — three times. \""Allah has made the earth"," or tayammum"," a means of purification.\""\n\nThis is a connected hadith. The complete account is found in the hadith sent by al-Awza'i from Ata'. [Hasan li-ghayrihi. Narrated by Ibn Hibban (1314)]"""
"1073","(1074) Abu Abd al-Hafiz and Abu Abd Allah Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Susi and Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Musa — they said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Mazid narrated to us: my father said: I heard al-Awza'i saying: It has reached me that Ata' ibn Abi Rabah heard Ibn Abbas narrating: A man sustained a wound during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and then he experienced a wet dream. He was ordered to perform ghusl, so he bathed, shivered, and died. This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \They killed him — may Allah destroy them. Was not the cure for ignorance to ask?\""\n\nAta' said: It reached us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about that"," and he said: \""If only he had washed his body and left his head where the wound was.\""\n\nThis mursal hadith necessitates washing the healthy part of him"," while the first hadith necessitates tayammum. Whoever obligates combining the two says: There is no contradiction between the two narrations"," except that one of them is mursal. [Hasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"1074","(1075) Abu Ali al-Rudhbari narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Antaki narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: from al-Zubayr ibn Khurayq, from Ata', from Jabir, who said: We set out on a journey, and a stone struck one of us, wounding his head. He then experienced a wet dream. He said to his companions, \Do you find any concession for me regarding tayammum?\"" They said"," \""We find no concession for you"," since you have access to water.\"" He performed ghusl and died. When we arrived before the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of that"," he said: \""They killed him — may Allah destroy them. Did they not ask when they did not know? The cure for ignorance is to ask. It would have been sufficient for him to perform tayammum and to bandage — or to wrap — his wound.\"" Musa was uncertain: \""with a cloth"," then wipe over it"," and wash the rest of his body.\""\n\nThis narration is connected"," combining washing the healthy part"," wiping the bandage"," and tayammum"," except that it contradicts the first two narrations in its chain of transmission. And Allah knows best. [Munkar. Narrated by Abu Dawud (336)]"""
"1075","(1076) Abu al-Hasan ibn Abdan narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadhan, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever leaves a place the size of a hair on his body from janabah without washing it"," such and such will be done to it from the Fire.\"" Ali said: \""From then on"," I grew hostile toward my hair.\""\n\nThis hadith and what has been narrated with its meaning necessitates washing the healthy part of him"," while the Book of Allah necessitates tayammum for that which one is unable to wash. And by Allah"," success is from Him.\n\nThe apparent meaning of the Book of Allah indicates using whatever water is available"," then resorting to tayammum if none is found. It has been narrated from Ishaq from Isa ibn Yunus from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah"," and it is mentioned that Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah said: \""He performs wudu and performs tayammum when in janabah"," finding only enough water for wudu.\"" And Marwan ibn Rashid held the same view. Al-Hasan and al-Zuhri used to say: \""He performs tayammum only.\"" [Da'if]"""
"1076","(1077) Abu Hazim Umar ibn Ahmad al-Abdawi al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath al-Sijistani in Baghdad narrated to us: Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Halabi in Antioch narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: from al-Zubayr ibn Khurayq, from Ata', from Jabir, who said: We set out on a journey, and a stone struck one of us, wounding his head. He then experienced a wet dream. He asked his companions, \Do you find any concession for me regarding tayammum?\"" They said"," \""We find no concession for you"," since you have access to water.\"" He performed ghusl and died. When we arrived before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of that"," he said: \""They killed him — may Allah destroy them. Did they not ask when they did not know? The cure for ignorance is to ask. It would have been sufficient for him to perform tayammum and to bandage his wound with a cloth"," then wipe over it and wash the rest of his body.\"" [Munkar]"""
"1077","(1078) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us: Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: Abu Amir Musa ibn Amir narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Hisham ibn al-Ghazi narrated to us: from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: \When there is no bandage on the wound"," he washes around it but does not wash it.\"" [Hasan]"""
"1078","(1079) With his chain of transmission, al-Walid said: Hisham ibn al-Ghazi informed me that he heard Nafi' narrating from Abd Allah ibn Umar that he used to say: \Whoever has a wound that is bandaged — he performs wudu"," wipes over the bandage"," and washes what is around the bandage.\"" [Hasan]"""
"1079","(1080) With his chain of transmission, al-Walid said: Sa'id narrated to us: from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: \His big toe was wounded"," and he covered it with something"," and he used to perform wudu over it.\"" [Da'if]"""
"1080","(1081) With his chain of transmission, al-Walid said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us: Musa ibn Yasar narrated to us: from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: \He performed wudu while his hand was bandaged; he wiped over it and over the bandage"," and washed everything else.\"" This is sahih from Ibn Umar.\n\nAbu Sa'id ibn Abi Amr narrated to us: Abu al-Abbas al-Asam narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman said: al-Shafi'i said: \""A hadith has been narrated from Ali — may Allah be pleased with him — that one of his forearms was broken"," and the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to wipe over the splints. Had I known its chain of transmission to be sound"," I would have ruled by it.\"" Meaning what? [Da'if]"""
"1081","(1082) Abū Saʿd — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Khalīl — informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdiyy — informed us; ʿImrān al-Sakhtiyyānī — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abān — narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Sālim al-Qaddāḥ — narrated to me; Isrāʾīl — from ʿAmr ibn Khālid — from Zayd ibn ʿAlī — from his father — from his grandfather — from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālliib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: One of my forearms broke, so I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \Wipe over the bandages (al-jabāʾir).\""\n\nʿAmr ibn Khālid al-Wāsiṭī was well-known for fabricating hadith. Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn"," and other imams of hadith declared him a liar. Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarraḥ attributed to him the fabrication of hadith"," saying: \""He was in our neighbourhood"," but when he was exposed"," he moved to Wāsiṭ.\""\n\nHe was followed in this by ʿUmūs ibn Mūsā ibn Wajīh"," who narrated it from Zayd ibn ʿAlī similarly. ʿUmūs ibn Mūsā is abandoned (matrūk) and attributed to fabrication — and we seek refuge in Allah from being led astray.\n\nIt has also been narrated through another unknown chain from Zayd ibn ʿAlī"," and it is nothing [of value].\n\nAbū al-Walīd — Khālid ibn Yazīd al-Makkī — narrated it through another chain from Zayd ibn ʿAlī from ʿAlī"," as a mursal narration. Abū al-Walīd is weak (ḍaʿīf).\n\nNothing is authentically established from the Prophet ﷺ on this topic. The most authentic narration in this regard is the hadith of ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ"," which has already been mentioned"," though it is not strong. The matter rests upon the statements of the fuqahāʾ from among the Tābiʿīn and those after them"," along with what has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar regarding wiping over the bandage. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Mawḍūʿ. Narrated by Ibn Mājah"," 657.]"""
"1082","(1083) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh — informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb — narrated to us; Shuʿbah — from ʿAmr (I think he meant ibn Murrah) — from Yūsuf al-Makkī, who said: A companion of ours experienced a wet dream while he had a wound, and he had bandaged his chest. So we asked ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr, and he said: \He should perform ghusl and wipe over the cloth","\"" or he said: \""He should wipe over his chest.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1083","(1084) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl — in Baghdad — informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik — narrated to us; Yazīd, meaning Ibn Hārūn — informed us; Sulaymān al-Taymī — narrated to us, saying: I asked Ṭāwūs about a scratch a person might have, who intends to perform wuḍūʾ or ghusl from janābah, and over which he had tied a cloth. He said: \If he fears [harm]"," then let him wipe over the cloth"," and if he does not fear"," then let him wash it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1084","(1085) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān al-Tanūkhī — narrated to us; Bishr ibn Bakr — narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī — narrated to us; Abū Bakr — narrated to me, saying: I heard ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, Mujāhid ibn Jabr, and Ṭāwūs saying regarding a man whose finger was wounded: \He should wash off the blood that has stained it"," then bandage it"," and then wipe over the bandage when he performs wuḍūʾ. If the blood seeps through and becomes apparent"," he should replace it with another bandage"," and then wipe over it when he performs wuḍūʾ.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1085","(1086) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bushrān — in Baghdad — informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr — narrated to us; Maʿmār ibn Sulaymān — from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā al-Baṣrī, that Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to him: A man came to al-Ḥasan and asked him — and I was listening — saying: \His thigh or shin has broken"," and he has become in a state of janābah.\"" So he (al-Ḥasan) commanded him to wipe over the bandages (al-jabāʾir).\n\nHe (the narrator) said: And Saʿdān narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh — narrated to us; ʿImrān ibn Ḥudayr — narrated to us"," saying: I had a severe wound from the plague"," and I became in a state of janābah. So I asked Abā Mijlaz"," and he said: \""Wipe — it will suffice you.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1086","(1087) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh — informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān — narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan — narrated to us; Abū ʿĀmir — narrated to us; al-Walīd, meaning Ibn Muslim — narrated to us, and Shaybān informed us from Ashʿath, who said: I asked Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī and said: \My hand has broken"," and upon it are its cloth"," its splints"," and its bandages"," and sometimes I become in a state of janābah.\"" He said: \""Wipe over it with water"," for Allah"," the Most High"," accepts the excuse (maʿdhirah).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1087","(1088) And through his chain, he said: al-Walīd narrated to us from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, who said: \The bandages and splints should not be placed over a wound or a break that is in the area of wuḍūʾ until he performs his wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh and washes the area of that wound from what has appeared of its blood.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1088","(1089) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad and Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib — both said: Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ — narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq — narrated to us; Maʿmar — from Hammām ibn Munabbih — from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The ṣalāh of any one of you is not accepted when he has broken his wuḍūʾ until he performs wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1089","(1090) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān — in Baghdad — informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh — narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān — narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm — narrated to us; Shuʿbah — from Abū al-Malīḥ, meaning Ibn Usāmah — from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Allah does not accept a ṣalāh without purification (ṭahūr)"," nor a ṣadaqah from ill-gotten wealth (ghulūl).\"" Abū al-Malīḥ is Ibn Usāmah ibn ʿUmayr al-Hudhalī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1090","(1091) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr — informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtī al-Qāḍī — narrated to us; Abū Ḥudhayfah — narrated to us; ʿIkrimah —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā — narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn Yūnus — narrated to us; ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār — narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr — narrated to me; Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — narrated to me; Sālim, the freed slave of al-Mahriyy, said: I went out with ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr to the funeral of Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and I passed by the chamber of ʿĀʾishah, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān called for water for wuḍūʾ. I heard ʿĀʾishah calling out to him: \O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," complete your wuḍūʾ thoroughly"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Woe to the heels from the Fire.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of Abū ʿAbd Allāh. Abū Saʿīd added in his hadith: \""So ʿĀʾishah ordered water for wuḍūʾ to be brought for him and said to him…\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in virtue of corroborating evidence. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 6/40.]"""
"1091","(1092) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr narrated to us; Ibn Fuḍayl narrated from Abū Mālik al-Ashjaʿī from Ribʿī from Ḥudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Its earth was made for me a means of purification when we do not find water.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 1522.]"""
"1092","(1093) Abū Saʿīd — Sharīk ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn al-Ḥasan al-Isfarāʾinī — informed us; Bishr ibn Aḥmad narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that he said: \No one should offer the funeral prayer except in a state of purity.\""\n\nAnd Mālik likewise narrated it from Nāfiʿ. As for what has been narrated from him regarding tayammum for the funeral prayer"," it may pertain to a journey when water is not available.\n\nIn the isnād of the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar regarding tayammum there is weakness"," which we have mentioned in the book al-Maʿrifah.\n\nAs for what al-Mughīrah ibn Ziyād narrated from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās in this regard"," it is not authentically established from him; it is merely the statement of ʿAṭāʾ. Likewise"," Ibn Jurayj narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ as his own statement. This is one of the things for which Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal and Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn criticized al-Mughīrah ibn Ziyād"," for he raised it to the Prophet ﷺ"," and it is an error"," which we have clarified in al-Khilāfiyyāt. And with Allah is success. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1093","(1094) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Asadī in Hamadhān narrated to us; ʿUmayr ibn Mirdās narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us; al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to us; Bakr ibn Sawādah narrated to us; ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār narrated to us; from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: \Two men went out on a journey and the time of prayer came upon them"," but they had no water with them. So they performed tayammum with clean earth and prayed. Then they found water within the time [of that prayer]. One of them repeated the prayer and performed wuḍūʾ"," while the other did not repeat. They then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said to the one who did not repeat: 'You have attained the Sunnah"," and your prayer is sufficient for you.' And he said to the one who performed wuḍūʾ and repeated: 'For you is the reward twice over.'\""\n\nIt was also narrated by other than ʿAbdullāh ibn Nāfiʿ from al-Layth from ʿUmayr ibn Abī Nājiyah from Bakr ibn Sawādah from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from the Prophet ﷺ"," as a mursal ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 338.]"""
"1094","(1095) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed it to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from ʿUmayr ibn Abī Nājiyah — and he mentioned it thus in my book as ʿUmayr, but the correct form is ʿUmayrah ibn Abī Nājiyah. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ḥākim, 1/287.]"
"1095","(1096) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd said: \The mention of Abū Saʿīd in this ḥadīth is an error (wahm) and is not preserved; it is mursal.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And in it there is a third point of disagreement.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1096","(1097) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed it to us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; Ibn Lahīʿah narrated to us; Bakr ibn Sawādah narrated to us; Abū ʿAbdillāh, the mawlā of Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUbayd, narrated to us; from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār: \That two men from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ — with the same meaning.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 339.]"""
"1097","(1098) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim al-Zāhid informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Juʿshum narrated to us; Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; from Nāfiʿ, who said: \Ibn ʿUmar performed tayammum at a distance of one or two miles from Madīnah and prayed ʿAṣr. He arrived [in Madīnah] while the sun was still high"," and he did not repeat the prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 1/289.]"""
"1098","(1099) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Raffāʾ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways and ʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ both said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to us from his father, who said: \The jurists whom I met and whose opinions were followed — among them Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib — and he mentioned the seven jurists of Madīnah"," and mentioned some of their positions"," including that they used to say: 'Whoever performs tayammum and prays"," then finds water"," whether within the time [of that prayer] or after the time has expired"," there is no repetition upon him. He should perform wuḍūʾ for future prayers and perform ghusl. And tayammum from janābah is equivalent to wuḍūʾ.'\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from al-Shaʿbī"," al-Nakhaʿī"," al-Zuhrī"," and others. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 339.]"""
"1099","(1100) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Khuzāʿī and ʿAbdullāh ibn Muslimah both said: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; al-Qāsim ibn Ghannām narrated to us; from some of his maternal aunts, from Umm Farwah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Which deed is best?' He said: 'Prayer at the beginning of its time.'\""\n\nAl-Khuzāʿī said in his ḥadīth: \""From an aunt of his called Umm Farwah who had given bayʿah to the Prophet ﷺ: that the Prophet ﷺ was asked.\"" And we have narrated from Ibn ʿUmar what has preceded. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 426.]"""
"1100","(1101) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān narrated to us; Muʿallā narrated to us; Sharīk narrated to us; Abū Isḥāq narrated to us; al-Ḥārith narrated to us; from ʿAlī, who said: \When a man becomes junub during a journey"," he should wait until the end of the time [of prayer]. If he does not find water"," he should perform tayammum and pray.\""\n\nAl-Ḥārith al-Aʿwar — no ḥujjah is established through him. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 1699.]"""
"1101","(1102) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Jurjānī informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAsqalānī informed us: Ḥarmalah informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed us: ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim narrated to him from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ — and he mentioned the hadith. She said: \Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ awoke and the time for prayer had come. Water was sought but was not found"," so the verse of tayammum was narrated.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1102","(1103) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ṣāʿid informed us: Muḥammad ibn Zunbūr informed us: Fuḍayl ibn ʿIyāḍ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān from Nāfiʿ: that Ibn ʿUmar performed tayammun at the enclosure of the sheep (murbad al-naʿam) and prayed, while he was at a distance of three miles from Madīnah. Then he entered Madīnah while the sun was still high, and he did not repeat the prayer.\n\nIt was narrated by Ibn ʿUyaynah and Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Ibn ʿAjlān, and it was narrated by Yaḥyā al-Anṣārī and Mālik from Nāfiʿ.\n[Ḥasan. It was narrated by al-Shāfiʿī, 115]"
"1103","(1104) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: Abū ʿĀmir informed us: al-Walīd, meaning Ibn Muslim, said: It was said to Abū ʿAmr, meaning al-Awzāʿī: \The time for prayer has come and the water is off the path — am I obligated to go to it?\"" He said: Mūsā ibn Yasār narrated to me from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: \""He would be on a journey and the time for prayer would come"," and the water would be at a distance of one or two leagues (ghalwah or ghalwatayn) or something like that"," and he would not deviate towards it.\""\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1104","(1105) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us: Ibrāhīm informed us: Abū ʿĀmir informed us: al-Walīd informed us: Sharīk and Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUmar informed us from Abū Isḥāq from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī, who said: \Seek water until the end of the time. If you do not find water"," then perform tayammum and pray.\""\n\nAnd this is not authentically established from ʿAlī. We hold the position established by the authentic narration from Ibn ʿUmar"," and with him is the apparent meaning of the Qurʾān.\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1105","(1106) And Abū Bakr informed us: Abū Muḥammad informed us: Ibrāhīm informed us: Abū ʿĀmir informed us: al-Walīd informed us: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrating from Ḥakīm ibn Ruzayq from his father, who said: I asked Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab about a shepherd among his sheep, or a shepherd who experiences janābah, and between him and the water there are two or three miles. He said: \He should perform tayammum with pure"," clean earth (ṣaʿīdan ṭayyiban).\""\n[Ḥasan]"""
"1106","(1107) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Bakr, meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah, informed us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ from ʿAṭāʾ from Zādhān from ʿAlī, who said: \If a man becomes junub in an open wilderness and he has a small amount of water with him"," let him give preference to himself with the water (i.e."," keep it for drinking) and let him perform tayammum with earth.\""\n[Ṣaḥīf in other than this chain. It was narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 1118]"""
"1107","(1108) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh informed us: My father informed us: Shuʿbah from ʿAṭāʾ from Zādhān from ʿAlī, who said: \If janābah befalls you and you wish to perform wuḍūʾ\"" — or he said \""to perform ghusl\"" — \""and you have no water with you except what you drink"," and you fear (death from thirst)"," then perform tayammum.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1108","(1109) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \If you are a traveler and you are junub"," or you are not in a state of wuḍūʾ"," and you fear that if you perform wuḍūʾ you will die of thirst"," then do not perform wuḍūʾ — preserve yourself.\""\n\nAnd we have received similar narrations from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī"," ʿAṭāʾ"," Mujāhid"," Ṭāwūs"," and others.\n[Ḍaʿīf. It was narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 1120]"""
"1109","(1110) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Jarīr from Ashʿath from Jaʿfar from Saʿīd, who said: \Ibn ʿAbbās was on a journey"," and with him were some of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ"," among them ʿAmmār. He led them in prayer while he was in a state of tayammum.\""\n\nAnd we have received similar narrations from Ibn al-Musayyab"," al-Ḥasan"," ʿAṭāʾ"," and al-Zuhrī. The hadith of ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ has already passed in this chapter.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1110","(1111) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-Muthannā informed us: Musaddad informed us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth from al-Ḥajjāj from Abū Isḥāq from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī: that he disliked for one who performed tayammum to lead those who had performed wuḍūʾ in prayer.\n\nAnd this is a chain of narration by which no proof can be established.\n[Ḍaʿīf]"
"1111","(1112) Abu 'Abd Allah informed us — Abu Bakr informed us — 'Abd Allah informed us — Ishaq informed us — Ibn Wahb informed us — Mu'awiyah ibn Salih informed us, from Al-'Ala' ibn al-Harith, from Nafi', who said: Ibn 'Umar experienced janabah (major ritual impurity) during a journey and performed tayammum (dry ablution). He then commanded me, and I led him in prayer while I was in a state of wudu' (minor ablution).\n\nThis hadith is carried upon the basis of istihbab (recommendation). And a weak hadith has been narrated regarding it. [Hasan]"
"1112","(1113) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed him — 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz informed us — Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Ramis informed us — 'Uthman ibn Ma'bad informed us — Sa'id ibn Sulayman ibn Matic al-Himyari informed us — Abu Isma'il al-Kufi, i.e., Asad ibn Sa'id, informed us — Salih ibn Bayan informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The one who performed tayammum should not lead those who have performed wudu' in prayer.\"" 'Ali said: Its chain of narration is weak. [Mawdu'. Al-Daraqutni narrated it (1/185)]"""
"1113","(1114) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu Bakr, i.e., Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan, informed us — Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami informed us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — Ma'mar informed us, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no harm in urinating in stagnant water that does not flow"," and then performing ghusl (ritual bath) from it.\"" And he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""When one of you awakens from sleep"," let him not place his hand in the vessel of wudu' until he washes it"," for he does not know where his hand spent the night.\""\n\nBoth of these hadiths were narrated by Muslim in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn Rafi'"," from 'Abd al-Razzaq.\n\nAl-Za'farani said: Al-Shafi'i said in al-Qadim: If dough is kneaded with impure water"," it is not to be eaten"," but it may be fed to animals.\n\nImam Ahmad said: And it has been narrated to us from 'Ata' and Mujahid that he would feed it to chickens. [Sahih. Muslim narrated it (282)]"""
"1114","(1115) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Ja'far, i.e., Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani', narrated to me — Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib informed us — Abu Musa, i.e., Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari and Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi, both said — Anas ibn Iyyad informed us — 'Ubayd Allah informed us, from Nafi', that Ibn 'Umar informed him: That the people descended upon al-Hijr, the land of Thamud, with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they drew water from its wells and kneaded dough with it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to pour out what they had drawn and to feed the dough to the camels. And he commanded them to draw water from the well that she-camels used to drink from.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari. And al-Bukhari narrated it from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir, from Anas ibn Iyyad.\n\nAnd this water, even if it was not impure (najis), when its use was prohibited, he commanded that it be poured out and commanded that what was kneaded with it be fed to the camels. So likewise, that which is prohibited due to its impurity. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari narrated it (319)]"
"1115","(1116) Abu Sa'd, i.e., Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sufi, informed us — Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz informed us — Ibn Salm informed us — Hisham ibn Khalid informed us — al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us — from Suwayd ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz — from Humayd — from Anas: That the Prophet ﷺ was asked about dough into which drops of blood had fallen, and the Prophet ﷺ prohibited eating it.\n\nAl-Walid said: Because fire does not absorb blood. Abu Ahmad said: Thus Ibn Salm narrated it to us from the original of his book.\n\nAnd this hadith is only narrated by Suwayd from Nuh ibn Dhakwan from al-Hasan from Anas.\n\nAbu Ahmad said: Salih ibn Abi al-Jinn narrated to us — Musa ibn Sulayman al-Manbiji informed us — Baqiyyah informed us — Suwayd ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us, from Nuh ibn Dhakwan, from al-Hasan, from Anas: That their young woman kneaded dough for them in a vessel, and her hand was cut by a blade in the dough, so she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \Do not eat it.\""\n\nAbu Ahmad said: And Suwayd"," who confused the narration of this hadith"," narrated it once from Nuh from al-Hasan and once from Humayd from Anas.\n\nAbu Ahmad said: And the bulk of his hadith is such that the trustworthy narrators do not corroborate it"," and it is weak (da'if)"," as they described it — meaning Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Yahya ibn Ma'in and other imams — they declared Suwayd weak. [Da'if. Al-Tabarani narrated it in al-Awsat (1/823)]"""
"1116","(1117) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah, i.e., Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, informed us — Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us — Abu 'Umar informed us — Shu'bah informed us, from al-Hakam, from Abi Juhaifah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out at midday and prayed Dhuhr and 'Asr at al-Bat-ha' as two rak'ahs each, and he set up a spear before him. He performed wudu', and the people began to wipe themselves with the leftover water of his wudu'.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it from Sulayman ibn Harb, from Shu'bah, and Muslim narrated it from another direction. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari narrated it (473)]"
"1117","(1118) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Sa'd, i.e., Ahmad ibn Ya'qub al-Thaqafi, and Abu Muhammad, i.e., 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Musa — and the wording is from al-Thaqafi — both said: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us — Abu al-Walid informed us — Shu'bah informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: I heard Jabir saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit me while I was ill and not conscious. He would perform wudu' and pour some of his wudu' water upon me, and I would regain consciousness. I said: O Messenger of Allah, to whom does the inheritance go? Only distant relatives (kalalah) will inherit from me. Then the verse of al-Fara'id (inheritance) was revealed.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Walid, and Muslim narrated it from another direction from Shu'bah. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari narrated it (191)]"
"1118","(1119) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr informed us — Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr informed us — Zā'idah informed us, from al-A'mash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Maymunah, who mentioned the ghusl of the Prophet ﷺ. She said: When he finished, he moved aside and washed his feet. I gave him a cloth, but he refused it and began to shake off the water with his hand.\n\nMuslim narrated it from the hadith of Zā'idah, from al-A'mash. [Sahih]"
"1119","(1120) Abu Hazim al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas, i.e., Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi, informed us — Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us — Rishdin, i.e., ibn Sa'd, informed us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um informed us — 'Utaybah ibn Humayd informed us — 'Ubadah ibn Nusayy informed us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm informed us, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he performed wudu', he wiped his face with the edge of his garment.\n\nAbu al-'Abbas said: I heard Abu Raja' saying: Ahmad ibn Hanbal asked me about this hadith, so I wrote it down. The Shaykh said: And its chain of narration is not strong.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Yunus ibn 'Ubayd that he said: Sometimes Muhammad ibn Sirin would not find a towel, so he would wipe his face with his garment. [Da'if. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it (54)]"
"1120","(1121) Abu Sa'd ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas informed us — al-Rabi' said: Al-Shafi'i said: If someone asks: From whence did it not become impure? It is said: Because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wudu', and there is no doubt that some of the wudu' water touched his garments, and it is not known whether he washed his garments from it or changed them, and I do not know of any Muslim who did that. And it is rationally understood that when no impurity touches the water, it does not become impure. [Sahih]"
"1121","(1122) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us — Abū al-Jamāhir narrated to us — Saʿīd narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding a man who bathes in a vessel and is then sprinkled by the water that was poured upon him into the vessel: He said, \Indeed"," the water is pure (ṭahūr)"," but it does not purify [another].\"" [Its chain is sound. Al-ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it (256).]"""
"1122","(1123) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān al-Ahwāzī informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings be upon him, performed wuḍūʾ. He scooped a handful and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water from it. Then he scooped a handful and washed his face. Then he scooped a handful and washed his right hand. Then he scooped a handful and washed his left hand. Then he took some water and wiped his head, placing the middle fingers of his hands on the inner part of his ears and the thumbs behind his ears. Then he scooped a handful and washed his right foot. Then he scooped a handful and washed his left foot. [Its chain is sound. Al-Nasāʾī narrated it (102).]"
"1123","(1124) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Ḥusayn ibn Ḥasan narrated to us — Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Sarḥ narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyá narrated to us — Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf narrated to me — Ibn Wahb informed me — ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that Ḥibbān ibn Wāsiʿ narrated to him, that his father narrated to him, that he heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd ibn ʿĀṣim al-Māzinī mentioning: That he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings and peace be upon him, performing wuḍūʾ. He rinsed his mouth, then blew his nose, then washed his face three times and his right hand three times, and the other [left hand] three times. Then he wiped his head with water other than the remainder of his hand, and washed his feet until he thoroughly cleaned them.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd, Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Sarḥ, and Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1124","(1125) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān al-Tanūkhī narrated to us — al-Haytham ibn Jamīl al-Anṭākī narrated to us — Sharīk narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl ibn Abī Ṭālib, from al-Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿawwidh ibn ʿAfrāʾ, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings be upon him, with a vessel containing a mudd or a mudd and a third. He said, \Pour it out.\"" She said"," \""So I poured it upon him"," and he washed his face and his arms up to his elbows. Then he took fresh water and wiped the front and back of his head"," and washed his feet three times.\""\n\nThus did Sharīk ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrate it"," and it is in agreement with the sound narration from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl something resembling its opposite and something resembling its agreement. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (126).]"""
"1125","(1126) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed him — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dāwūd narrated from Sufyān ibn Saʿīd, from Ibn ʿAqīl, from al-Rubayyiʿ: That the Prophet, peace be blessings be upon him, wiped his head with the remainder of water that was in his hand.\n\nThus did a group narrate it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dāwūd and others from al-Thawrī, and some of them said, \With the wetness of his hands.\""\n\nAnd it is as though he intended that he took fresh water"," poured some of it"," and wiped his head with the wetness of his hands.\n\nAnd ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl was not a ḥāfiẓ"," and the scholars of ḥadīth differ regarding the permissibility of using his narrations as proof.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī said: I heard Yaḥyá ibn Maʿīn saying"," \""Ibn ʿAqīl — his ḥadīth is not used as proof.\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿĪsá said: I asked al-Bukhārī about ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl"," and he said"," \""I saw Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm"," and al-Ḥumaydī using his ḥadīth as proof"," and he is a narrator of approximate [acceptability].\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated therein from Abū al-Dardāʾ from the Prophet"," peace be blessings be upon him"," and its chain is weak.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from ʿAlī"," Ibn ʿAbbās"," Ibn Masʿūd"," ʿĀʾishah"," and Anas ibn Mālik from the Prophet"," peace be blessings be upon him"," regarding ghusl with a similar meaning"," but none of that is authentic due to the weakness of their chains"," as I have clarified in al-Khilāfiyyāt.\n\nAnd the most authentic thing in it is what Abū Dāwūd narrated in al-Marāsīl from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl"," from Ḥammād"," from Isḥāq ibn Suwayd"," from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Ziyād"," from the Prophet"," peace be blessings be upon him: That he performed ghusl and noticed a spot on his shoulder that the water had not reached. He took a lock of hair from his head and squeezed it upon his shoulder"," then passed his hand over that place. And this is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (1130).]"""
"1126","(1127) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that Abū al-Sāʾib, the mawlā of Hishām ibn Zuhrah, narrated to him, that he heard Abū Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings be upon him, said, \None of you should bathe in standing water while he is in a state of janābah.\"" He asked"," \""How should he do it"," O Abū Hurayrah?\"" He said"," \""He should take it by scooping it out.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd"," Abū al-Ṭāhir"," and Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsá — all of them from Ibn Wahb. Thus it was narrated with this chain.\n\nAnd it is understood to refer to standing water that is less than two qullahs. If one bathes in it"," it becomes mustaʿmal (used)"," and it is not possible for another to purify himself with it. So he commanded that it be taken by scooping so that what remains in it does not become mustaʿmal. And Allah knows best. And thus is the meaning of what —\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (283).]"""
"1127","(1128) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — Yaḥyá, that is, ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān, narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, who said: I heard my father narrating from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings be upon him, said, \None of you should urinate in standing water"," nor should he bathe therein from janābah.\"" Thus did Ibn ʿAjlān narrate it from his father with this wording. [Its chain is sound. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (70).]"""
"1128","(1129) And it has been narrated from him, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings be upon him: That he forbade urinating in standing water and bathing therein from janābah.\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed him — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us — Yaḥyá ibn Bukayr narrated to us — al-Layth narrated from Ibn ʿAjlān, from Abū al-Zinād, and he mentioned it. And it has been said regarding it from him, from Abū al-Zinād, with another wording. [Its chain is sound.]"
"1129","(1130) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us — Yaḥyá ibn Muḥammad ibn Qays narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān narrated from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah: That the Prophet, peace be blessings be upon him, forbade urinating in standing water and then bathing from it for janābah.\n\nThis wording is the one that was narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from this ḥadīth: \Then bathe from it\"" — except that \""for janābah\"" was not included in the narration. [Its chain is sound.]"""
"1130","(1131) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Thaqafī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us — Abū al-Yamān informed us — Shuʿayb narrated — Abū al-Zinād informed us that he heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj narrating that he heard Abū Hurayrah saying: He heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings be upon him, saying, \None of you should urinate in standing water and then bathe from it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān.\n\nAnd thus did Abū al-Zinād narrate it from Mūsā ibn Abī ʿUthmān"," from his father"," from Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (236).]"""
"1131","(1132) It was narrated to us by Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl in Baghdad, who was informed by Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Razzaz, who narrated to us Sa'dan ibn Nasr, who narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Abu al-Zinad, from Musa ibn Abi 'Uthman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who attributed it (marfu'an) and said: \None of you should urinate in standing water and then bathe from it.\"" This was likewise established from Muhammad ibn Sirin"," from Abu Hurayrah. [Sahih]"""
"1132","(1133) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, who was informed by Abu 'Abd al-Rahman Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Tajir, who was informed by Abu Hatim al-Razi, who narrated to us al-Ansari, who narrated to us Hisham ibn Hassan. And it was narrated to us by Abu 'Abd Allah, who said: and I was informed by Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd Allah — the wording being his — who was informed by al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, who narrated to us 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, who narrated to us Jarir, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \None of you should urinate in standing water and then perform wudu or bathe from it.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Zuhayr ibn Harb"," from Jarir"," and he said in the hadith: \""then bathe from it\"" — without any doubt. Likewise"," it was narrated by 'Awf from Muhammad ibn Sirin"," as a marfu' hadith. [Sahih]"""
"1133","(1134) It was narrated to us by Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri', who was informed by al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who was informed by Yusuf ibn Ya'qub, who narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, who narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Awf, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He said: And Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \None of you should urinate in standing water and then purify yourselves from it.\"" However"," Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani contradicted them both"," narrating it from Muhammad as a mawquf narration traced to Abu Hurayrah. [Sahih]"""
"1134","(1135) It was narrated to us by 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran in Baghdad, who was informed by Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Razzaz, who narrated to us Sa'dan ibn Nasr, who narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: \None of you should urinate in standing water and then bathe from it.\"" Likewise"," it was narrated by Yazid ibn Ibrahim from Muhammad ibn Sirin as a mawquf narration. And it was narrated by Hammam ibn Munabbih from Abu Hurayrah as a marfu' hadith. [Sahih. Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated it"," 1/15]"""
"1135","(1136) It was narrated to us by Abu Tahir al-Faqih, who was informed by Abu Bakr al-Qattan, who was informed by Ahmad ibn Yusuf, who narrated to us 'Abd al-Razzaq, who informed us Ma'mar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Let no one urinate in stagnant water that does not flow"," then bathe from it.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Rafi'"," from 'Abd al-Razzaq. And likewise it was established from Muhammad ibn Sirin"," from Abu Hurayrah"," and from Hammam ibn Munabbih"," from Abu Hurayrah. [Sahih. Ahmad narrated it"," 2/494]"""
"1136","(1137) It was narrated from 'Ata' ibn Mina, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \None of you should urinate in standing water"," then perform wudu from it or drink from it.\"" It was narrated to us by Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq"," who narrated to us Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub"," who narrated to us Bahr ibn Nasr"," who said: it was recited to Ibn Wahb: Anas ibn Iyyad informed you"," from al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman"," from 'Ata' ibn Mina… and he mentioned it. [Hasan. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it"," 66]"""
"1137","(1138) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, who narrated to us Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Marzuq, who narrated to us Sa'id ibn 'Amir, from Shu'bah, from Sulayman, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Ibn 'Abbas: that he was asked about eight people who bathed from a single pool, one of them being in a state of janabah. Ibn 'Abbas said: \Water is not rendered impure by anything.\"" This is permissible if they take from it by scooping; and if they immerse themselves in it and the water amounts to two qullahs or more"," it is also permissible; and if it is less than that"," then the immersion of a person in a state of janabah renders it musta'mal (used). The evidence indicates that it does not become najis (impure). And Allah knows best. [Sahih]"""
"1138","(1139) And it was narrated to us by Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sufi, who was informed by Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz, who said: I heard 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz say: my grandfather Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, who narrated to us Hushaym, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: \One of us would come to the pond while in a state of janabah and bathe from one side of it.\"" [Da'if. Ibn 'Adi narrated it in al-Kamil"," 6/125]"""
"1139","(1140) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, who was informed by Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq and Abu al-Nadr ibn Yusuf, who both said: Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Hafiz narrated to us, who narrated to us 'Ali ibn Hajr al-Sa'di, who narrated to us 'Ali ibn Mushhir, who informed us al-A'mash, who narrated to us Abu Razin and Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When a dog licks the vessel of any one of you"," let him pour it out"," then wash it seven times.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from 'Ali ibn Hajr. [Sahih. Muslim narrated it"," 279]"""
"1140","(1141) It was narrated to us by Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki and Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Ahmad al-Fami, who both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, who informed us al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman, who informed us al-Shafi'i, who informed us Malik. And it was narrated to us by Abu Hazim al-Hafiz, who said: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Abdah al-Saliti narrated to us, who informed us Abu al-Fadl Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Turk, who narrated to us Yahya ibn Yahya, who said: I recited to Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When a dog drinks from the vessel of any one of you"," let him wash it seven times.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf"," from Malik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya. Likewise"," it was narrated by Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah and others from Abu al-Zinad. And it was narrated by 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak from Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash"," from Hisham ibn 'Urwah and others"," from Abu al-Zinad"," from al-A'raj"," from Abu Hurayrah"," from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," regarding a dog that licks a vessel: that it should be washed three"," five"," or seven times. This is extremely da'if. 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak is matruk (abandoned)"," and Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash is not used as a proof"," especially when he narrates from the people of the Hijaz. And it was narrated by 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah"," from Isma'il"," from Hisham"," from Abu al-Zinad: \""Wash it seven times","\"" as narrated by the trustworthy narrators. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari narrated it"," 170]"""
"1141","(1142) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar reported from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The purification of the vessel of any one of you"," when a dog licks it"," is that he wash it seven times.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās as a musnad narration"," and in what we have mentioned there is sufficiency. And it has been narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās"," Abū Hurayrah"," and ʿĀʾishah regarding washing the vessel seven times after a dog licks it"," from their fatwā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 279]"""
"1142","(1143) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr al-Zāhid informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr ibn Sābiq al-Khawlānī informed us; Bishr ibn Bakr informed us; al-Awzāʿī reported from Ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The purification of the vessel of any one of you"," when a dog licks it"," is that he wash it seven times"," the first of them with earth (turāb).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 279]"""
"1143","(1144) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed us; my father informed us; Ismāʿīl reported from Hishām ibn Ḥassān from Ibn Sīrīn, and he mentioned it with its like. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1144","(1145) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibn ʿUyaynah reported from Ayyūb ibn Abī Tamīmah from Ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When a dog licks the vessel of any one of you"," let him wash it seven times"," the first or the last of them with earth (turāb).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī"," 91]"""
"1145","(1146) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us; Abān informed us; Qatādah reported that Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated to him from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When a dog licks the vessel"," wash it seven times"," the seventh with earth (turāb).\""\n\nAnd Saʿīd ibn Bashīr said from Qatādah: \""The first with earth (turāb).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 73]"""
"1146","(1147) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated it to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Hāniʾ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakkār informed us; Saʿīd ibn Bashīr reported from Qatādah with his chain of narration, similar to it, except that he said: \The first with earth (turāb).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/64]"""
"1147","(1148) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar informed us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us; Yazīd ibn Sinān informed us; Muʿādh ibn Hishām informed us; my father reported from Qatādah from Khilās from Abū Rāfiʿ from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \When a dog licks the vessel"," wash it seven times"," the first of them with earth (turāb).\""\n\nThis is a gharīb hadith. If Muʿādh preserved it accurately"," it is ḥasan"," because earth (turāb) in this hadith was not narrated by any trustworthy narrator other than Ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah. And those other than Hishām narrated it from Qatādah from Ibn Sīrīn"," as has been previously mentioned.\n\nAnd mention of earth (turāb) has been established in the hadith of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mughaffal from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 338]"""
"1148","(1149) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq informed us; Wahb ibn Jarīr informed us; Shuʿbah informed us; Abū al-Tayyāḥ reported from Muṭarrif from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mughaffal that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded the killing of dogs, then he said: \What is the matter with me and with dogs?\"" And he permitted the hunting dog and the sheepdog"," and he said: \""When a dog licks the vessel"," wash it seven times"," and the eighth rub it with earth (turāb).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ through various routes from Shuʿbah.\n\nAnd Abū Hurayrah is the most proficient narrator of this hadith in his era"," so his narration is more deserving.\n\nAnd Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah his fatwā of seven"," as he narrated it"," and in that there is evidence of the error of the narration of ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān from ʿAṭāʾ from Abū Hurayrah regarding three.\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Malik is not accepted when he contradicts trustworthy narrators. And with Allah is the success. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 280]"""
